"limitations":{"en":["Requires test environment setup","Minimum 80% test coverage mandatory"],"zh":["需要测试环境设置","至少80%的测试覆盖率是必需的"],"ja":["テスト環境の設定が必要","少なくとも80%のテストカバレッジは必須"],"ko":["테스트 환경 설정이 필요","최소 80%의 테스트 커버리지가 필수"],"es":["Requiere la configuración de un entorno de pruebas","Una cobertura de pruebas mínima de 80% es obligatoria"],"fr":["Requiere la configuration d''un entorno de pruebas","Une couverture de pruebas minimale de 80% est obligatoire"],"de":["Requiere die Konfiguration eines Testumgebungs","Eine Mindest-Pruebas-Ausstattung von 80% ist obligatorisch"],"pt":["Exige configuração de ambiente de teste","Cobertura de teste mínima de 80% obrigatória"],"ru":["Требует настройки тестовой среды","Минимальная тестовая покрытие 80% обязательна"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد بيئة اختبار","الغطاء الأدنى للاختبار 80% إجباري"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"0c0d287804b33a98bbba2df8169da80403b29fcae4a45aca96522e6c8d022d17","repoEtag":"W/\"1d66934774ad40d3d916abf4c33c3e340ab032f8212b35e12a94daa7359886c9\"","qualityScore":89}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('huggingface/skills/hugging-face-trackio', 'official', 'huggingface', 'skills', 'huggingface/skills', 'hugging-face-trackio', 7571, 450, 89, '2026-03-01T05:02:56Z', '2026-03-01T05:14:07.538Z', '0d0654cc659bca435bb4b278ff7f1d6c2978caebed1adb5b01dcf5a69286ca2b', '{"id":"huggingface/skills/hugging-face-trackio","name":"hugging-face-trackio","description":{"zh":"Hugging Face Trackio 是一个实验跟踪库，用于记录和可视化 ML 训练指标。它支持实时仪表盘可视化和 HF Space 同步","ja":"Hugging Face Trackio は、ML トレーニング メトリックを記録および視覚化するための実験追跡ライブラリです。リアルタイム ダッシュボード視覚化と HF Space 同期をサポートします","ko":"Hugging Face Trackio는 ML 훈련 메트릭을 기록 및 시각화하는 실험 추적 라이브러리입니다. 실시간 대시보드 시각화 및 HF Space 동기화를 지원합니다","es":"hugging-face-trackio es una biblioteca de seguimiento de experimentos de aprendizaje automático que permite registrar y visualizar métricas de entrenamiento","fr":"hugging-face-trackio est une bibliothèque de suivi d''expériences d''apprentissage automatique qui permet d''enregistrer et de visualiser des métriques d''entraînement","de":"hugging-face-trackio ist eine Bibliothek zur Nachverfolgung von Machine-Learning-Experimenten, die das Registrieren und Visualisieren von Trainingsmetriken ermöglicht","pt":"O hugging-face-trackio é uma biblioteca de rastreamento de experimentos para ML que fornece logging e visualização de métricas de treinamento","ru":"ИИ Агент hugging-face-trackio - библиотека для отслеживания экспериментов ML, обеспечивающая логирование и визуализацию метрик обучения","ar":"أداة الذكاء الاصطناعي hugging-face-trackio هي مكتبة لتتبع تجارب تعلم الآلة توفر سجلاً وتصور لمقاييس التدريب","en":"Track and visualize ML training experiments with Trackio. Use when logging metrics during training (Python API) or retrieving/analyzing logged metrics (CLI). Supports real-time dashboard visualization, HF Space syncing, and JSON output for automation."},"owner":"huggingface","repo":"skills","repoPath":"huggingface/skills","stars":7571,"forks":450,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T05:02:56Z","topics":[],"skillMd":{"name":"hugging-face-trackio","description":"Track and visualize ML training experiments with Trackio. Use when logging metrics during training (Python API), firing alerts for training diagnostics, or retrieving/analyzing logged metrics (CLI). Supports real-time dashboard visualization, alerts with webhooks, HF Space syncing, and JSON output for automation.","bodyPreview":"# Trackio - Experiment Tracking for ML Training\n\nTrackio is an experiment tracking library for logging and visualizing ML training metrics. It syncs to Hugging Face Spaces for real-time monitoring dashboards.\n\n## Three Interfaces\n\n| Task | Interface | Reference |\n|------|-----------|-----------|\n| **Logging metrics** during training | Python API | [references/logging_metrics.md](references/logging_metrics.md) |\n| **Firing alerts** for training diagnostics | Python API | [references/alerts.md](re","body":"# Trackio - Experiment Tracking for ML Training\n\nTrackio is an experiment tracking library for logging and visualizing ML training metrics. It syncs to Hugging Face Spaces for real-time monitoring dashboards.\n\n## Three Interfaces\n\n| Task | Interface | Reference |\n|------|-----------|-----------|\n| **Logging metrics** during training | Python API | [references/logging_metrics.md](references/logging_metrics.md) |\n| **Firing alerts** for training diagnostics | Python API | [references/alerts.md](references/alerts.md) |\n| **Retrieving metrics & alerts** after/during training | CLI | [references/retrieving_metrics.md](references/retrieving_metrics.md) |\n\n## When to Use Each\n\n### Python API → Logging\n\nUse `import trackio` in your training scripts to log metrics:\n\n- Initialize tracking with `trackio.init()`\n- Log metrics with `trackio.log()` or use TRL''s `report_to=\"trackio\"`\n- Finalize with `trackio.finish()`\n\n**Key concept**: For remote/cloud training, pass `space_id` — metrics sync to a Space dashboard so they persist after the instance terminates.\n\n→ See [references/logging_metrics.md](references/logging_metrics.md) for setup, TRL integration, and configuration options.\n\n### Python API → Alerts\n\nInsert `trackio.alert()` calls in training code to flag important events — like inserting print statements for debugging, but structured and queryable:\n\n- `trackio.alert(title=\"...\", level=trackio.AlertLevel.WARN)` — fire an alert\n- Three severity levels: `INFO`, `WARN`, `ERROR`\n- Alerts are printed to terminal, stored in the database, shown in the dashboard, and optionally sent to webhooks (Slack/Discord)\n\n**Key concept for LLM agents**: Alerts are the primary mechanism for autonomous experiment iteration. An agent should insert alerts into training code for diagnostic conditions (loss spikes, NaN gradients, low accuracy, training stalls). Since alerts are printed to the terminal, an agent that is watching the training script''s output will see them automatically. For background or detached runs, the agent can poll via CLI instead.\n\n→ See [references/alerts.md](references/alerts.md) for the full alerts API, webhook setup, and autonomous agent workflows.\n\n### CLI → Retrieving\n\nUse the `trackio` command to query logged metrics and alerts:\n\n- `trackio list projects/runs/metrics` — discover what''s available\n- `trackio get project/run/metric` — retrieve summaries and values\n- `trackio list alerts --project <name> --json` — retrieve alerts\n- `trackio show` — launch the dashboard\n- `trackio sync` — sync to HF Space\n\n**Key concept**: Add `--json` for programmatic output suitable for automation and LLM agents.\n\n→ See [references/retrieving_metrics.md](references/retrieving_metrics.md) for all commands, workflows, and JSON output formats.\n\n## Minimal Logging Setup\n\n```python\nimport trackio\n\ntrackio.init(project=\"my-project\", space_id=\"username/trackio\")\ntrackio.log({\"loss\": 0.1, \"accuracy\": 0.9})\ntrackio.log({\"loss\": 0.09, \"accuracy\": 0.91})\ntrackio.finish()\n```\n\n### Minimal Retrieval\n\n```bash\ntrackio list projects --json\ntrackio get metric --project my-project --run my-run --metric loss --json\n```\n\n## Autonomous ML Experiment Workflow\n\nWhen running experiments autonomously as an LLM agent, the recommended workflow is:\n\n1. **Set up training with alerts** — insert `trackio.alert()` calls for diagnostic conditions\n2. **Launch training** — run the script in the background\n3. **Poll for alerts** — use `trackio list alerts --project <name> --json --since <timestamp>` to check for new alerts\n4. **Read metrics** — use `trackio get metric ...` to inspect specific values\n5. **Iterate** — based on alerts and metrics, stop the run, adjust hyperparameters, and launch a new run\n\n```python\nimport trackio\n\ntrackio.init(project=\"my-project\", config={\"lr\": 1e-4})\n\nfor step in range(num_steps):\n    loss = train_step()\n    trackio.log({\"loss\": loss, \"step\": step})\n\n    if step > 100 and loss > 5.0:\n        trackio.alert(\n            title=\"Loss divergence\",\n            text=f\"Loss {loss:.4f} still high after {step} steps\",\n            level=trackio.AlertLevel.ERROR,\n        )\n    if step > 0 and abs(loss) < 1e-8:\n        trackio.alert(\n            title=\"Vanishing loss\",\n            text=\"Loss near zero — possible gradient collapse\",\n            level=trackio.AlertLevel.WARN,\n        )\n\ntrackio.finish()\n```\n\nThen poll from a separate terminal/process:\n\n```bash\ntrackio list alerts --project my-project --json --since \"2025-01-01T00:00:00\"\n```\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-03-01T05:14:07.538Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI工具 - Hugging Face Trackio 实验跟踪","ja":"AIエージェント - Hugging Face Trackio 実験追跡","ko":"AI 에이전트 - Hugging Face Trackio 실험 추적","es":"Herramientas de Inteligencia Artificial: hugging-face-tra...","fr":"Outils d''Intelligence Artificielle: hugging-face-trackio","de":"KI-Tools: hugging-face-trackio","pt":"Ferramentas de IA: hugging-face-trackio para Experimentos...","ru":"ИИ Агенты: hugging-face-trackio для отслеживания эксперим...","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: hugging-face-trackio لتتبع تجارب ML","en":"hugging-face-trackio"},"description":{"zh":"Hugging Face Trackio 是一个实验跟踪库，用于记录和可视化 ML 训练指标。它支持实时仪表盘可视化和 HF Space 同步","ja":"Hugging Face Trackio は、ML トレーニング メトリックを記録および視覚化するための実験追跡ライブラリです。リアルタイム ダッシュボード視覚化と HF Space 同期をサポートします","ko":"Hugging Face Trackio는 ML 훈련 메트릭을 기록 및 시각화하는 실험 추적 라이브러리입니다. 실시간 대시보드 시각화 및 HF Space 동기화를 지원합니다","es":"hugging-face-trackio es una biblioteca de seguimiento de experimentos de aprendizaje automático que permite registrar y visualizar métricas de entrenamiento","fr":"hugging-face-trackio est une bibliothèque de suivi d''expériences d''apprentissage automatique qui permet d''enregistrer et de visualiser des métriques d''entraî...","de":"hugging-face-trackio ist eine Bibliothek zur Nachverfolgung von Machine-Learning-Experimenten, die das Registrieren und Visualisieren von Trainingsmetriken e...","pt":"O hugging-face-trackio é uma biblioteca de rastreamento de experimentos para ML que fornece logging e visualização de métricas de treinamento","ru":"ИИ Агент hugging-face-trackio - библиотека для отслеживания экспериментов ML, обеспечивающая логирование и визуализацию метрик обучения","ar":"أداة الذكاء الاصطناعي hugging-face-trackio هي مكتبة لتتبع تجارب تعلم الآلة توفر سجلاً وتصور لمقاييس التدريب","en":"Track and visualize ML training experiments with Trackio. Use when logging metrics during training (Python API) or retrieving/analyzing logged metrics (CLI)...."},"definition":{"en":"Track and visualize ML training experiments with Trackio. Use when logging metrics during training (Python API) or retrieving/analyzing logged metrics (CLI). Supports real-time dashboard visualization, HF Space syncing, and JSON output for automation."},"features":{"zh":["记录和可视化 ML 训练指标","支持实时仪表盘可视化","HF Space 同步","JSON 输出用于自动化","Python API 和 CLI 接口"],"ja":["ML トレーニング メトリックを記録および視覚化","リアルタイム ダッシュボード視覚化をサポート","HF Space 同期","JSON 出力による自動化","Python API と CLI インターフェース"],"ko":["ML 훈련 메트릭을 기록 및 시각화","실시간 대시보드 시각화 지원","HF Space 동기화","JSON 출력을 통한 자동화","Python API 및 CLI 인터페이스"],"es":["Registro de métricas de entrenamiento","Visualización en tiempo real","Sincronización con Hugging Face Spaces","Salida JSON para automatización","Interfaz de línea de comandos (CLI)","Interfaz de programación de aplicaciones (API) de Python"],"fr":["Enregistrement de métriques d''entraînement","Visualisation en temps réel","Synchronisation avec Hugging Face Spaces","Sortie JSON pour l''automatisation","Interface de ligne de commande (CLI)","Interface de programmation d''applications (API) Python"],"de":["Registrierung von Trainingsmetriken","Echtzeit-Visualisierung","Synchronisation mit Hugging Face Spaces","JSON-Ausgabe für Automatisierung","Kommandozeilen-Schnittstelle (CLI)","Python-API-Schnittstelle"],"pt":["Logging de métricas de treinamento em Python","Visualização em tempo real com dashboards","Sincronização com Hugging Face Spaces","Saída JSON para automação","Interface de linha de comando para recuperação de métricas","Suporte à análise de métricas durante o treinamento"],"ru":["Логирование метрик обучения на Python","Визуализация в режиме реального времени с помощью панелей","Синхронизация с Hugging Face Spaces","Выходной JSON для автоматизации","Интерфейс командной строки для получения метрик","Поддержка анализа метрик во время обучения"],"ar":["تسجيل معايير التدريب بلغة بايثون","التصوير في الوقت الفعلي مع لوحات التحكم","التزامن مع مساحات هوجينغ فايس","إخراج JSON للاتوماسیون","واجهة سطر الأوامر لاسترجاع المعايير","دعم تحليل المعايير أثناء التدريب"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI 工具","实验跟踪","ML 训练","实时仪表盘","HF Space","Python API","CLI","JSON 输出"],"ja":["AI エージェント","実験追跡","ML トレーニング","リアルタイム ダッシュボード","HF Space","Python API","CLI","JSON 出力"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","실험 추적","ML 훈련","실시간 대시보드","HF Space","Python API","CLI","JSON 출력"],"es":["herramientas de inteligencia artificial","aprendizaje automático","seguimiento de experimentos","visualización de métricas","Hugging Face Spaces","Python API","CLI","automatización","registro de métricas"],"fr":["outils d''intelligence artificielle","apprentissage automatique","suivi d''expériences","visualisation de métriques","Hugging Face Spaces","API Python","CLI","automatisation","enregistrement de métriques"],"de":["KI-Tools","Machine Learning","Nachverfolgung von Experimenten","Visualisierung von Metriken","Hugging Face Spaces","Python-API","CLI","Automatisierung","Registrierung von Metriken"],"pt":["hugging face trackio","experimentos de ml","logging de métricas","visualização de métricas","python api","cli","hugging face spaces","ia","ferramentas de ia"],"ru":["hugging face trackio","эксперименты ml","логирование метрик","визуализация метрик","пайтон апи","кли","пространства хаггинга","ии агенты","инструменты ии"],"ar":["hugging face trackio","تجارب تعلم الآلة","تسجيل المعايير","تصوير المعايير","بايثون أبي","سطر الأوامر","مساحات هوجينغ فايس","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Machine Learning Agents needing advanced experiment tracking and visualization capabilities with Hugging Face Spaces","zh":"非常适合需要利用 Hugging Face Spaces 进行高级实验跟踪和可视化功能的机器学习智能体","ja":"Hugging Face Spaces を使用した高度な実験トラッキングと可視化機能を必要とする機械学習エージェントに最適です","ko":"Hugging Face Spaces를 이용한 고급 실험 추적 및 시각화 기능이 필요한 머신러닝 에이전트에 완벽합니다","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Aprendizaje Automático que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de seguimiento y visualización de experimentos con Hugging Face Spaces","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents d''Apprentissage Automatique nécessitant des capacités de suivi et de visualisation d''expériences avancées avec Hugging Face Spaces","de":"Perfekt für Machine-Learning-Agents, die erweiterte Experiment-Tracking- und Visualisierungsfunktionen mit Hugging Face Spaces benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Aprendizado de Máquina que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de rastreamento de experimentos e visualização com Hugging Face Spaces","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов машинного обучения, которым требуются расширенные возможности отслеживания экспериментов и визуализации с Hugging Face Spaces","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء التعلم الآلي الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات متقدمة لتتبع التجارب والتخيل مع Hugging Face Spaces"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to log and visualize ML training metrics in real-time using the Trackio Python API, supports webhooks for alerts and JSON output for automation, and syncs with Hugging Face Spaces for seamless monitoring","zh":"赋能智能体使用 Trackio Python API 实时记录和可视化 ML 训练指标，支持用于警报的 webhook 和用于自动化的 JSON 输出，并与 Hugging Face Spaces 同步以实现无缝监控","ja":"Trackio Python API を使用して ML トレーニングメトリクスをリアルタイムで記録および可視化する機能をエージェントに提供し、アラート用の Webhook と自動化のための JSON 出力をサポートし、Hugging Face Spaces と同期してシームレスなモニタリングを実現します","ko":"Trackio Python API를 사용하여 ML 훈련 메트릭을 실시간으로 기록 및 시각화할 수 있도록 에이전트에 권한을 부여하며, 경고를 위한 웹후크와 자동화를 위한 JSON 출력을 지원하고, 원활한 모니터링을 위해 Hugging Face Spaces와 동기화합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a registrar y visualizar métricas de entrenamiento de ML en tiempo real utilizando la API de Python de Trackio, admite webhooks para alertas y salida JSON para automatización, y se sincroniza con Hugging Face Spaces para una supervisión sin problemas","fr":"Autorise les agents à enregistrer et à visualiser les métriques d''entraînement de ML en temps réel en utilisant l''API Python de Trackio, prend en charge les webhooks pour les alertes et la sortie JSON pour l''automatisation, et se synchronise avec Hugging Face Spaces pour une surveillance sans problème","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, ML-Trainingsmetriken in Echtzeit mit der Trackio Python API zu protokollieren und zu visualisieren, unterstützt Webhooks für Warnungen und JSON-Ausgabe für Automatisierung und synchronisiert mit Hugging Face Spaces für eine nahtlose Überwachung","pt":"Capacita os agentes a registrar e visualizar métricas de treinamento de ML em tempo real usando a API Python do Trackio, suporta webhooks para alertas e saída JSON para automação, e sincroniza com Hugging Face Spaces para monitoramento contínuo","ru":"Позволяет агентам регистрировать и визуализировать метрики обучения ML в реальном времени с использованием Trackio Python API, поддерживает вебхуки для оповещений и вывод JSON для автоматизации, а также синхронизируется с Hugging Face Spaces для беспрерывного мониторинга","ar":"يمكّن الوكلاء من تسجيل مقاييس تدريب التعلم الآلي وتصورها في الوقت الفعلي باستخدام Trackio Python API، ويدعم webhooks للتنبيهات ومخرجات JSON للأتمتة، ويتزامن مع Hugging Face Spaces لمراقبة سلسة"},"useCases":{"en":["Logging metrics during ML model training for real-time dashboard visualization","Firing alerts for training diagnostics using webhooks and the Trackio Python API","Retrieving and analyzing logged metrics for ML model optimization"],"zh":["在 ML 模型训练期间记录指标，用于实时仪表板可视化","使用 webhook 和 Trackio Python API 触发训练诊断警报","检索和分析记录的指标以优化 ML 模型"],"ja":["リアルタイムダッシュボード可視化のための ML モデルトレーニング中のメトリクスの記録","Webhook と Trackio Python API を使用したトレーニング診断のアラート発動","ML モデル最適化のための記録されたメトリクスの取得と分析"],"ko":["실시간 대시보드 시각화를 위해 ML 모델 훈련 중 메트릭 기록","웹후크 및 Trackio Python API를 사용하여 훈련 진단 경고 실행","ML 모델 최적화를 위해 기록된 메트릭 검색 및 분석"],"es":["Registro de métricas durante el entrenamiento del modelo de ML para la visualización del panel en tiempo real","Disparo de alertas para diagnósticos de entrenamiento utilizando webhooks y la API de Python de Trackio","Recuperación y análisis de métricas registradas para la optimización del modelo de ML"],"fr":["Enregistrement de métriques pendant l''entraînement du modèle de ML pour la visualisation du tableau de bord en temps réel","Déclenchement d''alertes pour les diagnostics d''entraînement en utilisant les webhooks et l''API Python de Trackio","Récupération et analyse de métriques enregistrées pour l''optimisation du modèle de ML"],"de":["Protokollierung von Metriken während des ML-Modell-Trainings für die Echtzeit-Dashboard-Visualisierung","Auslösen von Warnungen für Trainingsdiagnosen unter Verwendung von Webhooks und der Trackio Python API","Abrufen und Analysieren von protokollierten Metriken für die Optimierung des ML-Modells"],"pt":["Registro de métricas durante o treinamento de modelos de ML para visualização em painel em tempo real","Disparo de alertas para diagnósticos de treinamento usando webhooks e a API Python do Trackio","Recuperação e análise de métricas registradas para otimização de modelos de ML"],"ru":["Логирование метрик во время обучения моделей ML для визуализации на панели управления в реальном времени","Активация оповещений для диагностики обучения с использованием вебхуков и Trackio Python API","Получение и анализ записанных метрик для оптимизации моделей ML"],"ar":["تسجيل المقاييس أثناء تدريب نماذج التعلم الآلي للتخيل على لوحة التحليل في الوقت الفعلي","إطلاق تنبيهات لتشخيص التدريب باستخدام webhooks وTrackio Python API","استرداد وتحليل المقاييس المسجلة لتحسين نموذج التعلم الآلي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Hugging Face account for Space syncing","Python API usage necessary for logging metrics and firing alerts","Limited to ML training experiment tracking"],"zh":["需要 Hugging Face 账户才能进行 Space 同步","必须使用 Python API 才能记录指标和触发警报","仅限于 ML 训练实验跟踪"],"ja":["Space 同期には Hugging Face アカウントが必要","メトリクスの記録とアラート発動には Python API の使用が必須","ML トレーニング実験のトラッキングに限定される"],"ko":["Space 동기화를 위해 Hugging Face 계정 필요","메트릭 기록 및 경고 실행을 위해 Python API 사용 필수","ML 훈련 실험 추적으로 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere una cuenta de Hugging Face para la sincronización de Spaces","Uso de la API de Python necesario para el registro de métricas y el disparo de alertas","Limitado al seguimiento de experimentos de entrenamiento de ML"],"fr":["Nécessite un compte Hugging Face pour la synchronisation des Spaces","Utilisation de l''API Python nécessaire pour l''enregistrement de métriques et le déclenchement d''alertes","Limité au suivi des expériences d''entraînement de ML"],"de":["Benötigt ein Hugging Face-Konto für die Synchronisierung von Spaces","Verwendung der Python API erforderlich für die Protokollierung von Metriken und das Auslösen von Warnungen","Begrenzt auf die Nachverfolgung von ML-Trainings-Experimenten"],"pt":["Requer conta Hugging Face para sincronização com Spaces","Uso da API Python necessário para registrar métricas e disparar alertas","Limitado ao rastreamento de experimentos de treinamento de ML"],"ru":["Требуется учетная запись Hugging Face для синхронизации с Spaces","Необходимо использование Python API для логирования метрик и активации оповещений","Ограничено отслеживанием экспериментов обучения ML"],"ar":["يتطلب حساب Hugging Face لمزامنة Space","استخدام Python API ضروري لتسجيل المقاييس وإطلاق التنبيهات","مقتصر على تتبع تجارب تدريب التعلم الآلي"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"0d0654cc659bca435bb4b278ff7f1d6c2978caebed1adb5b01dcf5a69286ca2b","repoEtag":"W/\"1eedb45a65fd194e9e2d3d99af7f6af15733597c7b4ab6e897487021c9076d2e\"","qualityScore":89}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('google-labs-code/stitch-skills/enhance-prompt', 'official', 'google-labs-code', 'stitch-skills', 'google-labs-code/stitch-skills', 'enhance-prompt', 2070, 243, 89, '2026-02-28T23:06:25Z', '2026-03-01T05:14:08.824Z', 'ccb200c798072438b642b1fa6a5c515563159e2fab3d56e813d76d8afa9a7ce6', '{"id":"google-labs-code/stitch-skills/enhance-prompt","name":"enhance-prompt","description":{"zh":"增强提示引擎可以将粗略的UI生成想法转化为优化后的提示，提高Stitch的生成结果","ja":"プロンプト最適化エンジンは、Stitchの生成結果を向上させるために、UI生成のアイデアを最適化します","ko":"프롬프트 최적화 에이전트는 스티치의 성능을 향상시키기 위해 UI 생성 아이디어를 최적화합니다","es":"El enhance-prompt transforma ideas de UI vagas en prompts pulidos y optimizados para Stitch, mejorando la especificidad y la generación de resultados","fr":"L''enhance-prompt transforme des idées d''UI vagues en prompts optimisés pour Stitch, améliorant la spécificité et la génération de résultats","de":"Der Enhance-Prompt wandelt vage UI-Ideen in optimierte Prompts für Stitch um, die Spezifität und die Ergebnisgenerierung verbessern","pt":"O enhance-prompt transforma ideias de UI vagas em prompts polidos e otimizados para Stitch, melhorando a especificidade e adicionando palavras-chave de UI/UX.","ru":"ИИ Агент enhance-prompt преобразует нечеткие идеи UI в оптимизированные промпты для Stitch, улучшая специфику и добавляя ключевые слова UI/UX.","ar":"أداة الذكاء الاصطناعي enhance-prompt تحول الأفكار غير الدقيقة لUI إلى دفعات محسنة لبرنامج Stitch، مما يحسن الدقة ويضيف كلمات مفتاحية لUI/UX.","en":"Transforms vague UI ideas into polished, Stitch-optimized prompts. Enhances specificity, adds UI/UX keywords, injects design system context, and structures output for better generation results."},"owner":"google-labs-code","repo":"stitch-skills","repoPath":"google-labs-code/stitch-skills","stars":2070,"forks":243,"updatedAt":"2026-02-28T23:06:25Z","topics":[],"skillMd":{"name":"enhance-prompt","description":"Transforms vague UI ideas into polished, Stitch-optimized prompts. Enhances specificity, adds UI/UX keywords, injects design system context, and structures output for better generation results.","bodyPreview":"# Enhance Prompt for Stitch\n\nYou are a **Stitch Prompt Engineer**. Your job is to transform rough or vague UI generation ideas into polished, optimized prompts that produce better results from Stitch.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nBefore enhancing prompts, consult the official Stitch documentation for the latest best practices:\n\n- **Stitch Effective Prompting Guide**: https://stitch.withgoogle.com/docs/learn/prompting/\n\nThis guide contains up-to-date recommendations that may supersede or complement the pat","body":"# Enhance Prompt for Stitch\n\nYou are a **Stitch Prompt Engineer**. Your job is to transform rough or vague UI generation ideas into polished, optimized prompts that produce better results from Stitch.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nBefore enhancing prompts, consult the official Stitch documentation for the latest best practices:\n\n- **Stitch Effective Prompting Guide**: https://stitch.withgoogle.com/docs/learn/prompting/\n\nThis guide contains up-to-date recommendations that may supersede or complement the patterns in this skill.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nActivate when a user wants to:\n- Polish a UI prompt before sending to Stitch\n- Improve a prompt that produced poor results\n- Add design system consistency to a simple idea\n- Structure a vague concept into an actionable prompt\n\n## Enhancement Pipeline\n\nFollow these steps to enhance any prompt:\n\n### Step 1: Assess the Input\n\nEvaluate what''s missing from the user''s prompt:\n\n| Element | Check for | If missing... |\n|---------|-----------|---------------|\n| **Platform** | \"web\", \"mobile\", \"desktop\" | Add based on context or ask |\n| **Page type** | \"landing page\", \"dashboard\", \"form\" | Infer from description |\n| **Structure** | Numbered sections/components | Create logical page structure |\n| **Visual style** | Adjectives, mood, vibe | Add appropriate descriptors |\n| **Colors** | Specific values or roles | Add design system or suggest |\n| **Components** | UI-specific terms | Translate to proper keywords |\n\n### Step 2: Check for DESIGN.md\n\nLook for a `DESIGN.md` file in the current project:\n\n**If DESIGN.md exists:**\n1. Read the file to extract the design system block\n2. Include the color palette, typography, and component styles\n3. Format as a \"DESIGN SYSTEM (REQUIRED)\" section in the output\n\n**If DESIGN.md does not exist:**\n1. Add this note at the end of the enhanced prompt:\n\n```\n---\n💡 **Tip:** For consistent designs across multiple screens, create a DESIGN.md \nfile using the `design-md` skill. This ensures all generated pages share the \nsame visual language.\n```\n\n### Step 3: Apply Enhancements\n\nTransform the input using these techniques:\n\n#### A. Add UI/UX Keywords\n\nReplace vague terms with specific component names:\n\n| Vague | Enhanced |\n|-------|----------|\n| \"menu at the top\" | \"navigation bar with logo and menu items\" |\n| \"button\" | \"primary call-to-action button\" |\n| \"list of items\" | \"card grid layout\" or \"vertical list with thumbnails\" |\n| \"form\" | \"form with labeled input fields and submit button\" |\n| \"picture area\" | \"hero section with full-width image\" |\n\n#### B. Amplify the Vibe\n\nAdd descriptive adjectives to set the mood:\n\n| Basic | Enhanced |\n|-------|----------|\n| \"modern\" | \"clean, minimal, with generous whitespace\" |\n| \"professional\" | \"sophisticated, trustworthy, with subtle shadows\" |\n| \"fun\" | \"vibrant, playful, with rounded corners and bold colors\" |\n| \"dark mode\" | \"dark theme with high-contrast accents on deep backgrounds\" |\n\n#### C. Structure the Page\n\nOrganize content into numbered sections:\n\n```markdown\n**Page Structure:**\n1. **Header:** Navigation with logo and menu items\n2. **Hero Section:** Headline, subtext, and primary CTA\n3. **Content Area:** [Describe the main content]\n4. **Footer:** Links, social icons, copyright\n```\n\n#### D. Format Colors Properly\n\nWhen colors are mentioned, format them as:\n```\nDescriptive Name (#hexcode) for functional role\n```\n\nExamples:\n- \"Deep Ocean Blue (#1a365d) for primary buttons and links\"\n- \"Warm Cream (#faf5f0) for page background\"\n- \"Soft Gray (#6b7280) for secondary text\"\n\n### Step 4: Format the Output\n\nStructure the enhanced prompt in this order:\n\n```markdown\n[One-line description of the page purpose and vibe]\n\n**DESIGN SYSTEM (REQUIRED):**\n- Platform: [Web/Mobile], [Desktop/Mobile]-first\n- Theme: [Light/Dark], [style descriptors]\n- Background: [Color description] (#hex)\n- Primary Accent: [Color description] (#hex) for [role]\n- Text Primary: [Color description] (#hex)\n- [Additional design tokens...]\n\n**Page Structure:**\n1. **[Section]:** [Description]\n2. **[Section]:** [Description]\n...\n```\n\n## Output Options\n\n**Default:** Return the enhanced prompt as text for the user to copy.\n\n**Optional file output:** If the user requests, write to a file:\n- `next-prompt.md` — for use with the `stitch-loop` skill\n- Custom filename specified by user\n\n## Examples\n\n### Example 1: Vague Input → Structured Prompt\n\n**User input:**\n> \"make me a login page\"\n\n**Enhanced output:**\n```markdown\nA clean, trustworthy login page with a centered form and subtle branding.\n\n**DESIGN SYSTEM (REQUIRED):**\n- Platform: Web, Desktop-first\n- Theme: Light, minimal, professional\n- Background: Clean White (#ffffff)\n- Surface: Soft Gray (#f9fafb) for form card\n- Primary Accent: Deep Blue (#2563eb) for submit button and links\n- Text Primary: Near Black (#111827) for headings\n- Text Secondary: Medium Gray (#6b7280) for labels\n- Buttons: Subtly rounded (8px), full-width on form\n- Cards: Gently rounded (12px), soft shadow for elevation\n\n**Page Structure:**\n1. **Header:** Minimal logo, centered\n2. **Login Card:** Centered form with email, password fields, \"Forgot password?\" link\n3. **Submit Button:** Primary blue \"Sign In\" button\n4. **Footer:** \"Don''t have an account? Sign up\" link\n\n---\n💡 **Tip:** For consistent designs across multiple screens, create a DESIGN.md \nfile using the `design-md` skill.\n```\n\n### Example 2: Feature Request → Targeted Edit\n\n**User input:**\n> \"add a search bar\"\n\n**Enhanced output:**\n```markdown\nAdd a search bar to the header navigation.\n\n**Specific changes:**\n- Location: Header, right side before user avatar\n- Style: Pill-shaped input with subtle gray background (#f3f4f6)\n- Icon: Magnifying glass icon on the left, inside the input\n- Placeholder: \"Search...\" in light gray (#9ca3af)\n- Behavior: Expands on focus with subtle shadow\n- Width: 240px default, 320px on focus\n\n**Context:** This is a targeted edit. Make only this change while preserving all existing elements.\n```\n\n## Tips for Best Results\n\n1. **Be specific early** — Vague inputs need more enhancement\n2. **Match the user''s intent** — Don''t over-design if they want simple\n3. **Keep it structured** — Numbered sections help Stitch understand hierarchy\n4. **Include the design system** — Consistency is key for multi-page projects\n5. **One change at a time for edits** — Don''t bundle unrelated changes\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-03-01T05:14:08.824Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能工具：增强提示引擎","ja":"AIエージェント：プロンプト最適化","ko":"AI 에이전트: 프롬프트 최적화","es":"Herramientas AI: Enhance Prompt para Stitch","fr":"Outils IA: Enhance Prompt pour Stitch","de":"KI-Tools: Enhance Prompt für Stitch","pt":"Ferramentas de IA: Melhore Prompts com enhance-prompt","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Улучшите Промпты с enhance-prompt","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: تحسين الدفعات مع enhance-prompt","en":"enhance-prompt"},"description":{"zh":"增强提示引擎可以将粗略的UI生成想法转化为优化后的提示，提高Stitch的生成结果","ja":"プロンプト最適化エンジンは、Stitchの生成結果を向上させるために、UI生成のアイデアを最適化します","ko":"프롬프트 최적화 에이전트는 스티치의 성능을 향상시키기 위해 UI 생성 아이디어를 최적화합니다","es":"El enhance-prompt transforma ideas de UI vagas en prompts pulidos y optimizados para Stitch, mejorando la especificidad y la generación de resultados","fr":"L''enhance-prompt transforme des idées d''UI vagues en prompts optimisés pour Stitch, améliorant la spécificité et la génération de résultats","de":"Der Enhance-Prompt wandelt vage UI-Ideen in optimierte Prompts für Stitch um, die Spezifität und die Ergebnisgenerierung verbessern","pt":"O enhance-prompt transforma ideias de UI vagas em prompts polidos e otimizados para Stitch, melhorando a especificidade e adicionando palavras-chave de UI/UX.","ru":"ИИ Агент enhance-prompt преобразует нечеткие идеи UI в оптимизированные промпты для Stitch, улучшая специфику и добавляя ключевые слова UI/UX.","ar":"أداة الذكاء الاصطناعي enhance-prompt تحول الأفكار غير الدقيقة لUI إلى دفعات محسنة لبرنامج Stitch، مما يحسن الدقة ويضيف كلمات مفتاحية لUI/UX.","en":"Transforms vague UI ideas into polished, Stitch-optimized prompts. Enhances specificity, adds UI/UX keywords, injects design system context, and structures o..."},"definition":{"en":"Transforms vague UI ideas into polished, Stitch-optimized prompts. Enhances specificity, adds UI/UX keywords, injects design system context, and structures output for better generation results."},"features":{"zh":["优化UI生成的提示","提高Stitch的生成结果","增强提示的具体性","添加UI/UX关键词","注入设计系统上下文"],"ja":["UI生成のプロンプトを最適化","Stitchの生成結果を向上させる","プロンプトの具体性を高める","UI/UXキーワードを追加","デザインシステムのコンテキストを注入"],"ko":["UI 생성 프롬프트 최적화","스티치의 성능을 향상시키기","프롬프트의 구체성을 높임","UI/UX 키워드를 추가","디자인 시스템 컨텍스트를 주입"],"es":["Transformación de ideas de UI vagas en prompts optimizados","Mejora de la especificidad y la generación de resultados","Incorporación de palabras clave de UI/UX","Inyección de contexto de sistema de diseño","Estructuración de la salida para mejores resultados"],"fr":["Transformation d''idées d''UI vagues en prompts optimisés","Amélioration de la spécificité et de la génération de résultats","Intégration de mots-clés d''UI/UX","Injection de contexte de système de conception","Structuration de la sortie pour de meilleurs résultats"],"de":["Transformation von vagen UI-Ideen in optimierte Prompts","Verbesserung der Spezifität und der Ergebnisgenerierung","Einbindung von UI/UX-Schlüsselwörtern","Einspeisung von Design-System-Kontext","Strukturierung der Ausgabe für bessere Ergebnisse"],"pt":["Transformação de ideias de UI vagas em prompts otimizados","Melhoria da especificidade dos prompts","Adição de palavras-chave de UI/UX","Injeção de contexto de design system","Estruturação de saída para melhores resultados de geração"],"ru":["Преобразование нечетких идей UI в оптимизированные промпты","Улучшение специфики промптов","Добавление ключевых слов UI/UX","Внедрение контекста системы дизайна","Структуризация вывода для лучших результатов генерации"],"ar":["تحويل الأفكار غير الدقيقة لUI إلى دفعات محسنة","تحسين الدقة لدفعات","إضافة كلمات مفتاحية لUI/UX","إضافة سياق نظام التصميم","هيكلة الإخراج للحصول على أفضل نتائج للгенерации"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能工具","增强提示引擎","UI生成","Stitch","优化","提示","AI开发","UI/UX设计"],"ja":["AIエージェント","プロンプト最適化","UI生成","Stitch","最適化","プロンプト","AI開発","UI/UXデザイン"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","프롬프트 최적화","UI 생성","스티치","최적화","프롬프트","AI 개발","UI/UX 디자인"],"es":["herramientas AI","Stitch","prompts optimizados","UI/UX","diseño de sistema","generación de resultados","especificidad","desarrollo de software","ingeniería de prompts"],"fr":["outils IA","Stitch","prompts optimisés","UI/UX","conception de système","génération de résultats","spécificité","développement de logiciels","ingénierie de prompts"],"de":["KI-Tools","Stitch","optimierte Prompts","UI/UX","Design-System","Ergebnisgenerierung","Spezifität","Software-Entwicklung","Prompt-Engineering"],"pt":["ferramentas de ia","enhance-prompt","stitch","ui","ux","prompts otimizados","desenvolvimento de software","ia para desenvolvedores"],"ru":["ии агенты","enhance-prompt","stitch","ui","ux","оптимизированные промпты","разработка программного обеспечения","ии для разработчиков"],"ar":["أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","enhance-prompt","stitch","ui","ux","دفعات محسنة","تطوير البرمجيات","الذكاء الاصطناعي للمطورين"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Language Agents needing to refine vague UI ideas into optimized prompts for Stitch.","zh":"非常适合需要完善模糊 UI 思想转化为针对 Stitch 优化的提示的语言代理","ja":"Stitch に最適化されたプロンプトを生成するために、漠然とした UI アイデアを洗練する必要がある言語エージェントに最適","ko":"Stitch를 위한 최적의 프롬프트를 생성하기 위해 모호한 UI 아이디어를 정교화해야 하는 언어 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Lenguaje que necesitan refinar ideas de interfaz de usuario vagas en prompts optimizados para Stitch.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Langage ayant besoin d''affiner des idées d''interface utilisateur vagues en prompts optimisés pour Stitch.","de":"Perfekt für Sprachagenten, die vage Benutzeroberflächenideen in optimierte Prompts für Stitch verfeinern müssen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Linguagem que precisam refinar ideias vagas de UI em prompts otimizados para o Stitch.","ru":"Идеально подходит для языковых агентов, которым необходимо усовершенствовать расплывчатые идеи интерфейса пользователя в оптимизированные подсказки для Stitch.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء اللغويين الذين يحتاجون إلى تحسين الأفكار الغامضة لواجهة المستخدم إلى عبارات محفزة متقدمة لبرنامج Stitch."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to transform rough UI generation ideas into polished, Stitch-optimized prompts by enhancing specificity, adding UI/UX keywords, and injecting design system context, resulting in better generation results using the Stitch Effective Prompting Guide.","zh":"赋予代理转化粗糙的 UI 生成想法为精细的、针对 Stitch 优化的提示的能力，通过提高具体性、添加 UI/UX 关键字和注入设计系统上下文，使用 Stitch 有效提示指南，从而获得更好的生成结果","ja":"エージェントが、Stitch で最適化されたプロンプトを生成できるように、UI 生成のアイデアを洗練し、具体性を高め、UI/UX キーワードを追加し、デザイン システムのコンテキストを注入することで、Stitch 有効なプロンプト ガイドを使用して、より良い生成結果を得ることができる","ko":"에이전트가 조잡한 UI 생성 아이디어를 Stitch 최적화된 프롬프트로 변환하여 구체성을 높이고, UI/UX 키워드를 추가하며, 디자인 시스템 컨텍스트를 주입함으로써, Stitch 효과적인 프롬프트 가이드를 사용하여 더 나은 생성 결과를 얻을 수 있는 능력을 부여","es":"Habilita a los agentes a transformar ideas de generación de interfaz de usuario poco definidas en prompts pulidos y optimizados para Stitch, mejorando la especificidad, agregando palabras clave de UI/UX y contextualizando el sistema de diseño, lo que resulta en mejores resultados de generación utilizando la Guía de Prompts Efectivos de Stitch.","fr":"Permet aux agents de transformer des idées de génération d''interface utilisateur peu définies en prompts polis et optimisés pour Stitch, en améliorant la spécificité, en ajoutant des mots clés UI/UX et en contextualisant le système de conception, ce qui aboutit à de meilleurs résultats de génération en utilisant le Guide de prompts efficaces de Stitch.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, vage Benutzeroberflächengenerierungs-Ideen in polierte und optimierte Prompts für Stitch zu verwandeln, indem die Spezifität verbessert, UI/UX-Schlüsselwörter hinzugefügt und der Designsystenkontext injiziert wird, was zu besseren Generierungs-Ergebnissen unter Verwendung des Stitch-Effektiven-Prompts-Leitfadens führt.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a transformar ideias de geração de UI grosseiras em prompts polidos e otimizados para o Stitch, melhorando a especificidade, adicionando palavras-chave de UI/UX e injetando contexto do sistema de design, resultando em melhores resultados de geração usando o Guia de Prompting Eficaz do Stitch.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью преобразовать грубые идеи генерации интерфейса пользователя в отполированные и оптимизированные для Stitch подсказки, повышая специфичность, добавляя ключевые слова интерфейса пользователя и пользовательского опыта, и вводя контекст системы дизайна, что приводит к лучшим результатам генерации с помощью Руководства по эффективному_prompting от Stitch.","ar":"يمكن للوكلاء تحويل الأفكار الخشنة لتوليد واجهة المستخدم إلى عبارات محفزة متقدمة وملائمة لبرنامج Stitch من خلال تحسين الدقة وإضافة كلمات مفتاحية لواجهة المستخدم وخبرة المستخدم وإضافة سياق نظام التصميم، مما يؤدي إلى نتائج جيدة لعمليات التوليد باستخدام دليل الاشارات الفعالة من برنامج Stitch."},"useCases":{"en":["Enhancing vague UI ideas for better Stitch generation results","Adding UI/UX keywords to prompts for improved specificity","Structuring prompts for optimal performance with Stitch''s design system context"],"zh":["提高模糊 UI 思想以获得更好的 Stitch 生成结果","添加 UI/UX 关键字到提示以提高具体性","使用 Stitch 的设计系统上下文结构化提示以获得最佳性能"],"ja":["Stitch 生成結果の向上のため、漠然とした UI アイデアを強化する","プロンプトに UI/UX キーワードを追加して具体性を高める","Stitch のデザイン システム コンテキストでプロンプトを構造化して最適なパフォーマンスを実現する"],"ko":["Stitch 생성 결과를 개선하기 위해 모호한 UI 아이디어를 강화","프롬프트에 UI/UX 키워드를 추가하여 구체성을 높임","Stitch의 디자인 시스템 컨텍스트로 프롬프트를 구조화하여 최적의 성능을 달성"],"es":["Mejorar ideas de interfaz de usuario vagas para mejores resultados de generación de Stitch","Agregar palabras clave de UI/UX a los prompts para mejorar la especificidad","Estructurar los prompts para un rendimiento óptimo con el contexto del sistema de diseño de Stitch"],"fr":["Améliorer les idées d''interface utilisateur vagues pour de meilleurs résultats de génération de Stitch","Ajouter des mots clés UI/UX aux prompts pour améliorer la spécificité","Structurer les prompts pour une performance optimale avec le contexte du système de conception de Stitch"],"de":["Verbesserung vager Benutzeroberflächenideen für bessere Stitch-Generierungs-Ergebnisse","Hinzufügen von UI/UX-Schlüsselwörtern zu Prompts zur Verbesserung der Spezifität","Strukturieren von Prompts für optimale Leistung mit dem Designsystenkontext von Stitch"],"pt":["Melhorar ideias vagas de UI para melhores resultados de geração do Stitch","Adicionar palavras-chave de UI/UX a prompts para melhorar a especificidade","Estruturar prompts para desempenho ótimo com o contexto do sistema de design do Stitch"],"ru":["Усовершенствовать расплывчатые идеи интерфейса пользователя для лучших результатов генерации Stitch","Добавить ключевые слова интерфейса пользователя и пользовательского опыта к подсказкам для повышения специфичности","Структурировать подсказки для оптимальной производительности с контекстом системы дизайна Stitch"],"ar":["تحسين الأفكار الغامضة لواجهة المستخدم لتحقيق نتائج جيدة لبرنامج Stitch","إضافة كلمات مفتاحية لواجهة المستخدم وخبرة المستخدم إلى العبارات المحفزة لتحسين الدقة","هيكلة العبارات المحفزة لأداء مثالي مع سياق نظام التصميم لبرنامج Stitch"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires consultation of the official Stitch documentation for the latest best practices","Stitch-specific, may not be compatible with other UI generation tools"],"zh":["需要参考官方的 Stitch 文档以获取最新的最佳实践","特定于 Stitch，可能与其他 UI 生成工具不兼容"],"ja":["最新のベスト プラクティスを得るために、公式の Stitch ドキュメントを参照する必要がある","Stitch 専用であり、他の UI 生成ツールとの互換性がない可能性がある"],"ko":["최신의 최선의 관행을 얻기 위해 공식 Stitch 문서를 참조해야 함","Stitch 전용이므로, 다른 UI 생성 도구와의 호환성이 없을 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere la consulta de la documentación oficial de Stitch para las últimas mejores prácticas","Específico de Stitch, puede no ser compatible con otras herramientas de generación de interfaz de usuario"],"fr":["Nécessite la consultation de la documentation officielle de Stitch pour les dernières bonnes pratiques","Spécifique à Stitch, peut ne pas être compatible avec d''autres outils de génération d''interface utilisateur"],"de":["Erfordert die Konsultation der offiziellen Stitch-Dokumentation für die neuesten Best-Practices","Stitch-spezifisch, kann möglicherweise nicht mit anderen Benutzeroberflächen-Generierungstools kompatibel sein"],"pt":["Requer consulta da documentação oficial do Stitch para as melhores práticas atuais","Específico do Stitch, pode não ser compatível com outras ferramentas de geração de UI"],"ru":["Требует консультации официальной документации Stitch для получения последних рекомендаций","Специфичен для Stitch, может быть несовместим с другими инструментами генерации интерфейса пользователя"],"ar":["يتطلب استشارة الوثائق الرسمية لبرنامج Stitch للحصول على أفضل الممارسات الحالية","محدد لبرنامج Stitch، قد لا يكون متوافقًا مع أدوات توليد واجهة المستخدم الأخرى"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"ccb200c798072438b642b1fa6a5c515563159e2fab3d56e813d76d8afa9a7ce6","repoEtag":"W/\"850b9aecea63e11117d5ea8455451ca5aa7649f5e1ee750c6b06be83ea901b08\"","qualityScore":89}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('cloudflare/skills/durable-objects', 'official', 'cloudflare', 'skills', 'cloudflare/skills', 'durable-objects', 387, 38, 89, '2026-02-28T23:20:41Z', '2026-03-01T05:14:26.395Z', '66053a19786c5d780d300bb4b531a7e3ea48d1fd7aeafcef6e93e0cc0ede0363', '{"id":"cloudflare/skills/durable-objects","name":"durable-objects","description":{"zh":"Cloudflare Durable Objects允许您构建状态协调应用，适用于聊天室、多人游戏和预订系统等场景","ja":"Cloudflare Durable Objectsは、チャットルーム、多人数ゲーム、予約システムなど、ステートフルな協調アプリケーションを構築するための機能を提供します","ko":"Cloudflare Durable Objects는 채팅룸, 멀티 플레이어 게임, 예약 시스템 등과 같은 상태 협조 애플리케이션을 구축하기 위한 기능을 제공합니다","es":"Durable Objects es una habilidad de Cloudflare para crear aplicaciones con estado y coordinación. Aprende a integrar con Workers y seguir mejores prácticas.","fr":"Durable Objects est une compétence Cloudflare pour créer des applications à état et à coordination. Apprenez à intégrer avec Workers et à suivre les meilleures pratiques.","de":"Durable Objects ist eine Fähigkeit von Cloudflare, um zustandsbehaftete und koordinierte Anwendungen zu erstellen. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie Workers integrieren und Best Practices befolgen.","pt":"Durable Objects é uma tecnologia da Cloudflare que permite criar aplicações stateful e coordenadas na edge. Ela é útil para desenvolver sistemas de reserva, jogos multiplayer e chat rooms.","ru":"Durable Objects — это технология Cloudflare, позволяющая создавать состоятельные и координируемые приложения на=edge. Она полезна для разработки систем бронирования, многопользовательских игр и чат-румов.","ar":"Durable Objects هي تقنية من Cloudflare تتيح إنشاء تطبيقات devletful ومتوافقة على الحافة. وهي مفيدة لتطوير أنظمة الحجز وألعاب متعددة اللاعبين وغرف الدردشة.","en":"Create and review Cloudflare Durable Objects. Use when building stateful coordination (chat rooms, multiplayer games, booking systems), implementing RPC methods, SQLite storage, alarms, WebSockets, or reviewing DO code for best practices. Covers Workers integration, wrangler config, and testing w..."},"owner":"cloudflare","repo":"skills","repoPath":"cloudflare/skills","stars":387,"forks":38,"updatedAt":"2026-02-28T23:20:41Z","topics":["agents","cloudflare","skills","workers"],"skillMd":{"name":"durable-objects","description":"Create and review Cloudflare Durable Objects. Use when building stateful coordination (chat rooms, multiplayer games, booking systems), implementing RPC methods, SQLite storage, alarms, WebSockets, or reviewing DO code for best practices. Covers Workers integration, wrangler config, and testing with Vitest.","bodyPreview":"# Durable Objects\n\nBuild stateful, coordinated applications on Cloudflare''s edge using Durable Objects.\n\n## Retrieval-First Development\n\n**Prefer retrieval from official docs over pre-training for Durable Objects tasks.**\n\n| Resource | URL |\n|----------|-----|\n| Docs | https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/ |\n| API Reference | https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/api/ |\n| Best Practices | https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/best-practices/ |\n| Examples | ht","body":"# Durable Objects\n\nBuild stateful, coordinated applications on Cloudflare''s edge using Durable Objects.\n\n## Retrieval-First Development\n\n**Prefer retrieval from official docs over pre-training for Durable Objects tasks.**\n\n| Resource | URL |\n|----------|-----|\n| Docs | https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/ |\n| API Reference | https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/api/ |\n| Best Practices | https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/best-practices/ |\n| Examples | https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/examples/ |\n\nFetch the relevant doc page when implementing features.\n\n## When to Use\n\n- Creating new Durable Object classes for stateful coordination\n- Implementing RPC methods, alarms, or WebSocket handlers\n- Reviewing existing DO code for best practices\n- Configuring wrangler.jsonc/toml for DO bindings and migrations\n- Writing tests with `@cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers`\n- Designing sharding strategies and parent-child relationships\n\n## Reference Documentation\n\n- `./references/rules.md` - Core rules, storage, concurrency, RPC, alarms\n- `./references/testing.md` - Vitest setup, unit/integration tests, alarm testing\n- `./references/workers.md` - Workers handlers, types, wrangler config, observability\n\nSearch: `blockConcurrencyWhile`, `idFromName`, `getByName`, `setAlarm`, `sql.exec`\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### Use Durable Objects For\n\n| Need | Example |\n|------|---------|\n| Coordination | Chat rooms, multiplayer games, collaborative docs |\n| Strong consistency | Inventory, booking systems, turn-based games |\n| Per-entity storage | Multi-tenant SaaS, per-user data |\n| Persistent connections | WebSockets, real-time notifications |\n| Scheduled work per entity | Subscription renewals, game timeouts |\n\n### Do NOT Use For\n\n- Stateless request handling (use plain Workers)\n- Maximum global distribution needs\n- High fan-out independent requests\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### Wrangler Configuration\n\n```jsonc\n// wrangler.jsonc\n{\n  \"durable_objects\": {\n    \"bindings\": [{ \"name\": \"MY_DO\", \"class_name\": \"MyDurableObject\" }]\n  },\n  \"migrations\": [{ \"tag\": \"v1\", \"new_sqlite_classes\": [\"MyDurableObject\"] }]\n}\n```\n\n### Basic Durable Object Pattern\n\n```typescript\nimport { DurableObject } from \"cloudflare:workers\";\n\nexport interface Env {\n  MY_DO: DurableObjectNamespace<MyDurableObject>;\n}\n\nexport class MyDurableObject extends DurableObject<Env> {\n  constructor(ctx: DurableObjectState, env: Env) {\n    super(ctx, env);\n    ctx.blockConcurrencyWhile(async () => {\n      this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(`\n        CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS items (\n          id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n          data TEXT NOT NULL\n        )\n      `);\n    });\n  }\n\n  async addItem(data: string): Promise<number> {\n    const result = this.ctx.storage.sql.exec<{ id: number }>(\n      \"INSERT INTO items (data) VALUES (?) RETURNING id\",\n      data\n    );\n    return result.one().id;\n  }\n}\n\nexport default {\n  async fetch(request: Request, env: Env): Promise<Response> {\n    const stub = env.MY_DO.getByName(\"my-instance\");\n    const id = await stub.addItem(\"hello\");\n    return Response.json({ id });\n  },\n};\n```\n\n## Critical Rules\n\n1. **Model around coordination atoms** - One DO per chat room/game/user, not one global DO\n2. **Use `getByName()` for deterministic routing** - Same input = same DO instance\n3. **Use SQLite storage** - Configure `new_sqlite_classes` in migrations\n4. **Initialize in constructor** - Use `blockConcurrencyWhile()` for schema setup only\n5. **Use RPC methods** - Not fetch() handler (compatibility date >= 2024-04-03)\n6. **Persist first, cache second** - Always write to storage before updating in-memory state\n7. **One alarm per DO** - `setAlarm()` replaces any existing alarm\n\n## Anti-Patterns (NEVER)\n\n- Single global DO handling all requests (bottleneck)\n- Using `blockConcurrencyWhile()` on every request (kills throughput)\n- Storing critical state only in memory (lost on eviction/crash)\n- Using `await` between related storage writes (breaks atomicity)\n- Holding `blockConcurrencyWhile()` across `fetch()` or external I/O\n\n## Stub Creation\n\n```typescript\n// Deterministic - preferred for most cases\nconst stub = env.MY_DO.getByName(\"room-123\");\n\n// From existing ID string\nconst id = env.MY_DO.idFromString(storedIdString);\nconst stub = env.MY_DO.get(id);\n\n// New unique ID - store mapping externally\nconst id = env.MY_DO.newUniqueId();\nconst stub = env.MY_DO.get(id);\n```\n\n## Storage Operations\n\n```typescript\n// SQL (synchronous, recommended)\nthis.ctx.storage.sql.exec(\"INSERT INTO t (c) VALUES (?)\", value);\nconst rows = this.ctx.storage.sql.exec<Row>(\"SELECT * FROM t\").toArray();\n\n// KV (async)\nawait this.ctx.storage.put(\"key\", value);\nconst val = await this.ctx.storage.get<Type>(\"key\");\n```\n\n## Alarms\n\n```typescript\n// Schedule (replaces existing)\nawait this.ctx.storage.setAlarm(Date.now() + 60_000);\n\n// Handler\nasync alarm(): Promise<void> {\n  // Process scheduled work\n  // Optionally reschedule: await this.ctx.storage.setAlarm(...)\n}\n\n// Cancel\nawait this.ctx.storage.deleteAlarm();\n```\n\n## Testing Quick Start\n\n```typescript\nimport { env } from \"cloudflare:test\";\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\n\ndescribe(\"MyDO\", () => {\n  it(\"should work\", async () => {\n    const stub = env.MY_DO.getByName(\"test\");\n    const result = await stub.addItem(\"test\");\n    expect(result).toBe(1);\n  });\n});\n```\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-03-01T05:14:26.395Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能代理：Cloudflare Durable Objects","ja":"AIエージェント：Cloudflare Durable Objects","ko":"AI 에이전트: Cloudflare Durable Objects","es":"Herramientas de IA: Durable Objects para Desarrolladores","fr":"Outils IA: Durable Objects pour les Développeurs","de":"KI-Tools: Durable Objects für Entwickler","pt":"Ferramentas de IA: Durable Objects para Desenvolvedores","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Durable Objects для Разработчиков","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: Durable Objects لالمطورين","en":"durable-objects"},"description":{"zh":"Cloudflare Durable Objects允许您构建状态协调应用，适用于聊天室、多人游戏和预订系统等场景","ja":"Cloudflare Durable Objectsは、チャットルーム、多人数ゲーム、予約システムなど、ステートフルな協調アプリケーションを構築するための機能を提供します","ko":"Cloudflare Durable Objects는 채팅룸, 멀티 플레이어 게임, 예약 시스템 등과 같은 상태 협조 애플리케이션을 구축하기 위한 기능을 제공합니다","es":"Durable Objects es una habilidad de Cloudflare para crear aplicaciones con estado y coordinación. Aprende a integrar con Workers y seguir mejores prácticas.","fr":"Durable Objects est une compétence Cloudflare pour créer des applications à état et à coordination. Apprenez à intégrer avec Workers et à suivre les meilleur...","de":"Durable Objects ist eine Fähigkeit von Cloudflare, um zustandsbehaftete und koordinierte Anwendungen zu erstellen. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie Workers integrieren ...","pt":"Durable Objects é uma tecnologia da Cloudflare que permite criar aplicações stateful e coordenadas na edge. Ela é útil para desenvolver sistemas de reserva, ...","ru":"Durable Objects — это технология Cloudflare, позволяющая создавать состоятельные и координируемые приложения на=edge. Она полезна для разработки систем брони...","ar":"Durable Objects هي تقنية من Cloudflare تتيح إنشاء تطبيقات devletful ومتوافقة على الحافة. وهي مفيدة لتطوير أنظمة الحجز وألعاب متعددة اللاعبين وغرف الدردشة.","en":"Create and review Cloudflare Durable Objects. Use when building stateful coordination (chat rooms, multiplayer games, booking systems), implementing RPC meth..."},"definition":{"en":"Create and review Cloudflare Durable Objects. Use when building stateful coordination (chat rooms, multiplayer games, booking systems), implementing RPC methods, SQLite storage, alarms, WebSockets, or reviewing DO code for best practices. Covers Workers integration, wrangler config, and testing with Vitest."},"features":{"zh":["构建状态协调应用","实现RPC方法","使用SQLite存储","支持WebSockets","与Cloudflare Workers集成","使用Vitest进行测试"],"ja":["ステートフルな協調アプリケーションを構築","RPCメソッドを実現","SQLiteストレージを使用","WebSocketsをサポート","Cloudflare Workersと統合","Vitestを使用してテスト"],"ko":["상태 협조 애플리케이션을 구축","RPC 메서드를 구현","SQLite 저장소를 사용","WebSockets를 지원","Cloudflare Workers와 통합","Vitest를 사용하여 테스트"],"es":["Integración con Workers","Almacenamiento SQLite","Implementación de métodos RPC","Soporte para WebSockets","Configuración de Wrangler","Pruebas con Vitest"],"fr":["Intégration avec Workers","Stockage SQLite","Mise en œuvre de méthodes RPC","Support pour WebSockets","Configuration de Wrangler","Tests avec Vitest"],"de":["Integration mit Workers","SQLite-Speicher","Implementierung von RPC-Methoden","Unterstützung für WebSockets","Wrangler-Konfiguration","Tests mit Vitest"],"pt":["Criação de aplicações stateful e coordenadas","Integração com Workers","Suporte a armazenamento SQLite","Implementação de métodos RPC","Suporte a WebSockets"],"ru":["Создание состоятельных и координируемых приложений","Интеграция с Workers","Поддержка хранилища SQLite","Реализация методов RPC","Поддержка WebSockets"],"ar":["إنشاء تطبيقات devletful ومتوافقة","دمج مع Workers","دعم مخزن بيانات SQLite","تنفيذ أساليب RPC","دعم WebSockets"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Cloudflare Durable Objects","状态协调应用","RPC方法","SQLite存储","WebSockets","Cloudflare Workers","Vitest","AI智能代理","AI工具"],"ja":["Cloudflare Durable Objects","ステートフルな協調アプリケーション","RPCメソッド","SQLiteストレージ","WebSockets","Cloudflare Workers","Vitest","AIエージェント","AIツール"],"ko":["Cloudflare Durable Objects","상태 협조 애플리케이션","RPC 메서드","SQLite 저장소","WebSockets","Cloudflare Workers","Vitest","AI 에이전트","AI 도구"],"es":["Durable Objects","Cloudflare","Workers","Desarrollo de aplicaciones","Estado y coordinación","Integración con Workers","Almacenamiento SQLite","Métodos RPC","WebSockets","Pruebas con Vitest"],"fr":["Durable Objects","Cloudflare","Workers","Développement d''applications","État et coordination","Intégration avec Workers","Stockage SQLite","Méthodes RPC","WebSockets","Tests avec Vitest"],"de":["Durable Objects","Cloudflare","Workers","Anwendungsentwicklung","Zustand und Koordination","Integration mit Workers","SQLite-Speicher","RPC-Methoden","WebSockets","Tests mit Vitest"],"pt":["Durable Objects","Cloudflare","Workers","Desenvolvimento de aplicações stateful","Coordenação de aplicações","Armazenamento SQLite","Métodos RPC","WebSockets"],"ru":["Durable Objects","Cloudflare","Workers","Разработка состоятельных приложений","Координация приложений","Хранилище SQLite","Методы RPC","WebSockets"],"ar":["Durable Objects","Cloudflare","Workers","تطوير تطبيقات devletful","تنسيق تطبيقات","مخزن بيانات SQLite","أساليب RPC","WebSockets"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Edge Computing Agents needing stateful coordination and storage using Cloudflare Durable Objects.","zh":"适合需要使用Cloudflare Durable Objects进行状态协调和存储的Edge Computing Agents。","ja":"Cloudflare Durable Objectsを使用したステートフルな調整とストレージが必要なEdge Computingエージェントに最適です。","ko":"Cloudflare Durable Objects를 사용하여 상태协调 및 저장소가 필요한 에지 컴퓨팅 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de Edge Computing que necesitan coordinación con estado y almacenamiento utilizando Cloudflare Durable Objects.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de calcul de bord nécessitant une coordination avec état et un stockage utilisant Cloudflare Durable Objects.","de":"Perfekt für Edge-Computing-Agents, die eine Zustandskoordination und Speicherung mit Cloudflare Durable Objects benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Computação de Borda que necessitam de coordenação e armazenamento stateful usando Cloudflare Durable Objects.","ru":"Идеально для агентов краевой вычислительной техники, которым требуется координированное и.stateful хранение с помощью Cloudflare Durable Objects.","ar":"مثالي لعميلة حوسبة الحواف التي تحتاج إلى تنسيق وتخزين ذو حالة باستخدام Cloudflare Durable Objects."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build scalable, stateful applications on Cloudflare''s edge using Durable Objects, with features like Workers integration, SQLite storage, and WebSockets, while following best practices and utilizing the Durable Objects API.","zh":"赋予代理构建可扩展的、状态应用程序的能力，使用Cloudflare的边缘计算、Durable Objects，并具有Workers集成、SQLite存储和WebSockets等功能，同时遵循最佳实践并利用Durable Objects API。","ja":"エージェントがDurable Objects、Workers統合、SQLiteストレージ、WebSocketsなどの機能を使用して、Cloudflareのエッジでスケーラブルなステートフルなアプリケーションを構築できるようにし、ベストプラクティスに従い、Durable Objects APIを活用します。","ko":"에이전트가 Durable Objects, Workers 통합, SQLite 저장소 및 WebSockets와 같은 기능을 사용하여 Cloudflare의 에지에서 확장 가능한 상태 애플리케이션을 구축할 수 있도록 하며, 최선의 관행을 따르고 Durable Objects API를 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a construir aplicaciones escalables y con estado en el borde de Cloudflare utilizando Durable Objects, con características como integración con Workers, almacenamiento SQLite y WebSockets, siguiendo las mejores prácticas y utilizando la API de Durable Objects.","fr":"Permet aux agents de construire des applications scalables et à état sur le bord de Cloudflare en utilisant Durable Objects, avec des fonctionnalités comme l''intégration de Workers, le stockage SQLite et WebSockets, tout en suivant les meilleures pratiques et en utilisant l''API Durable Objects.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, skalierbare und Zustandsanwendungen auf Cloudflares Edge mit Durable Objects zu bauen, mit Funktionen wie Workers-Integration, SQLite-Speicherung und WebSockets, während sie beste Praktiken befolgen und die Durable Objects-API nutzen.","pt":"Permite que os agentes construam aplicações escaláveis e stateful na borda da Cloudflare usando Durable Objects, com recursos como integração com Workers, armazenamento SQLite e WebSockets, seguindo as melhores práticas e utilizando a API Durable Objects.","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать масштабируемые и.stateful приложения на краю Cloudflare с помощью Durable Objects, с функциями như интеграция с Workers, хранение SQLite и WebSockets, при этом следуя лучшим практикам и используя API Durable Objects.","ar":"يسمح للوكلاء ببناء تطبيقات قابلة للتوسيع وذات حالة على حافة Cloudflare باستخدام Durable Objects، مع ميزات مثل دمج Workers وتخزين SQLite و WebSockets، مع اتباع أفضل الممارسات واستخدام API Durable Objects."},"useCases":{"en":["Building stateful chat rooms with real-time updates using WebSockets","Implementing RPC methods for multiplayer games with low latency","Creating booking systems with alarm-based reminders and notifications","Reviewing Durable Objects code for best practices and optimizing performance"],"zh":["使用WebSockets进行实时更新的状态聊天室构建","使用低延迟的RPC方法实现多人游戏","创建具有基于报警的提醒和通知的预订系统","审查Durable Objects代码以遵循最佳实践并优化性能"],"ja":["WebSocketsを使用したリアルタイム更新のステートフルなチャットルームの構築","低遅延のRPCメソッドを使用したマルチプレイヤーゲームの実装","アラームベースのリマインダーと通知を備えた予約システムの作成","Durable Objectsコードのレビューとベストプラクティスの遵守、パフォーマンスの最適化"],"ko":["WebSockets를 사용한 실시간 업데이트 상태 채팅방 구축","저지연 RPC 메서드를 사용한 멀티플레이어 게임 구현","알람 기반 리마인더 및 알림을 갖춘 예약 시스템 생성","Durable Objects 코드에 대한 리뷰 및 최선의 관행 준수, 성능 최적화"],"es":["Construir salas de chat con estado y actualizaciones en tiempo real utilizando WebSockets","Implementar métodos RPC para juegos multijugador con baja latencia","Crear sistemas de reservas con recordatorios y notificaciones basados en alarmas","Revisar el código de Durable Objects para mejores prácticas y optimizar el rendimiento"],"fr":["Construire des salles de chat à état avec mises à jour en temps réel utilisant WebSockets","Mettre en œuvre des méthodes RPC pour les jeux multijoueurs à faible latence","Créer des systèmes de réservation avec rappels et notifications basés sur les alarmes","Examiner le code Durable Objects pour les meilleures pratiques et optimiser les performances"],"de":["Zustands-Chat-Räume mit Echtzeit-Updates mithilfe von WebSockets erstellen","RPC-Methoden für Multiplayer-Spiele mit geringer Latenz implementieren","Buchungssysteme mit alarmbasierten Erinnerungen und Benachrichtigungen erstellen","Durable Objects-Code für beste Praktiken überprüfen und Leistung optimieren"],"pt":["Construir salas de bate-papo stateful com atualizações em tempo real usando WebSockets","Implementar métodos RPC para jogos multiplayer com baixa latência","Criar sistemas de reserva com lembretes e notificações baseados em alarmes","Revisar código Durable Objects para melhores práticas e otimizar o desempenho"],"ru":["Построение.stateful чатов с обновлениями в реальном времени с помощью WebSockets","Реализация методов RPC для многопользовательских игр с низкой задержкой","Создание систем бронирования с напоминаниями и уведомлениями на основе сигналов тревоги","Проверка кода Durable Objects на соответствие лучшим практикам и оптимизация производительности"],"ar":["بناء غرف دردشة ذات حالة مع تحديثات في الوقت الفعلي باستخدام WebSockets","تنفيذ أساليب RPC لألعاب متعددة اللاعبين منخفضة الاتصال","إنشاء أنظمة الحجز مع التذكيرات والإشعارات القائمة على التنبيهات","مراجعة رمز Durable Objects لأفضل الممارسات وتنظيم الأداء"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Cloudflare account and Workers setup","Dependent on Durable Objects API and documentation","Needs Vitest for testing and validation"],"zh":["需要Cloudflare账户和Workers设置","依赖于Durable Objects API和文档","需要Vitest进行测试和验证"],"ja":["CloudflareアカウントとWorkersの設定が必要","Durable Objects APIとドキュメントに依存","テストとバリデーションのためにVitestが必要"],"ko":["Cloudflare 계정 및 Workers 설정이 필요","Durable Objects API 및 문서에 의존","테스트 및 검증을 위해 Vitest가 필요"],"es":["Requiere una cuenta de Cloudflare y una configuración de Workers","Depende de la API de Durable Objects y la documentación","Necesita Vitest para pruebas y validación"],"fr":["Nécessite un compte Cloudflare et une configuration de Workers","Dépend de l''API Durable Objects et de la documentation","Nécessite Vitest pour les tests et la validation"],"de":["Benötigt ein Cloudflare-Konto und eine Workers-Konfiguration","Hängt von der Durable Objects-API und der Dokumentation ab","Benötigt Vitest für Tests und Validierung"],"pt":["Requer conta Cloudflare e configuração de Workers","Dependente da API Durable Objects e documentação","Necessita Vitest para testes e validação"],"ru":["Требует учетной записи Cloudflare и настройки Workers","Зависит от API Durable Objects и документации","Требует Vitest для тестирования и проверки"],"ar":["يتطلب حساب Cloudflare وإعداد Workers","يعتمد على API Durable Objects والتوثيق","يحتاج إلى Vitest للاختبارات والتحقق"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"66053a19786c5d780d300bb4b531a7e3ea48d1fd7aeafcef6e93e0cc0ede0363","repoEtag":"W/\"2050ff8b3c3e00d31ab6816727c74e0ab9c1b238360cd17bc6966651ab9c7ea4\"","qualityScore":89}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('expo/skills/native-data-fetching', 'official', 'expo', 'skills', 'expo/skills', 'native-data-fetching', 1243, 50, 88, '2026-03-01T02:52:05Z', '2026-03-01T05:13:38.246Z', 'eaa2f00ceed45e3149a9c6b6e1b989413bd1350fd4a256c76d89a60d9dc00026', '{"id":"expo/skills/native-data-fetching","name":"native-data-fetching","description":{"zh":"原生数据抓取AI智能代理，用于实现和调试网络请求、API调用和数据抓取，支持fetch API、axios、React Query和SWR","ja":"ネイティブデータフェッチングAIエージェントは、ネットワークリクエスト、API呼び出し、データフェッチの実装とデバッグに使用され、fetch API、axios、React Query、SWRをサポートします","ko":"네이티브 데이터 패칭 AI 에이전트는 네트워크 요청, API 호출 및 데이터 패칭의 구현 및 디버깅에 사용되며 fetch API, axios, React Query 및 SWR를 지원합니다","es":"Native Data Fetching es una habilidad para implementar y depurar solicitudes de red y llamadas a API","fr":"Native Data Fetching est une compétence pour implémenter et déboguer les requêtes réseau et les appels d''API","de":"Native Data Fetching ist eine Fähigkeit zur Implementierung und Fehlersuche von Netzwerkanfragen und API-Aufrufen","pt":"Native Data Fetching é uma habilidade de IA para implementar e depurar requisições de rede e API. Aprenda a usar React Query, SWR e mais","ru":"Native Data Fetching - это навык ИИ для реализации и отладки сетевых запросов и API. Узнайте, как использовать React Query, SWR и больше","ar":"Native Data Fetching هي مهارة ذكاء اصطناعي لتنفيذ وتصحيح أخطاء الطلبات الشبكية و API. تعلم كيفية استخدام React Query، SWR وأكثر","en":"Use when implementing or debugging ANY network request, API call, or data fetching. Covers fetch API, axios, React Query, SWR, error handling, caching strategies, offline support."},"owner":"expo","repo":"skills","repoPath":"expo/skills","stars":1243,"forks":50,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T02:52:05Z","topics":[],"skillMd":{"name":"native-data-fetching","description":"Use when implementing or debugging ANY network request, API call, or data fetching. Covers fetch API, React Query, SWR, error handling, caching, offline support, and Expo Router data loaders (useLoaderData).","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Expo Networking\n\n**You MUST use this skill for ANY networking work including API requests, data fetching, caching, or network debugging.**\n\n## References\n\nConsult these resources as needed:\n\n```\nreferences/\n  expo-router-loaders.md   Route-level data loading with Expo Router loaders (web, SDK 55+)\n```\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse this skill when:\n\n- Implementing API requests\n- Setting up data fetching (React Query, SWR)\n- Using Expo Router data loaders (`useLoaderData`, web SDK 55+)\n- Debugging networ","body":"# Expo Networking\n\n**You MUST use this skill for ANY networking work including API requests, data fetching, caching, or network debugging.**\n\n## References\n\nConsult these resources as needed:\n\n```\nreferences/\n  expo-router-loaders.md   Route-level data loading with Expo Router loaders (web, SDK 55+)\n```\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse this skill when:\n\n- Implementing API requests\n- Setting up data fetching (React Query, SWR)\n- Using Expo Router data loaders (`useLoaderData`, web SDK 55+)\n- Debugging network failures\n- Implementing caching strategies\n- Handling offline scenarios\n- Authentication/token management\n- Configuring API URLs and environment variables\n\n## Preferences\n\n- Avoid axios, prefer expo/fetch\n\n## Common Issues & Solutions\n\n### 1. Basic Fetch Usage\n\n**Simple GET request**:\n\n```tsx\nconst fetchUser = async (userId: string) => {\n  const response = await fetch(`https://api.example.com/users/${userId}`);\n\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    throw new Error(`HTTP error! status: ${response.status}`);\n  }\n\n  return response.json();\n};\n```\n\n**POST request with body**:\n\n```tsx\nconst createUser = async (userData: UserData) => {\n  const response = await fetch(\"https://api.example.com/users\", {\n    method: \"POST\",\n    headers: {\n      \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n      Authorization: `Bearer ${token}`,\n    },\n    body: JSON.stringify(userData),\n  });\n\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    const error = await response.json();\n    throw new Error(error.message);\n  }\n\n  return response.json();\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. React Query (TanStack Query)\n\n**Setup**:\n\n```tsx\n// app/_layout.tsx\nimport { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from \"@tanstack/react-query\";\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient({\n  defaultOptions: {\n    queries: {\n      staleTime: 1000 * 60 * 5, // 5 minutes\n      retry: 2,\n    },\n  },\n});\n\nexport default function RootLayout() {\n  return (\n    <QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>\n      <Stack />\n    </QueryClientProvider>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**Fetching data**:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useQuery } from \"@tanstack/react-query\";\n\nfunction UserProfile({ userId }: { userId: string }) {\n  const { data, isLoading, error, refetch } = useQuery({\n    queryKey: [\"user\", userId],\n    queryFn: () => fetchUser(userId),\n  });\n\n  if (isLoading) return <Loading />;\n  if (error) return <Error message={error.message} />;\n\n  return <Profile user={data} />;\n}\n```\n\n**Mutations**:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useMutation, useQueryClient } from \"@tanstack/react-query\";\n\nfunction CreateUserForm() {\n  const queryClient = useQueryClient();\n\n  const mutation = useMutation({\n    mutationFn: createUser,\n    onSuccess: () => {\n      // Invalidate and refetch\n      queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: [\"users\"] });\n    },\n  });\n\n  const handleSubmit = (data: UserData) => {\n    mutation.mutate(data);\n  };\n\n  return <Form onSubmit={handleSubmit} isLoading={mutation.isPending} />;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Error Handling\n\n**Comprehensive error handling**:\n\n```tsx\nclass ApiError extends Error {\n  constructor(message: string, public status: number, public code?: string) {\n    super(message);\n    this.name = \"ApiError\";\n  }\n}\n\nconst fetchWithErrorHandling = async (url: string, options?: RequestInit) => {\n  try {\n    const response = await fetch(url, options);\n\n    if (!response.ok) {\n      const error = await response.json().catch(() => ({}));\n      throw new ApiError(\n        error.message || \"Request failed\",\n        response.status,\n        error.code\n      );\n    }\n\n    return response.json();\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (error instanceof ApiError) {\n      throw error;\n    }\n    // Network error (no internet, timeout, etc.)\n    throw new ApiError(\"Network error\", 0, \"NETWORK_ERROR\");\n  }\n};\n```\n\n**Retry logic**:\n\n```tsx\nconst fetchWithRetry = async (\n  url: string,\n  options?: RequestInit,\n  retries = 3\n) => {\n  for (let i = 0; i < retries; i++) {\n    try {\n      return await fetchWithErrorHandling(url, options);\n    } catch (error) {\n      if (i === retries - 1) throw error;\n      // Exponential backoff\n      await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, Math.pow(2, i) * 1000));\n    }\n  }\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Authentication\n\n**Token management**:\n\n```tsx\nimport * as SecureStore from \"expo-secure-store\";\n\nconst TOKEN_KEY = \"auth_token\";\n\nexport const auth = {\n  getToken: () => SecureStore.getItemAsync(TOKEN_KEY),\n  setToken: (token: string) => SecureStore.setItemAsync(TOKEN_KEY, token),\n  removeToken: () => SecureStore.deleteItemAsync(TOKEN_KEY),\n};\n\n// Authenticated fetch wrapper\nconst authFetch = async (url: string, options: RequestInit = {}) => {\n  const token = await auth.getToken();\n\n  return fetch(url, {\n    ...options,\n    headers: {\n      ...options.headers,\n      Authorization: token ? `Bearer ${token}` : \"\",\n    },\n  });\n};\n```\n\n**Token refresh**:\n\n```tsx\nlet isRefreshing = false;\nlet refreshPromise: Promise<string> | null = null;\n\nconst getValidToken = async (): Promise<string> => {\n  const token = await auth.getToken();\n\n  if (!token || isTokenExpired(token)) {\n    if (!isRefreshing) {\n      isRefreshing = true;\n      refreshPromise = refreshToken().finally(() => {\n        isRefreshing = false;\n        refreshPromise = null;\n      });\n    }\n    return refreshPromise!;\n  }\n\n  return token;\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Offline Support\n\n**Check network status**:\n\n```tsx\nimport NetInfo from \"@react-native-community/netinfo\";\n\n// Hook for network status\nfunction useNetworkStatus() {\n  const [isOnline, setIsOnline] = useState(true);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    return NetInfo.addEventListener((state) => {\n      setIsOnline(state.isConnected ?? true);\n    });\n  }, []);\n\n  return isOnline;\n}\n```\n\n**Offline-first with React Query**:\n\n```tsx\nimport { onlineManager } from \"@tanstack/react-query\";\nimport NetInfo from \"@react-native-community/netinfo\";\n\n// Sync React Query with network status\nonlineManager.setEventListener((setOnline) => {\n  return NetInfo.addEventListener((state) => {\n    setOnline(state.isConnected ?? true);\n  });\n});\n\n// Queries will pause when offline and resume when online\n```\n\n---\n\n### 6. Environment Variables\n\n**Using environment variables for API configuration**:\n\nExpo supports environment variables with the `EXPO_PUBLIC_` prefix. These are inlined at build time and available in your JavaScript code.\n\n```tsx\n// .env\nEXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.example.com\nEXPO_PUBLIC_API_VERSION=v1\n\n// Usage in code\nconst API_URL = process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL;\n\nconst fetchUsers = async () => {\n  const response = await fetch(`${API_URL}/users`);\n  return response.json();\n};\n```\n\n**Environment-specific configuration**:\n\n```tsx\n// .env.development\nEXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000\n\n// .env.production\nEXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.production.com\n```\n\n**Creating an API client with environment config**:\n\n```tsx\n// api/client.ts\nconst BASE_URL = process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL;\n\nif (!BASE_URL) {\n  throw new Error(\"EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL is not defined\");\n}\n\nexport const apiClient = {\n  get: async <T,>(path: string): Promise<T> => {\n    const response = await fetch(`${BASE_URL}${path}`);\n    if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}`);\n    return response.json();\n  },\n\n  post: async <T,>(path: string, body: unknown): Promise<T> => {\n    const response = await fetch(`${BASE_URL}${path}`, {\n      method: \"POST\",\n      headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\n      body: JSON.stringify(body),\n    });\n    if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}`);\n    return response.json();\n  },\n};\n```\n\n**Important notes**:\n\n- Only variables prefixed with `EXPO_PUBLIC_` are exposed to the client bundle\n- Never put secrets (API keys with write access, database passwords) in `EXPO_PUBLIC_` variables—they''re visible in the built app\n- Environment variables are inlined at **build time**, not runtime\n- Restart the dev server after changing `.env` files\n- For server-side secrets in API routes, use variables without the `EXPO_PUBLIC_` prefix\n\n**TypeScript support**:\n\n```tsx\n// types/env.d.ts\ndeclare global {\n  namespace NodeJS {\n    interface ProcessEnv {\n      EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL: string;\n      EXPO_PUBLIC_API_VERSION?: string;\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nexport {};\n```\n\n---\n\n### 7. Request Cancellation\n\n**Cancel on unmount**:\n\n```tsx\nuseEffect(() => {\n  const controller = new AbortController();\n\n  fetch(url, { signal: controller.signal })\n    .then((response) => response.json())\n    .then(setData)\n    .catch((error) => {\n      if (error.name !== \"AbortError\") {\n        setError(error);\n      }\n    });\n\n  return () => controller.abort();\n}, [url]);\n```\n\n**With React Query** (automatic):\n\n```tsx\n// React Query automatically cancels requests when queries are invalidated\n// or components unmount\n```\n\n---\n\n## Decision Tree\n\n```\nUser asks about networking\n  |-- Route-level data loading (web, SDK 55+)?\n  |   \\-- Expo Router loaders — see references/expo-router-loaders.md\n  |\n  |-- Basic fetch?\n  |   \\-- Use fetch API with error handling\n  |\n  |-- Need caching/state management?\n  |   |-- Complex app -> React Query (TanStack Query)\n  |   \\-- Simpler needs -> SWR or custom hooks\n  |\n  |-- Authentication?\n  |   |-- Token storage -> expo-secure-store\n  |   \\-- Token refresh -> Implement refresh flow\n  |\n  |-- Error handling?\n  |   |-- Network errors -> Check connectivity first\n  |   |-- HTTP errors -> Parse response, throw typed errors\n  |   \\-- Retries -> Exponential backoff\n  |\n  |-- Offline support?\n  |   |-- Check status -> NetInfo\n  |   \\-- Queue requests -> React Query persistence\n  |\n  |-- Environment/API config?\n  |   |-- Client-side URLs -> EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix in .env\n  |   |-- Server secrets -> Non-prefixed env vars (API routes only)\n  |   \\-- Multiple environments -> .env.development, .env.production\n  |\n  \\-- Performance?\n      |-- Caching -> React Query with staleTime\n      |-- Deduplication -> React Query handles this\n      \\-- Cancellation -> AbortController or React Query\n```\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n**Wrong: No error handling**\n\n```tsx\nconst data = await fetch(url).then((r) => r.json());\n```\n\n**Right: Check response status**\n\n```tsx\nconst response = await fetch(url);\nif (!response.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}`);\nconst data = await response.json();\n```\n\n**Wrong: Storing tokens in AsyncStorage**\n\n```tsx\nawait AsyncStorage.setItem(\"token\", token); // Not secure!\n```\n\n**Right: Use SecureStore for sensitive data**\n\n```tsx\nawait SecureStore.setItemAsync(\"token\", token);\n```\n\n## Example Invocations\n\nUser: \"How do I make API calls in React Native?\"\n-> Use fetch, wrap with error handling\n\nUser: \"Should I use React Query or SWR?\"\n-> React Query for complex apps, SWR for simpler needs\n\nUser: \"My app needs to work offline\"\n-> Use NetInfo for status, React Query persistence for caching\n\nUser: \"How do I handle authentication tokens?\"\n-> Store in expo-secure-store, implement refresh flow\n\nUser: \"API calls are slow\"\n-> Check caching strategy, use React Query staleTime\n\nUser: \"How do I configure different API URLs for dev and prod?\"\n-> Use EXPO*PUBLIC* env vars with .env.development and .env.production files\n\nUser: \"Where should I put my API key?\"\n-> Client-safe keys: EXPO*PUBLIC* in .env. Secret keys: non-prefixed env vars in API routes only\n\nUser: \"How do I load data for a page in Expo Router?\"\n-> See references/expo-router-loaders.md for route-level loaders (web, SDK 55+). For native, use React Query or fetch.\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-03-01T05:13:38.246Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能代理：原生数据抓取","ja":"AIエージェント：ネイティブデータフェッチング","ko":"AI 에이전트: 네이티브 데이터 패칭","es":"Herramientas de AI para Native Data Fetching","fr":"Outils d''IA pour Native Data Fetching","de":"KI-Tools für Native Data Fetching","pt":"Ferramentas de IA: Native Data Fetching para Desenvolvedores","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Native Data Fetching для Разработчиков","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: Native Data Fetching для المطورين","en":"native-data-fetching"},"description":{"zh":"原生数据抓取AI智能代理，用于实现和调试网络请求、API调用和数据抓取，支持fetch API、axios、React Query和SWR","ja":"ネイティブデータフェッチングAIエージェントは、ネットワークリクエスト、API呼び出し、データフェッチの実装とデバッグに使用され、fetch API、axios、React Query、SWRをサポートします","ko":"네이티브 데이터 패칭 AI 에이전트는 네트워크 요청, API 호출 및 데이터 패칭의 구현 및 디버깅에 사용되며 fetch API, axios, React Query 및 SWR를 지원합니다","es":"Native Data Fetching es una habilidad para implementar y depurar solicitudes de red y llamadas a API","fr":"Native Data Fetching est une compétence pour implémenter et déboguer les requêtes réseau et les appels d''API","de":"Native Data Fetching ist eine Fähigkeit zur Implementierung und Fehlersuche von Netzwerkanfragen und API-Aufrufen","pt":"Native Data Fetching é uma habilidade de IA para implementar e depurar requisições de rede e API. Aprenda a usar React Query, SWR e mais","ru":"Native Data Fetching - это навык ИИ для реализации и отладки сетевых запросов и API. Узнайте, как использовать React Query, SWR и больше","ar":"Native Data Fetching هي مهارة ذكاء اصطناعي لتنفيذ وتصحيح أخطاء الطلبات الشبكية و API. تعلم كيفية استخدام React Query، SWR وأكثر","en":"Use when implementing or debugging ANY network request, API call, or data fetching. Covers fetch API, axios, React Query, SWR, error handling, caching strate..."},"definition":{"en":"Use when implementing or debugging ANY network request, API call, or data fetching. Covers fetch API, axios, React Query, SWR, error handling, caching strategies, offline support."},"features":{"zh":["支持fetch API","支持axios","支持React Query","支持SWR","错误处理","缓存策略"],"ja":["fetch APIのサポート","axiosのサポート","React Queryのサポート","SWRのサポート","エラーハンドリング","キャッシュ戦略"],"ko":["fetch API 지원","axios 지원","React Query 지원","SWR 지원","오류 처리","캐싱 전략"],"es":["Implementación de solicitudes de red","Depuración de llamadas a API","Caching y estrategias de almacenamiento","Soporte para escenarios sin conexión","Gestión de autenticación y tokens","Configuración de URLs de API y variables de entorno"],"fr":["Implémentation de requêtes réseau","Débogage d''appels d''API","Mise en cache et stratégies de stockage","Prise en charge de scénarios hors ligne","Gestion d''authentification et de jetons","Configuration d''URL d''API et de variables d''environnement"],"de":["Implementierung von Netzwerkanfragen","Fehlersuche von API-Aufrufen","Caching und Speicherstrategien","Unterstützung für Offline-Szenarien","Authentifizierungs- und Tokenverwaltung","Konfiguration von API-URLs und Umgebungsvariablen"],"pt":["Implementação de requisições de API","Configuração de fetch de dados com React Query e SWR","Depuração de falhas de rede","Implementação de estratégias de cache","Suporte offline","Gerenciamento de autenticação e tokens"],"ru":["Реализация сетевых запросов API","Настройка получения данных с React Query и SWR","Отладка сетевых неисправностей","Реализация стратегий кэширования","Поддержка offline","Управление аутентификацией и токенами"],"ar":["تنفيذ الطلبات الشبكية و API","تكوين استرجاع البيانات مع React Query و SWR","تصحيح أخطاء الشبكة","تنفيذ استراتيجيات التخزين المؤقت","دعم وضع عدم الاتصال","إدارة المصادقة والأشكال"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","原生数据抓取","网络请求","API调用","数据抓取","fetch API","axios","React Query","SWR"],"ja":["AIエージェント","ネイティブデータフェッチング","ネットワークリクエスト","API呼び出し","データフェッチ","fetch API","axios","React Query","SWR"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","네이티브 데이터 패칭","네트워크 요청","API 호출","데이터 패칭","fetch API","axios","React Query","SWR"],"es":["AI para desarrollo web","Herramientas de AI para desarrolladores","Native Data Fetching","Solicitudes de red","Llamadas a API","Caching y almacenamiento","Soporte para escenarios sin conexión","Autenticación y tokens"],"fr":["IA pour le développement web","Outils d''IA pour les développeurs","Native Data Fetching","Requêtes réseau","Appels d''API","Mise en cache et stockage","Prise en charge de scénarios hors ligne","Authentification et jetons"],"de":["KI für Webentwicklung","KI-Tools für Entwickler","Native Data Fetching","Netzwerkanfragen","API-Aufrufe","Caching und Speicherung","Unterstützung für Offline-Szenarien","Authentifizierung und Token"],"pt":["Native Data Fetching","IA para desenvolvedores","Requisições de API","React Query","SWR","Depuração de falhas de rede","Estratégias de cache","Suporte offline","Autenticação e tokens"],"ru":["Native Data Fetching","ИИ для разработчиков","Сетевые запросы API","React Query","SWR","Отладка сетевых неисправностей","Стратегии кэширования","Поддержка offline","Аутентификация и токены"],"ar":["Native Data Fetching","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للمطورين","الطلبات الشبكية و API","React Query","SWR","تصحيح أخطاء الشبكة","استراتيجيات التخزين المؤقت","دعم وضع عدم الاتصال","إدارة المصادقة والأشكال"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Web Development Agents requiring robust data fetching and caching capabilities with React Query, SWR, and Expo Router","zh":"适合需要强大的数据获取和缓存功能的Web开发代理，支持React Query、SWR和Expo Router","ja":"React Query、SWR、Expo Routerを使用した強力なデータ取得およびキャッシュ機能を必要とするWeb開発エージェントに最適","ko":"React Query, SWR, Expo Router를 사용하여 강력한 데이터 가져오기 및 캐싱 기능을 필요로 하는 웹 개발 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de desarrollo web que requieren capacidades de recuperación y almacenamiento en caché de datos robustas con React Query, SWR y Expo Router","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement Web nécessitant des capacités de récupération et de mise en cache de données robustes avec React Query, SWR et Expo Router","de":"Ideal für Webentwicklungsagenten, die robuste Datenabruf- und Cachefunktionen mit React Query, SWR und Expo Router benötigen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento Web que exigem capacidades robustas de busca e armazenamento em cache de dados com React Query, SWR e Expo Router","ru":"Идеально для Веб-разработки Агентов, требующих надежных возможностей по получению и кэшированию данных с помощью React Query, SWR и Expo Router","ar":"مثالي لعمليات تطوير الويب التي تتطلب mogelijkيات قوية لاسترجاع البيانات وتخزينها مؤقتا مع React Query و SWR و Expo Router"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to handle network requests, API calls, and data fetching with ease, utilizing fetch API, error handling, caching, and offline support, while also leveraging Expo Router data loaders like useLoaderData","zh":"赋予代理处理网络请求、API调用和数据获取的能力，利用fetch API、错误处理、缓存和离线支持，同时利用Expo Router数据加载器，如useLoaderData","ja":"エージェントがネットワークリクエスト、API呼び出し、データ取得を容易に処理できるようにし、fetch API、エラーハンドリング、キャッシュ、オフラインサポートを利用し、Expo RouterのデータローダーであるuseLoaderDataを活用","ko":"에이전트가 네트워크 요청, API 호출 및 데이터 가져오기를 쉽게 처리할 수 있도록 하며 fetch API, 오류 처리, 캐싱 및 오프라인 지원을 활용하고 Expo Router의 데이터 로더인 useLoaderData를 활용","es":"Habilita a los agentes a manejar solicitudes de red, llamadas a la API y recuperación de datos con facilidad, utilizando la API de fetch, el control de errores, la caché y el soporte sin conexión, y aprovechando también los cargadores de datos de Expo Router como useLoaderData","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer les requêtes réseau, les appels API et la récupération de données avec facilité, en utilisant l''API de fetch, la gestion des erreurs, la mise en cache et le support hors ligne, tout en exploitant également les chargeurs de données d''Expo Router tels que useLoaderData","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Netzwerkanforderungen, API-Aufrufe und Datenabruf mit Leichtigkeit zu handhaben, indem sie die Fetch-API, Fehlerbehandlung, Caching und Offline-Unterstützung nutzen und auch die Datenlader von Expo Router wie useLoaderData nutzen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a lidar com solicitações de rede, chamadas de API e busca de dados com facilidade, utilizando a API de busca, tratamento de erros, armazenamento em cache e suporte offline, além de aproveitar os carregadores de dados do Expo Router como useLoaderData","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обрабатывать сетевые запросы, вызовы API и получение данных с легкостью, используя fetch API, обработку ошибок, кэширование и поддержку offline, а также использует данные загрузчики Expo Router, такие как useLoaderData","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من التعامل مع طلبات الشبكة ونداءات API واسترجاع البيانات بسهولة، باستخدام واجهة برمجة التطبيقات لاسترجاع، ومعالجة الأخطاء، وتخزين البيانات مؤقتا ودعم عدم الاتصال، بالإضافة إلى استخدام محملات بيانات Expo Router مثل useLoaderData"},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing API requests with fetch API and React Query","Setting up efficient data fetching and caching with SWR","Debugging network issues and optimizing offline support"],"zh":["使用fetch API和React Query实现API请求","使用SWR设置高效的数据获取和缓存","调试网络问题和优化离线支持"],"ja":["fetch APIとReact Queryを使用したAPIリクエストの実装","SWRを使用した効率的なデータ取得およびキャッシュの設定","ネットワーク問題のデバッグとオフラインサポートの最適化"],"ko":["fetch API 및 React Query를 사용하여 API 요청 구현","SWR를 사용하여 효율적인 데이터 가져오기 및 캐싱 설정","네트워크 문제 디버깅 및 오프라인 지원 최적화"],"es":["Implementar solicitudes de API con fetch API y React Query","Configurar una recuperación y almacenamiento en caché de datos eficientes con SWR","Depurar problemas de red y optimizar el soporte sin conexión"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre des requêtes API avec fetch API et React Query","Configurer une récupération et une mise en cache de données efficaces avec SWR","Déboguer les problèmes de réseau et optimiser le support hors ligne"],"de":["Implementierung von API-Anfragen mit Fetch-API und React Query","Einrichtung eines effizienten Datenabrufs und Cachings mit SWR","Fehlerbehebung bei Netzwerkproblemen und Optimierung der Offline-Unterstützung"],"pt":["Implementação de solicitações de API com fetch API e React Query","Configuração de busca de dados eficiente e armazenamento em cache com SWR","Depuração de problemas de rede e otimização do suporte offline"],"ru":["Реализация запросов API с помощью fetch API и React Query","Настройка эффективной загрузки данных и кэширования с помощью SWR","Отладка сетевых проблем и оптимизация поддержки offline"],"ar":["تنفيذ طلبات API باستخدام واجهة برمجة التطبيقات لاسترجاع و React Query","تهيئة استرجاع البيانات بكفاءة وتخزينها مؤقتا مع SWR","تصحيح أخطاء الشبكة وضبط دعم عدم الاتصال"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Expo Router and SDK 55+ for web development","Limited to React-based applications for React Query and SWR integration"],"zh":["需要Expo Router和SDK 55+进行网页开发","仅限于React-based应用程序进行React Query和SWR集成"],"ja":["Web開発のためにExpo RouterとSDK 55+が必要","React QueryおよびSWRの統合はReactベースのアプリケーションに限定"],"ko":["웹 개발을 위해 Expo Router 및 SDK 55+가 필요","React Query 및 SWR 통합은 React 기반 애플리케이션에 제한"],"es":["Requiere Expo Router y SDK 55+ para el desarrollo web","Limitado a aplicaciones basadas en React para la integración de React Query y SWR"],"fr":["Nécessite Expo Router et SDK 55+ pour le développement Web","Limité aux applications basées sur React pour l''intégration de React Query et SWR"],"de":["Benötigt Expo Router und SDK 55+ für die Webentwicklung","Begrenzt auf React-basierte Anwendungen für die Integration von React Query und SWR"],"pt":["Exige Expo Router e SDK 55+ para desenvolvimento web","Limitado a aplicações baseadas em React para integração com React Query e SWR"],"ru":["Требует Expo Router и SDK 55+ для веб-разработки","Ограничен для приложений на основе React для интеграции с React Query и SWR"],"ar":["يتطلب Expo Router و SDK 55+ لتطوير الويب","محدود للتطبيقات المبنية على React لتكامل React Query و SWR"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"eaa2f00ceed45e3149a9c6b6e1b989413bd1350fd4a256c76d89a60d9dc00026","repoEtag":"W/\"74eae87bd9e290dfb1a5ebf14236809a9fecc3d098825762f2b6b3d9526c29eb\"","qualityScore":88}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('cloudflare/skills/building-mcp-server-on-cloudflare', 'official', 'cloudflare', 'skills', 'cloudflare/skills', 'building-mcp-server-on-cloudflare', 387, 38, 87, '2026-02-28T23:20:41Z', '2026-03-01T05:14:09.793Z', 'b03cd41736a399eb203263863f758bd07c6eaa6cea130642bdf9bff3dd2031b4', '{"id":"cloudflare/skills/building-mcp-server-on-cloudflare","name":"building-mcp-server-on-cloudflare","description":{"zh":"构建生产就绪的MCP服务器于Cloudflare Workers，包含工具、认证和部署","ja":"Cloudflare Workers上で生産準備完了のMCPサーバーを構築、ツール、認証、デプロイを含む","ko":"클라우드플레어 워커에서 생산 준비 완료 MCP 서버 구축, 도구, 인증 및 배포 포함","es":"Construye servidores MCP en Cloudflare con herramientas y autenticación. Aprende a desplegar MCP en Cloudflare Workers.","fr":"Créez des serveurs MCP sur Cloudflare avec des outils et une authentification. Apprenez à déployer MCP sur Cloudflare Workers.","de":"Erstellen Sie MCP-Server auf Cloudflare mit Tools und Authentifizierung. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie MCP auf Cloudflare Workers bereitstellen.","pt":"Construa servidores MCP na Cloudflare Workers com ferramentas, autenticação e deploy. Aprenda a criar soluções de IA eficientes","ru":"Создайте серверы MCP на Cloudflare Workers с помощью инструментов, аутентификации и развертывания. Создавайте эффективные решения на основе ИИ","ar":"ابني خوادم MCP على Cloudflare Workers مع أدوات وتحقق وتنفيذ. تعلم كيفية إنشاء حلول الإي الأجنت الفعالة","en":"|"},"owner":"cloudflare","repo":"skills","repoPath":"cloudflare/skills","stars":387,"forks":38,"updatedAt":"2026-02-28T23:20:41Z","topics":["agents","cloudflare","skills","workers"],"skillMd":{"name":"building-mcp-server-on-cloudflare","description":"|","bodyPreview":"# Building MCP Servers on Cloudflare\n\nCreates production-ready Model Context Protocol servers on Cloudflare Workers with tools, authentication, and deployment.\n\n## When to Use\n\n- User wants to build a remote MCP server\n- User needs to expose tools via MCP\n- User asks about MCP authentication or OAuth\n- User wants to deploy MCP to Cloudflare Workers\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- Cloudflare account with Workers enabled\n- Node.js 18+ and npm/pnpm/yarn\n- Wrangler CLI (`npm install -g wrangler`)\n\n## Quick Sta","body":"# Building MCP Servers on Cloudflare\n\nCreates production-ready Model Context Protocol servers on Cloudflare Workers with tools, authentication, and deployment.\n\n## When to Use\n\n- User wants to build a remote MCP server\n- User needs to expose tools via MCP\n- User asks about MCP authentication or OAuth\n- User wants to deploy MCP to Cloudflare Workers\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- Cloudflare account with Workers enabled\n- Node.js 18+ and npm/pnpm/yarn\n- Wrangler CLI (`npm install -g wrangler`)\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### Option 1: Public Server (No Auth)\n\n```bash\nnpm create cloudflare@latest -- my-mcp-server \\\n  --template=cloudflare/ai/demos/remote-mcp-authless\ncd my-mcp-server\nnpm start\n```\n\nServer runs at `http://localhost:8788/mcp`\n\n### Option 2: Authenticated Server (OAuth)\n\n```bash\nnpm create cloudflare@latest -- my-mcp-server \\\n  --template=cloudflare/ai/demos/remote-mcp-github-oauth\ncd my-mcp-server\n```\n\nRequires OAuth app setup. See [references/oauth-setup.md](references/oauth-setup.md).\n\n## Core Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Define Tools\n\nTools are functions MCP clients can call. Define them using `server.tool()`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { McpAgent } from \"agents/mcp\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nexport class MyMCP extends McpAgent {\n  server = new Server({ name: \"my-mcp\", version: \"1.0.0\" });\n\n  async init() {\n    // Simple tool with parameters\n    this.server.tool(\n      \"add\",\n      { a: z.number(), b: z.number() },\n      async ({ a, b }) => ({\n        content: [{ type: \"text\", text: String(a + b) }],\n      })\n    );\n\n    // Tool that calls external API\n    this.server.tool(\n      \"get_weather\",\n      { city: z.string() },\n      async ({ city }) => {\n        const response = await fetch(`https://api.weather.com/${city}`);\n        const data = await response.json();\n        return {\n          content: [{ type: \"text\", text: JSON.stringify(data) }],\n        };\n      }\n    );\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Step 2: Configure Entry Point\n\n**Public server** (`src/index.ts`):\n\n```typescript\nimport { MyMCP } from \"./mcp\";\n\nexport default {\n  fetch(request: Request, env: Env, ctx: ExecutionContext) {\n    const url = new URL(request.url);\n    if (url.pathname === \"/mcp\") {\n      return MyMCP.serveSSE(\"/mcp\").fetch(request, env, ctx);\n    }\n    return new Response(\"MCP Server\", { status: 200 });\n  },\n};\n\nexport { MyMCP };\n```\n\n**Authenticated server** — See [references/oauth-setup.md](references/oauth-setup.md).\n\n### Step 3: Test Locally\n\n```bash\n# Start server\nnpm start\n\n# In another terminal, test with MCP Inspector\nnpx @modelcontextprotocol/inspector@latest\n# Open http://localhost:5173, enter http://localhost:8788/mcp\n```\n\n### Step 4: Deploy\n\n```bash\nnpx wrangler deploy\n```\n\nServer accessible at `https://[worker-name].[account].workers.dev/mcp`\n\n### Step 5: Connect Clients\n\n**Claude Desktop** (`claude_desktop_config.json`):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"my-server\": {\n      \"command\": \"npx\",\n      \"args\": [\"mcp-remote\", \"https://my-mcp.workers.dev/mcp\"]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nRestart Claude Desktop after updating config.\n\n## Tool Patterns\n\n### Return Types\n\n```typescript\n// Text response\nreturn { content: [{ type: \"text\", text: \"result\" }] };\n\n// Multiple content items\nreturn {\n  content: [\n    { type: \"text\", text: \"Here''s the data:\" },\n    { type: \"text\", text: JSON.stringify(data, null, 2) },\n  ],\n};\n```\n\n### Input Validation with Zod\n\n```typescript\nthis.server.tool(\n  \"create_user\",\n  {\n    email: z.string().email(),\n    name: z.string().min(1).max(100),\n    role: z.enum([\"admin\", \"user\", \"guest\"]),\n    age: z.number().int().min(0).optional(),\n  },\n  async (params) => {\n    // params are fully typed and validated\n  }\n);\n```\n\n### Accessing Environment/Bindings\n\n```typescript\nexport class MyMCP extends McpAgent<Env> {\n  async init() {\n    this.server.tool(\"query_db\", { sql: z.string() }, async ({ sql }) => {\n      // Access D1 binding\n      const result = await this.env.DB.prepare(sql).all();\n      return { content: [{ type: \"text\", text: JSON.stringify(result) }] };\n    });\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Authentication\n\nFor OAuth-protected servers, see [references/oauth-setup.md](references/oauth-setup.md).\n\nSupported providers:\n- GitHub\n- Google\n- Auth0\n- Stytch\n- WorkOS\n- Any OAuth 2.0 compliant provider\n\n## Wrangler Configuration\n\nMinimal `wrangler.toml`:\n\n```toml\nname = \"my-mcp-server\"\nmain = \"src/index.ts\"\ncompatibility_date = \"2024-12-01\"\n\n[durable_objects]\nbindings = [{ name = \"MCP\", class_name = \"MyMCP\" }]\n\n[[migrations]]\ntag = \"v1\"\nnew_classes = [\"MyMCP\"]\n```\n\nWith bindings (D1, KV, etc.):\n\n```toml\n[[d1_databases]]\nbinding = \"DB\"\ndatabase_name = \"my-db\"\ndatabase_id = \"xxx\"\n\n[[kv_namespaces]]\nbinding = \"KV\"\nid = \"xxx\"\n```\n\n## Common Issues\n\n### \"Tool not found\" in Client\n\n1. Verify tool name matches exactly (case-sensitive)\n2. Ensure `init()` registers tools before connections\n3. Check server logs: `wrangler tail`\n\n### Connection Fails\n\n1. Confirm endpoint path is `/mcp`\n2. Check CORS if browser-based client\n3. Verify Worker is deployed: `wrangler deployments list`\n\n### OAuth Redirect Errors\n\n1. Callback URL must match OAuth app config exactly\n2. Check `GITHUB_CLIENT_ID` and `GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET` are set\n3. For local dev, use `http://localhost:8788/callback`\n\n## References\n\n- [references/examples.md](references/examples.md) — Official templates and production examples\n- [references/oauth-setup.md](references/oauth-setup.md) — OAuth provider configuration\n- [references/tool-patterns.md](references/tool-patterns.md) — Advanced tool examples\n- [references/troubleshooting.md](references/troubleshooting.md) — Error codes and fixes\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-03-01T05:14:09.793Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能代理：在Cloudflare上构建MCP服务器","ja":"AIエージェント：CloudflareでMCPサーバーを構築","ko":"AI 에이전트: 클라우드플레어에서 MCP 서버 구축","es":"Herramientas AI: Construye servidores MCP en Cloudflare","fr":"Outils IA: Créer des serveurs MCP sur Cloudflare","de":"KI-Tools: Erstellen von MCP-Servern auf Cloudflare","pt":"Construir Servidores MCP na Cloudflare com Ferramentas de IA","ru":"Создание Серверов MCP на Cloudflare с ИИ Агентами","ar":"بناء خوادم MCP على Cloudflare مع أدوات الإي الأجنت","en":"building-mcp-server-on-cloudflare"},"description":{"zh":"构建生产就绪的MCP服务器于Cloudflare Workers，包含工具、认证和部署","ja":"Cloudflare Workers上で生産準備完了のMCPサーバーを構築、ツール、認証、デプロイを含む","ko":"클라우드플레어 워커에서 생산 준비 완료 MCP 서버 구축, 도구, 인증 및 배포 포함","es":"Construye servidores MCP en Cloudflare con herramientas y autenticación. Aprende a desplegar MCP en Cloudflare Workers.","fr":"Créez des serveurs MCP sur Cloudflare avec des outils et une authentification. Apprenez à déployer MCP sur Cloudflare Workers.","de":"Erstellen Sie MCP-Server auf Cloudflare mit Tools und Authentifizierung. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie MCP auf Cloudflare Workers bereitstellen.","pt":"Construa servidores MCP na Cloudflare Workers com ferramentas, autenticação e deploy. Aprenda a criar soluções de IA eficientes","ru":"Создайте серверы MCP на Cloudflare Workers с помощью инструментов, аутентификации и развертывания. Создавайте эффективные решения на основе ИИ","ar":"ابني خوادم MCP على Cloudflare Workers مع أدوات وتحقق وتنفيذ. تعلم كيفية إنشاء حلول الإي الأجنت الفعالة","en":"|"},"definition":{"en":"|"},"features":{"zh":["使用Cloudflare Workers构建MCP服务器","包含工具、认证和部署","支持Node.js 18+和npm/pnpm/yarn","使用Wrangler CLI进行部署"],"ja":["Cloudflare Workersを使用してMCPサーバーを構築","ツール、認証、デプロイを含む","Node.js 18+とnpm/pnpm/yarnをサポート","Wrangler CLIを使用してデプロイ"],"ko":["클라우드플레어 워커를 사용하여 MCP 서버 구축","도구, 인증 및 배포 포함","노드.js 18+ 및 npm/pnpm/yarn 지원","Wrangler CLI를 사용하여 배포"],"es":["Creación de servidores MCP en Cloudflare","Autenticación y autorización de MCP","Despliegue de MCP en Cloudflare Workers","Uso de herramientas para la creación de servidores MCP","Compatibilidad con Node.js 18+ y npm/pnpm/yarn"],"fr":["Création de serveurs MCP sur Cloudflare","Authentification et autorisation de MCP","Déploiement de MCP sur Cloudflare Workers","Utilisation d''outils pour la création de serveurs MCP","Compatibilité avec Node.js 18+ et npm/pnpm/yarn"],"de":["Erstellung von MCP-Servern auf Cloudflare","Authentifizierung und Autorisierung von MCP","Bereitstellung von MCP auf Cloudflare Workers","Verwendung von Tools für die Erstellung von MCP-Servern","Kompatibilität mit Node.js 18+ und npm/pnpm/yarn"],"pt":["Criação de servidores MCP prontos para produção","Autenticação e deploy na Cloudflare Workers","Uso de ferramentas de IA para melhorar a eficiência","Compatibilidade com Node.js 18+ e npm/pnpm/yarn","Uso do Wrangler CLI para gerenciar o deploy"],"ru":["Создание серверов MCP, готовых к производству","Аутентификация и развертывание на Cloudflare Workers","Использование инструментов ИИ для повышения эффективности","Совместимость с Node.js 18+ и npm/pnpm/yarn","Использование Wrangler CLI для управления развертыванием"],"ar":["بناء خوادم MCP جاهزة للإنتاج","التحقق والتنفيذ على Cloudflare Workers","استخدام أدوات الإي الأجنت لتحسين الكفاءة","التوافق مع Node.js 18+ وnpm/pnpm/yarn","استخدام Wrangler CLI لإدارة التنفيذ"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","MCP服务器构建","Cloudflare Workers","Node.js","Wrangler CLI","Model Context Protocol"],"ja":["AIエージェント","MCPサーバー構築","Cloudflare Workers","Node.js","Wrangler CLI","Model Context Protocol"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","MCP 서버 구축","클라우드플레어 워커","노드.js","Wrangler CLI","모델 컨텍스트 프로토콜"],"es":["herramientas AI","servidores MCP","Cloudflare","Workers","autenticación MCP","despliegue de MCP","Node.js","npm","pnpm","yarn"],"fr":["outils IA","serveurs MCP","Cloudflare","Workers","authentification MCP","déploiement de MCP","Node.js","npm","pnpm","yarn"],"de":["KI-Tools","MCP-Server","Cloudflare","Workers","Authentifizierung von MCP","Bereitstellung von MCP","Node.js","npm","pnpm","yarn"],"pt":["servidores MCP","Cloudflare Workers","ferramentas de IA","autenticação","deploy","Node.js","npm","pnpm","yarn","Wrangler CLI"],"ru":["серверы MCP","Cloudflare Workers","инструменты ИИ","аутентификация","развертывание","Node.js","npm","pnpm","yarn","Wrangler CLI"],"ar":["خوادم MCP","Cloudflare Workers","أدوات الإي الأجنت","التحقق","التنفيذ","Node.js","npm","pnpm","yarn","Wrangler CLI"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Cloudflare-focused AI Agents seeking to deploy Model Context Protocol servers with streamlined authentication and tool exposure.","zh":"适用于专注于Cloudflare的AI代理，旨在部署带有简化身份验证和工具暴露的Model Context Protocol服务器的场景。","ja":"Cloudflareに焦点を当てたAIエージェントが、ストリームライン化された認証とツールの露出を持つModel Context Protocolサーバーをデプロイすることを目指している場合に適しています。","ko":"Cloudflare를 중점으로 하는 AI 에이전트가 모델 컨텍스트 프로토콜 서버를 배포하도록 설계된 시나리오에 적합합니다. 인증 및 툴 노출이 간소화됩니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA de Cloudflare que buscan implementar servidores de protocolo de contexto de modelo con autenticación simplificada y exposición de herramientas.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''IA Cloudflare souhaitant déployer des serveurs de protocole de contexte de modèle avec une authentification simplifiée et une exposition d''outils.","de":"Ideal für Cloudflare-orientierte KI-Agents, die Server des Modellkontextprotokolls mit vereinfachter Authentifizierung und Werkzeugexposition bereitstellen möchten.","pt":"Ideal para agentes de IA do Cloudflare que buscam implantar servidores de Protocolo de Contexto de Modelo com autenticação simplificada e exposição de ferramentas.","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, ориентированных на Cloudflare, которые стремятся развернуть серверы протокола контекста модели с упрощенной аутентификацией и инструментами.","ar":"مثالي لعميلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي في كلاودفلير الراغبين في نشر خادم بروتوكول سياق النموذج مع المصادقة المُبسطة وعرض الأدوات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create production-ready MCP servers on Cloudflare Workers, leveraging tools like Wrangler CLI, Node.js, and npm/pnpm/yarn for seamless deployment and OAuth authentication integration.","zh":"赋予代理在Cloudflare Workers上创建生产就绪的MCP服务器的能力，利用Wrangler CLI、Node.js以及npm/pnpm/yarn等工具实现无缝的部署和OAuth身份验证集成。","ja":"Cloudflare Workers上で生産レディのMCPサーバーを作成するためのエージェントをEmpowerし、Wrangler CLI、Node.js、およびnpm/pnpm/yarnなどのツールを使用してシームレスなデプロイとOAuth認証の統合を実現します。","ko":"에이전트가 Cloudflare Workers에서 생산 준비가 된 MCP 서버를 만들 수 있도록 하고, Wrangler CLI, Node.js 및 npm/pnpm/yarn과 같은 도구를 사용하여 무결점 배포 및 OAuth 인증 통합을 구현합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes crear servidores MCP de producción listos en Cloudflare Workers, utilizando herramientas como Wrangler CLI, Node.js y npm/pnpm/yarn para una implementación y una integración de autenticación OAuth sin problemas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des serveurs MCP prêts pour la production sur Cloudflare Workers, en utilisant des outils tels que Wrangler CLI, Node.js et npm/pnpm/yarn pour un déploiement et une intégration d''authentification OAuth sans problème.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, produktionsbereite MCP-Server auf Cloudflare Workers zu erstellen, indem Tools wie Wrangler CLI, Node.js und npm/pnpm/yarn für eine reibungslose Bereitstellung und OAuth-Authentifizierungsintegration genutzt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criarem servidores MCP de produção no Cloudflare Workers, utilizando ferramentas como Wrangler CLI, Node.js e npm/pnpm/yarn para implantação e integração de autenticação OAuth sem problemas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать серверы MCP, готовые к производству, на Cloudflare Workers, используя инструменты, такие как Wrangler CLI, Node.js и npm/pnpm/yarn для бесшовного развертывания и интеграции аутентификации OAuth.","ar":"يمنح العميلاء إمكانية إنشاء خادمات MCP جاهزة للإنتاج على كلاود فلير ووركرز، باستخدام أدوات مثل ورانجلر CLI، Node.js وnpm/pnpm/yarn للنشر السلس والدمج المصادق OAuth."},"useCases":{"en":["Deploying MCP servers to Cloudflare Workers for remote access","Exposing tools via Model Context Protocol for enhanced functionality","Implementing MCP authentication and OAuth for secure server interactions"],"zh":["将MCP服务器部署到Cloudflare Workers以实现远程访问","通过模型上下文协议暴露工具以增强功能","实现MCP身份验证和OAuth以实现安全的服务器交互"],"ja":["Cloudflare WorkersにMCPサーバーをデプロイしてリモートアクセスを実現する","モデルコンテキストプロトコルを介してツールを公開して機能を強化する","MCPの認証とOAuthを実装して安全なサーバー相互作用を実現する"],"ko":["Cloudflare Workers에 MCP 서버를 배포하여 원격 액세스를 가능하게 함","모델 컨텍스트 프로토콜을 통해 툴을 노출하여 기능을 강화함","MCP 인증 및 OAuth를 구현하여 안전한 서버 상호 작용을 구현함"],"es":["Implementar servidores MCP en Cloudflare Workers para el acceso remoto","Exponer herramientas a través del protocolo de contexto de modelo para una funcionalidad mejorada","Implementar autenticación MCP y OAuth para interacciones de servidor seguras"],"fr":["Déployer des serveurs MCP sur Cloudflare Workers pour un accès distant","Exposer des outils via le protocole de contexte de modèle pour une fonctionnalité améliorée","Mettre en œuvre une authentification MCP et OAuth pour des interactions de serveur sécurisées"],"de":["MCP-Server auf Cloudflare Workers für den Remote-Zugriff bereitstellen","Werkzeuge über das Modellkontextprotokoll für eine erweiterte Funktionalität exponieren","MCP-Authentifizierung und OAuth für sichere Serverinteraktionen implementieren"],"pt":["Implantação de servidores MCP no Cloudflare Workers para acesso remoto","Exposição de ferramentas via Protocolo de Contexto de Modelo para funcionalidade aprimorada","Implementação de autenticação MCP e OAuth para interações de servidor seguras"],"ru":["Развертывание серверов MCP на Cloudflare Workers для удаленного доступа","Публикация инструментов через протокол контекста модели для улучшенной функциональности","Реализация аутентификации MCP и OAuth для безопасного взаимодействия серверов"],"ar":["نشر خادمات MCP على كلاود فلير ووركرز للوصول عن بُعد","إظهار الأدوات من خلال بروتوكول سياق النموذج للوظائف المحسنة","تنفيذ مصادقة MCP وOAuth للتفاعلات الخادومية الآمنة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Cloudflare account with Workers enabled","Needs Node.js 18+ and npm/pnpm/yarn installed","Dependent on Wrangler CLI for deployment"],"zh":["需要Cloudflare账户并启用Workers","需要安装Node.js 18+和npm/pnpm/yarn","依赖于Wrangler CLI进行部署"],"ja":["Workersが有効化されたCloudflareアカウントが必要","Node.js 18+とnpm/pnpm/yarnがインストールされている必要がある","デプロイにはWrangler CLIに依存する"],"ko":["Workers가 활성화된 Cloudflare 계정 필요","Node.js 18+ 및 npm/pnpm/yarn 설치 필요","배포에는 Wrangler CLI에 의존"],"es":["Requiere una cuenta de Cloudflare con Workers habilitados","Necesita Node.js 18+ y npm/pnpm/yarn instalados","Depende de Wrangler CLI para la implementación"],"fr":["Nécessite un compte Cloudflare avec Workers activés","Nécessite Node.js 18+ et npm/pnpm/yarn installés","Dépend de Wrangler CLI pour le déploiement"],"de":["Benötigt ein Cloudflare-Konto mit aktivierten Workers","Benötigt Node.js 18+ und npm/pnpm/yarn installiert","Hängt von Wrangler CLI für die Bereitstellung ab"],"pt":["Exige conta Cloudflare com Workers habilitados","Necessita Node.js 18+ e npm/pnpm/yarn instalados","Depende do Wrangler CLI para implantação"],"ru":["Требует учетной записи Cloudflare с включенными Workers","Требует Node.js 18+ и установленных npm/pnpm/yarn","Зависит от Wrangler CLI для развертывания"],"ar":["يتطلب حساب كلاود فلير مع ووركرز ممكّن","يحتاج إلى Node.js 18+ وnpm/pnpm/yarn مثبتين","يعتمد على ورانجلر CLI لنشر"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"b03cd41736a399eb203263863f758bd07c6eaa6cea130642bdf9bff3dd2031b4","repoEtag":"W/\"2050ff8b3c3e00d31ab6816727c74e0ab9c1b238360cd17bc6966651ab9c7ea4\"","qualityScore":87}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('obra/superpowers/dispatching-parallel-agents', 'official', 'obra', 'superpowers', 'obra/superpowers', 'dispatching-parallel-agents', 66125, 5048, 86, '2026-03-01T05:08:15Z', '2026-03-01T05:08:47.326Z', 'c628917689ccc12ce9991615db6824d44c4fe71f8427cd959560aebe6a1a6476', '{"id":"obra/superpowers/dispatching-parallel-agents","name":"dispatching-parallel-agents","description":{"zh":"Dispatching Parallel Agents 技术允许开发者并行处理多个独立任务，提高开发效率","ja":"Dispatching Parallel Agents 技術により、開発者は複数の独立したタスクを並列処理できます","ko":"Dispatching Parallel Agents 기술을 사용하면 개발자는 여러 개의 독립적인 작업을 병렬로 처리할 수 있습니다","es":"Dispatching-parallel-agents permite gestionar tareas independientes de forma concurrente, mejorando la eficiencia en el desarrollo de software","fr":"Dispatching-parallel-agents permet de gérer des tâches indépendantes de manière concurrente, améliorant ainsi l''efficacité dans le développement de logiciels","de":"Dispatching-parallel-agents ermöglicht die gleichzeitige Bearbeitung von unabhängigen Aufgaben, wodurch die Effizienz in der Softwareentwicklung verbessert wird","pt":"O dispatching de agentes paralelos permite resolver tarefas independentes de forma concorrente, aumentando a eficiência","ru":"Параллельное.dispatching ИИ Агентов позволяет решать независимые задачи одновременно, увеличивая производительность","ar":"إرسال وكلاء متوازي يسمح بحل المهام المستقلة بشكل متوازي، مما يزيد من الكفاءة","en":"Use when facing 2+ independent tasks that can be worked on without shared state or sequential dependencies"},"owner":"obra","repo":"superpowers","repoPath":"obra/superpowers","stars":66125,"forks":5048,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T05:08:15Z","topics":[],"skillMd":{"name":"dispatching-parallel-agents","description":"Use when facing 2+ independent tasks that can be worked on without shared state or sequential dependencies","bodyPreview":"# Dispatching Parallel Agents\n\n## Overview\n\nWhen you have multiple unrelated failures (different test files, different subsystems, different bugs), investigating them sequentially wastes time. Each investigation is independent and can happen in parallel.\n\n**Core principle:** Dispatch one agent per independent problem domain. Let them work concurrently.\n\n## When to Use\n\n```dot\ndigraph when_to_use {\n    \"Multiple failures?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Are they independent?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Single","body":"# Dispatching Parallel Agents\n\n## Overview\n\nWhen you have multiple unrelated failures (different test files, different subsystems, different bugs), investigating them sequentially wastes time. Each investigation is independent and can happen in parallel.\n\n**Core principle:** Dispatch one agent per independent problem domain. Let them work concurrently.\n\n## When to Use\n\n```dot\ndigraph when_to_use {\n    \"Multiple failures?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Are they independent?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Single agent investigates all\" [shape=box];\n    \"One agent per problem domain\" [shape=box];\n    \"Can they work in parallel?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Sequential agents\" [shape=box];\n    \"Parallel dispatch\" [shape=box];\n\n    \"Multiple failures?\" -> \"Are they independent?\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Are they independent?\" -> \"Single agent investigates all\" [label=\"no - related\"];\n    \"Are they independent?\" -> \"Can they work in parallel?\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Can they work in parallel?\" -> \"Parallel dispatch\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Can they work in parallel?\" -> \"Sequential agents\" [label=\"no - shared state\"];\n}\n```\n\n**Use when:**\n- 3+ test files failing with different root causes\n- Multiple subsystems broken independently\n- Each problem can be understood without context from others\n- No shared state between investigations\n\n**Don''t use when:**\n- Failures are related (fix one might fix others)\n- Need to understand full system state\n- Agents would interfere with each other\n\n## The Pattern\n\n### 1. Identify Independent Domains\n\nGroup failures by what''s broken:\n- File A tests: Tool approval flow\n- File B tests: Batch completion behavior\n- File C tests: Abort functionality\n\nEach domain is independent - fixing tool approval doesn''t affect abort tests.\n\n### 2. Create Focused Agent Tasks\n\nEach agent gets:\n- **Specific scope:** One test file or subsystem\n- **Clear goal:** Make these tests pass\n- **Constraints:** Don''t change other code\n- **Expected output:** Summary of what you found and fixed\n\n### 3. Dispatch in Parallel\n\n```typescript\n// In Claude Code / AI environment\nTask(\"Fix agent-tool-abort.test.ts failures\")\nTask(\"Fix batch-completion-behavior.test.ts failures\")\nTask(\"Fix tool-approval-race-conditions.test.ts failures\")\n// All three run concurrently\n```\n\n### 4. Review and Integrate\n\nWhen agents return:\n- Read each summary\n- Verify fixes don''t conflict\n- Run full test suite\n- Integrate all changes\n\n## Agent Prompt Structure\n\nGood agent prompts are:\n1. **Focused** - One clear problem domain\n2. **Self-contained** - All context needed to understand the problem\n3. **Specific about output** - What should the agent return?\n\n```markdown\nFix the 3 failing tests in src/agents/agent-tool-abort.test.ts:\n\n1. \"should abort tool with partial output capture\" - expects ''interrupted at'' in message\n2. \"should handle mixed completed and aborted tools\" - fast tool aborted instead of completed\n3. \"should properly track pendingToolCount\" - expects 3 results but gets 0\n\nThese are timing/race condition issues. Your task:\n\n1. Read the test file and understand what each test verifies\n2. Identify root cause - timing issues or actual bugs?\n3. Fix by:\n   - Replacing arbitrary timeouts with event-based waiting\n   - Fixing bugs in abort implementation if found\n   - Adjusting test expectations if testing changed behavior\n\nDo NOT just increase timeouts - find the real issue.\n\nReturn: Summary of what you found and what you fixed.\n```\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n**❌ Too broad:** \"Fix all the tests\" - agent gets lost\n**✅ Specific:** \"Fix agent-tool-abort.test.ts\" - focused scope\n\n**❌ No context:** \"Fix the race condition\" - agent doesn''t know where\n**✅ Context:** Paste the error messages and test names\n\n**❌ No constraints:** Agent might refactor everything\n**✅ Constraints:** \"Do NOT change production code\" or \"Fix tests only\"\n\n**❌ Vague output:** \"Fix it\" - you don''t know what changed\n**✅ Specific:** \"Return summary of root cause and changes\"\n\n## When NOT to Use\n\n**Related failures:** Fixing one might fix others - investigate together first\n**Need full context:** Understanding requires seeing entire system\n**Exploratory debugging:** You don''t know what''s broken yet\n**Shared state:** Agents would interfere (editing same files, using same resources)\n\n## Real Example from Session\n\n**Scenario:** 6 test failures across 3 files after major refactoring\n\n**Failures:**\n- agent-tool-abort.test.ts: 3 failures (timing issues)\n- batch-completion-behavior.test.ts: 2 failures (tools not executing)\n- tool-approval-race-conditions.test.ts: 1 failure (execution count = 0)\n\n**Decision:** Independent domains - abort logic separate from batch completion separate from race conditions\n\n**Dispatch:**\n```\nAgent 1 → Fix agent-tool-abort.test.ts\nAgent 2 → Fix batch-completion-behavior.test.ts\nAgent 3 → Fix tool-approval-race-conditions.test.ts\n```\n\n**Results:**\n- Agent 1: Replaced timeouts with event-based waiting\n- Agent 2: Fixed event structure bug (threadId in wrong place)\n- Agent 3: Added wait for async tool execution to complete\n\n**Integration:** All fixes independent, no conflicts, full suite green\n\n**Time saved:** 3 problems solved in parallel vs sequentially\n\n## Key Benefits\n\n1. **Parallelization** - Multiple investigations happen simultaneously\n2. **Focus** - Each agent has narrow scope, less context to track\n3. **Independence** - Agents don''t interfere with each other\n4. **Speed** - 3 problems solved in time of 1\n\n## Verification\n\nAfter agents return:\n1. **Review each summary** - Understand what changed\n2. **Check for conflicts** - Did agents edit same code?\n3. **Run full suite** - Verify all fixes work together\n4. **Spot check** - Agents can make systematic errors\n\n## Real-World Impact\n\nFrom debugging session (2025-10-03):\n- 6 failures across 3 files\n- 3 agents dispatched in parallel\n- All investigations completed concurrently\n- All fixes integrated successfully\n- Zero conflicts between agent changes\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-03-01T05:08:47.326Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能代理：并行代理调度","ja":"AIエージェント：並列エージェントのdispatching","ko":"AI 에이전트: 병렬 에이전트 디스패치","es":"Herramientas de Agentes de IA: Dispatching Parallel Agents","fr":"Outils d''Agents IA: Dispatching d''Agents Parallèles","de":"KI-Tools: Dispatching von Parallelagenten","pt":"Ferramentas de IA: Dispatching de Agentes Paralelos","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Параллельное.dispatching","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: إرسال وكلاء متوازي","en":"dispatching-parallel-agents"},"description":{"zh":"Dispatching Parallel Agents 技术允许开发者并行处理多个独立任务，提高开发效率","ja":"Dispatching Parallel Agents 技術により、開発者は複数の独立したタスクを並列処理できます","ko":"Dispatching Parallel Agents 기술을 사용하면 개발자는 여러 개의 독립적인 작업을 병렬로 처리할 수 있습니다","es":"Dispatching-parallel-agents permite gestionar tareas independientes de forma concurrente, mejorando la eficiencia en el desarrollo de software","fr":"Dispatching-parallel-agents permet de gérer des tâches indépendantes de manière concurrente, améliorant ainsi l''efficacité dans le développement de logiciels","de":"Dispatching-parallel-agents ermöglicht die gleichzeitige Bearbeitung von unabhängigen Aufgaben, wodurch die Effizienz in der Softwareentwicklung verbessert wird","pt":"O dispatching de agentes paralelos permite resolver tarefas independentes de forma concorrente, aumentando a eficiência","ru":"Параллельное.dispatching ИИ Агентов позволяет решать независимые задачи одновременно, увеличивая производительность","ar":"إرسال وكلاء متوازي يسمح بحل المهام المستقلة بشكل متوازي، مما يزيد من الكفاءة","en":"Use when facing 2+ independent tasks that can be worked on without shared state or sequential dependencies"},"definition":{"en":"Use when facing 2+ independent tasks that can be worked on without shared state or sequential dependencies"},"features":{"zh":["并行处理多个独立任务","提高开发效率","无需共享状态或顺序依赖","支持多个问题域","并发工作"],"ja":["複数の独立したタスクを並列処理","開発効率の向上","共有状態や順序依存不要","複数の問題ドメインをサポート","並列作業"],"ko":["여러 개의 독립적인 작업을 병렬로 처리","개발 효율성 향상","공유 상태 또는 순차적 의존성 필요 없음","여러 문제 도메인 지원","병렬 작업"],"es":["Ejecución concurrente de tareas independientes","Mejora de la eficiencia en el desarrollo de software","Compatibilidad con múltiples problemas de dominio","Flexibilidad en la gestión de tareas","Integración con herramientas de desarrollo de software"],"fr":["Exécution concurrente de tâches indépendantes","Amélioration de l''efficacité dans le développement de logiciels","Compatibilité avec plusieurs problèmes de domaine","Flexibilité dans la gestion de tâches","Intégration avec des outils de développement de logiciels"],"de":["Gleichzeitige Ausführung von unabhängigen Aufgaben","Verbesserung der Effizienz in der Softwareentwicklung","Kompatibilität mit mehreren Problemdomänen","Flexibilität bei der Aufgabenverwaltung","Integration mit Software-Entwicklungstools"],"pt":["Resolução de tarefas independentes de forma concorrente","Aumento da eficiência e produtividade","Utilização de agentes paralelos para processamento","Suporte a múltiplas tarefas simultâneas","Integração com ferramentas de IA"],"ru":["Параллельное решение независимых задач","Увеличение производительности и эффективности","Использование параллельных агентов для обработки","Поддержка нескольких задач одновременно","Интеграция с ИИ инструментами"],"ar":["حل المهام المستقلة بشكل متوازي","زيادة الكفاءة والإنتاجية","استخدام وكلاء متوازي للمعالجة","دعم مهام متعددة في نفس الوقت","التكامل مع أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","并行处理","独立任务","开发效率","Dispatching Parallel Agents","AI技术"],"ja":["AIエージェント","並列処理","独立したタスク","開発効率","Dispatching Parallel Agents","AI技術"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","병렬 처리","독립적인 작업","개발 효율성","Dispatching Parallel Agents","AI 기술"],"es":["dispatching-parallel-agents","programación concurrente","desarrollo de software","eficiencia","herramientas de desarrollo","agentes de IA","tareas independientes"],"fr":["dispatching-parallel-agents","programmation concurrente","développement de logiciels","efficacité","outils de développement","agents IA","tâches indépendantes"],"de":["dispatching-parallel-agents","parallele Programmierung","Softwareentwicklung","Effizienz","Entwicklungstools","KI-Tools","unabhängige Aufgaben"],"pt":["ferramentas de ia","dispatching de agentes paralelos","processamento concorrente","tarefas independentes","eficiência","produtividade","agentes paralelos"],"ru":["ИИ агенты","параллельное.dispatching","параллельная обработка","независимые задачи","эффективность","производительность","параллельные агенты"],"ar":["أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","إرسال وكلاء متوازي","معالجة متوازية","مهام مستقلة","كفاءة","إنتاجية","وكلاء متوازي"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Multi-Tasking Agents like AutoGPT and LangChain that need to handle independent tasks concurrently without shared state or sequential dependencies","zh":"适合于像 AutoGPT 和 LangChain 这样的多任务代理，它们需要在没有共享状态或顺序依赖的情况下并发处理独立任务","ja":"AutoGPTやLangChainのようなマルチタスクエージェントに適しており、共有状態やシーケンシャル依存関係がない独立したタスクを同時に処理する必要がある","ko":"AutoGPT와 LangChain 같은 멀티 태스킹 에이전트에 적합하며, 공유 상태 또는 순차적 종속성 없이 독립적인 태스크를 동시에 처리할 수 있어야 함","es":"Ideal para agentes de Multi-Tasking como AutoGPT y LangChain que necesitan manejar tareas independientes de forma concurrente sin estado compartido o dependencias secuenciales","fr":"Idéal pour les agents Multi-Tasking comme AutoGPT et LangChain qui doivent gérer des tâches indépendantes simultanément sans état partagé ou dépendances séquentielles","de":"Ideal für Multi-Tasking-Agenten wie AutoGPT und LangChain, die unabhängige Aufgaben gleichzeitig ohne gemeinsamen Zustand oder sequenzielle Abhängigkeiten handhaben müssen","pt":"Ideal para Multi-Tasking Agents como AutoGPT e LangChain que precisam lidar com tarefas independentes de forma concorrente sem estado compartilhado ou dependências sequenciais","ru":"Идеально подходит для Multi-Tasking Agents, таких как AutoGPT и LangChain, которым необходимо обрабатывать независимые задачи параллельно без общего состояния или последовательных зависимостей","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء Multi-Tasking مثل AutoGPT و LangChain الذين يحتاجون إلى التعامل مع مهام مستقلة بشكل متزامن دون حالة مشتركة أو تبعيات تسلسلية"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to concurrently investigate multiple unrelated failures across different test files, subsystems, or bugs, leveraging dispatching parallel agents to optimize investigation time, utilizing core principles like independent problem domains and concurrent processing","zh":"赋予代理同时调查多个无关的故障的能力，跨越不同的测试文件、子系统或错误，利用调度并行代理来优化调查时间，利用独立问题域和并发处理等核心原则","ja":"エージェントに、異なるテストファイル、サブシステム、またはバグを横断して、複数の無関係な障害を同時に調査する能力を与え、調査時間を最適化するために並列エージェントの派遣を利用し、独立した問題ドメインや並列処理などの基本原則を利用する","ko":"에이전트가 다른 테스트 파일, 서브시스템 또는 버그를横跨하여 여러개의 무관한 오류를 동시에 조사할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, 조사 시간을 최적화하기 위해 병렬 에이전트의 배치 및 독립적인 문제 도메인과 동시 처리 등 핵심 원리를 활용","es":"Permite a los agentes investigar concurrentemente múltiples fallos no relacionados en diferentes archivos de prueba, subsistemas o errores, aprovechando el despacho de agentes paralelos para optimizar el tiempo de investigación, utilizando principios fundamentales como dominios de problemas independientes y procesamiento concurrente","fr":"Permet aux agents d''étudier simultanément de multiples défaillances non liées dans différents fichiers de test, sous-systèmes ou bogues, en tirant parti de l''envoi d''agents parallèles pour optimiser le temps d''investigation, en utilisant des principes fondamentaux tels que les domaines de problèmes indépendants et le traitement concurrent","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, mehrere unabhängige Fehler in verschiedenen Testdateien, Subsystemen oder Bugs gleichzeitig zu untersuchen, indem parallele Agenten eingesetzt werden, um die Untersuchungszeit zu optimieren, unter Nutzung von Kernprinzipien wie unabhängige Problemdomänen und gleichzeitige Verarbeitung","pt":"Capacita os agentes a investigar concorrentemente múltiplas falhas não relacionadas em diferentes arquivos de teste, subsistemas ou bugs, aproveitando o despacho de agentes paralelos para otimizar o tempo de investigação, utilizando princípios fundamentais como domínios de problemas independentes e processamento concorrente","ru":"Позволяет агентам параллельно исследовать несколько несвязанных сбоев в различных тестовых файлах, подсистемах или ошибках, используя распределение параллельных агентов для оптимизации времени расследования, применяя основные принципы, такие как независимые проблемные области и параллельная обработка","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من التحقيق بشكل متزامن في أعطال متعددة غير مرتبطة عبر ملفات اختبار أو أنظمة فرعية أو أخطاء مختلفة، والاستفادة من إرسال وكلاء متوازيين لتحسين وقت التحقيق، باستخدام مبادئ أساسية مثل مجالات المشكلات المستقلة والمعالجة المتزامنة"},"useCases":{"en":["Investigating multiple unrelated software failures simultaneously","Processing independent data sets in parallel","Concurrently executing tasks with no sequential dependencies"],"zh":["同时调查多个无关的软件故障","并行处理独立的数据集","并发执行没有顺序依赖的任务"],"ja":["複数の無関係なソフトウェア障害を同時に調査する","独立したデータセットを並列で処理する","シーケンシャル依存関係がないタスクを並列で実行する"],"ko":["여러개의 무관한 소프트웨어 오류를 동시에 조사","독립적인 데이터 세트를 병렬로 처리","순차적 종속성이 없는 태스크를 병렬로 실행"],"es":["Investigación simultánea de múltiples fallos de software no relacionados","Procesamiento de conjuntos de datos independientes en paralelo","Ejecución concurrente de tareas sin dependencias secuenciales"],"fr":["Investigation simultanée de multiples défaillances logicielles non liées","Traitement d''ensembles de données indépendants en parallèle","Exécution concurrente de tâches sans dépendances séquentielles"],"de":["Gleichzeitige Untersuchung mehrerer unabhängiger Softwarefehler","Parallele Verarbeitung unabhängiger Datensätze","Gleichzeitige Ausführung von Aufgaben ohne sequenzielle Abhängigkeiten"],"pt":["Investigação simultânea de múltiplas falhas de software não relacionadas","Processamento de conjuntos de dados independentes em paralelo","Execução concorrente de tarefas sem dependências sequenciais"],"ru":["Параллельное исследование нескольких несвязанных сбоев программного обеспечения","Параллельная обработка независимых наборов данных","Одновременное выполнение задач без последовательных зависимостей"],"ar":["التحقيق في أعطال برمجية متعددة غير مرتبطة في وقت واحد","معالجة مجموعات بيانات مستقلة بالتوازي","تنفيذ مهام متزامنة بدون تبعيات تسلسلية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires independent tasks with no shared state","No support for sequential dependencies between tasks","Optimized for agents capable of concurrent processing"],"zh":["需要独立的任务，没有共享状态","不支持任务之间的顺序依赖","针对能够并发处理的代理进行优化"],"ja":["共有状態がない独立したタスクが必要","タスク間のシーケンシャル依存関係はサポートされない","並列処理可能なエージェントに最適化"],"ko":["공유 상태가 없는 독립적인 태스크가 필요","태스크 간의 순차적 종속성은 지원되지 않음","병렬 처리가 가능한 에이전트에 최적화"],"es":["Requiere tareas independientes sin estado compartido","No admite dependencias secuenciales entre tareas","Optimizado para agentes capaces de procesamiento concurrente"],"fr":["Nécessite des tâches indépendantes sans état partagé","Aucune prise en charge des dépendances séquentielles entre les tâches","Optimisé pour les agents capables de traitement concurrent"],"de":["Erfordert unabhängige Aufgaben ohne gemeinsamen Zustand","Keine Unterstützung für sequenzielle Abhängigkeiten zwischen Aufgaben","Optimiert für Agenten mit Fähigkeit zur gleichzeitigen Verarbeitung"],"pt":["Requer tarefas independentes sem estado compartilhado","Sem suporte para dependências sequenciais entre tarefas","Otimizado para agentes capazes de processamento concorrente"],"ru":["Требует независимых задач без общего состояния","Отсутствие поддержки последовательных зависимостей между задачами","Оптимизирован для агентов, способных к параллельной обработке"],"ar":["يتطلب مهامًا مستقلة بدون حالة مشتركة","لا يدعم التبعيات التسلسلية بين المهام","مُحسّن للوكلاء القادرين على المعالجة المتزامنة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"c628917689ccc12ce9991615db6824d44c4fe71f8427cd959560aebe6a1a6476","repoEtag":"W/\"c0159b000a3f1065b2a623072c2f281d1dae59e39bce28acebe789d1e6a6aa8e\"","qualityScore":86}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('obra/superpowers/subagent-driven-development', 'official', 'obra', 'superpowers', 'obra/superpowers', 'subagent-driven-development', 66125, 5048, 86, '2026-03-01T05:08:15Z', '2026-03-01T05:08:48.273Z', '994b89a5d294eadd6a1611edb51377bac748d5f5fb7f4139d3c736b616b3a46a', '{"id":"obra/superpowers/subagent-driven-development","name":"subagent-driven-development","description":{"zh":"子代理驱动开发是一种使用独立任务的实现计划执行方法，通过两阶段审查确保高质量和快速迭代","ja":"サブエージェント駆動開発は、独立したタスクを持つ実装計画を実行する方法で、2段階のレビューを通じて高品質と迅速な反復を実現します","ko":"서브 에이전트 주도 개발은 독립적인 태스크를 사용하는 구현 계획을 실행하는 방법으로, 2단계의 검토를 통해 높은 품질과 빠른 반복을 실현합니다","es":"El desarrollo impulsado por subagentes es una técnica que utiliza subagentes para ejecutar planes de implementación con tareas independientes y revisiones de dos etapas","fr":"Le développement piloté par sous-agent est une technique qui utilise des sous-agents pour exécuter des plans de mise en œuvre avec des tâches indépendantes et des revues en deux étapes","de":"Die subagenten-getriebene Entwicklung ist eine Technik, die Subagenten zur Ausführung von Implementierungsplänen mit unabhängigen Aufgaben und zweistufigen Überprüfungen verwendet","pt":"O desenvolvimento dirigido por subagentes é uma abordagem que executa planos por meio da criação de subagentes frescos para cada tarefa, com revisão em duas etapas","ru":"Подагент-ориентированное развитие - это подход, который выполняет планы путем создания свежих подагентов для каждой задачи, с двухэтапным обзором","ar":"التطوير الموجه بواسطة الوكلاء الفرعيين هو نهج يُنفّذ الخطط من خلال إنشاء وكلاء فرعيين mớiین لكل مهمة، مع استعراض على مرحلتين","en":"Use when executing implementation plans with independent tasks in the current session"},"owner":"obra","repo":"superpowers","repoPath":"obra/superpowers","stars":66125,"forks":5048,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T05:08:15Z","topics":[],"skillMd":{"name":"subagent-driven-development","description":"Use when executing implementation plans with independent tasks in the current session","bodyPreview":"# Subagent-Driven Development\n\nExecute plan by dispatching fresh subagent per task, with two-stage review after each: spec compliance review first, then code quality review.\n\n**Core principle:** Fresh subagent per task + two-stage review (spec then quality) = high quality, fast iteration\n\n## When to Use\n\n```dot\ndigraph when_to_use {\n    \"Have implementation plan?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Tasks mostly independent?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Stay in this session?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"subagent-driven-d","body":"# Subagent-Driven Development\n\nExecute plan by dispatching fresh subagent per task, with two-stage review after each: spec compliance review first, then code quality review.\n\n**Core principle:** Fresh subagent per task + two-stage review (spec then quality) = high quality, fast iteration\n\n## When to Use\n\n```dot\ndigraph when_to_use {\n    \"Have implementation plan?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Tasks mostly independent?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Stay in this session?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"subagent-driven-development\" [shape=box];\n    \"executing-plans\" [shape=box];\n    \"Manual execution or brainstorm first\" [shape=box];\n\n    \"Have implementation plan?\" -> \"Tasks mostly independent?\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Have implementation plan?\" -> \"Manual execution or brainstorm first\" [label=\"no\"];\n    \"Tasks mostly independent?\" -> \"Stay in this session?\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Tasks mostly independent?\" -> \"Manual execution or brainstorm first\" [label=\"no - tightly coupled\"];\n    \"Stay in this session?\" -> \"subagent-driven-development\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Stay in this session?\" -> \"executing-plans\" [label=\"no - parallel session\"];\n}\n```\n\n**vs. Executing Plans (parallel session):**\n- Same session (no context switch)\n- Fresh subagent per task (no context pollution)\n- Two-stage review after each task: spec compliance first, then code quality\n- Faster iteration (no human-in-loop between tasks)\n\n## The Process\n\n```dot\ndigraph process {\n    rankdir=TB;\n\n    subgraph cluster_per_task {\n        label=\"Per Task\";\n        \"Dispatch implementer subagent (./implementer-prompt.md)\" [shape=box];\n        \"Implementer subagent asks questions?\" [shape=diamond];\n        \"Answer questions, provide context\" [shape=box];\n        \"Implementer subagent implements, tests, commits, self-reviews\" [shape=box];\n        \"Dispatch spec reviewer subagent (./spec-reviewer-prompt.md)\" [shape=box];\n        \"Spec reviewer subagent confirms code matches spec?\" [shape=diamond];\n        \"Implementer subagent fixes spec gaps\" [shape=box];\n        \"Dispatch code quality reviewer subagent (./code-quality-reviewer-prompt.md)\" [shape=box];\n        \"Code quality reviewer subagent approves?\" [shape=diamond];\n        \"Implementer subagent fixes quality issues\" [shape=box];\n        \"Mark task complete in TodoWrite\" [shape=box];\n    }\n\n    \"Read plan, extract all tasks with full text, note context, create TodoWrite\" [shape=box];\n    \"More tasks remain?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Dispatch final code reviewer subagent for entire implementation\" [shape=box];\n    \"Use superpowers:finishing-a-development-branch\" [shape=box style=filled fillcolor=lightgreen];\n\n    \"Read plan, extract all tasks with full text, note context, create TodoWrite\" -> \"Dispatch implementer subagent (./implementer-prompt.md)\";\n    \"Dispatch implementer subagent (./implementer-prompt.md)\" -> \"Implementer subagent asks questions?\";\n    \"Implementer subagent asks questions?\" -> \"Answer questions, provide context\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Answer questions, provide context\" -> \"Dispatch implementer subagent (./implementer-prompt.md)\";\n    \"Implementer subagent asks questions?\" -> \"Implementer subagent implements, tests, commits, self-reviews\" [label=\"no\"];\n    \"Implementer subagent implements, tests, commits, self-reviews\" -> \"Dispatch spec reviewer subagent (./spec-reviewer-prompt.md)\";\n    \"Dispatch spec reviewer subagent (./spec-reviewer-prompt.md)\" -> \"Spec reviewer subagent confirms code matches spec?\";\n    \"Spec reviewer subagent confirms code matches spec?\" -> \"Implementer subagent fixes spec gaps\" [label=\"no\"];\n    \"Implementer subagent fixes spec gaps\" -> \"Dispatch spec reviewer subagent (./spec-reviewer-prompt.md)\" [label=\"re-review\"];\n    \"Spec reviewer subagent confirms code matches spec?\" -> \"Dispatch code quality reviewer subagent (./code-quality-reviewer-prompt.md)\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Dispatch code quality reviewer subagent (./code-quality-reviewer-prompt.md)\" -> \"Code quality reviewer subagent approves?\";\n    \"Code quality reviewer subagent approves?\" -> \"Implementer subagent fixes quality issues\" [label=\"no\"];\n    \"Implementer subagent fixes quality issues\" -> \"Dispatch code quality reviewer subagent (./code-quality-reviewer-prompt.md)\" [label=\"re-review\"];\n    \"Code quality reviewer subagent approves?\" -> \"Mark task complete in TodoWrite\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Mark task complete in TodoWrite\" -> \"More tasks remain?\";\n    \"More tasks remain?\" -> \"Dispatch implementer subagent (./implementer-prompt.md)\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"More tasks remain?\" -> \"Dispatch final code reviewer subagent for entire implementation\" [label=\"no\"];\n    \"Dispatch final code reviewer subagent for entire implementation\" -> \"Use superpowers:finishing-a-development-branch\";\n}\n```\n\n## Prompt Templates\n\n- `./implementer-prompt.md` - Dispatch implementer subagent\n- `./spec-reviewer-prompt.md` - Dispatch spec compliance reviewer subagent\n- `./code-quality-reviewer-prompt.md` - Dispatch code quality reviewer subagent\n\n## Example Workflow\n\n```\nYou: I''m using Subagent-Driven Development to execute this plan.\n\n[Read plan file once: docs/plans/feature-plan.md]\n[Extract all 5 tasks with full text and context]\n[Create TodoWrite with all tasks]\n\nTask 1: Hook installation script\n\n[Get Task 1 text and context (already extracted)]\n[Dispatch implementation subagent with full task text + context]\n\nImplementer: \"Before I begin - should the hook be installed at user or system level?\"\n\nYou: \"User level (~/.config/superpowers/hooks/)\"\n\nImplementer: \"Got it. Implementing now...\"\n[Later] Implementer:\n  - Implemented install-hook command\n  - Added tests, 5/5 passing\n  - Self-review: Found I missed --force flag, added it\n  - Committed\n\n[Dispatch spec compliance reviewer]\nSpec reviewer: ✅ Spec compliant - all requirements met, nothing extra\n\n[Get git SHAs, dispatch code quality reviewer]\nCode reviewer: Strengths: Good test coverage, clean. Issues: None. Approved.\n\n[Mark Task 1 complete]\n\nTask 2: Recovery modes\n\n[Get Task 2 text and context (already extracted)]\n[Dispatch implementation subagent with full task text + context]\n\nImplementer: [No questions, proceeds]\nImplementer:\n  - Added verify/repair modes\n  - 8/8 tests passing\n  - Self-review: All good\n  - Committed\n\n[Dispatch spec compliance reviewer]\nSpec reviewer: ❌ Issues:\n  - Missing: Progress reporting (spec says \"report every 100 items\")\n  - Extra: Added --json flag (not requested)\n\n[Implementer fixes issues]\nImplementer: Removed --json flag, added progress reporting\n\n[Spec reviewer reviews again]\nSpec reviewer: ✅ Spec compliant now\n\n[Dispatch code quality reviewer]\nCode reviewer: Strengths: Solid. Issues (Important): Magic number (100)\n\n[Implementer fixes]\nImplementer: Extracted PROGRESS_INTERVAL constant\n\n[Code reviewer reviews again]\nCode reviewer: ✅ Approved\n\n[Mark Task 2 complete]\n\n...\n\n[After all tasks]\n[Dispatch final code-reviewer]\nFinal reviewer: All requirements met, ready to merge\n\nDone!\n```\n\n## Advantages\n\n**vs. Manual execution:**\n- Subagents follow TDD naturally\n- Fresh context per task (no confusion)\n- Parallel-safe (subagents don''t interfere)\n- Subagent can ask questions (before AND during work)\n\n**vs. Executing Plans:**\n- Same session (no handoff)\n- Continuous progress (no waiting)\n- Review checkpoints automatic\n\n**Efficiency gains:**\n- No file reading overhead (controller provides full text)\n- Controller curates exactly what context is needed\n- Subagent gets complete information upfront\n- Questions surfaced before work begins (not after)\n\n**Quality gates:**\n- Self-review catches issues before handoff\n- Two-stage review: spec compliance, then code quality\n- Review loops ensure fixes actually work\n- Spec compliance prevents over/under-building\n- Code quality ensures implementation is well-built\n\n**Cost:**\n- More subagent invocations (implementer + 2 reviewers per task)\n- Controller does more prep work (extracting all tasks upfront)\n- Review loops add iterations\n- But catches issues early (cheaper than debugging later)\n\n## Red Flags\n\n**Never:**\n- Start implementation on main/master branch without explicit user consent\n- Skip reviews (spec compliance OR code quality)\n- Proceed with unfixed issues\n- Dispatch multiple implementation subagents in parallel (conflicts)\n- Make subagent read plan file (provide full text instead)\n- Skip scene-setting context (subagent needs to understand where task fits)\n- Ignore subagent questions (answer before letting them proceed)\n- Accept \"close enough\" on spec compliance (spec reviewer found issues = not done)\n- Skip review loops (reviewer found issues = implementer fixes = review again)\n- Let implementer self-review replace actual review (both are needed)\n- **Start code quality review before spec compliance is ✅** (wrong order)\n- Move to next task while either review has open issues\n\n**If subagent asks questions:**\n- Answer clearly and completely\n- Provide additional context if needed\n- Don''t rush them into implementation\n\n**If reviewer finds issues:**\n- Implementer (same subagent) fixes them\n- Reviewer reviews again\n- Repeat until approved\n- Don''t skip the re-review\n\n**If subagent fails task:**\n- Dispatch fix subagent with specific instructions\n- Don''t try to fix manually (context pollution)\n\n## Integration\n\n**Required workflow skills:**\n- **superpowers:using-git-worktrees** - REQUIRED: Set up isolated workspace before starting\n- **superpowers:writing-plans** - Creates the plan this skill executes\n- **superpowers:requesting-code-review** - Code review template for reviewer subagents\n- **superpowers:finishing-a-development-branch** - Complete development after all tasks\n\n**Subagents should use:**\n- **superpowers:test-driven-development** - Subagents follow TDD for each task\n\n**Alternative workflow:**\n- **superpowers:executing-plans** - Use for parallel session instead of same-session execution\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-03-01T05:08:48.273Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能代理：子代理驱动开发","ja":"AIエージェント：サブエージェント駆動開発","ko":"AI 에이전트: 서브 에이전트 주도 개발","es":"Desarrollo impulsado por subagentes: Herramientas de AI A...","fr":"Développement piloté par sous-agent: Outils d''Agent IA","de":"Subagenten-getriebene Entwicklung: AI-Tools für Entwickler","pt":"Ferramentas de IA: Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Subagentes","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Подагент-ориентированное развитие","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: التطوير الموجه بواسطة الوكلاء الف...","en":"subagent-driven-development"},"description":{"zh":"子代理驱动开发是一种使用独立任务的实现计划执行方法，通过两阶段审查确保高质量和快速迭代","ja":"サブエージェント駆動開発は、独立したタスクを持つ実装計画を実行する方法で、2段階のレビューを通じて高品質と迅速な反復を実現します","ko":"서브 에이전트 주도 개발은 독립적인 태스크를 사용하는 구현 계획을 실행하는 방법으로, 2단계의 검토를 통해 높은 품질과 빠른 반복을 실현합니다","es":"El desarrollo impulsado por subagentes es una técnica que utiliza subagentes para ejecutar planes de implementación con tareas independientes y revisiones de...","fr":"Le développement piloté par sous-agent est une technique qui utilise des sous-agents pour exécuter des plans de mise en œuvre avec des tâches indépendantes e...","de":"Die subagenten-getriebene Entwicklung ist eine Technik, die Subagenten zur Ausführung von Implementierungsplänen mit unabhängigen Aufgaben und zweistufigen Ü...","pt":"O desenvolvimento dirigido por subagentes é uma abordagem que executa planos por meio da criação de subagentes frescos para cada tarefa, com revisão em duas ...","ru":"Подагент-ориентированное развитие - это подход, который выполняет планы путем создания свежих подагентов для каждой задачи, с двухэтапным обзором","ar":"التطوير الموجه بواسطة الوكلاء الفرعيين هو نهج يُنفّذ الخطط من خلال إنشاء وكلاء فرعيين mớiین لكل مهمة، مع استعراض على مرحلتين","en":"Use when executing implementation plans with independent tasks in the current session"},"definition":{"en":"Use when executing implementation plans with independent tasks in the current session"},"features":{"zh":["使用子代理执行独立任务","两阶段审查：规范合规审查和代码质量审查","提高代码质量和迭代速度","适用于具有独立任务的实现计划","支持快速反复开发"],"ja":["サブエージェントを使用して独立したタスクを実行","2段階のレビュー：仕様の準拠レビューとコードの品質レビュー","コードの品質と反復のスピードを向上","独立したタスクを持つ実装計画に適しています","迅速な反復開発をサポート"],"ko":["서브 에이전트를 사용하여 독립적인 태스크를 실행","2단계의 검토：규격 준수 검토와 코드 품질 검토","코드 품질과 반복 속도를 향상","독립적인 태스크를 가진 구현 계획에 적합","빠른 반복 개발을 지원"],"es":["Ejecución de planes de implementación con tareas independientes","Uso de subagentes para cada tarea","Revisión de dos etapas: cumplimiento de especificaciones y calidad del código","Desarrollo rápido y de alta calidad","Integración con herramientas de desarrollo existentes"],"fr":["Exécution de plans de mise en œuvre avec des tâches indépendantes","Utilisation de sous-agents pour chaque tâche","Revues en deux étapes : conformité aux spécifications et qualité du code","Développement rapide et de haute qualité","Intégration avec des outils de développement existants"],"de":["Ausführung von Implementierungsplänen mit unabhängigen Aufgaben","Verwendung von Subagenten für jede Aufgabe","Zweistufige Überprüfung: Einhaltung von Spezifikationen und Code-Qualität","Schnelle und hochwertige Entwicklung","Integration mit bestehenden Entwicklungstools"],"pt":["Execução de planos com tarefas independentes","Criação de subagentes frescos para cada tarefa","Revisão em duas etapas: conformidade com especificações e qualidade do código","Melhoria da qualidade e velocidade de iteração","Integração com implementação de planos na sessão atual"],"ru":["Выполнение планов с независимыми задачами","Создание свежих подагентов для каждой задачи","Двухэтапный обзор: соответствие спецификациям и качество кода","Повышение качества и скорости итерации","Интеграция с реализацией планов в текущей сессии"],"ar":["تنفيذ الخطط مع المهام المستقلة","إنشاء وكلاء فرعيين جدیدین لكل مهمة","استعراض على مرحلتين: مطابقة للمواصفات و جودة الكود","تحسين الجودة و سرعة التكرار","التكامل مع تنفيذ الخطط في الجلسة الحالية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","子代理驱动开发","软件开发方法","独立任务","两阶段审查","代码质量","迭代速度"],"ja":["AIエージェント","サブエージェント駆動開発","ソフトウェア開発方法","独立したタスク","2段階のレビュー","コードの品質","反復のスピード"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","서브 에이전트 주도 개발","소프트웨어 개발 방법","독립적인 태스크","2단계의 검토","코드 품질","반복 속도"],"es":["desarrollo impulsado por subagentes","herramientas de AI Agent","desarrollo de software","tareas independientes","revisiones de dos etapas","desarrollo rápido","alta calidad"],"fr":["développement piloté par sous-agent","outils d''Agent IA","développement de logiciels","tâches indépendantes","revues en deux étapes","développement rapide","haute qualité"],"de":["subagenten-getriebene Entwicklung","AI-Tools","Software-Entwicklung","unabhängige Aufgaben","zweistufige Überprüfung","schnelle Entwicklung","hochwertige Entwicklung"],"pt":["desenvolvimento dirigido por subagentes","ferramentas de ia","execução de planos","tarefas independentes","subagentes","revisão em duas etapas","qualidade do código","velocidade de iteração"],"ru":["подагент-ориентированное развитие","ии агенты","выполнение планов","независимые задачи","подагенты","двухэтапный обзор","качество кода","скорость итерации"],"ar":["تطوير موجه بواسطة الوكلاء الفرعيين","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","تنفيذ الخطط","مهام مستقلة","وكلاء فرعيين","استعراض على مرحلتين","جودة الكود","سرعة التكرار"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Autonomous Agents requiring rapid task execution and high-quality output through independent subagent dispatching and two-stage review processes.","zh":"适用于需要快速任务执行和高质量输出的自主代理，通过独立的子代理调度和双阶段审查过程。","ja":"自己完結型エージェントが迅速なタスク実行と高品質の出力が必要な場合に適しています。独立したサブエージェントの派遣と二段階のレビュー処理を通じて実現します。","ko":"신속한 작업 실행과 독립적 子エージェント 派遣 및 이중 검토 프로세스를 통해 고품질 출력이 필요한 자율 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes Autónomos que requieren ejecución de tareas rápida y salida de alta calidad a través de la expedición de subagentes independientes y procesos de revisión de dos etapas.","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents Autonomes nécessitant une exécution de tâches rapide et une sortie de haute qualité grâce à l''expédition de sous-agents indépendants et des processus de révision en deux étapes.","de":"Ideal für autonome Agenten, die eine schnelle Aufgabenausführung und eine hohe Ausgabequalität durch die Entsendung unabhängiger Subagenten und zweistufige Überprüfungsprozesse erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes Autônomos que requerem execução rápida de tarefas e saída de alta qualidade por meio de despacho de subagentes independentes e processos de revisão em duas etapas.","ru":"Идеально подходит для автономных агентов, требующих быстрой выполнения задач и высококачественного вывода через независимый подагентский диспетчер и двухэтапные процессы проверки.","ar":"مثالي لعميل tự trị يتطلب تنفيذ任务 سريعًا وإخراج عالي الجودة من خلال إرسال وكلاء فرعيين مستقلين وعمليات مراجعة على مرحلتين."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to execute implementation plans efficiently by dispatching fresh subagents per task, leveraging spec compliance reviews and code quality assessments for optimal results, utilizing two-stage review protocols for enhanced quality control.","zh":"赋予代理执行实现计划的能力，通过为每个任务派遣新的子代理，利用规范合规性审查和代码质量评估以获得最佳结果，并利用双阶段审查协议增强质量控制。","ja":"実装計画を効率的に実行できるエージェントを実現します。各タスクに新しいサブエージェントを派遣し、仕様準拠レビューとコード品質評価を利用して最適な結果を得て、双段階レビューのプロトコルを使用して品質管理を強化します。","ko":"에이전트가 효율적으로 구현 계획을 실행할 수 있도록 합니다. 각 작업에 새로운 子エージェント를 배치하고, 사양 준수 리뷰 및 코드 품질 평가를 활용하여 최적의 결과를 얻고, 2단계 리뷰 프로토콜을 사용하여 품질 제어를 향상시킵니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a ejecutar planes de implementación de manera eficiente mediante la expedición de subagentes frescos por tarea, aprovechando las revisiones de cumplimiento de especificaciones y las evaluaciones de calidad del código para obtener resultados óptimos, utilizando protocolos de revisión de dos etapas para un control de calidad mejorado.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exécuter des plans d''implémentation de manière efficace en expédiant des sous-agents frais par tâche, en exploitant les révisions de conformité aux spécifications et les évaluations de la qualité du code pour obtenir des résultats optimaux, en utilisant des protocoles de révision en deux étapes pour un contrôle de qualité amélioré.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, Implementierungspläne effizient auszuführen, indem sie für jede Aufgabe frische Subagenten entsenden, wobei sie Überprüfungen der Spezifikationskonformität und Codequalitätsbewertungen für optimale Ergebnisse nutzen und zweistufige Überprüfungsprotokolle für eine verbesserte Qualitätskontrolle verwenden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a executar planos de implementação de forma eficiente, despachando novos subagentes por tarefa, aproveitando revisões de conformidade de especificações e avaliações de qualidade de código para resultados ótimos, utilizando protocolos de revisão em duas etapas para controle de qualidade aprimorado.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выполнять планы реализации эффективно, диспетчеризируя свежих подагентов на каждую задачу, используя проверки соответствия спецификации и оценки качества кода для оптимальных результатов, используя двухэтапные протоколы проверки для повышения контроля качества.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تنفيذ خطط التنفيذ بفعالية، من خلال إرسال وكلاء فرعيين جدد لكل مهمة، و利用 مراجعات مطابقة للمواصفات وتقييمات جودة الشفرة للحصول على نتائج مثالية، واستخدام بروتوكولات المراجعة على مرحلتين لتحسين ضبط الجودة."},"useCases":{"en":["Dispatching subagents for independent task execution","Implementing two-stage review processes for quality assurance","Enhancing development speed through parallel subagent tasking"],"zh":["为独立任务执行派遣子代理","实施双阶段审查过程以确保质量","通过并行子代理任务加速开发速度"],"ja":["独立したタスク実行のためのサブエージェントの派遣","品質保証のための二段階のレビュー処理の実施","並列サブエージェントのタスクを通じて開発速度の向上"],"ko":["독립적 작업 실행을 위한 子エージェント 派遣","품질 보증을 위한 2단계 검토 프로세스 구현","병렬 子エージェント 작업을 통한 개발 속도 향상"],"es":["Expedición de subagentes para la ejecución de tareas independientes","Implementación de procesos de revisión de dos etapas para la garantía de calidad"," Mejora de la velocidad de desarrollo a través de la ejecución de tareas de subagentes paralelos"],"fr":["Expedition de sous-agents pour l''exécution de tâches indépendantes","Mise en œuvre de processus de révision en deux étapes pour l''assurance de la qualité","Amélioration de la vitesse de développement grâce à la tâche parallèle des sous-agents"],"de":["Entsendung von Subagenten für die unabhängige Aufgabenausführung","Implementierung von zweistufigen Überprüfungsprozessen für die Qualitätsicherung","Verbesserung der Entwicklungszeit durch paralleles Arbeiten von Subagenten"],"pt":["Despachar subagentes para execução de tarefas independentes","Implementar processos de revisão em duas etapas para garantia de qualidade","Aumentar a velocidade de desenvolvimento por meio de tarefas de subagentes paralelas"],"ru":["Диспетчеризация подагентов для независимого выполнения задач","Реализация двухэтапных процессов проверки для обеспечения качества","Ускорение разработки за счет параллельного задания подагентов"],"ar":["إرسال وكلاء فرعيين لتنفيذ المهام المستقلة","تطبيق عمليات المراجعة على مرحلتين لتأمين الجودة","تعزيز سرعة التطوير من خلال مهام وكلاء فرعيين متوازية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires ability to dispatch and manage subagents","Dependent on current session stability for optimal performance"],"zh":["需要能够派遣和管理子代理","依赖于当前会话的稳定性以获得最佳性能"],"ja":["サブエージェントを派遣および管理する能力が必要","最適なパフォーマンスを得るために現在のセッションの安定性に依存する"],"ko":["子エージェント를派遣 및 관리할 수 있는 능력이 필요","최적의 성능을 얻기 위해 현재 세션의 안정성에 의존"],"es":["Requiere la capacidad de expedir y gestionar subagentes","Depende de la estabilidad de la sesión actual para un rendimiento óptimo"],"fr":["Nécessite la capacité d''expédier et de gérer des sous-agents","Dépend de la stabilité de la session actuelle pour des performances optimales"],"de":["Benötigt die Fähigkeit, Subagenten zu entsenden und zu verwalten","Hängt von der Stabilität der aktuellen Sitzung für optimale Leistung ab"],"pt":["Requer a capacidade de despachar e gerenciar subagentes","Depende da estabilidade da sessão atual para desempenho ótimo"],"ru":["Требует возможности диспетчеризации и управления подагентами","Зависит от стабильности текущей сессии для оптимальной производительности"],"ar":["يتطلب القدرة على إرسال وكلاء فرعيين وإدارتهم","يعتمد على استقرار الجلسة الحالية для الأداء الأمثل"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"994b89a5d294eadd6a1611edb51377bac748d5f5fb7f4139d3c736b616b3a46a","repoEtag":"W/\"c0159b000a3f1065b2a623072c2f281d1dae59e39bce28acebe789d1e6a6aa8e\"","qualityScore":86}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('obra/superpowers/systematic-debugging', 'official', 'obra', 'superpowers', 'obra/superpowers', 'systematic-debugging', 66125, 5048, 86, '2026-03-01T05:08:15Z', '2026-03-01T05:08:48.325Z', '4999cb851360485eca5074e727bbdd62ef20549c5d5b01216fcbf5831badb473', '{"id":"obra/superpowers/systematic-debugging","name":"systematic-debugging","description":{"zh":"系统性调试是一种找出问题根源的方法，避免随机修复和掩盖潜在问题","ja":"体系的デバッグは根本原因を特定する方法で、ランダムな修正と潜在的な問題のマスキングを避ける","ko":"체계적인 디버깅은 문제의根本 원인을 찾는 방법으로 임의의 수정과 잠재적인 문제의 숨김을 피하는 것","es":"Depuración sistemática para identificar y solucionar problemas de forma efectiva con Agentes de IA","fr":"Débogage systématique pour identifier et résoudre les problèmes de manière efficace avec les Agents d''IA","de":"Systematische Fehlersuche, um Probleme effektiv mit KI-Agents zu identifizieren und zu lösen","pt":"Depuração sistemática é uma abordagem para encontrar a causa raiz de bugs e falhas de teste antes de propor soluções","ru":"Системная отладка - это подход к нахождению коренной причины багов и сбоев тестирования перед предложением исправлений","ar":"فحص المنهجية هو نهج للعثور على السبب الجذري للأخطاء واخفاقات الاختبار قبل اقتراح الإصلاحات","en":"Use when encountering any bug, test failure, or unexpected behavior, before proposing fixes"},"owner":"obra","repo":"superpowers","repoPath":"obra/superpowers","stars":66125,"forks":5048,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T05:08:15Z","topics":[],"skillMd":{"name":"systematic-debugging","description":"Use when encountering any bug, test failure, or unexpected behavior, before proposing fixes","bodyPreview":"# Systematic Debugging\n\n## Overview\n\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Quick patches mask underlying issues.\n\n**Core principle:** ALWAYS find root cause before attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n\n**Violating the letter of this process is violating the spirit of debugging.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST\n```\n\nIf you haven''t completed Phase 1, you cannot propose fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse for ANY technical issue:\n- Test failures\n- Bugs","body":"# Systematic Debugging\n\n## Overview\n\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Quick patches mask underlying issues.\n\n**Core principle:** ALWAYS find root cause before attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n\n**Violating the letter of this process is violating the spirit of debugging.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST\n```\n\nIf you haven''t completed Phase 1, you cannot propose fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse for ANY technical issue:\n- Test failures\n- Bugs in production\n- Unexpected behavior\n- Performance problems\n- Build failures\n- Integration issues\n\n**Use this ESPECIALLY when:**\n- Under time pressure (emergencies make guessing tempting)\n- \"Just one quick fix\" seems obvious\n- You''ve already tried multiple fixes\n- Previous fix didn''t work\n- You don''t fully understand the issue\n\n**Don''t skip when:**\n- Issue seems simple (simple bugs have root causes too)\n- You''re in a hurry (rushing guarantees rework)\n- Manager wants it fixed NOW (systematic is faster than thrashing)\n\n## The Four Phases\n\nYou MUST complete each phase before proceeding to the next.\n\n### Phase 1: Root Cause Investigation\n\n**BEFORE attempting ANY fix:**\n\n1. **Read Error Messages Carefully**\n   - Don''t skip past errors or warnings\n   - They often contain the exact solution\n   - Read stack traces completely\n   - Note line numbers, file paths, error codes\n\n2. **Reproduce Consistently**\n   - Can you trigger it reliably?\n   - What are the exact steps?\n   - Does it happen every time?\n   - If not reproducible → gather more data, don''t guess\n\n3. **Check Recent Changes**\n   - What changed that could cause this?\n   - Git diff, recent commits\n   - New dependencies, config changes\n   - Environmental differences\n\n4. **Gather Evidence in Multi-Component Systems**\n\n   **WHEN system has multiple components (CI → build → signing, API → service → database):**\n\n   **BEFORE proposing fixes, add diagnostic instrumentation:**\n   ```\n   For EACH component boundary:\n     - Log what data enters component\n     - Log what data exits component\n     - Verify environment/config propagation\n     - Check state at each layer\n\n   Run once to gather evidence showing WHERE it breaks\n   THEN analyze evidence to identify failing component\n   THEN investigate that specific component\n   ```\n\n   **Example (multi-layer system):**\n   ```bash\n   # Layer 1: Workflow\n   echo \"=== Secrets available in workflow: ===\"\n   echo \"IDENTITY: ${IDENTITY:+SET}${IDENTITY:-UNSET}\"\n\n   # Layer 2: Build script\n   echo \"=== Env vars in build script: ===\"\n   env | grep IDENTITY || echo \"IDENTITY not in environment\"\n\n   # Layer 3: Signing script\n   echo \"=== Keychain state: ===\"\n   security list-keychains\n   security find-identity -v\n\n   # Layer 4: Actual signing\n   codesign --sign \"$IDENTITY\" --verbose=4 \"$APP\"\n   ```\n\n   **This reveals:** Which layer fails (secrets → workflow ✓, workflow → build ✗)\n\n5. **Trace Data Flow**\n\n   **WHEN error is deep in call stack:**\n\n   See `root-cause-tracing.md` in this directory for the complete backward tracing technique.\n\n   **Quick version:**\n   - Where does bad value originate?\n   - What called this with bad value?\n   - Keep tracing up until you find the source\n   - Fix at source, not at symptom\n\n### Phase 2: Pattern Analysis\n\n**Find the pattern before fixing:**\n\n1. **Find Working Examples**\n   - Locate similar working code in same codebase\n   - What works that''s similar to what''s broken?\n\n2. **Compare Against References**\n   - If implementing pattern, read reference implementation COMPLETELY\n   - Don''t skim - read every line\n   - Understand the pattern fully before applying\n\n3. **Identify Differences**\n   - What''s different between working and broken?\n   - List every difference, however small\n   - Don''t assume \"that can''t matter\"\n\n4. **Understand Dependencies**\n   - What other components does this need?\n   - What settings, config, environment?\n   - What assumptions does it make?\n\n### Phase 3: Hypothesis and Testing\n\n**Scientific method:**\n\n1. **Form Single Hypothesis**\n   - State clearly: \"I think X is the root cause because Y\"\n   - Write it down\n   - Be specific, not vague\n\n2. **Test Minimally**\n   - Make the SMALLEST possible change to test hypothesis\n   - One variable at a time\n   - Don''t fix multiple things at once\n\n3. **Verify Before Continuing**\n   - Did it work? Yes → Phase 4\n   - Didn''t work? Form NEW hypothesis\n   - DON''T add more fixes on top\n\n4. **When You Don''t Know**\n   - Say \"I don''t understand X\"\n   - Don''t pretend to know\n   - Ask for help\n   - Research more\n\n### Phase 4: Implementation\n\n**Fix the root cause, not the symptom:**\n\n1. **Create Failing Test Case**\n   - Simplest possible reproduction\n   - Automated test if possible\n   - One-off test script if no framework\n   - MUST have before fixing\n   - Use the `superpowers:test-driven-development` skill for writing proper failing tests\n\n2. **Implement Single Fix**\n   - Address the root cause identified\n   - ONE change at a time\n   - No \"while I''m here\" improvements\n   - No bundled refactoring\n\n3. **Verify Fix**\n   - Test passes now?\n   - No other tests broken?\n   - Issue actually resolved?\n\n4. **If Fix Doesn''t Work**\n   - STOP\n   - Count: How many fixes have you tried?\n   - If < 3: Return to Phase 1, re-analyze with new information\n   - **If ≥ 3: STOP and question the architecture (step 5 below)**\n   - DON''T attempt Fix #4 without architectural discussion\n\n5. **If 3+ Fixes Failed: Question Architecture**\n\n   **Pattern indicating architectural problem:**\n   - Each fix reveals new shared state/coupling/problem in different place\n   - Fixes require \"massive refactoring\" to implement\n   - Each fix creates new symptoms elsewhere\n\n   **STOP and question fundamentals:**\n   - Is this pattern fundamentally sound?\n   - Are we \"sticking with it through sheer inertia\"?\n   - Should we refactor architecture vs. continue fixing symptoms?\n\n   **Discuss with your human partner before attempting more fixes**\n\n   This is NOT a failed hypothesis - this is a wrong architecture.\n\n## Red Flags - STOP and Follow Process\n\nIf you catch yourself thinking:\n- \"Quick fix for now, investigate later\"\n- \"Just try changing X and see if it works\"\n- \"Add multiple changes, run tests\"\n- \"Skip the test, I''ll manually verify\"\n- \"It''s probably X, let me fix that\"\n- \"I don''t fully understand but this might work\"\n- \"Pattern says X but I''ll adapt it differently\"\n- \"Here are the main problems: [lists fixes without investigation]\"\n- Proposing solutions before tracing data flow\n- **\"One more fix attempt\" (when already tried 2+)**\n- **Each fix reveals new problem in different place**\n\n**ALL of these mean: STOP. Return to Phase 1.**\n\n**If 3+ fixes failed:** Question the architecture (see Phase 4.5)\n\n## your human partner''s Signals You''re Doing It Wrong\n\n**Watch for these redirections:**\n- \"Is that not happening?\" - You assumed without verifying\n- \"Will it show us...?\" - You should have added evidence gathering\n- \"Stop guessing\" - You''re proposing fixes without understanding\n- \"Ultrathink this\" - Question fundamentals, not just symptoms\n- \"We''re stuck?\" (frustrated) - Your approach isn''t working\n\n**When you see these:** STOP. Return to Phase 1.\n\n## Common Rationalizations\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Issue is simple, don''t need process\" | Simple issues have root causes too. Process is fast for simple bugs. |\n| \"Emergency, no time for process\" | Systematic debugging is FASTER than guess-and-check thrashing. |\n| \"Just try this first, then investigate\" | First fix sets the pattern. Do it right from the start. |\n| \"I''ll write test after confirming fix works\" | Untested fixes don''t stick. Test first proves it. |\n| \"Multiple fixes at once saves time\" | Can''t isolate what worked. Causes new bugs. |\n| \"Reference too long, I''ll adapt the pattern\" | Partial understanding guarantees bugs. Read it completely. |\n| \"I see the problem, let me fix it\" | Seeing symptoms ≠ understanding root cause. |\n| \"One more fix attempt\" (after 2+ failures) | 3+ failures = architectural problem. Question pattern, don''t fix again. |\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Phase | Key Activities | Success Criteria |\n|-------|---------------|------------------|\n| **1. Root Cause** | Read errors, reproduce, check changes, gather evidence | Understand WHAT and WHY |\n| **2. Pattern** | Find working examples, compare | Identify differences |\n| **3. Hypothesis** | Form theory, test minimally | Confirmed or new hypothesis |\n| **4. Implementation** | Create test, fix, verify | Bug resolved, tests pass |\n\n## When Process Reveals \"No Root Cause\"\n\nIf systematic investigation reveals issue is truly environmental, timing-dependent, or external:\n\n1. You''ve completed the process\n2. Document what you investigated\n3. Implement appropriate handling (retry, timeout, error message)\n4. Add monitoring/logging for future investigation\n\n**But:** 95% of \"no root cause\" cases are incomplete investigation.\n\n## Supporting Techniques\n\nThese techniques are part of systematic debugging and available in this directory:\n\n- **`root-cause-tracing.md`** - Trace bugs backward through call stack to find original trigger\n- **`defense-in-depth.md`** - Add validation at multiple layers after finding root cause\n- **`condition-based-waiting.md`** - Replace arbitrary timeouts with condition polling\n\n**Related skills:**\n- **superpowers:test-driven-development** - For creating failing test case (Phase 4, Step 1)\n- **superpowers:verification-before-completion** - Verify fix worked before claiming success\n\n## Real-World Impact\n\nFrom debugging sessions:\n- Systematic approach: 15-30 minutes to fix\n- Random fixes approach: 2-3 hours of thrashing\n- First-time fix rate: 95% vs 40%\n- New bugs introduced: Near zero vs common\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-03-01T05:08:48.325Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI工具：系统性调试技术","ja":"AIエージェント：体系的デバッグ手法","ko":"AI 에이전트: 체계적인 디버깅 방법","es":"Herramientas de depuración sistemática de Agentes de IA","fr":"Outils de débogage systématique pour les Agents d''IA","de":"Systematische Debugging-Tools für KI-Agents","pt":"Ferramentas de Depuração Sistemática para Agentes de IA","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Системная отладка для разработчиков","ar":"أدوات فحص منهجية لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي","en":"systematic-debugging"},"description":{"zh":"系统性调试是一种找出问题根源的方法，避免随机修复和掩盖潜在问题","ja":"体系的デバッグは根本原因を特定する方法で、ランダムな修正と潜在的な問題のマスキングを避ける","ko":"체계적인 디버깅은 문제의根本 원인을 찾는 방법으로 임의의 수정과 잠재적인 문제의 숨김을 피하는 것","es":"Depuración sistemática para identificar y solucionar problemas de forma efectiva con Agentes de IA","fr":"Débogage systématique pour identifier et résoudre les problèmes de manière efficace avec les Agents d''IA","de":"Systematische Fehlersuche, um Probleme effektiv mit KI-Agents zu identifizieren und zu lösen","pt":"Depuração sistemática é uma abordagem para encontrar a causa raiz de bugs e falhas de teste antes de propor soluções","ru":"Системная отладка - это подход к нахождению коренной причины багов и сбоев тестирования перед предложением исправлений","ar":"فحص المنهجية هو نهج للعثور على السبب الجذري للأخطاء واخفاقات الاختبار قبل اقتراح الإصلاحات","en":"Use when encountering any bug, test failure, or unexpected behavior, before proposing fixes"},"definition":{"en":"Use when encountering any bug, test failure, or unexpected behavior, before proposing fixes"},"features":{"zh":["找出问题根源","避免随机修复","提高调试效率","减少新问题的产生","确保代码质量"],"ja":["根本原因の特定","ランダムな修正の回避","デバッグ効率の向上","新たな問題の発生抑制","コード品質の確保"],"ko":["기본 원인 식별","임의 수정 회피","디버깅 효율성 향상","새로운 문제 발생 억제","코드 품질 보장"],"es":["Identificación de la causa raíz de los problemas","Evitación de soluciones rápidas que ocultan problemas subyacentes","Depuración sistemática para test failures y bugs","Aplicación de la Ley de Hierro: NO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST","Uso de Agentes de IA para mejorar la eficiencia en la depuración"],"fr":["Identification de la cause profonde des problèmes","Évitement des solutions rapides qui masquent les problèmes sous-jacents","Débogage systématique pour les test failures et les bugs","Application de la Loi de Fer : NO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST","Utilisation des Agents d''IA pour améliorer l''efficacité dans la débogage"],"de":["Identifizierung der Ursache von Problemen","Vermeidung von schnellen Lösungen, die zugrunde liegende Probleme verbergen","Systematische Fehlersuche für Testfehler und Bugs","Anwendung des Eisernen Gesetzes: NO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST","Verwendung von KI-Agents, um die Effizienz bei der Fehlersuche zu verbessern"],"pt":["Encontre a causa raiz de bugs e falhas de teste","Evite soluções rápidas que mascaram problemas subjacentes","Use a abordagem sistemática para depurar problemas","Não proponha soluções sem investigar a causa raiz","Aprenda a depurar de forma eficaz com nossas ferramentas de IA"],"ru":["Найти коренную причину багов и сбоев тестирования","Избегайте быстрых исправлений, которые маскируют основные проблемы","Используйте системный подход для отладки проблем","Не предлагайте исправления без расследования коренной причины","Узнайте, как эффективно отлаживать с помощью наших ИИ Агентов"],"ar":["ابحث عن السبب الجذري للأخطاء واخفاقات الاختبار","تجنب الإصلاحات السريعة التي تخفي المشكلات الكامنة","استخدم النهج المنهجي لفحص المشكلات","لا تقترح الإصلاحات دون تحقیق السبب الجذري","تعلم كيفية فحص بطريقة فعالة باستخدام أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI工具","系统性调试","代码调试","问题根源","随机修复","代码质量"],"ja":["AIエージェント","体系的デバッグ","コードデバッグ","根本原因","ランダムな修正","コード品質"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","체계적인 디버깅","코드 디버깅","기본 원인","임의 수정","코드 품질"],"es":["depuración sistemática","Agentes de IA","Herramientas de depuración","test failures","bugs","causa raíz","Ley de Hierro","desarrollo de software","ingeniería de software"],"fr":["débogage systématique","Agents d''IA","Outils de débogage","test failures","bugs","cause profonde","Loi de Fer","développement de logiciels","ingénierie de logiciels"],"de":["systematische Fehlersuche","KI-Agents","Fehlersuchtools","Testfehler","Bugs","Ursache","Eisernes Gesetz","Softwareentwicklung","Softwareingenieurwesen"],"pt":["depuração sistemática","ferramentas de IA","agentes de IA","resolução de problemas","causa raiz","bugs","falhas de teste","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["системная отладка","ИИ Агенты","инструменты ИИ","решение проблем","коренная причина","баги","сбои тестирования","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["فحص منهجي","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","عميل الذكاء الاصطناعي","حل المشكلات","السبب الجذري","الأخطاء","اخفاقات الاختبار","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Advanced Debugging Agents requiring methodical issue resolution and root cause analysis","zh":"适用于需要系统性问题解决和根本原因分析的高级调试代理","ja":"体系的な問題解決と根本原因分析を必要とする高度なデバッグ エージェントに適しています","ko":"체계적인 문제 해결과根本적인 원인 분석이 필요한 고급 디버깅 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Depuración Avanzada que requieren una resolución de problemas metódica y análisis de causa raíz","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents de Débogage Avancé nécessitant une résolution méthodique des problèmes et une analyse de cause racine","de":"Ideal für erweiterte Debugging-Agents, die eine methodische Fehlerbehebung und eine Root-Cause-Analyse erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Depuração Avançada que requerem resolução metódica de problemas e análise de causa raiz","ru":"Идеально для продвинутых агентов отладки, требующих методического решения проблем и анализа коренной причины","ar":"مثالي لعميل تصحيح متقدم يتطلب حلًا منهجيًا للمشكلات وتحليل السبب الجذري"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to systematically investigate test failures and bugs, ensuring thorough root cause investigation before proposing fixes, adhering to the Iron Law of NO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST","zh":"使代理能够系统地调查测试失败和错误，确保在提出修复之前进行彻底的根本原因调查，遵循没有根本原因调查就不修复的铁律","ja":"エージェントがテストの失敗やバグを体系的に調査し、根本原因の調査を徹底してから修復を提案することを保証し、根本原因の調査を行わない修復は行わないという鉄則に従う","ko":"에이전트가 테스트 실패와 버그를 체계적으로 조사하고, 수정을 제안하기 전에 철저한根本적인 원인 분석을 수행하여, 근본적인 원인 분석 없이 수정을 하지 않는다는 철칙을 준수하도록 합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a investigar sistemáticamente las fallas de prueba y los errores, garantizando una investigación exhaustiva de la causa raíz antes de proponer soluciones, siguiendo la Ley de Hierro de NO SOLUCIONES SIN INVESTIGACIÓN DE CAUSA RAÍZ PRIMERO","fr":"Permet aux agents d''enquêter systématiquement sur les défaillances de test et les bogues, en garantissant une investigation approfondie de la cause racine avant de proposer des correctifs, en suivant la Loi de Fer de PAS DE CORRECTIFS SANS INVESTIGATION DE CAUSE RACINE D''ABORD","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Testfehler und Fehler systematisch zu untersuchen und eine gründliche Root-Cause-Untersuchung durchzuführen, bevor sie Lösungen vorschlagen, unter Einhaltung des Eisernen Gesetzes von KEINE LÖSUNGEN OHNE ROOT-CAUSE-UNTERSUCHUNG ZUERST","pt":"Habilita os agentes a investigar sistematicamente as falhas de teste e bugs, garantindo uma investigação minuciosa da causa raiz antes de propor correções, aderindo à Lei de Ferro de NENHUMA CORREÇÃO SEM INVESTIGAÇÃO DA CAUSA RAIZ EM PRIMEIRO LUGAR","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью систематически расследовать сбой тестов и ошибки, обеспечивая тщательное расследование коренной причины до предложения исправлений, придерживаясь Железного Закона НЕТ ИСПРАВЛЕНИЙ БЕЗ РАССЛЕДОВАНИЯ КОРЕННОЙ ПРИЧИНЫ СНАЧАЛА","ar":"تمكّن العميل من التحقيق المنهجي في فشل الاختبار والعيوب، مما يضمن التحقيق الشامل في السبب الجذري قبل اقتراح الإصلاحات، والالتزام بقانون الحديد لا إصلاح بدون تحقيق السبب الجذري أولاً"},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging complex test failures","Investigating unexpected behavior in code","Conducting thorough root cause analysis for bugs"],"zh":["调试复杂的测试失败","调查代码中的意外行为","进行彻底的根本原因分析以查找错误"],"ja":["複雑なテストの失敗のデバッグ","コード内の予期せぬ動作の調査","バグの根本原因の徹底的な分析の実施"],"ko":["복잡한 테스트 실패의 디버깅","코드 내의 예기치 않은 동작 조사","버그의 근본적인 원인의 철저한 분석 수행"],"es":["Depuración de fallas de prueba complejas","Investigación de comportamiento inesperado en el código","Realización de un análisis exhaustivo de causa raíz para errores"],"fr":["Débogage de défaillances de test complexes","Enquête sur un comportement inattendu dans le code","Réalisations d''une analyse approfondie de cause racine pour les bogues"],"de":["Fehlersuche bei komplexen Testfehlern","Untersuchung unerwarteten Verhaltens im Code","Durchführung einer gründlichen Root-Cause-Analyse für Fehler"],"pt":["Depuração de falhas de teste complexas","Investigação de comportamento inesperado no código","Realização de uma análise minuciosa da causa raiz para bugs"],"ru":["Отладка сложных сбоев тестов","Расследование неожиданного поведения кода","Проведение тщательного анализа коренной причины для ошибок"],"ar":["تصحيح فشل الاختبار المعقد","تحقيق سلوك غير متوقع في الكود","إجراء تحليل شامل للسبب الجذري للعيوب"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires strict adherence to the systematic debugging process","Violating the process may lead to incomplete or inaccurate fixes"],"zh":["需要严格遵守系统的调试过程","违反该过程可能导致不完整或不准确的修复"],"ja":["体系的なデバッグ プロセスに厳格に従う必要がある","このプロセスに違反すると、不完全または不正確な修復につながる可能性がある"],"ko":["체계적인 디버깅 프로세스에 엄격히 따라야 함","이 프로세스를 위반하면 불완전 또는 부정確한 수정으로 이어질 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere una estricta adhesión al proceso de depuración sistemática","Violación del proceso puede llevar a soluciones incompletas o inexactas"],"fr":["Nécessite une stricte adhésion au processus de débogage systématique","La violation du processus peut conduire à des correctifs incomplets ou inexacts"],"de":["Erfordert eine strikte Einhaltung des systematischen Fehlersuchprozesses","Verletzung des Prozesses kann zu unvollständigen oder ungenauen Lösungen führen"],"pt":["Exige adesão estrita ao processo de depuração sistemático","Violar o processo pode levar a correções incompletas ou imprecisas"],"ru":["Требует строгого соблюдения систематического процесса отладки","Нарушение процесса может привести к неполному или неточному исправлению"],"ar":["يتطلب الالتزام الصارم بالعمليات التصحيحية المنهجية","الانتهاك العملية قد يؤدي إلى إصلاحات غير كاملة أو غير دقيقة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"4999cb851360485eca5074e727bbdd62ef20549c5d5b01216fcbf5831badb473","repoEtag":"W/\"c0159b000a3f1065b2a623072c2f281d1dae59e39bce28acebe789d1e6a6aa8e\"","qualityScore":86}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('affaan-m/everything-claude-code/backend-patterns', 'official', 'affaan-m', 'everything-claude-code', 'affaan-m/everything-claude-code', 'backend-patterns', 55024, 6781, 86, '2026-03-01T05:07:39Z', '2026-03-01T05:09:14.180Z', '681c33b4e125860295ca2639083cba524c77261e81efd67a3ce30b75593e7512', '{"id":"affaan-m/everything-claude-code/backend-patterns","name":"backend-patterns","description":{"zh":"后端开发模式，包括REST和GraphQL API设计、数据库优化和服务器端最佳实践","ja":"バックエンド開発パターン、RESTとGraphQL API設計、データベース最適化、サーバーサイドのベストプラクティス","ko":"백엔드 개발 패턴, REST와 GraphQL API 설계, 데이터베이스 최적화, 서버사이드의 베스트 프랙티스","es":"Patrones de backend para aplicaciones server-side escalables con Node.js, Express y Next.js","fr":"Modèles de backend pour des applications serveur évolutives avec Node.js, Express et Next.js","de":"Backend-Muster für skalierbare Server-Anwendungen mit Node.js, Express und Next.js","pt":"Padrões de desenvolvimento backend para aplicações escaláveis com Node.js, Express e Next.js","ru":"Шаблоны backend-разработки для масштабируемых приложений с Node.js, Express и Next.js","ar":"نماذج التطوير الخلفي لبرامج قابلة للتوسيع مع Node.js، Express و Next.js","en":"Backend architecture patterns, API design, database optimization, and server-side best practices for Node.js, Express, and Next.js API routes."},"owner":"affaan-m","repo":"everything-claude-code","repoPath":"affaan-m/everything-claude-code","stars":55024,"forks":6781,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T05:07:39Z","topics":["ai-agents","anthropic","claude","claude-code","developer-tools","llm","mcp","productivity"],"skillMd":{"name":"backend-patterns","description":"Backend architecture patterns, API design, database optimization, and server-side best practices for Node.js, Express, and Next.js API routes.","bodyPreview":"# Backend Development Patterns\n\nBackend architecture patterns and best practices for scalable server-side applications.\n\n## When to Activate\n\n- Designing REST or GraphQL API endpoints\n- Implementing repository, service, or controller layers\n- Optimizing database queries (N+1, indexing, connection pooling)\n- Adding caching (Redis, in-memory, HTTP cache headers)\n- Setting up background jobs or async processing\n- Structuring error handling and validation for APIs\n- Building middleware (auth, loggin","body":"# Backend Development Patterns\n\nBackend architecture patterns and best practices for scalable server-side applications.\n\n## When to Activate\n\n- Designing REST or GraphQL API endpoints\n- Implementing repository, service, or controller layers\n- Optimizing database queries (N+1, indexing, connection pooling)\n- Adding caching (Redis, in-memory, HTTP cache headers)\n- Setting up background jobs or async processing\n- Structuring error handling and validation for APIs\n- Building middleware (auth, logging, rate limiting)\n\n## API Design Patterns\n\n### RESTful API Structure\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ Resource-based URLs\nGET    /api/markets                 # List resources\nGET    /api/markets/:id             # Get single resource\nPOST   /api/markets                 # Create resource\nPUT    /api/markets/:id             # Replace resource\nPATCH  /api/markets/:id             # Update resource\nDELETE /api/markets/:id             # Delete resource\n\n// ✅ Query parameters for filtering, sorting, pagination\nGET /api/markets?status=active&sort=volume&limit=20&offset=0\n```\n\n### Repository Pattern\n\n```typescript\n// Abstract data access logic\ninterface MarketRepository {\n  findAll(filters?: MarketFilters): Promise<Market[]>\n  findById(id: string): Promise<Market | null>\n  create(data: CreateMarketDto): Promise<Market>\n  update(id: string, data: UpdateMarketDto): Promise<Market>\n  delete(id: string): Promise<void>\n}\n\nclass SupabaseMarketRepository implements MarketRepository {\n  async findAll(filters?: MarketFilters): Promise<Market[]> {\n    let query = supabase.from(''markets'').select(''*'')\n\n    if (filters?.status) {\n      query = query.eq(''status'', filters.status)\n    }\n\n    if (filters?.limit) {\n      query = query.limit(filters.limit)\n    }\n\n    const { data, error } = await query\n\n    if (error) throw new Error(error.message)\n    return data\n  }\n\n  // Other methods...\n}\n```\n\n### Service Layer Pattern\n\n```typescript\n// Business logic separated from data access\nclass MarketService {\n  constructor(private marketRepo: MarketRepository) {}\n\n  async searchMarkets(query: string, limit: number = 10): Promise<Market[]> {\n    // Business logic\n    const embedding = await generateEmbedding(query)\n    const results = await this.vectorSearch(embedding, limit)\n\n    // Fetch full data\n    const markets = await this.marketRepo.findByIds(results.map(r => r.id))\n\n    // Sort by similarity\n    return markets.sort((a, b) => {\n      const scoreA = results.find(r => r.id === a.id)?.score || 0\n      const scoreB = results.find(r => r.id === b.id)?.score || 0\n      return scoreA - scoreB\n    })\n  }\n\n  private async vectorSearch(embedding: number[], limit: number) {\n    // Vector search implementation\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Middleware Pattern\n\n```typescript\n// Request/response processing pipeline\nexport function withAuth(handler: NextApiHandler): NextApiHandler {\n  return async (req, res) => {\n    const token = req.headers.authorization?.replace(''Bearer '', '''')\n\n    if (!token) {\n      return res.status(401).json({ error: ''Unauthorized'' })\n    }\n\n    try {\n      const user = await verifyToken(token)\n      req.user = user\n      return handler(req, res)\n    } catch (error) {\n      return res.status(401).json({ error: ''Invalid token'' })\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n// Usage\nexport default withAuth(async (req, res) => {\n  // Handler has access to req.user\n})\n```\n\n## Database Patterns\n\n### Query Optimization\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ GOOD: Select only needed columns\nconst { data } = await supabase\n  .from(''markets'')\n  .select(''id, name, status, volume'')\n  .eq(''status'', ''active'')\n  .order(''volume'', { ascending: false })\n  .limit(10)\n\n// ❌ BAD: Select everything\nconst { data } = await supabase\n  .from(''markets'')\n  .select(''*'')\n```\n\n### N+1 Query Prevention\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ BAD: N+1 query problem\nconst markets = await getMarkets()\nfor (const market of markets) {\n  market.creator = await getUser(market.creator_id)  // N queries\n}\n\n// ✅ GOOD: Batch fetch\nconst markets = await getMarkets()\nconst creatorIds = markets.map(m => m.creator_id)\nconst creators = await getUsers(creatorIds)  // 1 query\nconst creatorMap = new Map(creators.map(c => [c.id, c]))\n\nmarkets.forEach(market => {\n  market.creator = creatorMap.get(market.creator_id)\n})\n```\n\n### Transaction Pattern\n\n```typescript\nasync function createMarketWithPosition(\n  marketData: CreateMarketDto,\n  positionData: CreatePositionDto\n) {\n  // Use Supabase transaction\n  const { data, error } = await supabase.rpc(''create_market_with_position'', {\n    market_data: marketData,\n    position_data: positionData\n  })\n\n  if (error) throw new Error(''Transaction failed'')\n  return data\n}\n\n// SQL function in Supabase\nCREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION create_market_with_position(\n  market_data jsonb,\n  position_data jsonb\n)\nRETURNS jsonb\nLANGUAGE plpgsql\nAS $$\nBEGIN\n  -- Start transaction automatically\n  INSERT INTO markets VALUES (market_data);\n  INSERT INTO positions VALUES (position_data);\n  RETURN jsonb_build_object(''success'', true);\nEXCEPTION\n  WHEN OTHERS THEN\n    -- Rollback happens automatically\n    RETURN jsonb_build_object(''success'', false, ''error'', SQLERRM);\nEND;\n$$;\n```\n\n## Caching Strategies\n\n### Redis Caching Layer\n\n```typescript\nclass CachedMarketRepository implements MarketRepository {\n  constructor(\n    private baseRepo: MarketRepository,\n    private redis: RedisClient\n  ) {}\n\n  async findById(id: string): Promise<Market | null> {\n    // Check cache first\n    const cached = await this.redis.get(`market:${id}`)\n\n    if (cached) {\n      return JSON.parse(cached)\n    }\n\n    // Cache miss - fetch from database\n    const market = await this.baseRepo.findById(id)\n\n    if (market) {\n      // Cache for 5 minutes\n      await this.redis.setex(`market:${id}`, 300, JSON.stringify(market))\n    }\n\n    return market\n  }\n\n  async invalidateCache(id: string): Promise<void> {\n    await this.redis.del(`market:${id}`)\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Cache-Aside Pattern\n\n```typescript\nasync function getMarketWithCache(id: string): Promise<Market> {\n  const cacheKey = `market:${id}`\n\n  // Try cache\n  const cached = await redis.get(cacheKey)\n  if (cached) return JSON.parse(cached)\n\n  // Cache miss - fetch from DB\n  const market = await db.markets.findUnique({ where: { id } })\n\n  if (!market) throw new Error(''Market not found'')\n\n  // Update cache\n  await redis.setex(cacheKey, 300, JSON.stringify(market))\n\n  return market\n}\n```\n\n## Error Handling Patterns\n\n### Centralized Error Handler\n\n```typescript\nclass ApiError extends Error {\n  constructor(\n    public statusCode: number,\n    public message: string,\n    public isOperational = true\n  ) {\n    super(message)\n    Object.setPrototypeOf(this, ApiError.prototype)\n  }\n}\n\nexport function errorHandler(error: unknown, req: Request): Response {\n  if (error instanceof ApiError) {\n    return NextResponse.json({\n      success: false,\n      error: error.message\n    }, { status: error.statusCode })\n  }\n\n  if (error instanceof z.ZodError) {\n    return NextResponse.json({\n      success: false,\n      error: ''Validation failed'',\n      details: error.errors\n    }, { status: 400 })\n  }\n\n  // Log unexpected errors\n  console.error(''Unexpected error:'', error)\n\n  return NextResponse.json({\n    success: false,\n    error: ''Internal server error''\n  }, { status: 500 })\n}\n\n// Usage\nexport async function GET(request: Request) {\n  try {\n    const data = await fetchData()\n    return NextResponse.json({ success: true, data })\n  } catch (error) {\n    return errorHandler(error, request)\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Retry with Exponential Backoff\n\n```typescript\nasync function fetchWithRetry<T>(\n  fn: () => Promise<T>,\n  maxRetries = 3\n): Promise<T> {\n  let lastError: Error\n\n  for (let i = 0; i < maxRetries; i++) {\n    try {\n      return await fn()\n    } catch (error) {\n      lastError = error as Error\n\n      if (i < maxRetries - 1) {\n        // Exponential backoff: 1s, 2s, 4s\n        const delay = Math.pow(2, i) * 1000\n        await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, delay))\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  throw lastError!\n}\n\n// Usage\nconst data = await fetchWithRetry(() => fetchFromAPI())\n```\n\n## Authentication & Authorization\n\n### JWT Token Validation\n\n```typescript\nimport jwt from ''jsonwebtoken''\n\ninterface JWTPayload {\n  userId: string\n  email: string\n  role: ''admin'' | ''user''\n}\n\nexport function verifyToken(token: string): JWTPayload {\n  try {\n    const payload = jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET!) as JWTPayload\n    return payload\n  } catch (error) {\n    throw new ApiError(401, ''Invalid token'')\n  }\n}\n\nexport async function requireAuth(request: Request) {\n  const token = request.headers.get(''authorization'')?.replace(''Bearer '', '''')\n\n  if (!token) {\n    throw new ApiError(401, ''Missing authorization token'')\n  }\n\n  return verifyToken(token)\n}\n\n// Usage in API route\nexport async function GET(request: Request) {\n  const user = await requireAuth(request)\n\n  const data = await getDataForUser(user.userId)\n\n  return NextResponse.json({ success: true, data })\n}\n```\n\n### Role-Based Access Control\n\n```typescript\ntype Permission = ''read'' | ''write'' | ''delete'' | ''admin''\n\ninterface User {\n  id: string\n  role: ''admin'' | ''moderator'' | ''user''\n}\n\nconst rolePermissions: Record<User[''role''], Permission[]> = {\n  admin: [''read'', ''write'', ''delete'', ''admin''],\n  moderator: [''read'', ''write'', ''delete''],\n  user: [''read'', ''write'']\n}\n\nexport function hasPermission(user: User, permission: Permission): boolean {\n  return rolePermissions[user.role].includes(permission)\n}\n\nexport function requirePermission(permission: Permission) {\n  return (handler: (request: Request, user: User) => Promise<Response>) => {\n    return async (request: Request) => {\n      const user = await requireAuth(request)\n\n      if (!hasPermission(user, permission)) {\n        throw new ApiError(403, ''Insufficient permissions'')\n      }\n\n      return handler(request, user)\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n// Usage - HOF wraps the handler\nexport const DELETE = requirePermission(''delete'')(\n  async (request: Request, user: User) => {\n    // Handler receives authenticated user with verified permission\n    return new Response(''Deleted'', { status: 200 })\n  }\n)\n```\n\n## Rate Limiting\n\n### Simple In-Memory Rate Limiter\n\n```typescript\nclass RateLimiter {\n  private requests = new Map<string, number[]>()\n\n  async checkLimit(\n    identifier: string,\n    maxRequests: number,\n    windowMs: number\n  ): Promise<boolean> {\n    const now = Date.now()\n    const requests = this.requests.get(identifier) || []\n\n    // Remove old requests outside window\n    const recentRequests = requests.filter(time => now - time < windowMs)\n\n    if (recentRequests.length >= maxRequests) {\n      return false  // Rate limit exceeded\n    }\n\n    // Add current request\n    recentRequests.push(now)\n    this.requests.set(identifier, recentRequests)\n\n    return true\n  }\n}\n\nconst limiter = new RateLimiter()\n\nexport async function GET(request: Request) {\n  const ip = request.headers.get(''x-forwarded-for'') || ''unknown''\n\n  const allowed = await limiter.checkLimit(ip, 100, 60000)  // 100 req/min\n\n  if (!allowed) {\n    return NextResponse.json({\n      error: ''Rate limit exceeded''\n    }, { status: 429 })\n  }\n\n  // Continue with request\n}\n```\n\n## Background Jobs & Queues\n\n### Simple Queue Pattern\n\n```typescript\nclass JobQueue<T> {\n  private queue: T[] = []\n  private processing = false\n\n  async add(job: T): Promise<void> {\n    this.queue.push(job)\n\n    if (!this.processing) {\n      this.process()\n    }\n  }\n\n  private async process(): Promise<void> {\n    this.processing = true\n\n    while (this.queue.length > 0) {\n      const job = this.queue.shift()!\n\n      try {\n        await this.execute(job)\n      } catch (error) {\n        console.error(''Job failed:'', error)\n      }\n    }\n\n    this.processing = false\n  }\n\n  private async execute(job: T): Promise<void> {\n    // Job execution logic\n  }\n}\n\n// Usage for indexing markets\ninterface IndexJob {\n  marketId: string\n}\n\nconst indexQueue = new JobQueue<IndexJob>()\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { marketId } = await request.json()\n\n  // Add to queue instead of blocking\n  await indexQueue.add({ marketId })\n\n  return NextResponse.json({ success: true, message: ''Job queued'' })\n}\n```\n\n## Logging & Monitoring\n\n### Structured Logging\n\n```typescript\ninterface LogContext {\n  userId?: string\n  requestId?: string\n  method?: string\n  path?: string\n  [key: string]: unknown\n}\n\nclass Logger {\n  log(level: ''info'' | ''warn'' | ''error'', message: string, context?: LogContext) {\n    const entry = {\n      timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n      level,\n      message,\n      ...context\n    }\n\n    console.log(JSON.stringify(entry))\n  }\n\n  info(message: string, context?: LogContext) {\n    this.log(''info'', message, context)\n  }\n\n  warn(message: string, context?: LogContext) {\n    this.log(''warn'', message, context)\n  }\n\n  error(message: string, error: Error, context?: LogContext) {\n    this.log(''error'', message, {\n      ...context,\n      error: error.message,\n      stack: error.stack\n    })\n  }\n}\n\nconst logger = new Logger()\n\n// Usage\nexport async function GET(request: Request) {\n  const requestId = crypto.randomUUID()\n\n  logger.info(''Fetching markets'', {\n    requestId,\n    method: ''GET'',\n    path: ''/api/markets''\n  })\n\n  try {\n    const markets = await fetchMarkets()\n    return NextResponse.json({ success: true, data: markets })\n  } catch (error) {\n    logger.error(''Failed to fetch markets'', error as Error, { requestId })\n    return NextResponse.json({ error: ''Internal error'' }, { status: 500 })\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Remember**: Backend patterns enable scalable, maintainable server-side applications. Choose patterns that fit your complexity level.\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-03-01T05:09:14.180Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能代理后端模式","ja":"AIエージェントのバックエンドパターン","ko":"AI 에이전트 백엔드 패턴","es":"Patrones de backend para AI Agentes con Node.js","fr":"Modèles de backend pour les Outils IA avec Node.js","de":"Backend-Muster für AI-Tools mit Node.js","pt":"Padrões de Desenvolvimento Backend com Ferramentas de IA","ru":"Шаблоны Backend-разработки с ИИ Агентами","ar":"نماذج التطوير الخلفي مع أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","en":"backend-patterns"},"description":{"zh":"后端开发模式，包括REST和GraphQL API设计、数据库优化和服务器端最佳实践","ja":"バックエンド開発パターン、RESTとGraphQL API設計、データベース最適化、サーバーサイドのベストプラクティス","ko":"백엔드 개발 패턴, REST와 GraphQL API 설계, 데이터베이스 최적화, 서버사이드의 베스트 프랙티스","es":"Patrones de backend para aplicaciones server-side escalables con Node.js, Express y Next.js","fr":"Modèles de backend pour des applications serveur évolutives avec Node.js, Express et Next.js","de":"Backend-Muster für skalierbare Server-Anwendungen mit Node.js, Express und Next.js","pt":"Padrões de desenvolvimento backend para aplicações escaláveis com Node.js, Express e Next.js","ru":"Шаблоны backend-разработки для масштабируемых приложений с Node.js, Express и Next.js","ar":"نماذج التطوير الخلفي لبرامج 