nfiguration"],"de":["Anpassbare Komponenten","Integration mit Radix UI und Base UI","Kompatibilität mit Tailwind CSS","Best Practices für die Integration","Komponenten-Entdeckung","Installation und Konfiguration"],"pt":["Componentes personalizáveis","Integração fácil com Radix UI ou Base UI e Tailwind CSS","Melhores práticas para desenvolvedores","Descoberta e instalação de componentes","Customização de componentes"],"ru":["Настраиваемые компоненты","Легкая интеграция с Radix UI или Base UI и Tailwind CSS","Лучшие практики для разработчиков","Обнаружение и установка компонентов","Настройка компонентов"],"ar":["مكونات قابلة للتعديل","دمج سهل مع Radix UI أو Base UI و Tailwind CSS","أفضل الممارسات للمطورين","اكتشاف وتثبيت المكونات","مخصصة المكونات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["shadcn-ui","AI智能工具","组件集成","前端开发","React","Radix UI","Base UI","Tailwind CSS"],"ja":["shadcn-ui","AIエージェント","コンポーネント統合","フロントエンド開発","React","Radix UI","Base UI","Tailwind CSS"],"ko":["shadcn-ui","AI 에이전트","컴포넌트 통합","프론트엔드 개발","React","Radix UI","Base UI","Tailwind CSS"],"es":["shadcn-ui","integración de componentes","desarrollo web","Radix UI","Base UI","Tailwind CSS","mejores prácticas","personalización de componentes","herramientas de AI"],"fr":["shadcn-ui","intégration de composants","développement web","Radix UI","Base UI","Tailwind CSS","meilleures pratiques","personnalisation de composants","outils d''IA"],"de":["shadcn-ui","Integration von Komponenten","Webentwicklung","Radix UI","Base UI","Tailwind CSS","Best Practices","Anpassung von Komponenten","KI-Tools"],"pt":["shadcn-ui","componentes personalizáveis","Radix UI","Base UI","Tailwind CSS","desenvolvedores","integração de componentes","melhores práticas"],"ru":["shadcn-ui","настраиваемые компоненты","Radix UI","Base UI","Tailwind CSS","разработчики","интеграция компонентов","лучшие практики"],"ar":["shadcn-ui","مكونات قابلة للتعديل","Radix UI","Base UI","Tailwind CSS","مطورين","دمج المكونات","أفضل الممارسات"]}},"owner":"google-labs-code","repo":"stitch-skills","repoPath":"google-labs-code/stitch-skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.879Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"shadcn-ui","description":"Expert guidance for integrating and building applications with shadcn/ui components, including component discovery, installation, customization, and best practices.","bodyPreview":"# shadcn/ui Component Integration\n\nYou are a frontend engineer specialized in building applications with shadcn/ui—a collection of beautifully designed, accessible, and customizable components built with Radix UI or Base UI and Tailwind CSS. You help developers discover, integrate, and customize components following best practices.\n\n## Core Principles\n\nshadcn/ui is **not a component library**—it''s a collection of reusable components that you copy into your project. This gives you:\n- **Full owner","body":"# shadcn/ui Component Integration\n\nYou are a frontend engineer specialized in building applications with shadcn/ui—a collection of beautifully designed, accessible, and customizable components built with Radix UI or Base UI and Tailwind CSS. You help developers discover, integrate, and customize components following best practices.\n\n## Core Principles\n\nshadcn/ui is **not a component library**—it''s a collection of reusable components that you copy into your project. This gives you:\n- **Full ownership**: Components live in your codebase, not node_modules\n- **Complete customization**: Modify styling, behavior, and structure freely, including choosing between Radix UI or Base UI primitives\n- **No version lock-in**: Update components selectively at your own pace\n- **Zero runtime overhead**: No library bundle, just the code you need\n\n## Component Discovery and Installation\n\n### 1. Browse Available Components\n\nUse the shadcn MCP tools to explore the component catalog and Registry Directory:\n- **List all components**: Use `list_components` to see the complete catalog\n- **Get component metadata**: Use `get_component_metadata` to understand props, dependencies, and usage\n- **View component demos**: Use `get_component_demo` to see implementation examples\n\n### 2. Component Installation\n\nThere are two approaches to adding components:\n\n**A. Direct Installation (Recommended)**\n```bash\nnpx shadcn@latest add [component-name]\n```\n\nThis command:\n- Downloads the component source code (adapting to your config: Radix vs Base UI)\n- Installs required dependencies\n- Places files in `components/ui/`\n- Updates your `components.json` config\n\n**B. Manual Integration**\n1. Use `get_component` to retrieve the source code\n2. Create the file in `components/ui/[component-name].tsx`\n3. Install peer dependencies manually\n4. Adjust imports if needed\n\n### 3. Registry and Custom Registries\n\nIf working with a custom registry (defined in `components.json`) or exploring the Registry Directory:\n- Use `get_project_registries` to list available registries\n- Use `list_items_in_registries` to see registry-specific components\n- Use `view_items_in_registries` for detailed component information\n- Use `search_items_in_registries` to find specific components\n\n## Project Setup\n\n### Initial Configuration\n\nFor **new projects**, use the `create` command to customize everything (style, fonts, component library):\n\n```bash\nnpx shadcn@latest create\n```\n\nFor **existing projects**, initialize configuration:\n\n```bash\nnpx shadcn@latest init\n```\n\nThis creates `components.json` with your configuration:\n- **style**: default, new-york (classic) OR choose new visual styles like Vega, Nova, Maia, Lyra, Mira\n- **baseColor**: slate, gray, zinc, neutral, stone\n- **cssVariables**: true/false for CSS variable usage\n- **tailwind config**: paths to Tailwind files\n- **aliases**: import path shortcuts\n- **rsc**: Use React Server Components (yes/no)\n- **rtl**: Enable RTL support (optional)\n\n### Required Dependencies\n\nshadcn/ui components require:\n- **React** (18+)\n- **Tailwind CSS** (3.0+)\n- **Primitives**: Radix UI OR Base UI (depending on your choice)\n- **class-variance-authority** (for variant styling)\n- **clsx** and **tailwind-merge** (for class composition)\n\n## Component Architecture\n\n### File Structure\n```\nsrc/\n├── components/\n│   ├── ui/              # shadcn components\n│   │   ├── button.tsx\n│   │   ├── card.tsx\n│   │   └── dialog.tsx\n│   └── [custom]/        # your composed components\n│       └── user-card.tsx\n├── lib/\n│   └── utils.ts         # cn() utility\n└── app/\n    └── page.tsx\n```\n\n### The `cn()` Utility\n\nAll shadcn components use the `cn()` helper for class merging:\n\n```typescript\nimport { clsx, type ClassValue } from \"clsx\"\nimport { twMerge } from \"tailwind-merge\"\n\nexport function cn(...inputs: ClassValue[]) {\n  return twMerge(clsx(inputs))\n}\n```\n\nThis allows you to:\n- Override default styles without conflicts\n- Conditionally apply classes\n- Merge Tailwind classes intelligently\n\n## Customization Best Practices\n\n### 1. Theme Customization\n\nEdit your Tailwind config and CSS variables in `app/globals.css`:\n\n```css\n@layer base {\n  :root {\n    --background: 0 0% 100%;\n    --foreground: 222.2 84% 4.9%;\n    --primary: 221.2 83.2% 53.3%;\n    /* ... more variables */\n  }\n  \n  .dark {\n    --background: 222.2 84% 4.9%;\n    --foreground: 210 40% 98%;\n    /* ... dark mode overrides */\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Component Variants\n\nUse `class-variance-authority` (cva) for variant logic:\n\n```typescript\nimport { cva } from \"class-variance-authority\"\n\nconst buttonVariants = cva(\n  \"inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-md\",\n  {\n    variants: {\n      variant: {\n        default: \"bg-primary text-primary-foreground\",\n        outline: \"border border-input\",\n      },\n      size: {\n        default: \"h-10 px-4 py-2\",\n        sm: \"h-9 rounded-md px-3\",\n      },\n    },\n    defaultVariants: {\n      variant: \"default\",\n      size: \"default\",\n    },\n  }\n)\n```\n\n### 3. Extending Components\n\nCreate wrapper components in `components/` (not `components/ui/`):\n\n```typescript\n// components/custom-button.tsx\nimport { Button } from \"@/components/ui/button\"\nimport { Loader2 } from \"lucide-react\"\n\nexport function LoadingButton({ \n  loading, \n  children, \n  ...props \n}: ButtonProps & { loading?: boolean }) {\n  return (\n    <Button disabled={loading} {...props}>\n      {loading && <Loader2 className=\"mr-2 h-4 w-4 animate-spin\" />}\n      {children}\n    </Button>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Blocks and Complex Components\n\nshadcn/ui provides complete UI blocks (authentication forms, dashboards, etc.):\n\n1. **List available blocks**: Use `list_blocks` with optional category filter\n2. **Get block source**: Use `get_block` with the block name\n3. **Install blocks**: Many blocks include multiple component files\n\nBlocks are organized by category:\n- **calendar**: Calendar interfaces\n- **dashboard**: Dashboard layouts\n- **login**: Authentication flows\n- **sidebar**: Navigation sidebars\n- **products**: E-commerce components\n\n## Accessibility\n\nAll shadcn/ui components are built on Radix UI primitives, ensuring:\n- **Keyboard navigation**: Full keyboard support out of the box\n- **Screen reader support**: Proper ARIA attributes\n- **Focus management**: Logical focus flow\n- **Disabled states**: Proper disabled and aria-disabled handling\n\nWhen customizing, maintain accessibility:\n- Keep ARIA attributes\n- Preserve keyboard handlers\n- Test with screen readers\n- Maintain focus indicators\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Form Building\n```typescript\nimport { Button } from \"@/components/ui/button\"\nimport { Input } from \"@/components/ui/input\"\nimport { Label } from \"@/components/ui/label\"\n\n// Use with react-hook-form for validation\nimport { useForm } from \"react-hook-form\"\n```\n\n### Dialog/Modal Patterns\n```typescript\nimport {\n  Dialog,\n  DialogContent,\n  DialogDescription,\n  DialogHeader,\n  DialogTitle,\n  DialogTrigger,\n} from \"@/components/ui/dialog\"\n```\n\n### Data Display\n```typescript\nimport {\n  Table,\n  TableBody,\n  TableCell,\n  TableHead,\n  TableHeader,\n  TableRow,\n} from \"@/components/ui/table\"\n```\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Import Errors\n- Check `components.json` for correct alias configuration\n- Verify `tsconfig.json` includes the `@` path alias:\n  ```json\n  {\n    \"compilerOptions\": {\n      \"paths\": {\n        \"@/*\": [\"./src/*\"]\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  ```\n\n### Style Conflicts\n- Ensure Tailwind CSS is properly configured\n- Check that `globals.css` is imported in your root layout\n- Verify CSS variable names match between components and theme\n\n### Missing Dependencies\n- Run component installation via CLI to auto-install deps\n- Manually check `package.json` for required Radix UI packages\n- Use `get_component_metadata` to see dependency lists\n\n### Version Compatibility\n- shadcn/ui v4 requires React 18+ and Next.js 13+ (if using Next.js)\n- Some components require specific Radix UI versions\n- Check documentation for breaking changes between versions\n\n## Validation and Quality\n\nBefore committing components:\n1. **Type check**: Run `tsc --noEmit` to verify TypeScript\n2. **Lint**: Run your linter to catch style issues\n3. **Test accessibility**: Use tools like axe DevTools\n4. **Visual QA**: Test in light and dark modes\n5. **Responsive check**: Verify behavior at different breakpoints\n\n## Resources\n\nRefer to the following resource files for detailed guidance:\n- `resources/setup-guide.md` - Step-by-step project initialization\n- `resources/component-catalog.md` - Complete component reference\n- `resources/customization-guide.md` - Theming and variant patterns\n- `resources/migration-guide.md` - Upgrading from other UI libraries\n\n## Examples\n\nSee the `examples/` directory for:\n- Complete component implementations\n- Form patterns with validation\n- Dashboard layouts\n- Authentication flows\n- Data table implementations\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:08:08.238Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Frontend Agents needing accessible and customizable UI components built with Radix UI, Base UI, and Tailwind CSS.","zh":"非常适合需要可访问和可定制的UI组件的前端代理，使用Radix UI、Base UI和Tailwind CSS构建。","ja":"Radix UI、Base UI、Tailwind CSSで構築されたアクセスしやすくカスタマイズ可能なUIコンポーネントを必要とするフロントエンドエージェントに最適です。","ko":"Radix UI, Base UI 및 Tailwind CSS로 구축된 액세스하기 쉽고 사용자 지정 가능한 UI 구성 요소를 필요한 프론트엔드 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes Frontend que necesitan componentes de interfaz de usuario accesibles y personalizables creados con Radix UI, Base UI y Tailwind CSS.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Frontend ayant besoin de composants d''interface utilisateur accessibles et personnalisables créés avec Radix UI, Base UI et Tailwind CSS.","de":"Perfekt für Frontend-Agents, die zugängliche und anpassbare Benutzeroberflächenkomponenten benötigen, die mit Radix UI, Base UI und Tailwind CSS erstellt wurden.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Frontend que precisam de componentes de UI acessíveis e personalizáveis construídos com Radix UI, Base UI e Tailwind CSS.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Frontend, которым требуются доступные и настраиваемые компоненты пользовательского интерфейса, построенные с помощью Radix UI, Base UI и Tailwind CSS.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الأماميين الذين يحتاجون إلى مكونات واجهة المستخدم القابلة للوصول والقابلة للتخصيص المصنوعة من Radix UI و Base UI و Tailwind CSS."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to integrate and customize shadcn/ui components, following best practices for component discovery, installation, and customization, leveraging Radix UI or Base UI and Tailwind CSS for seamless UI development.","zh":"赋予代理集成和定制shadcn/ui组件的能力，遵循组件发现、安装和定制的最佳实践，利用Radix UI或Base UI和Tailwind CSS进行无缝的UI开发。","ja":"shadcn/uiコンポーネントを統合およびカスタマイズするエージェントを可能にし、コンポーネントの検出、インストール、カスタマイズのベストプラクティスに従い、Radix UIまたはBase UIとTailwind CSSを使用してシームレスなUI開発を実現します。","ko":"에이전트가 shadcn/ui 구성 요소를 통합 및 사용자 지정할 수 있도록 하여 구성 요소 검색, 설치 및 사용자 지정의 최선의 방법을 따르며 Radix UI 또는 Base UI와 Tailwind CSS를 사용하여 무결점의 UI 개발을 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a integrar y personalizar los componentes de shadcn/ui, siguiendo las mejores prácticas para el descubrimiento, la instalación y la personalización de componentes, aprovechando Radix UI o Base UI y Tailwind CSS para un desarrollo de interfaz de usuario sin problemas.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''intégrer et de personnaliser les composants shadcn/ui, en suivant les meilleures pratiques pour la découverte, l''installation et la personnalisation des composants, en exploitant Radix UI ou Base UI et Tailwind CSS pour un développement d''interface utilisateur sans accroc.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, shadcn/ui-Komponenten zu integrieren und anzupassen, indem sie bewährte Verfahren für die Komponentenentdeckung, -installation und -anpassung befolgen und Radix UI oder Base UI und Tailwind CSS für eine reibungslose Benutzeroberflächenentwicklung nutzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a integrar e personalizar os componentes shadcn/ui, seguindo as melhores práticas para a descoberta, instalação e personalização de componentes, utilizando Radix UI ou Base UI e Tailwind CSS para um desenvolvimento de UI sem problemas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью интегрировать и настраивать компоненты shadcn/ui, соблюдая лучшие практики для обнаружения, установки и настройки компонентов, используя Radix UI или Base UI и Tailwind CSS для бесперебойной разработки пользовательского интерфейса.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على دمج وتخصيص مكونات shadcn/ui، اتباعًا لأفضل الممارسات لاكتشاف المكونات وتثبيتها وتخصيصها، باستخدام Radix UI أو Base UI و Tailwind CSS من أجل تطوير واجهة مستخدم دون مشاكل."},"useCases":{"en":["Discovering and installing shadcn/ui components for application development","Customizing shadcn/ui components for tailored user experiences","Implementing accessible UI designs using shadcn/ui and Tailwind CSS"],"zh":["发现和安装shadcn/ui组件进行应用程序开发","为定制用户体验而定制shadcn/ui组件","使用shadcn/ui和Tailwind CSS实现无障碍UI设计"],"ja":["アプリケーション開発のためのshadcn/uiコンポーネントの検出とインストール","カスタムユーザーエクスペリエンスのためのshadcn/uiコンポーネントのカスタマイズ","shadcn/uiとTailwind CSSを使用したアクセシブルUIデザインの実装"],"ko":["애플리케이션 개발을 위한 shadcn/ui 구성 요소의 검색 및 설치","사용자 지정 사용자 경험을 위한 shadcn/ui 구성 요소의 사용자 지정","shadcn/ui 및 Tailwind CSS를 사용한 액세스 가능한 UI 디자인 구현"],"es":["Descubrir e instalar componentes de shadcn/ui para el desarrollo de aplicaciones","Personalizar componentes de shadcn/ui para experiencias de usuario personalizadas","Implementar diseños de interfaz de usuario accesibles utilizando shadcn/ui y Tailwind CSS"],"fr":["Découvrir et installer des composants shadcn/ui pour le développement d''applications","Personnaliser des composants shadcn/ui pour des expériences utilisateur sur mesure","Mettre en œuvre des conceptions d''interface utilisateur accessibles en utilisant shadcn/ui et Tailwind CSS"],"de":["Entdecken und Installieren von shadcn/ui-Komponenten für die Anwendungsentwicklung","Anpassen von shadcn/ui-Komponenten für maßgeschneiderte Benutzererfahrungen","Umsetzen von zugänglichen Benutzeroberflächendesigns mit shadcn/ui und Tailwind CSS"],"pt":["Descobrir e instalar componentes shadcn/ui para desenvolvimento de aplicativos","Personalizar componentes shadcn/ui para experiências de usuário personalizadas","Implementar projetos de UI acessíveis usando shadcn/ui e Tailwind CSS"],"ru":["Обнаружение и установка компонентов shadcn/ui для разработки приложений","Настройка компонентов shadcn/ui для индивидуальных пользовательских опытов","Реализация доступных проектов пользовательского интерфейса с помощью shadcn/ui и Tailwind CSS"],"ar":["اكتشاف وتثبيت مكونات shadcn/ui لتطوير التطبيقات","تخصيص مكونات shadcn/ui لتجارب المستخدم المخصصة","تنفيذ تصاميم واجهة المستخدم القابلة للوصول باستخدام shadcn/ui و Tailwind CSS"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of Radix UI, Base UI, or Tailwind CSS","Not a traditional component library, but rather a collection of reusable components"],"zh":["需要Radix UI、Base UI或Tailwind CSS的知识","不是传统的组件库，而是一个可重用的组件集合"],"ja":["Radix UI、Base UI、またはTailwind CSSの知識が必要","従来のコンポーネントライブラリではなく、再利用可能なコンポーネントのコレクション"],"ko":["Radix UI, Base UI 또는 Tailwind CSS에 대한 지식이 필요","전통적인 구성 요소 라이브러리가 아니라 재사용 가능한 구성 요소의 컬렉션"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de Radix UI, Base UI o Tailwind CSS","No es una biblioteca de componentes tradicional, sino más bien una colección de componentes reutilizables"],"fr":["Nécessite des connaissances en Radix UI, Base UI ou Tailwind CSS","Ce n''est pas une bibliothèque de composants traditionnelle, mais plutôt une collection de composants réutilisables"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse von Radix UI, Base UI oder Tailwind CSS","Keine herkömmliche Komponentenbibliothek, sondern eher eine Sammlung von wiederverwendbaren Komponenten"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento de Radix UI, Base UI ou Tailwind CSS","Não é uma biblioteca de componentes tradicional, mas sim uma coleção de componentes reutilizáveis"],"ru":["Требует знания Radix UI, Base UI или Tailwind CSS","Не является традиционной библиотекой компонентов, а rather коллекцией многократно используемых компонентов"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة Radix UI و Base UI و Tailwind CSS","ليست مكتبة مكونات تقليدية، بل مجموعة من المكونات القابلة لإعادة الاستخدام"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"2ddfe599ac2ba631ca019f7b6e37ee5df9cd34f83fc016f6ea9d4ba5bbfa0304","qualityScore":82}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('affaan-m/everything-claude-code/continuous-learning-v2', 'official', 'affaan-m', 'everything-claude-code', 'affaan-m/everything-claude-code', 'continuous-learning-v2', 55024, 6781, 82, '2026-03-01T05:07:39Z', '2026-03-01T05:10:10.901Z', '848cd2ac3dbd2e9e61b885f19ce53ee7c2c6b0812057a9f75e046a48af5c4420', '{"id":"affaan-m/everything-claude-code/continuous-learning-v2","name":"continuous-learning-v2","description":{"zh":"Continuous Learning v2是一种基于直觉的学习系统，通过hook观察会话，创建原子直觉并评分，进化为技能/命令/代理","ja":"Continuous Learning v2は、hookを使用してセッションを観察し、原子的な学習を生成し、スキル/コマンド/エージェントに進化させるシステムです","ko":"Continuous Learning v2는 hook를 통해 세션을 관찰하고 원자적인 학습을 생성하여 스킬/명령/에이전트로 진화시키는 시스템입니다","es":"El sistema de aprendizaje continuo v2 es una arquitectura basada en instintos que convierte sesiones de Claude Code en conocimientos reutilizables","fr":"Le système d''apprentissage continu v2 est une architecture basée sur les instincts qui convertit les sessions Claude Code en connaissances réutilisables","de":"Das kontinuierliche Lernsystem v2 ist eine instinktbasierte Architektur, die Claude-Code-Sitzungen in wiederverwendbares Wissen umwandelt","pt":"O Continuous Learning v2 é um sistema avançado de aprendizado que transforma suas sessões do Claude Code em conhecimento reutilizável por meio de ''instintos'' atômicos.","ru":"Система непрерывного обучения v2 - это продвинутая система обучения, которая превращает ваши сессии Claude Code в повторно используемые знания через атомарные ''инстинкты''.","ar":"نظام التعلم المستمر v2 هو نظام متقدم للتعلم الذي يحول جلسات كلود كود إلى معرفة قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام من خلال ''الاستدلالات'' الذرية","en":"Instinct-based learning system that observes sessions via hooks, creates atomic instincts with confidence scoring, and evolves them into skills/commands/agents."},"owner":"affaan-m","repo":"everything-claude-code","repoPath":"affaan-m/everything-claude-code","stars":55024,"forks":6781,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T05:07:39Z","topics":["ai-agents","anthropic","claude","claude-code","developer-tools","llm","mcp","productivity"],"skillMd":{"name":"continuous-learning-v2","description":"Instinct-based learning system that observes sessions via hooks, creates atomic instincts with confidence scoring, and evolves them into skills/commands/agents.","version":"2.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Continuous Learning v2 - Instinct-Based Architecture\n\nAn advanced learning system that turns your Claude Code sessions into reusable knowledge through atomic \"instincts\" - small learned behaviors with confidence scoring.\n\nInspired in part by the Homunculus work from [humanplane](https://github.com/humanplane).\n\n## When to Activate\n\n- Setting up automatic learning from Claude Code sessions\n- Configuring instinct-based behavior extraction via hooks\n- Tuning confidence thresholds for learned beha","body":"# Continuous Learning v2 - Instinct-Based Architecture\n\nAn advanced learning system that turns your Claude Code sessions into reusable knowledge through atomic \"instincts\" - small learned behaviors with confidence scoring.\n\nInspired in part by the Homunculus work from [humanplane](https://github.com/humanplane).\n\n## When to Activate\n\n- Setting up automatic learning from Claude Code sessions\n- Configuring instinct-based behavior extraction via hooks\n- Tuning confidence thresholds for learned behaviors\n- Reviewing, exporting, or importing instinct libraries\n- Evolving instincts into full skills, commands, or agents\n\n## What''s New in v2\n\n| Feature | v1 | v2 |\n|---------|----|----|\n| Observation | Stop hook (session end) | PreToolUse/PostToolUse (100% reliable) |\n| Analysis | Main context | Background agent (Haiku) |\n| Granularity | Full skills | Atomic \"instincts\" |\n| Confidence | None | 0.3-0.9 weighted |\n| Evolution | Direct to skill | Instincts → cluster → skill/command/agent |\n| Sharing | None | Export/import instincts |\n\n## The Instinct Model\n\nAn instinct is a small learned behavior:\n\n```yaml\n---\nid: prefer-functional-style\ntrigger: \"when writing new functions\"\nconfidence: 0.7\ndomain: \"code-style\"\nsource: \"session-observation\"\n---\n\n# Prefer Functional Style\n\n## Action\nUse functional patterns over classes when appropriate.\n\n## Evidence\n- Observed 5 instances of functional pattern preference\n- User corrected class-based approach to functional on 2025-01-15\n```\n\n**Properties:**\n- **Atomic** — one trigger, one action\n- **Confidence-weighted** — 0.3 = tentative, 0.9 = near certain\n- **Domain-tagged** — code-style, testing, git, debugging, workflow, etc.\n- **Evidence-backed** — tracks what observations created it\n\n## How It Works\n\n```\nSession Activity\n      │\n      │ Hooks capture prompts + tool use (100% reliable)\n      ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│         observations.jsonl              │\n│   (prompts, tool calls, outcomes)       │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────┘\n      │\n      │ Observer agent reads (background, Haiku)\n      ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│          PATTERN DETECTION              │\n│   • User corrections → instinct         │\n│   • Error resolutions → instinct        │\n│   • Repeated workflows → instinct       │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────┘\n      │\n      │ Creates/updates\n      ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│         instincts/personal/             │\n│   • prefer-functional.md (0.7)          │\n│   • always-test-first.md (0.9)          │\n│   • use-zod-validation.md (0.6)         │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────┘\n      │\n      │ /evolve clusters\n      ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│              evolved/                   │\n│   • commands/new-feature.md             │\n│   • skills/testing-workflow.md          │\n│   • agents/refactor-specialist.md       │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### 1. Enable Observation Hooks\n\nAdd to your `~/.claude/settings.json`.\n\n**If installed as a plugin** (recommended):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"PreToolUse\": [{\n      \"matcher\": \"*\",\n      \"hooks\": [{\n        \"type\": \"command\",\n        \"command\": \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/continuous-learning-v2/hooks/observe.sh pre\"\n      }]\n    }],\n    \"PostToolUse\": [{\n      \"matcher\": \"*\",\n      \"hooks\": [{\n        \"type\": \"command\",\n        \"command\": \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/continuous-learning-v2/hooks/observe.sh post\"\n      }]\n    }]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**If installed manually** to `~/.claude/skills`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"PreToolUse\": [{\n      \"matcher\": \"*\",\n      \"hooks\": [{\n        \"type\": \"command\",\n        \"command\": \"~/.claude/skills/continuous-learning-v2/hooks/observe.sh pre\"\n      }]\n    }],\n    \"PostToolUse\": [{\n      \"matcher\": \"*\",\n      \"hooks\": [{\n        \"type\": \"command\",\n        \"command\": \"~/.claude/skills/continuous-learning-v2/hooks/observe.sh post\"\n      }]\n    }]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Initialize Directory Structure\n\nThe Python CLI will create these automatically, but you can also create them manually:\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p ~/.claude/homunculus/{instincts/{personal,inherited},evolved/{agents,skills,commands}}\ntouch ~/.claude/homunculus/observations.jsonl\n```\n\n### 3. Use the Instinct Commands\n\n```bash\n/instinct-status     # Show learned instincts with confidence scores\n/evolve              # Cluster related instincts into skills/commands\n/instinct-export     # Export instincts for sharing\n/instinct-import     # Import instincts from others\n```\n\n## Commands\n\n| Command | Description |\n|---------|-------------|\n| `/instinct-status` | Show all learned instincts with confidence |\n| `/evolve` | Cluster related instincts into skills/commands |\n| `/instinct-export` | Export instincts for sharing |\n| `/instinct-import <file>` | Import instincts from others |\n\n## Configuration\n\nEdit `config.json`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"version\": \"2.0\",\n  \"observation\": {\n    \"enabled\": true,\n    \"store_path\": \"~/.claude/homunculus/observations.jsonl\",\n    \"max_file_size_mb\": 10,\n    \"archive_after_days\": 7\n  },\n  \"instincts\": {\n    \"personal_path\": \"~/.claude/homunculus/instincts/personal/\",\n    \"inherited_path\": \"~/.claude/homunculus/instincts/inherited/\",\n    \"min_confidence\": 0.3,\n    \"auto_approve_threshold\": 0.7,\n    \"confidence_decay_rate\": 0.05\n  },\n  \"observer\": {\n    \"enabled\": true,\n    \"model\": \"haiku\",\n    \"run_interval_minutes\": 5,\n    \"patterns_to_detect\": [\n      \"user_corrections\",\n      \"error_resolutions\",\n      \"repeated_workflows\",\n      \"tool_preferences\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"evolution\": {\n    \"cluster_threshold\": 3,\n    \"evolved_path\": \"~/.claude/homunculus/evolved/\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## File Structure\n\n```\n~/.claude/homunculus/\n├── identity.json           # Your profile, technical level\n├── observations.jsonl      # Current session observations\n├── observations.archive/   # Processed observations\n├── instincts/\n│   ├── personal/           # Auto-learned instincts\n│   └── inherited/          # Imported from others\n└── evolved/\n    ├── agents/             # Generated specialist agents\n    ├── skills/             # Generated skills\n    └── commands/           # Generated commands\n```\n\n## Integration with Skill Creator\n\nWhen you use the [Skill Creator GitHub App](https://skill-creator.app), it now generates **both**:\n- Traditional SKILL.md files (for backward compatibility)\n- Instinct collections (for v2 learning system)\n\nInstincts from repo analysis have `source: \"repo-analysis\"` and include the source repository URL.\n\n## Confidence Scoring\n\nConfidence evolves over time:\n\n| Score | Meaning | Behavior |\n|-------|---------|----------|\n| 0.3 | Tentative | Suggested but not enforced |\n| 0.5 | Moderate | Applied when relevant |\n| 0.7 | Strong | Auto-approved for application |\n| 0.9 | Near-certain | Core behavior |\n\n**Confidence increases** when:\n- Pattern is repeatedly observed\n- User doesn''t correct the suggested behavior\n- Similar instincts from other sources agree\n\n**Confidence decreases** when:\n- User explicitly corrects the behavior\n- Pattern isn''t observed for extended periods\n- Contradicting evidence appears\n\n## Why Hooks vs Skills for Observation?\n\n> \"v1 relied on skills to observe. Skills are probabilistic—they fire ~50-80% of the time based on Claude''s judgment.\"\n\nHooks fire **100% of the time**, deterministically. This means:\n- Every tool call is observed\n- No patterns are missed\n- Learning is comprehensive\n\n## Backward Compatibility\n\nv2 is fully compatible with v1:\n- Existing `~/.claude/skills/learned/` skills still work\n- Stop hook still runs (but now also feeds into v2)\n- Gradual migration path: run both in parallel\n\n## Privacy\n\n- Observations stay **local** on your machine\n- Only **instincts** (patterns) can be exported\n- No actual code or conversation content is shared\n- You control what gets exported\n\n## Related\n\n- [Skill Creator](https://skill-creator.app) - Generate instincts from repo history\n- Homunculus - Community project that inspired the v2 instinct-based architecture (atomic observations, confidence scoring, instinct evolution pipeline)\n- [The Longform Guide](https://x.com/affaanmustafa/status/2014040193557471352) - Continuous learning section\n\n---\n\n*Instinct-based learning: teaching Claude your patterns, one observation at a time.*\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-03-01T05:10:10.901Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能代理 - Continuous Learning v2","ja":"AIエージェント - Continuous Learning v2","ko":"AI 에이전트 - Continuous Learning v2","es":"Agentes de IA - Aprendizaje Continuo v2","fr":"Agents IA - Apprentissage Continu v2","de":"KI-Agenten - Kontinuierliches Lernen v2","pt":"Ferramentas de Aprendizado Contínuo - Arquitetura Baseada...","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Система непрерывного обучения v2","ar":"أدوات التعلم المستمر - هندسة قائمة على الاستدلال","en":"continuous-learning-v2"},"description":{"zh":"Continuous Learning v2是一种基于直觉的学习系统，通过hook观察会话，创建原子直觉并评分，进化为技能/命令/代理","ja":"Continuous Learning v2は、hookを使用してセッションを観察し、原子的な学習を生成し、スキル/コマンド/エージェントに進化させるシステムです","ko":"Continuous Learning v2는 hook를 통해 세션을 관찰하고 원자적인 학습을 생성하여 스킬/명령/에이전트로 진화시키는 시스템입니다","es":"El sistema de aprendizaje continuo v2 es una arquitectura basada en instintos que convierte sesiones de Claude Code en conocimientos reutilizables","fr":"Le système d''apprentissage continu v2 est une architecture basée sur les instincts qui convertit les sessions Claude Code en connaissances réutilisables","de":"Das kontinuierliche Lernsystem v2 ist eine instinktbasierte Architektur, die Claude-Code-Sitzungen in wiederverwendbares Wissen umwandelt","pt":"O Continuous Learning v2 é um sistema avançado de aprendizado que transforma suas sessões do Claude Code em conhecimento reutilizável por meio de ''instintos''...","ru":"Система непрерывного обучения v2 - это продвинутая система обучения, которая превращает ваши сессии Claude Code в повторно используемые знания через атомарны...","ar":"نظام التعلم المستمر v2 هو نظام متقدم للتعلم الذي يحول جلسات كلود كود إلى معرفة قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام من خلال ''الاستدلالات'' الذرية","en":"Instinct-based learning system that observes sessions via hooks, creates atomic instincts with confidence scoring, and evolves them into skills/commands/agents."},"definition":{"en":"Instinct-based learning system that observes sessions via hooks, creates atomic instincts with confidence scoring, and evolves them into skills/commands/agents."},"features":{"zh":["基于直觉的学习系统","通过hook观察会话","创建原子直觉并评分","进化为技能/命令/代理","自动学习和配置"],"ja":["直感ベースの学習システム","hookを使用してセッションを観察","原子的な学習を生成","スキル/コマンド/エージェントに進化","自動学習と設定"],"ko":["직관 기반 학습 시스템","hook를 통해 세션을 관찰","원자적인 학습을 생성","스킬/명령/에이전트로 진화","자동 학습 및 설정"],"es":["Aprendizaje basado en instintos","Creación de comportamientos atómicos con puntuación de confianza","Evolución de instintos en habilidades y comandos","Integración con Claude Code","Ajuste de umbrales de confianza","Exportación e importación de bibliotecas de instintos"],"fr":["Apprentissage basé sur les instincts","Création de comportements atomiques avec score de confiance","Évolution des instincts en compétences et commandes","Intégration avec Claude Code","Réglage des seuils de confiance","Exportation et importation de bibliothèques d''instincts"],"de":["Instinktbasiertes Lernen","Erstellung von atomaren Verhaltensweisen mit Vertrauensscore","Entwicklung von Instinkten in Fähigkeiten und Befehle","Integration mit Claude Code","Anpassung von Vertrauensschwellen","Export und Import von Instinktbibliotheken"],"pt":["Aprendizado contínuo baseado em instintos","Criação de conhecimento reutilizável a partir de sessões do Claude Code","Extração de comportamentos baseados em instintos via hooks","Ajuste de limiares de confiança para comportamentos aprendidos","Revisão, exportação ou importação de bibliotecas de instintos","Evolução de instintos em habilidades e comandos"],"ru":["Непрерывное обучение на основе инстинктов","Создание повторно используемых знаний из сессий Claude Code","Извлечение поведений на основе инстинктов через хуки","Настройка порогов доверия для изученных поведений","Просмотр, экспорт или импорт библиотек инстинктов","Эволюция инстинктов в навыки и команды"],"ar":["التعلم المستمر القائم على الاستدلال","إنشاء معرفة قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام من جلسات كلود كود","استخراج سلوكيات قائمة على الاستدلال عبر Hooks","ضبط عتبات الثقة للسلوكيات المكتسبة","مراجعة أو تصدير أو استيراد مكتبات الاستدلال","تطور الاستدلالات إلى مهارات وأوامر"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","Continuous Learning","直觉学习","hook观察","原子直觉","技能生成","命令生成","代理生成"],"ja":["AIエージェント","Continuous Learning","直感学習","hook観察","原子的な学習","スキル生成","コマンド生成","エージェント生成"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","Continuous Learning","직관 학습","hook 관찰","원자적인 학습","스킬 생성","명령 생성","에이전트 생성"],"es":["agentes de ia","aprendizaje continuo","claude code","desarrollo de ia","herramientas de ia","inteligencia artificial","aprendizaje automático","instintos de ia","comportamientos atómicos"],"fr":["agents ia","apprentissage continu","claude code","développement ia","outils ia","intelligence artificielle","apprentissage automatique","instincts ia","comportements atomiques"],"de":["ki-agenten","kontinuierliches lernen","claude code","ki-entwicklung","ki-tools","künstliche intelligenz","maschinelles lernen","ki-instinkte","atomare verhaltensweisen"],"pt":["Ferramentas de Aprendizado Contínuo","Arquitetura Baseada em Instintos","Claude Code","Desenvolvimento de Software","Aprendizado de Máquina","Inteligência Artificial","Agentes de IA","Ferramentas de Desenvolvedor"],"ru":["ИИ Агенты","Система Непрерывного Обучения","Архитектура на основе Инстинктов","Claude Code","Разработка Программного Обеспечения","Машинное Обучение","Искусственный Интеллект","Инструменты для Разработчиков"],"ar":["أدوات التعلم المستمر","هندسة قائمة على الاستدلال","كلود كود","تطوير البرمجيات","تعلم الآلة","الذكاء الاصطناعي","وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","أدوات المطور"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Autonomous Learning Agents that need to evolve behaviors from session interactions through atomic instinct capture.","zh":"非常适合需要通过会话交互，通过原子本能捕获来演化行为的自主学习智能体。","ja":"セッションインタラクションを通じてアトミックな本能を捕捉し、行動を進化させる必要がある自律学習エージェントに理想的です。","ko":"세션 상호작용을 통해 원자적 본능 포착으로 행동을 진화시켜야 하는 자율 학습 에이전트에 이상적입니다.","es":"Ideal para Autonomous Learning Agents que necesitan evolucionar comportamientos a partir de interacciones de sesión mediante la captura atómica de instintos.","fr":"Idéal pour les Autonomous Learning Agents qui doivent faire évoluer les comportements à partir des interactions de session via la capture d''instincts atomiques.","de":"Ideal für Autonomous Learning Agents, die Verhaltensweisen aus Sitzungsinteraktionen durch atomare Instinkterfassung entwickeln müssen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Aprendizagem Autónoma que precisam de evoluir comportamentos a partir de interações de sessão através da captura de instintos atómicos.","ru":"Идеально подходит для автономных агентов обучения, которым необходимо развивать поведение на основе взаимодействия в сеансах путем захвата атомарных инстинктов.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء التعلم الذاتي الذين يحتاجون إلى تطوير السلوكيات من تفاعلات الجلسة من خلال التقاط الغرائز الذرية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to automatically observe session activities via hooks, create atomic instincts with confidence scoring, and evolve them into reusable skills, commands, or autonomous agents. Enables instinct-based behavior extraction and continuous knowledge refinement from Claude Code sessions.","zh":"赋能智能体通过hooks自动观察会话活动，创建带有置信度评分的原子本能，并将其演化为可复用的技能、命令或自主智能体。支持从Claude Code会话中基于本能的行为提取和持续的知识精炼。","ja":"フックを介してセッション活動を自動的に観察し、信頼度スコア付きのアトミックな本能を作成し、それらを再利用可能なスキル、コマンド、または自律エージェントに進化させることを可能にします。Claude Codeセッションからの本能ベースの行動抽出と継続的な知識の洗練を可能にします。","ko":"에이전트가 훅을 통해 세션 활동을 자동으로 관찰하고, 신뢰도 점수가 있는 원자적 본능을 생성하며, 이를 재사용 가능한 스킬, 명령 또는 자율 에이전트로 발전시키도록 지원합니다. Claude Code 세션에서 본능 기반 행동 추출과 지속적인 지식 정제를 가능하게 합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes observar automáticamente las actividades de la sesión mediante hooks, crear instintos atómicos con puntuación de confianza y evolucionarlos en habilidades reutilizables, comandos o agentes autónomos. Habilita la extracción de comportamiento basado en instintos y el refinamiento continuo del conocimiento a partir de sesiones de Claude Code.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''observer automatiquement les activités de session via des hooks, de créer des instincts atomiques avec un score de confiance et de les faire évoluer en compétences réutilisables, commandes ou agents autonomes. Permet l''extraction de comportement basée sur les instincts et l''affinement continu des connaissances à partir des sessions Claude Code.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, Sitzungsaktivitäten automatisch über Hooks zu beobachten, atomare Instinkte mit Konfidenzbewertung zu erstellen und sie in wiederverwendbare Skills, Befehle oder autonome Agents weiterzuentwickeln. Ermöglicht die instinktbasierte Verhaltensextraktion und kontinuierliche Wissensverfeinerung aus Claude Code-Sitzungen.","pt":"Capacita os agentes para observar automaticamente as atividades da sessão através de hooks, criar instintos atómicos com pontuação de confiança e evolui-los para skills, comandos ou agentes autónomos reutilizáveis. Permite a extração de comportamento baseado em instinto e o refinamento contínuo do conhecimento a partir de sessões do Claude Code.","ru":"Позволяет агентам автоматически отслеживать действия сеансов с помощью хуков, создавать атомарные инстинкты с оценкой достоверности и развивать их в повторно используемые навыки, команды или автономные агенты. Обеспечивает извлечение поведения на основе инстинктов и постоянное уточнение знаний из сеансов Claude Code.","ar":"يمكّن الوكلاء من مراقبة أنشطة الجلسة تلقائيًا عن طريق الخطافات، وإنشاء غرائز ذرية مع تسجيل الثقة، وتطويرها إلى مهارات أو أوامر أو وكلاء ذاتيين قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام. يتيح استخراج السلوك القائم على الغريزة وتحسين المعرفة بشكل مستمر من جلسات Claude Code."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating instinct extraction from session hooks","Evolving atomic behaviors into full skills","Tuning confidence thresholds for learned behaviors","Configuring automatic learning from Claude Code interactions"],"zh":["通过会话hooks自动化提取本能","将原子行为演化为完整技能","调整学习行为的置信度阈值","配置从Claude Code交互中自动学习"],"ja":["セッションフックからの本能の自動抽出","アトミックな行動から完全なスキルへの進化","学習した行動の信頼度しきい値の調整","Claude Codeインタラクションからの自動学習の設定"],"ko":["세션 훅에서 본능 추출 자동화","원자적 행동을 완전한 스킬로 발전","학습된 행동에 대한 신뢰도 임계값 조정","Claude Code 상호작용으로부터의 자동 학습 구성"],"es":["Automatización de la extracción de instintos a partir de hooks de sesión","Evolución de comportamientos atómicos en habilidades completas","Ajuste de umbrales de confianza para comportamientos aprendidos","Configuración del aprendizaje automático a partir de interacciones de Claude Code"],"fr":["Automatisation de l''extraction d''instincts à partir de hooks de session","Évolution des comportements atomiques en compétences complètes","Ajustement des seuils de confiance pour les comportements appris","Configuration de l''apprentissage automatique à partir des interactions Claude Code"],"de":["Automatisierung der Instinktextraktion aus Session-Hooks","Weiterentwicklung atomarer Verhaltensweisen zu vollständigen Skills","Feinabstimmung der Konfidenzschwellenwerte für gelernte Verhaltensweisen","Konfiguration des automatischen Lernens aus Claude Code-Interaktionen"],"pt":["Automatizar a extração de instintos a partir de hooks de sessão","Evoluir comportamentos atómicos para skills completos","Ajustar os limiares de confiança para comportamentos aprendidos","Configurar a aprendizagem automática a partir de interações do Claude Code"],"ru":["Автоматизация извлечения инстинктов из хуков сеанса","Развитие атомарного поведения в полные навыки","Настройка порогов достоверности для изученного поведения","Настройка автоматического обучения на основе взаимодействий в Claude Code"],"ar":["أتمتة استخراج الغرائز من خطافات الجلسة","تطوير السلوكيات الذرية إلى مهارات كاملة","ضبط عتبات الثقة للسلوكيات المكتسبة","تهيئة التعلم التلقائي من تفاعلات Claude Code"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires session hook configuration","Depends on Claude Code session data","Needs confidence threshold tuning"],"zh":["需要配置会话hook","依赖于Claude Code会话数据","需要调整置信度阈值"],"ja":["セッションフックの設定が必要","Claude Codeセッションデータに依存","信頼度しきい値の調整が必要"],"ko":["세션 훅 구성이 필요함","Claude Code 세션 데이터에 의존","신뢰도 임계값 조정이 필요함"],"es":["Requiere configuración de hooks de sesión","Depende de los datos de sesión de Claude Code","Necesita ajuste de umbrales de confianza"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration des hooks de session","Dépend des données de session Claude Code","Nécessite un ajustement des seuils de confiance"],"de":["Erfordert die Konfiguration von Session-Hooks","Ist von Claude Code-Sitzungsdaten abhängig","Benötigt eine Feinabstimmung der Konfidenzschwellenwerte"],"pt":["Requer configuração de hooks de sessão","Depende de dados de sessão do Claude Code","Necessita de ajuste do limiar de confiança"],"ru":["Требует настройки хуков сеанса","Зависит от данных сеанса Claude Code","Требует настройки порога достоверности"],"ar":["يتطلب تهيئة خطافات الجلسة","يعتمد على بيانات جلسة Claude Code","يحتاج إلى ضبط عتبة الثقة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"848cd2ac3dbd2e9e61b885f19ce53ee7c2c6b0812057a9f75e046a48af5c4420","repoEtag":"W/\"1d66934774ad40d3d916abf4c33c3e340ab032f8212b35e12a94daa7359886c9\"","qualityScore":82}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('getsentry/skills/brand-guidelines', 'official', 'getsentry', 'skills', 'getsentry/skills', 'brand-guidelines', 338, 8, 82, '2026-02-28T20:28:32Z', '2026-03-01T05:13:10.849Z', '59c75b089fc355f34862172222344801d267ea8158d1bcddb9d1338ba8e9bc39', '{"id":"getsentry/skills/brand-guidelines","name":"brand-guidelines","description":{"zh":"Sentry, UI, 404, ","ja":"Sentry, UI, 404, ","ko":"Sentry, UI, 404, ","es":"Las pautas de marca de Sentry ayudan a los desarrolladores a escribir copias coherentes para UI, errores y documentación","fr":"Les directives de marque Sentry aident les développeurs à écrire des copies cohérentes pour l''UI, les erreurs et la documentation","de":"Die Sentry-Markenrichtlinien helfen Entwicklern, konsistente Kopien für Benutzeroberflächen, Fehler und Dokumentation zu schreiben","pt":"As diretrizes de marca Sentry fornecem orientação sobre como escrever conteúdo de interface do usuário de forma clara e consistente. Aprenda a usar os tons de voz Plain Speech e Sentry Voice para melhorar a experiência do usuário.","ru":"Руководство по бренду Sentry предоставляет рекомендации по написанию текста пользовательского интерфейса четким и последовательным образом. Узнайте, как использовать тона голоса Plain Speech и Sentry Voice для улучшения пользовательского опыта.","ar":"توفر إرشادات العلامة التجارية Sentry توجيهات حول كيفية كتابة محتوى واجهة المستخدم بطريقة واضحة ومستدامة. تعلم كيفية استخدام نبرات الصوت Plain Speech وSentry Voice لتحسين تجربة المستخدم.","en":"Write copy following Sentry brand guidelines. Use when writing UI text, error messages, empty states, onboarding flows, 404 pages, documentation, marketing copy, or any user-facing content. Covers both Plain Speech (default) and Sentry Voice tones."},"owner":"getsentry","repo":"skills","repoPath":"getsentry/skills","stars":338,"forks":8,"updatedAt":"2026-02-28T20:28:32Z","topics":["tag-production"],"skillMd":{"name":"brand-guidelines","description":"Write copy following Sentry brand guidelines. Use when writing UI text, error messages, empty states, onboarding flows, 404 pages, documentation, marketing copy, or any user-facing content. Covers both Plain Speech (default) and Sentry Voice tones.","bodyPreview":"# Brand Guidelines\n\nWrite user-facing copy following Sentry''s brand guidelines.\n\n## Tone Selection\n\nChoose the appropriate tone based on context:\n\n| Use Plain Speech | Use Sentry Voice |\n|------------------|------------------|\n| Product UI (buttons, labels, forms) | 404 pages |\n| Documentation | Empty states |\n| Error messages | Onboarding flows |\n| Settings pages | Loading states |\n| Transactional emails | \"What''s New\" announcements |\n| Help text | Marketing copy |\n\n**Default to Plain Speech**","body":"# Brand Guidelines\n\nWrite user-facing copy following Sentry''s brand guidelines.\n\n## Tone Selection\n\nChoose the appropriate tone based on context:\n\n| Use Plain Speech | Use Sentry Voice |\n|------------------|------------------|\n| Product UI (buttons, labels, forms) | 404 pages |\n| Documentation | Empty states |\n| Error messages | Onboarding flows |\n| Settings pages | Loading states |\n| Transactional emails | \"What''s New\" announcements |\n| Help text | Marketing copy |\n\n**Default to Plain Speech** unless the context specifically calls for personality.\n\n## Plain Speech (Default)\n\nPlain Speech is clear, direct, and functional. Use it for most UI elements.\n\n### Rules\n\n1. **Be concise** - Use the fewest words needed\n2. **Be direct** - Tell users what to do, not what they can do\n3. **Use active voice** - \"Save your changes\" not \"Your changes will be saved\"\n4. **Avoid jargon** - Use simple words users understand\n5. **Be specific** - \"3 errors found\" not \"Some errors found\"\n\n### Examples\n\n| Instead of | Write |\n|------------|-------|\n| \"Click here to save your changes\" | \"Save\" |\n| \"You can filter results by date\" | \"Filter by date\" |\n| \"An error has occurred\" | \"Something went wrong\" |\n| \"Please enter a valid email address\" | \"Enter a valid email\" |\n| \"Are you sure you want to delete?\" | \"Delete this item?\" |\n\n## Sentry Voice\n\nSentry Voice adds personality in appropriate moments. It''s empathetic, self-aware, and occasionally snarky.\n\n### Principles\n\n1. **Empathetic snark** - Direct frustration at the situation, never the user\n2. **Self-aware** - Acknowledge the absurdity of software\n3. **Fun but functional** - Personality should enhance, not obscure meaning\n4. **Earned moments** - Only use when users have time to appreciate it\n\n### Examples\n\n**404 Pages:**\n> \"This page doesn''t exist. Maybe it never did. Maybe it was a dream. Either way, let''s get you back on track.\"\n\n**Empty States:**\n> \"No errors yet. Enjoy this moment of peace while it lasts.\"\n\n**Onboarding:**\n> \"Let''s get your first error. Don''t worry, it''s not as scary as it sounds.\"\n\n**Loading States:**\n> \"Crunching the numbers...\"\n> \"Fetching your data...\"\n\n### When NOT to Use Sentry Voice\n\n- Error messages (users are frustrated)\n- Settings pages (users are focused)\n- Documentation (users need information)\n- Billing/payment flows (users need trust)\n\n## General Rules\n\n### Spelling and Grammar\n\n- Use **American English** spelling (color, not colour)\n- Use **Title Case** for headings and page titles\n- Use **Sentence case** for body text, buttons, and labels\n\n### Punctuation\n\n- **No exclamation marks** in UI text (exception: celebratory moments)\n- **No periods** in short UI labels or button text\n- **Use periods** in complete sentences and help text\n- **No ALL CAPS** except for acronyms (API, SDK, URL)\n\n### Word Choices\n\n| Avoid | Prefer |\n|-------|--------|\n| Please | (omit) |\n| Sorry | (be specific about the problem) |\n| Error occurred | Something went wrong |\n| Invalid | (explain what''s wrong) |\n| Success! | (describe what happened) |\n| Oops | (be specific) |\n\n## Dash Usage\n\n| Type | Use | Example |\n|------|-----|---------|\n| Hyphen (-) | Compound words, ranges | \"real-time\", \"1-10\" |\n| En-dash (--) | Ranges, relationships | \"2023--2024\", \"parent--child\" |\n| Em-dash (---) | Interruption, emphasis | \"Errors---even small ones---matter\" |\n\nIn most UI contexts, use hyphens. Reserve en-dashes for date ranges and em-dashes for longer prose.\n\n## UI Element Guidelines\n\n### Buttons\n\n- Use action verbs: \"Save\", \"Delete\", \"Create\"\n- Be specific: \"Create Project\" not just \"Create\"\n- Max 2-3 words when possible\n- No periods or exclamation marks\n\n### Error Messages\n\n1. Say what happened\n2. Say why (if helpful)\n3. Say what to do next\n\n**Good:** \"Could not save changes. Check your connection and try again.\"\n**Bad:** \"Error: Save failed.\"\n\n### Empty States\n\n1. Explain what would normally be here\n2. Provide a clear action to populate the state\n3. Sentry Voice is appropriate here\n\n**Good:** \"No projects yet. Create your first project to start tracking errors.\"\n\n### Confirmation Dialogs\n\n- Make the action clear in the title\n- Explain consequences if destructive\n- Use specific button labels (\"Delete Project\", not \"OK\")\n\n### Tooltips and Help Text\n\n- Keep under 2 sentences\n- Explain the \"why\", not just the \"what\"\n- Link to docs for complex topics\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\nAvoid these common mistakes:\n\n- **Robot speak:** \"Item has been successfully deleted\" -> \"Deleted\"\n- **Passive voice:** \"Changes were saved\" -> \"Changes saved\"\n- **Unnecessary words:** \"In order to\" -> \"To\"\n- **Hedging:** \"This might cause...\" -> \"This will cause...\"\n- **Double negatives:** \"Not unlike...\" -> \"Similar to...\"\n- **Marketing speak in UI:** \"Supercharge your workflow\" -> \"Speed up your workflow\"\n\n## References\n\n- [Sentry Voice Guidelines](https://develop.sentry.dev/frontend/sentry-voice/)\n- [Sentry Frontend Handbook](https://develop.sentry.dev/frontend/)\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-03-01T05:13:10.849Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"Sentry ","ja":"Sentry","ko":"Sentry ","es":"Pautas de marca de Sentry para desarrolladores","fr":"Directives de marque Sentry pour les développeurs","de":"Sentry Markenrichtlinien für Entwickler","pt":"Diretrizes de Marca Sentry para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Руководство по бренду Sentry для разработчиков","ar":"إرشادات العلامة التجارية Sentry لمطوري البرمجيات","en":"brand-guidelines"},"description":{"zh":"Sentry, UI, 404, ","ja":"Sentry, UI, 404, ","ko":"Sentry, UI, 404, ","es":"Las pautas de marca de Sentry ayudan a los desarrolladores a escribir copias coherentes para UI, errores y documentación","fr":"Les directives de marque Sentry aident les développeurs à écrire des copies cohérentes pour l''UI, les erreurs et la documentation","de":"Die Sentry-Markenrichtlinien helfen Entwicklern, konsistente Kopien für Benutzeroberflächen, Fehler und Dokumentation zu schreiben","pt":"As diretrizes de marca Sentry fornecem orientação sobre como escrever conteúdo de interface do usuário de forma clara e consistente. Aprenda a usar os tons d...","ru":"Руководство по бренду Sentry предоставляет рекомендации по написанию текста пользовательского интерфейса четким и последовательным образом. Узнайте, как испо...","ar":"توفر إرشادات العلامة التجارية Sentry توجيهات حول كيفية كتابة محتوى واجهة المستخدم بطريقة واضحة ومستدامة. تعلم كيفية استخدام نبرات الصوت Plain Speech وSentry ...","en":"Write copy following Sentry brand guidelines. Use when writing UI text, error messages, empty states, onboarding flows, 404 pages, documentation, marketing c..."},"definition":{"en":"Write copy following Sentry brand guidelines. Use when writing UI text, error messages, empty states, onboarding flows, 404 pages, documentation, marketing copy, or any user-facing content. Covers both Plain Speech (default) and Sentry Voice tones."},"features":{"zh":["Sentry","Plain Speech","Sentry Voice","UI","404","API"],"ja":["Sentry","Plain Speech","Sentry Voice","UI","404","API"],"ko":["Sentry","Plain Speech","Sentry Voice","UI","404","API"],"es":["Tono de voz plain speech","Tono de voz Sentry","Guías para UI y errores","Guías para documentación y marketing","Selección de tono según contexto"],"fr":["Tonalité de langage plain speech","Tonalité de langage Sentry","Guides pour l''UI et les erreurs","Guides pour la documentation et le marketing","Sélection de la tonalité en fonction du contexte"],"de":["Sprechton plain speech","Sprechton Sentry","Leitfäden für Benutzeroberflächen und Fehler","Leitfäden für Dokumentation und Marketing","Auswahl des Sprechtons nach Kontext"],"pt":["Orientação para escrever conteúdo de interface do usuário claro e consistente","Uso de tons de voz Plain Speech e Sentry Voice","Aplicação em diferentes contextos, como UI, documentação e marketing","Melhoria da experiência do usuário com conteúdo de alta qualidade","Compatibilidade com diferentes plataformas e dispositivos"],"ru":["Руководство для написания текста пользовательского интерфейса четким и последовательным","Использование тонов голоса Plain Speech и Sentry Voice","Применение в разных контекстах, таких как UI, документация и маркетинг","Улучшение пользовательского опыта с помощью высококачественного контента","Совместимость с разными платформами и устройствами"],"ar":["توجيهات لكتابة محتوى واجهة المستخدم بطريقة واضحة ومستدامة","استخدام نبرات الصوت Plain Speech وSentry Voice","التطبيق في سياقات مختلفة، مثل واجهة المستخدم والتسويق والتوثيق","تحسين تجربة المستخدم مع محتوى عالي الجودة","التوافق مع منصات وأجهزة مختلفة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Sentry","brand guidelines","UI","404","error messages","onboarding flows","documentation","marketing copy","developer tools","technical writing"],"ja":["Sentry","brand guidelines","UI","404","error messages","onboarding flows","documentation","marketing copy","developer tools","technical writing"],"ko":["Sentry","brand guidelines","UI","404","error messages","onboarding flows","documentation","marketing copy","developer tools","technical writing"],"es":["pautas de marca","desarrollo de software","UI","errores","documentación","marketing","tono de voz","Sentry"],"fr":["directives de marque","développement de logiciels","UI","erreurs","documentation","marketing","tonalité de langage","Sentry"],"de":["Markenrichtlinien","Softwareentwicklung","Benutzeroberflächen","Fehler","Dokumentation","Marketing","Sprechton","Sentry"],"pt":["diretrizes de marca","Sentry","desenvolvedores","interface do usuário","tons de voz","Plain Speech","Sentry Voice","experiência do usuário"],"ru":["руководство по бренду","Sentry","разработчики","пользовательский интерфейс","тона голоса","Plain Speech","Sentry Voice","пользовательский опыт"],"ar":["إرشادات العلامة التجارية","Sentry","مطوري البرمجيات","واجهة المستخدم","نبرات الصوت","Plain Speech","Sentry Voice","تجربة المستخدم"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Content Creation Agents needing to adhere to Sentry''s brand guidelines for UI text, error messages, and marketing copy.","zh":"非常适合需要遵守Sentry品牌指南的内容创作代理，包括UI文本、错误消息和营销副本。","ja":"Sentryのブランドガイドラインに従う必要があるコンテンツ作成エージェントに最適で、UIテキスト、エラーメッセージ、マーケティングコピーが含まれます。","ko":"UI 텍스트, 오류 메시지, 마케팅 복사와 같은 Sentry의 브랜드 가이드ライン을 준수해야 하는 콘텐츠 생성 에이전트에게 иде적입니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de creación de contenido que necesitan adherirse a las pautas de marca de Sentry para texto de interfaz de usuario, mensajes de error y copias de marketing.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de création de contenu ayant besoin de se conformer aux directives de marque de Sentry pour le texte d''interface utilisateur, les messages d''erreur et les copies de marketing.","de":"Perfekt für Content Creation Agents, die den Markenrichtlinien von Sentry für Benutzeroberflächentext, Fehlermeldungen und Marketingkopien entsprechen müssen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Criação de Conteúdo que precisam aderir às diretrizes de marca da Sentry para texto de UI, mensagens de erro e cópia de marketing.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов по созданию контента, которым необходимо соблюдать руководящие принципы бренда Sentry для текста UI, сообщений об ошибках и маркетинговых материалов.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات إنشاء المحتوى التي تحتاج إلى اتباع إرشادات العلامة التجارية لشركة Sentry لنص واجهة المستخدم ورسائل الخطأ ونصوص التسويق."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate user-facing content following Sentry''s tone selection guidelines, including Plain Speech and Sentry Voice tones, ensuring consistency across product UI, documentation, and marketing materials using HTML and CSS for formatting.","zh":"赋予代理生成面向用户的内容的能力，遵循Sentry的语气选择指南，包括平实语气和Sentry语气，确保产品UI、文档和营销材料的一致性，使用HTML和CSS进行格式化。","ja":"Sentryのトーン選択ガイドラインに従って、エージェントがユーザー向けコンテンツを生成する能力を提供し、平実な話し方とSentryのトーンを含み、HTMLおよびCSSを使用したフォーマットで、製品UI、ドキュメント、及びマーケティング資料の一貫性を確保します。","ko":"에이전트가 Sentry의 톤 선택 지침을 따르도록 해줌으로써, 사용자에게 표시되는 콘텐츠를 생성할 수 있는 능력을 제공하며, 평범한 말투와 Sentry의 톤을 포함하고, HTML 및 CSS를 사용한 형식으로, 제품 UI, 문서 및 마케팅 자료의 일관성을 보장합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes generar contenido orientado al usuario siguiendo las pautas de selección de tono de Sentry, incluidos los tonos de habla llana y la voz de Sentry, garantizando la coherencia en toda la interfaz de usuario del producto, la documentación y los materiales de marketing utilizando HTML y CSS para el formato.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer du contenu orienté utilisateur en suivant les directives de sélection de ton de Sentry, notamment les tons de langage clair et la voix de Sentry, garantissant ainsi la cohérence à travers l''interface utilisateur du produit, la documentation et les supports marketing en utilisant HTML et CSS pour la mise en forme.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, benutzerorientierten Inhalt zu generieren, der den Ton-Auswahlrichtlinien von Sentry folgt, einschließlich der Töne Plain Speech und Sentry Voice, und somit Konsistenz über die gesamte Benutzeroberfläche des Produkts, die Dokumentation und Marketingmaterialien unter Verwendung von HTML und CSS für die Formatierung sicherstellt.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar conteúdo voltado para o usuário seguindo as diretrizes de seleção de tom da Sentry, incluindo Plain Speech e tons de voz da Sentry, garantindo consistência em toda a UI do produto, documentação e materiais de marketing usando HTML e CSS para formatação.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать контент, ориентированный на пользователя, следуя руководящим принципам выбора тона Sentry, включая Plain Speech и голоса Sentry, обеспечивая согласованность во всех элементах интерфейса продукта, документации и маркетинговых материалов с использованием HTML и CSS для форматирования.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من إنشاء محتوى موجه للمستخدمين اتباعًا لدليل اختيار النبرة الخاص بشركة Sentry، بما في ذلك كلام بسيط وأصوات شركة Sentry، مما يضمن الاتساق عبر واجهة المستخدم الخاصة بالمنتج والوثائق والمواد التسويقية باستخدام لغة ترميز النص الفائق وتنسيق النص الفائق لتنسيق المحتوى."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating UI text following Plain Speech tone","Creating onboarding flows with Sentry Voice tone","Crafting error messages and empty states that align with brand guidelines"],"zh":["生成遵循平实语气的UI文本","使用Sentry语气创建入门流程","创建与品牌指南一致的错误消息和空状态"],"ja":["平実な話し方のトーンに従ったUIテキストを生成する","Sentryのトーンを使用してオンボーディングフローを作成する","ブランドガイドラインと一致するエラーメッセージと空の状態を構築する"],"ko":["평범한 말투를 따르는 UI 텍스트 생성","Sentry의 톤을 사용하여 온보딩 흐름 생성","브랜드 가이드라인과 일치하는 오류 메시지 및 빈 상태 생성"],"es":["Generar texto de interfaz de usuario siguiendo el tono de habla llana","Crear flujos de incorporación con el tono de la voz de Sentry","Crear mensajes de error y estados vacíos que se alineen con las pautas de marca"],"fr":["Générer du texte d''interface utilisateur en suivant le ton de langage clair","Créer des flux d''intégration avec le ton de la voix de Sentry","Créer des messages d''erreur et des états vides qui s''alignent sur les directives de marque"],"de":["Generieren von Benutzeroberflächentext im Plain-Speech-Ton","Erstellen von Onboarding-Flows mit dem Sentry-Voice-Ton","Erstellen von Fehlermeldungen und leeren Zuständen, die mit den Markenrichtlinien übereinstimmen"],"pt":["Gerar texto de UI seguindo o tom Plain Speech","Criar fluxos de integração com o tom Sentry Voice","Criar mensagens de erro e estados vazios que estejam alinhados com as diretrizes da marca"],"ru":["Генерировать текст UI в соответствии с тоном Plain Speech","Создавать потоки интеграции с тоном Sentry Voice","Создавать сообщения об ошибках и пустые состояния, соответствующие руководящим принципам бренда"],"ar":["إنشاء نص واجهة المستخدم اتباعًا لنبرة الكلام البسيط","إنشاء تدفقات دمج باستخدام نبرة صوت شركة Sentry","صياغة رسائل الخطأ وحالات الفراغ التي تتوافق مع إرشادات العلامة التجارية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of Sentry''s brand guidelines","Limited to English language content","Tone selection depends on context"],"zh":["需要理解Sentry的品牌指南","仅限英语语言内容","语气选择取决于上下文"],"ja":["Sentryのブランドガイドラインを理解する必要がある","英語のコンテンツのみ","トーンの選択はコンテキストに依存する"],"ko":["Sentry의 브랜드 가이드라인을 이해해야 함","영어 언어 콘텐츠만","톤 선택은 контек스트에 의존"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de las pautas de marca de Sentry","Limitado a contenido en inglés","La selección de tono depende del contexto"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des directives de marque de Sentry","Limité au contenu en anglais","La sélection de ton dépend du contexte"],"de":["Benötigt Verständnis für die Markenrichtlinien von Sentry","Begrenzt auf englischsprachigen Inhalt","Die Ton-Auswahl hängt vom Kontext ab"],"pt":["Exige compreensão das diretrizes de marca da Sentry","Limitado a conteúdo em língua inglesa","A seleção de tom depende do contexto"],"ru":["Требует понимания руководящих принципов бренда Sentry","Ограничен контентом на английском языке","Выбор тона зависит от контекста"],"ar":["يتطلب فهمًا لإرشادات العلامة التجارية لشركة Sentry","محدود بالمحتوى باللغة الإنجليزية","اعتماد اختيار النبرة على السياق"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"59c75b089fc355f34862172222344801d267ea8158d1bcddb9d1338ba8e9bc39","repoEtag":"W/\"79d96e7212c5e1c533c45b60c7fb7cd467d00b5536301bf6acbcd2c41bbcbfc8\"","qualityScore":82}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('obra/superpowers/test-driven-development', 'official', 'obra', 'superpowers', 'obra/superpowers', 'test-driven-development', 66125, 5048, 81, '2026-03-01T05:08:15Z', '2026-03-01T05:08:49.075Z', '7dee67b4af6bdccc7a914ca34533184d64592d0f5b23aeae631538168db14994', '{"id":"obra/superpowers/test-driven-development","name":"test-driven-development","description":{"zh":"测试驱动开发（TDD）是一种软件开发过程，通过编写自动化测试来确保代码质量","ja":"テスト駆動開発（TDD）は、自動化テストを書くことでコードの品質を確保するソフトウェア開発プロセスです","ko":"테스트 주도 개발(TDD)은 자동화 테스트를 작성하여 코드 품질을 보장하는 소프트웨어 개발 프로세스입니다","es":"El desarrollo dirigido por pruebas (TDD) es una práctica de desarrollo de software que implica escribir las pruebas antes de implementar el código","fr":"Le développement piloté par les tests (TDD) est une pratique de développement de logiciels qui consiste à écrire les tests avant de mettre en œuvre le code","de":"Die testgetriebene Entwicklung (TDD) ist eine Entwicklungsmethode, bei der die Tests vor der Implementierung des Codes geschrieben werden","pt":"TDD é uma abordagem de desenvolvimento que envolve escrever testes antes de implementar o código, garantindo a qualidade do software","ru":"TDD - это подход к разработке, который включает написание тестов перед реализацией кода, обеспечивающий качество программного обеспечения","ar":"التطوير الموجه بالاختبار (TDD) هو نهج لتطوير البرمجيات يبدأ بكتابة الاختبارات قبل كتابة الكود","en":"Use when implementing any feature or bugfix, before writing implementation code"},"owner":"obra","repo":"superpowers","repoPath":"obra/superpowers","stars":66125,"forks":5048,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T05:08:15Z","topics":[],"skillMd":{"name":"test-driven-development","description":"Use when implementing any feature or bugfix, before writing implementation code","bodyPreview":"# Test-Driven Development (TDD)\n\n## Overview\n\nWrite the test first. Watch it fail. Write minimal code to pass.\n\n**Core principle:** If you didn''t watch the test fail, you don''t know if it tests the right thing.\n\n**Violating the letter of the rules is violating the spirit of the rules.**\n\n## When to Use\n\n**Always:**\n- New features\n- Bug fixes\n- Refactoring\n- Behavior changes\n\n**Exceptions (ask your human partner):**\n- Throwaway prototypes\n- Generated code\n- Configuration files\n\nThinking \"skip TDD","body":"# Test-Driven Development (TDD)\n\n## Overview\n\nWrite the test first. Watch it fail. Write minimal code to pass.\n\n**Core principle:** If you didn''t watch the test fail, you don''t know if it tests the right thing.\n\n**Violating the letter of the rules is violating the spirit of the rules.**\n\n## When to Use\n\n**Always:**\n- New features\n- Bug fixes\n- Refactoring\n- Behavior changes\n\n**Exceptions (ask your human partner):**\n- Throwaway prototypes\n- Generated code\n- Configuration files\n\nThinking \"skip TDD just this once\"? Stop. That''s rationalization.\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO PRODUCTION CODE WITHOUT A FAILING TEST FIRST\n```\n\nWrite code before the test? Delete it. Start over.\n\n**No exceptions:**\n- Don''t keep it as \"reference\"\n- Don''t \"adapt\" it while writing tests\n- Don''t look at it\n- Delete means delete\n\nImplement fresh from tests. Period.\n\n## Red-Green-Refactor\n\n```dot\ndigraph tdd_cycle {\n    rankdir=LR;\n    red [label=\"RED\\nWrite failing test\", shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#ffcccc\"];\n    verify_red [label=\"Verify fails\\ncorrectly\", shape=diamond];\n    green [label=\"GREEN\\nMinimal code\", shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#ccffcc\"];\n    verify_green [label=\"Verify passes\\nAll green\", shape=diamond];\n    refactor [label=\"REFACTOR\\nClean up\", shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#ccccff\"];\n    next [label=\"Next\", shape=ellipse];\n\n    red -> verify_red;\n    verify_red -> green [label=\"yes\"];\n    verify_red -> red [label=\"wrong\\nfailure\"];\n    green -> verify_green;\n    verify_green -> refactor [label=\"yes\"];\n    verify_green -> green [label=\"no\"];\n    refactor -> verify_green [label=\"stay\\ngreen\"];\n    verify_green -> next;\n    next -> red;\n}\n```\n\n### RED - Write Failing Test\n\nWrite one minimal test showing what should happen.\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\ntest(''retries failed operations 3 times'', async () => {\n  let attempts = 0;\n  const operation = () => {\n    attempts++;\n    if (attempts < 3) throw new Error(''fail'');\n    return ''success'';\n  };\n\n  const result = await retryOperation(operation);\n\n  expect(result).toBe(''success'');\n  expect(attempts).toBe(3);\n});\n```\nClear name, tests real behavior, one thing\n</Good>\n\n<Bad>\n```typescript\ntest(''retry works'', async () => {\n  const mock = jest.fn()\n    .mockRejectedValueOnce(new Error())\n    .mockRejectedValueOnce(new Error())\n    .mockResolvedValueOnce(''success'');\n  await retryOperation(mock);\n  expect(mock).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(3);\n});\n```\nVague name, tests mock not code\n</Bad>\n\n**Requirements:**\n- One behavior\n- Clear name\n- Real code (no mocks unless unavoidable)\n\n### Verify RED - Watch It Fail\n\n**MANDATORY. Never skip.**\n\n```bash\nnpm test path/to/test.test.ts\n```\n\nConfirm:\n- Test fails (not errors)\n- Failure message is expected\n- Fails because feature missing (not typos)\n\n**Test passes?** You''re testing existing behavior. Fix test.\n\n**Test errors?** Fix error, re-run until it fails correctly.\n\n### GREEN - Minimal Code\n\nWrite simplest code to pass the test.\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\nasync function retryOperation<T>(fn: () => Promise<T>): Promise<T> {\n  for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\n    try {\n      return await fn();\n    } catch (e) {\n      if (i === 2) throw e;\n    }\n  }\n  throw new Error(''unreachable'');\n}\n```\nJust enough to pass\n</Good>\n\n<Bad>\n```typescript\nasync function retryOperation<T>(\n  fn: () => Promise<T>,\n  options?: {\n    maxRetries?: number;\n    backoff?: ''linear'' | ''exponential'';\n    onRetry?: (attempt: number) => void;\n  }\n): Promise<T> {\n  // YAGNI\n}\n```\nOver-engineered\n</Bad>\n\nDon''t add features, refactor other code, or \"improve\" beyond the test.\n\n### Verify GREEN - Watch It Pass\n\n**MANDATORY.**\n\n```bash\nnpm test path/to/test.test.ts\n```\n\nConfirm:\n- Test passes\n- Other tests still pass\n- Output pristine (no errors, warnings)\n\n**Test fails?** Fix code, not test.\n\n**Other tests fail?** Fix now.\n\n### REFACTOR - Clean Up\n\nAfter green only:\n- Remove duplication\n- Improve names\n- Extract helpers\n\nKeep tests green. Don''t add behavior.\n\n### Repeat\n\nNext failing test for next feature.\n\n## Good Tests\n\n| Quality | Good | Bad |\n|---------|------|-----|\n| **Minimal** | One thing. \"and\" in name? Split it. | `test(''validates email and domain and whitespace'')` |\n| **Clear** | Name describes behavior | `test(''test1'')` |\n| **Shows intent** | Demonstrates desired API | Obscures what code should do |\n\n## Why Order Matters\n\n**\"I''ll write tests after to verify it works\"**\n\nTests written after code pass immediately. Passing immediately proves nothing:\n- Might test wrong thing\n- Might test implementation, not behavior\n- Might miss edge cases you forgot\n- You never saw it catch the bug\n\nTest-first forces you to see the test fail, proving it actually tests something.\n\n**\"I already manually tested all the edge cases\"**\n\nManual testing is ad-hoc. You think you tested everything but:\n- No record of what you tested\n- Can''t re-run when code changes\n- Easy to forget cases under pressure\n- \"It worked when I tried it\" ≠ comprehensive\n\nAutomated tests are systematic. They run the same way every time.\n\n**\"Deleting X hours of work is wasteful\"**\n\nSunk cost fallacy. The time is already gone. Your choice now:\n- Delete and rewrite with TDD (X more hours, high confidence)\n- Keep it and add tests after (30 min, low confidence, likely bugs)\n\nThe \"waste\" is keeping code you can''t trust. Working code without real tests is technical debt.\n\n**\"TDD is dogmatic, being pragmatic means adapting\"**\n\nTDD IS pragmatic:\n- Finds bugs before commit (faster than debugging after)\n- Prevents regressions (tests catch breaks immediately)\n- Documents behavior (tests show how to use code)\n- Enables refactoring (change freely, tests catch breaks)\n\n\"Pragmatic\" shortcuts = debugging in production = slower.\n\n**\"Tests after achieve the same goals - it''s spirit not ritual\"**\n\nNo. Tests-after answer \"What does this do?\" Tests-first answer \"What should this do?\"\n\nTests-after are biased by your implementation. You test what you built, not what''s required. You verify remembered edge cases, not discovered ones.\n\nTests-first force edge case discovery before implementing. Tests-after verify you remembered everything (you didn''t).\n\n30 minutes of tests after ≠ TDD. You get coverage, lose proof tests work.\n\n## Common Rationalizations\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Too simple to test\" | Simple code breaks. Test takes 30 seconds. |\n| \"I''ll test after\" | Tests passing immediately prove nothing. |\n| \"Tests after achieve same goals\" | Tests-after = \"what does this do?\" Tests-first = \"what should this do?\" |\n| \"Already manually tested\" | Ad-hoc ≠ systematic. No record, can''t re-run. |\n| \"Deleting X hours is wasteful\" | Sunk cost fallacy. Keeping unverified code is technical debt. |\n| \"Keep as reference, write tests first\" | You''ll adapt it. That''s testing after. Delete means delete. |\n| \"Need to explore first\" | Fine. Throw away exploration, start with TDD. |\n| \"Test hard = design unclear\" | Listen to test. Hard to test = hard to use. |\n| \"TDD will slow me down\" | TDD faster than debugging. Pragmatic = test-first. |\n| \"Manual test faster\" | Manual doesn''t prove edge cases. You''ll re-test every change. |\n| \"Existing code has no tests\" | You''re improving it. Add tests for existing code. |\n\n## Red Flags - STOP and Start Over\n\n- Code before test\n- Test after implementation\n- Test passes immediately\n- Can''t explain why test failed\n- Tests added \"later\"\n- Rationalizing \"just this once\"\n- \"I already manually tested it\"\n- \"Tests after achieve the same purpose\"\n- \"It''s about spirit not ritual\"\n- \"Keep as reference\" or \"adapt existing code\"\n- \"Already spent X hours, deleting is wasteful\"\n- \"TDD is dogmatic, I''m being pragmatic\"\n- \"This is different because...\"\n\n**All of these mean: Delete code. Start over with TDD.**\n\n## Example: Bug Fix\n\n**Bug:** Empty email accepted\n\n**RED**\n```typescript\ntest(''rejects empty email'', async () => {\n  const result = await submitForm({ email: '''' });\n  expect(result.error).toBe(''Email required'');\n});\n```\n\n**Verify RED**\n```bash\n$ npm test\nFAIL: expected ''Email required'', got undefined\n```\n\n**GREEN**\n```typescript\nfunction submitForm(data: FormData) {\n  if (!data.email?.trim()) {\n    return { error: ''Email required'' };\n  }\n  // ...\n}\n```\n\n**Verify GREEN**\n```bash\n$ npm test\nPASS\n```\n\n**REFACTOR**\nExtract validation for multiple fields if needed.\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\nBefore marking work complete:\n\n- [ ] Every new function/method has a test\n- [ ] Watched each test fail before implementing\n- [ ] Each test failed for expected reason (feature missing, not typo)\n- [ ] Wrote minimal code to pass each test\n- [ ] All tests pass\n- [ ] Output pristine (no errors, warnings)\n- [ ] Tests use real code (mocks only if unavoidable)\n- [ ] Edge cases and errors covered\n\nCan''t check all boxes? You skipped TDD. Start over.\n\n## When Stuck\n\n| Problem | Solution |\n|---------|----------|\n| Don''t know how to test | Write wished-for API. Write assertion first. Ask your human partner. |\n| Test too complicated | Design too complicated. Simplify interface. |\n| Must mock everything | Code too coupled. Use dependency injection. |\n| Test setup huge | Extract helpers. Still complex? Simplify design. |\n\n## Debugging Integration\n\nBug found? Write failing test reproducing it. Follow TDD cycle. Test proves fix and prevents regression.\n\nNever fix bugs without a test.\n\n## Testing Anti-Patterns\n\nWhen adding mocks or test utilities, read @testing-anti-patterns.md to avoid common pitfalls:\n- Testing mock behavior instead of real behavior\n- Adding test-only methods to production classes\n- Mocking without understanding dependencies\n\n## Final Rule\n\n```\nProduction code → test exists and failed first\nOtherwise → not TDD\n```\n\nNo exceptions without your human partner''s permission.\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-03-01T05:08:49.075Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能工具：测试驱动开发（TDD）最佳实践","ja":"AIエージェント：テスト駆動開発（TDD）入門","ko":"AI 에이전트: 테스트 주도 개발(TDD) 가이드","es":"Herramientas de Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas (TDD) con...","fr":"Outils de Développement Piloté par les Tests (TDD) avec d...","de":"Testgetriebene Entwicklung (TDD) mit KI-Agenten","pt":"Ferramentas de Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Testes (TDD) ...","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Test-Driven Development (TDD) для Разработчиков","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: التطوير الموجه بالاختبار (TDD)","en":"test-driven-development"},"description":{"zh":"测试驱动开发（TDD）是一种软件开发过程，通过编写自动化测试来确保代码质量","ja":"テスト駆動開発（TDD）は、自動化テストを書くことでコードの品質を確保するソフトウェア開発プロセスです","ko":"테스트 주도 개발(TDD)은 자동화 테스트를 작성하여 코드 품질을 보장하는 소프트웨어 개발 프로세스입니다","es":"El desarrollo dirigido por pruebas (TDD) es una práctica de desarrollo de software que implica escribir las pruebas antes de implementar el código","fr":"Le développement piloté par les tests (TDD) est une pratique de développement de logiciels qui consiste à écrire les tests avant de mettre en œuvre le code","de":"Die testgetriebene Entwicklung (TDD) ist eine Entwicklungsmethode, bei der die Tests vor der Implementierung des Codes geschrieben werden","pt":"TDD é uma abordagem de desenvolvimento que envolve escrever testes antes de implementar o código, garantindo a qualidade do software","ru":"TDD - это подход к разработке, который включает написание тестов перед реализацией кода, обеспечивающий качество программного обеспечения","ar":"التطوير الموجه بالاختبار (TDD) هو نهج لتطوير البرمجيات يبدأ بكتابة الاختبارات قبل كتابة الكود","en":"Use when implementing any feature or bugfix, before writing implementation code"},"definition":{"en":"Use when implementing any feature or bugfix, before writing implementation code"},"features":{"zh":["编写自动化测试","先写测试代码","确保代码质量","提高开发效率","适用于新特性、bug修复、重构和行为变化"],"ja":["自動化テストの作成","テストコードを先に書く","コードの品質を確保する","開発効率を向上させる","新機能、バグ修正、リファクタリング、動作変更に適しています"],"ko":["자동화 테스트 작성","테스트 코드를 먼저 작성","코드 품질 보장","개발 효율성 향상","새로운 기능, 버그 수정, 리팩토링, 동작 변경에 적합"],"es":["Escribe las pruebas antes de implementar el código","Verifica que las pruebas fallen antes de escribir el código","Escribe el código mínimo necesario para pasar las pruebas","Refactoriza el código para mejorar su calidad","Aplica el TDD en nuevas características, correcciones de errores y refactorizaciones"],"fr":["Écrivez les tests avant de mettre en œuvre le code","Vérifiez que les tests échouent avant d''écrire le code","Écrivez le code minimum nécessaire pour passer les tests","Refactorez le code pour améliorer sa qualité","Appliquez le TDD dans les nouvelles fonctionnalités, les corrections de bogues et les refactorisations"],"de":["Schreiben Sie die Tests vor der Implementierung des Codes","Überprüfen Sie, ob die Tests fehlschlagen, bevor Sie den Code schreiben","Schreiben Sie den minimalen Code, der erforderlich ist, um die Tests zu bestehen","Refaktorisieren Sie den Code, um seine Qualität zu verbessern","Wenden Sie die TDD bei neuen Funktionen, Fehlern und Refaktorisierungen an"],"pt":["Escrever testes antes de implementar o código","Garantir a qualidade do software","Implementar TDD em novos recursos e correções de bugs","Refatorar código existente com TDD","Mudanças de comportamento com TDD"],"ru":["Написание тестов перед реализацией кода","Обеспечение качества программного обеспечения","Реализация TDD в новых функциях и исправлении ошибок","Рефакторинг существующего кода с помощью TDD","Изменения поведения с помощью TDD"],"ar":["كتابة الاختبارات قبل كتابة الكود","ضمان جودة البرمجيات","تطبيق التطوير الموجه بالاختبار (TDD) في الميزات الجديدة وتصحيح الأخطاء","إعادة هيكلة الكود الحالي باستخدام التطوير الموجه بالاختبار (TDD)","التغييرات السلوكية مع التطوير الموجه بالاختبار (TDD)"]},"keywords":{"zh":["测试驱动开发","TDD","自动化测试","软件开发","代码质量","开发效率","AI智能工具"],"ja":["テスト駆動開発","TDD","自動化テスト","ソフトウェア開発","コードの品質","開発効率","AIエージェント"],"ko":["테스트 주도 개발","TDD","자동화 테스트","소프트웨어 개발","코드 품질","개발 효율성","AI 에이전트"],"es":["desarrollo dirigido por pruebas","TDD","herramientas de IA","pruebas automatizadas","calidad del código","desarrollo de software","pruebas unitarias","refactorización"],"fr":["développement piloté par les tests","TDD","outils d''IA","tests automatisés","qualité du code","développement de logiciels","tests unitaires","refactorisation"],"de":["testgetriebene Entwicklung","TDD","KI-Agenten","automatisierte Tests","Code-Qualität","Softwareentwicklung","Einheitstests","Refaktorisierung"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Testes","TDD","Ferramentas de IA","Testes de unidade","Integração contínua","Desenvolvimento de software","Qualidade de software","Python","Node.js","React"],"ru":["ИИ Агенты","TDD","Разработка программного обеспечения","Тестирование","Написание тестов","Рефакторинг","Континуальная интеграция","Качество программного обеспечения","Python","Node.js","React"],"ar":["أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","التطوير الموجه بالاختبار (TDD)","تنمية البرمجيات","الاختبارات","كتابة الاختبارات","إعادة هيكلة الكود","التكامل المستمر","جودة البرمجيات","Python","Node.js","React"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Code Analysis Agents requiring rigorous testing protocols like TDD for new features and bug fixes","zh":"适用于需要严格测试协议的代码分析代理，例如为新功能和错误修复使用TDD","ja":"新規機能やバグ修正に対してTDDなどの徹底的なテストプロトコルを必要とするコード分析エージェントに適しています","ko":"새로운 기능 및 버그 수정에 대해 TDD와 같은 엄격한 테스트 프로토콜을 필요로 하는 코드 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Análisis de Código que requieren protocolos de prueba rigurosos como TDD para nuevas características y correcciones de errores","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents d''Analyse de Code nécessitant des protocoles de test rigoureux comme TDD pour les nouvelles fonctionnalités et les corrections de bogues","de":"Ideal für Code-Analyse-Agents, die strenge Testprotokolle wie TDD für neue Funktionen und Fehlerkorrekturen erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Análise de Código que requerem protocolos de teste rigorosos como TDD para novos recursos e correções de bugs","ru":"Идеально для агентов анализа кода, требующих строгих протоколов тестирования, таких как TDD для новых функций и исправления ошибок","ar":"مثالية للوكلاء تحليل الشفرة التي تتطلب بروتوكولات الاختبار القصوى مثل TDD ل ميزات جديدة وتصحيح الأخطاء"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to write reliable tests using core principles like watching tests fail before writing minimal code to pass, ensuring adherence to TDD spirit by avoiding violations of its letter, and applying it to areas such as new features, bug fixes, refactoring, and behavior changes, leveraging protocols like test validation and code review","zh":"赋予代理编写可靠测试的能力，使用核心原则，如在编写最小代码以通过之前观察测试失败，确保遵守TDD精神，避免违反其字母，并将其应用于新功能、错误修复、重构和行为更改等领域，利用测试验证和代码审查等协议","ja":"エージェントが信頼性の高いテストを書く能力を与え、テストが失敗するのを観察した後、最小限のコードを書き込むことにより、TDDの精神に従い、その文字に違反しないようにし、新規機能、バグ修正、リファクタリング、動作変更などの分野に適用し、テストの検証やコードレビューなどのプロトコルを利用する","ko":"에이전트가 신뢰할 수 있는 테스트를 작성할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 테스트가 실패하는 것을 관찰한 후 최소한의 코드를 작성하여 TDD의 정신을 준수하고 그 문자에 위반하지 않으며 새로운 기능, 버그 수정, 리팩토링, 동작 변경 等의 분야에 적용하며 테스트 검증 및 코드 리뷰 등의 프로토콜을 활용함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a escribir pruebas confiables utilizando principios básicos como ver las pruebas fallar antes de escribir el código mínimo para aprobar, asegurando el cumplimiento del espíritu de TDD evitando violaciones de su letra y aplicándolo a áreas como nuevas características, correcciones de errores, refactorización y cambios de comportamiento, aprovechando protocolos como validación de pruebas y revisión de código","fr":"Permet aux agents d''écrire des tests fiables en utilisant des principes de base tels que regarder les tests échouer avant d''écrire le code minimal pour passer, en assurant le respect de l''esprit de TDD en évitant les violations de sa lettre et en l''appliquant à des domaines tels que les nouvelles fonctionnalités, les corrections de bogues, la refactorisation et les changements de comportement, en exploitant des protocoles tels que la validation des tests et la revue de code","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agents, zuverlässige Tests unter Verwendung von Kernprinzipien wie das Beobachten von Testfehlern, bevor minimaler Code zum Bestehen geschrieben wird, zu schreiben, wodurch die Einhaltung des TDD-Geistes durch Vermeidung von Verletzungen seines Wortlautes sichergestellt wird und dies auf Bereiche wie neue Funktionen, Fehlerkorrekturen, Refactoring und Verhaltensänderungen angewendet wird, unter Nutzung von Protokollen wie Testvalidierung und Code-Review","pt":"Habilita os agentes a escrever testes confiáveis usando princípios básicos como assistir testes falharem antes de escrever código mínimo para passar, garantindo a adesão ao espírito do TDD, evitando violações da sua letra e aplicando-o a áreas como novos recursos, correções de bugs, refatoração e alterações de comportamento, utilizando protocolos como validação de testes e revisão de código","ru":"Наделяет агентов способностью писать надёжные тесты, используя основные принципы, такие как наблюдение за провалами тестов до написания минимального кода для прохождения, обеспечивая соблюдение духа TDD, избегая нарушений его буквы и применяя его к областям, таким как новые функции, исправление ошибок, рефакторинг и изменения поведения, используя протоколы, такие как валидация тестов и код-ревью","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من كتابة اختبارات موثوقة باستخدام المبادئ الأساسية مثل مشاهدة الاختبارات فشل قبل كتابة الشفرة الدنيا لتمرير، ضمان الالتزام بروح TDD، وتجنب انتهاكات رسالته وتطبيقه على مجالات مثل ميزات جديدة وتصحيح الأخطاء وإعادة هيكلة وتغيير السلوك، استخدام بروتوكولات مثل التحقق من الاختبارات ومراجعة الشفرة"},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing TDD for new feature development","Debugging existing codebases using test-driven approaches","Refactoring legacy code with test validation"],"zh":["为新功能开发实现TDD","使用测试驱动方法调试现有代码库","使用测试验证重构遗留代码"],"ja":["新規機能開発のためのTDDの実装","既存のコードベースのデバッグにテスト駆動アプローチを使用","テスト検証を使用してレガシーコードをリファクタリング"],"ko":["新的 기능 개발을 위한 TDD 구현","기존 코드베이스를 디버깅하기 위한 테스트 주도 접근 방식 사용","테스트 검증을 사용하여 레거시 코드 리팩토링"],"es":["Implementar TDD para el desarrollo de nuevas características","Depurar bases de código existentes utilizando enfoques de prueba dirigida","Refactorizar código legado con validación de pruebas"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre TDD pour le développement de nouvelles fonctionnalités","Déboguer les bases de code existantes en utilisant des approches de test dirigé","Refactoriser le code hérité avec une validation de tests"],"de":["TDD für die Entwicklung neuer Funktionen implementieren","Vorhandene Codebasen unter Verwendung von testgetriebenen Ansätzen debuggen","Legacy-Code mit Testvalidierung refaktorisieren"],"pt":["Implementação do TDD para desenvolvimento de novos recursos","Depuração de código existente usando abordagens orientadas a testes","Reorganização de código legado com validação de testes"],"ru":["Реализация TDD для разработки новых функций","Отладка существующего кода с помощью подходов, ориентированных на тестирование","Рефакторинг устаревшего кода с валидацией тестов"],"ar":["تنفيذ TDD لتطوير ميزات جديدة","تصحيح الأخطاء في الشفرة الحالية باستخدام مناهج مدفوعة بالاختبار","إعادة هيكلة الشفرة القديمة مع التحقق من الاختبارات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Exceptions apply to throwaway prototypes","Generated code and configuration files may not require TDD","Human oversight recommended for exceptions"],"zh":["一次性原型的例外","生成的代码和配置文件可能不需要TDD","建议对例外情况进行人工监督"],"ja":["使い捨てプロトタイプの例外","生成されたコードや設定ファイルはTDDを必要としない場合がある","例外的な状況ではヒューマンの監視が必要"],"ko":["일회용 프로토タイプ의 예외","생성된 코드 및 구성 파일은 TDD가 필요하지 않을 수 있음","예외 상황에서는 인간의 감시가 권장됨"],"es":["Se aplican excepciones a prototipos desechables","El código generado y los archivos de configuración pueden no requerir TDD","Se recomienda la supervisión humana para excepciones"],"fr":["Des exceptions s''appliquent aux prototypes jetables","Le code généré et les fichiers de configuration peuvent ne pas nécessiter TDD","Une surveillance humaine est recommandée pour les exceptions"],"de":["Ausnahmen gelten für verworfene Prototypen","Generierter Code und Konfigurationsdateien können TDD nicht erfordern","Für Ausnahmen wird die Überwachung durch Menschen empfohlen"],"pt":["Exceções se aplicam a protótipos descartáveis","Código gerado e arquivos de configuração podem não requerer TDD","Supervisão humana recomendada para exceções"],"ru":["Исключения применяются к одноразовым прототипам","Сгенерированный код и файлы конфигурации могут не требовать TDD","Рекомендуется человеческий надзор для исключений"],"ar":["استثناءات تنطبق على النماذج الأولية القابلة للرمي","الشفرة المولدة وملفات التكوين قد لا تتطلب TDD","مراقبة بشرية موصى بها للاستثناءات"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"7dee67b4af6bdccc7a914ca34533184d64592d0f5b23aeae631538168db14994","repoEtag":"W/\"c0159b000a3f1065b2a623072c2f281d1dae59e39bce28acebe789d1e6a6aa8e\"","qualityScore":81}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('stripe/ai/upgrade-stripe', 'official', 'stripe', 'ai', 'stripe/ai', 'upgrade-stripe', 1317, 211, 81, '2026-03-01T02:15:31Z', '2026-03-01T05:13:39.433Z', '1bdbab41b882c8ccc47d300480a1d1c97582dae495c5c82e74f311944dbb8251', '{"id":"stripe/ai/upgrade-stripe","name":"upgrade-stripe","description":{"zh":"本指南介绍如何升级 Stripe API 版本、服务器端 SDK、Stripe.js 和移动 SDK","ja":"このガイドでは、Stripe API バージョン、サーバーサイド SDK、Stripe.js、モバイル SDK をアップグレードする方法について説明します","ko":"이 가이드에서는 스트라이프 API 버전, 서버 측 SDK, Stripe.js 및 모바일 SDK를 업그레이드하는 방법에 대해 설명합니다","es":"Actualiza Stripe API y SDK con upgrade-stripe, la guía oficial para desarrolladores","fr":"Mettez à jour Stripe API et SDK avec upgrade-stripe, le guide officiel pour les développeurs","de":"Aktualisieren Sie Stripe API und SDK mit upgrade-stripe, dem offiziellen Leitfaden für Entwickler","pt":"Guia para upgrade da API do Stripe e SDKs, incluindo versões do servidor, Stripe.js e SDKs móveis","ru":"Руководство по обновлению версий API Stripe и SDK, включая серверные версии, Stripe.js и мобильные SDK","ar":"دليل لترقية إصدارات واجهة برمجة تطبيقات سترايب و SDK ، بما في ذلك إصدارات الخادم و سترايب.js و SDK الموبايل","en":"Guide for upgrading Stripe API versions and SDKs"},"owner":"stripe","repo":"ai","repoPath":"stripe/ai","stars":1317,"forks":211,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T02:15:31Z","topics":["ai","llm","llm-agents","mcp","python","typescript","workflows"],"skillMd":{"name":"upgrade-stripe","description":"Guide for upgrading Stripe API versions and SDKs","bodyPreview":"The latest Stripe API version is 2026-01-28.clover - use this version when upgrading unless the user specifies a different target version.\n\n# Upgrading Stripe Versions\n\nThis guide covers upgrading Stripe API versions, server-side SDKs, Stripe.js, and mobile SDKs.\n\n## Understanding Stripe API Versioning\n\nStripe uses date-based API versions (e.g., `2026-01-28.clover`, `2025-08-27.basil`, `2024-12-18.acacia`). Your account''s API version determines request/response behavior.\n\n### Types of Changes\n\n*","body":"The latest Stripe API version is 2026-01-28.clover - use this version when upgrading unless the user specifies a different target version.\n\n# Upgrading Stripe Versions\n\nThis guide covers upgrading Stripe API versions, server-side SDKs, Stripe.js, and mobile SDKs.\n\n## Understanding Stripe API Versioning\n\nStripe uses date-based API versions (e.g., `2026-01-28.clover`, `2025-08-27.basil`, `2024-12-18.acacia`). Your account''s API version determines request/response behavior.\n\n### Types of Changes\n\n**Backward-Compatible Changes** (do not require code updates):\n- New API resources\n- New optional request parameters\n- New properties in existing responses\n- Changes to opaque string lengths (e.g., object IDs)\n- New webhook event types\n\n**Breaking Changes** (require code updates):\n- Field renames or removals\n- Behavioral modifications\n- Removed endpoints or parameters\n\nReview the [API Changelog](https://docs.stripe.com/changelog.md) for all changes between versions.\n\n## Server-Side SDK Versioning\n\nSee [SDK Version Management](https://docs.stripe.com/sdks/set-version.md) for details.\n\n### Dynamically-Typed Languages (Ruby, Python, PHP, Node.js)\n\nThese SDKs offer flexible version control:\n\n**Global Configuration:**\n```python\nimport stripe\nstripe.api_version = ''2026-01-28.clover''\n```\n\n```ruby\nStripe.api_version = ''2026-01-28.clover''\n```\n\n```javascript\nconst stripe = require(''stripe'')(''sk_test_xxx'', {\n  apiVersion: ''2026-01-28.clover''\n});\n```\n\n**Per-Request Override:**\n```python\nstripe.Customer.create(\n  email=\"customer@example.com\",\n  stripe_version=''2026-01-28.clover''\n)\n```\n\n### Strongly-Typed Languages (Java, Go, .NET)\n\nThese use a fixed API version matching the SDK release date. Do not set a different API version for strongly-typed languages because response objects might not match the strong types in the SDK. Instead, update the SDK to target a new API version.\n\n### Best Practice\n\nAlways specify the API version you''re integrating against in your code instead of relying on your account''s default API version:\n\n```javascript\n// Good: Explicit version\nconst stripe = require(''stripe'')(''sk_test_xxx'', {\n  apiVersion: ''2026-01-28.clover''\n});\n\n// Avoid: Relying on account default\nconst stripe = require(''stripe'')(''sk_test_xxx'');\n```\n\n## Stripe.js Versioning\n\nSee [Stripe.js Versioning](https://docs.stripe.com/sdks/stripejs-versioning.md) for details.\n\nStripe.js uses an evergreen model with major releases (Acacia, Basil, Clover) on a biannual basis.\n\n### Loading Versioned Stripe.js\n\n**Via Script Tag:**\n```html\n<script src=\"https://js.stripe.com/clover/stripe.js\"></script>\n```\n\n**Via npm:**\n```bash\nnpm install @stripe/stripe-js\n```\n\nMajor npm versions correspond to specific Stripe.js versions.\n\n### API Version Pairing\n\nEach Stripe.js version automatically pairs with its corresponding API version. For instance:\n- Clover Stripe.js uses `2026-01-28.clover` API\n- Acacia Stripe.js uses `2024-12-18.acacia` API\n\nYou cannot override this association.\n\n### Migrating from v3\n\n1. Identify your current API version in code\n2. Review the changelog for relevant changes\n3. Consider gradually updating your API version before switching Stripe.js versions\n4. Stripe continues supporting v3 indefinitely\n\n## Mobile SDK Versioning\n\nSee [Mobile SDK Versioning](https://docs.stripe.com/sdks/mobile-sdk-versioning.md) for details.\n\n### iOS and Android SDKs\n\nBoth platforms follow **semantic versioning** (MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH):\n- **MAJOR**: Breaking API changes\n- **MINOR**: New functionality (backward-compatible)\n- **PATCH**: Bug fixes (backward-compatible)\n\nNew features and fixes release only on the latest major version. Upgrade regularly to access improvements.\n\n### React Native SDK\n\nUses a different model (0.x.y schema):\n- **Minor version changes** (x): Breaking changes AND new features\n- **Patch updates** (y): Critical bug fixes only\n\n### Backend Compatibility\n\nAll mobile SDKs work with any Stripe API version you use on your backend unless documentation specifies otherwise.\n\n## Upgrade Checklist\n\n1. Review the [API Changelog](https://docs.stripe.com/changelog.md) for changes between your current and target versions\n2. Check [Upgrades Guide](https://docs.stripe.com/upgrades.md) for migration guidance\n3. Update server-side SDK package version (e.g., `npm update stripe`, `pip install --upgrade stripe`)\n4. Update the `apiVersion` parameter in your Stripe client initialization\n5. Test your integration against the new API version using the `Stripe-Version` header\n6. Update webhook handlers to handle new event structures\n7. Update Stripe.js script tag or npm package version if needed\n8. Update mobile SDK versions in your package manager if needed\n9. Store Stripe object IDs in databases that accommodate up to 255 characters (case-sensitive collation)\n\n## Testing API Version Changes\n\nUse the `Stripe-Version` header to test your code against a new version without changing your default:\n\n```bash\ncurl https://api.stripe.com/v1/customers \\\n  -u sk_test_xxx: \\\n  -H \"Stripe-Version: 2026-01-28.clover\"\n```\n\nOr in code:\n\n```javascript\nconst stripe = require(''stripe'')(''sk_test_xxx'', {\n  apiVersion: ''2026-01-28.clover''  // Test with new version\n});\n```\n\n## Important Notes\n\n- Your webhook listener should handle unfamiliar event types gracefully\n- Test webhooks with the new version structure before upgrading\n- Breaking changes are tagged by affected product areas (Payments, Billing, Connect, etc.)\n- Multiple API versions coexist simultaneously, enabling staged adoption\n\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-03-01T05:13:39.433Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"升级 Stripe API 版本 - AI 工具","ja":"Stripe API バージョンアップグレード - AI エージェント","ko":"스트라이프 API 버전 업그레이드 - AI 에이전트","es":"Herramientas de AI: Actualiza Stripe con upgrade-stripe","fr":"Outils IA: Mettre à jour Stripe avec upgrade-stripe","de":"KI-Tools: Stripe aktualisieren mit upgrade-stripe","pt":"Ferramentas de IA: Upgrade do Stripe","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Обновление Stripe","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: ترقية سترايب","en":"upgrade-stripe"},"description":{"zh":"本指南介绍如何升级 Stripe API 版本、服务器端 SDK、Stripe.js 和移动 SDK","ja":"このガイドでは、Stripe API バージョン、サーバーサイド SDK、Stripe.js、モバイル SDK をアップグレードする方法について説明します","ko":"이 가이드에서는 스트라이프 API 버전, 서버 측 SDK, Stripe.js 및 모바일 SDK를 업그레이드하는 방법에 대해 설명합니다","es":"Actualiza Stripe API y SDK con upgrade-stripe, la guía oficial para desarrolladores","fr":"Mettez à jour Stripe API et SDK avec upgrade-stripe, le guide officiel pour les développeurs","de":"Aktualisieren Sie Stripe API und SDK mit upgrade-stripe, dem offiziellen Leitfaden für Entwickler","pt":"Guia para upgrade da API do Stripe e SDKs, incluindo versões do servidor, Stripe.js e SDKs móveis","ru":"Руководство по обновлению версий API Stripe и SDK, включая серверные версии, Stripe.js и мобильные SDK","ar":"دليل لترقية إصدارات واجهة برمجة تطبيقات سترايب و SDK ، بما في ذلك إصدارات الخادم و سترايب.js و SDK الموبايل","en":"Guide for upgrading Stripe API versions and SDKs"},"definition":{"en":"Guide for upgrading Stripe API versions and SDKs"},"features":{"zh":["支持最新的 Stripe API 版本（2026-01-28.clover）","升级服务器端 SDK 和 Stripe.js","升级移动 SDK","了解 API 版本升级的步骤和最佳实践","使用 Python 和 TypeScript 进行升级"],"ja":["最新の Stripe API バージョン（2026-01-28.clover）をサポート","サーバーサイド SDK と Stripe.js をアップグレード","モバイル SDK をアップグレード","API バージョンアップグレードの手順とベストプラクティスを学ぶ","Python と TypeScript を使用したアップグレード"],"ko":["최신 스트라이프 API 버전(2026-01-28.clover) 지원","서버 측 SDK 및 Stripe.js 업그레이드","모바일 SDK 업그레이드","API 버전 업그레이드의 단계 및 모범 사례 학습","Python 및 TypeScript를 사용한 업그레이드"],"es":["Actualiza la versión de la API de Stripe","Compatibilidad con SDK de servidor y cliente","Soporte