стирования","ar":"أدوات اختبار E2E مع وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","en":"e2e-testing"},"description":{"zh":"e2e-testing是使用Playwright进行终端到终端测试的综合解决方案，包括测试文件组织、页面对象模型、配置、CI/CD集成、构件管理和不稳定测试策略","ja":"e2e-testingはPlaywrightを使用した終端から終端までのテストの総合的な解決策であり、テストファイルの組織、ページオブジェクトモデル、設定、CI/CD統合、成果物管理、および不安定なテスト戦略を含む","ko":"e2e-testing은 Playwright를 사용하여 엔드 투 엔드 테스팅을 수행하는 종합적인 솔루션으로, 테스트 파일 구성, 페이지 객체 모델, 구성, CI/CD 통합, 아티팩트 관리 및 불안정한 테스트 전략을 포함","es":"Playwright E2E testing patrones para construir suites de pruebas estables, rápidas y mantenibles","fr":"Modèles de tests E2E Playwright pour construire des suites de tests stables, rapides et maintenables","de":"Playwright E2E-Test-Muster für den Aufbau von stabilen, schnellen und wartbaren Test-Suiten","pt":"Implemente padrões de teste E2E com Playwright e Agentes de IA para melhorar a estabilidade e velocidade dos testes","ru":"Реализуйте шаблоны тестирования E2E с Playwright и ИИ Агентами для повышения стабильности и скорости тестов","ar":"نفذ أنماط الاختبار E2E مع Playwright ووكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي لتحسين الاستقرار وسرعة الاختبارات","en":"Playwright E2E testing patterns, Page Object Model, configuration, CI/CD integration, artifact management, and flaky test strategies."},"definition":{"en":"Playwright E2E testing patterns, Page Object Model, configuration, CI/CD integration, artifact management, and flaky test strategies."},"features":{"zh":["Playwright测试文件组织","页面对象模型","CI/CD集成","构件管理","不稳定测试策略"],"ja":["Playwrightテストファイルの組織","ページオブジェクトモデル","CI/CD統合","成果物管理","不安定なテスト戦略"],"ko":["Playwright 테스트 파일 구성","페이지 객체 모델","CI/CD 통합","아티팩트 관리","불안정한 테스트 전략"],"es":["Patrones de pruebas E2E con Playwright","Modelo de objetos de página para una mejor organización","Integración con CI/CD para una entrega continua","Gestión de artefactos para una mejor trazabilidad","Estrategias para tests fallidos para reducir la fricción"],"fr":["Modèles de tests E2E avec Playwright","Modèle d''objets de page pour une meilleure organisation","Intégration avec CI/CD pour une livraison continue","Gestion des artefacts pour une meilleure traçabilité","Stratégies pour les tests défaillants pour réduire la friction"],"de":["E2E-Test-Muster mit Playwright","Seitenobjektmodell für eine bessere Organisation","Integration mit CI/CD für eine kontinuierliche Lieferung","Artefakt-Management für eine bessere Nachverfolgbarkeit","Strategien für fehlerhafte Tests, um die Reibung zu reduzieren"],"pt":["Padrões de teste E2E com Playwright","Modelo de Objeto de Página","Configuração e integração com CI/CD","Gerenciamento de artefatos","Estratégias para testes instáveis"],"ru":["Шаблоны тестирования E2E с Playwright","Модель Объекта Страницы","Настройка и интеграция с CI/CD","Управление артефактами","Стратегии для нестабильных тестов"],"ar":["أنماط الاختبار E2E مع Playwright","نموذج كائن الصفحة","التكوين والدمج مع CI/CD","إدارة الملفات","استراتيجيات للاختبارات غير المستقرة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能工具","e2e-testing","Playwright","终端到终端测试","CI/CD集成","构件管理","不稳定测试策略"],"ja":["AIエージェント","e2e-testing","Playwright","終端から終端までのテスト","CI/CD統合","成果物管理","不安定なテスト戦略"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","e2e-testing","Playwright","엔드 투 엔드 테스팅","CI/CD 통합","아티팩트 관리","불안정한 테스트 전략"],"es":["pruebas E2E","Playwright","patrones de pruebas","modelo de objetos de página","integración con CI/CD","gestión de artefactos","estrategias para tests fallidos","desarrollo de software","herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["tests E2E","Playwright","modèles de tests","modèle d''objets de page","intégration avec CI/CD","gestion des artefacts","stratégies pour les tests défaillants","développement de logiciel","outils de développement"],"de":["E2E-Tests","Playwright","Test-Muster","Seitenobjektmodell","Integration mit CI/CD","Artefakt-Management","Strategien für fehlerhafte Tests","Software-Entwicklung","Entwicklungstools"],"pt":["teste E2E","Agentes de IA","Playwright","desenvolvimento de software","testes automatizados","CI/CD","estabilidade de testes","velocidade de testes"],"ru":["тестирование E2E","ИИ Агенты","Playwright","разработка программного обеспечения","автоматизированное тестирование","CI/CD","стабильность тестов","скорость тестов"],"ar":["الاختبار من النهاية إلى النهاية","وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","Playwright","تطوير البرمجيات","الاختبارات الآلية","CI/CD","استقرار الاختبارات","سرعة الاختبارات"]}},"owner":"affaan-m","repo":"everything-claude-code","repoPath":"affaan-m/everything-claude-code","stars":55501,"forks":6825,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T12:42:49Z","topics":["ai-agents","anthropic","claude","claude-code","developer-tools","llm","mcp","productivity"],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"e2e-testing","description":"Playwright E2E testing patterns, Page Object Model, configuration, CI/CD integration, artifact management, and flaky test strategies.","bodyPreview":"# E2E Testing Patterns\n\nComprehensive Playwright patterns for building stable, fast, and maintainable E2E test suites.\n\n## Test File Organization\n\n```\ntests/\n├── e2e/\n│   ├── auth/\n│   │   ├── login.spec.ts\n│   │   ├── logout.spec.ts\n│   │   └── register.spec.ts\n│   ├── features/\n│   │   ├── browse.spec.ts\n│   │   ├── search.spec.ts\n│   │   └── create.spec.ts\n│   └── api/\n│       └── endpoints.spec.ts\n├── fixtures/\n│   ├── auth.ts\n│   └── data.ts\n└── playwright.config.ts\n```\n\n## Page Object Mode","body":"# E2E Testing Patterns\n\nComprehensive Playwright patterns for building stable, fast, and maintainable E2E test suites.\n\n## Test File Organization\n\n```\ntests/\n├── e2e/\n│   ├── auth/\n│   │   ├── login.spec.ts\n│   │   ├── logout.spec.ts\n│   │   └── register.spec.ts\n│   ├── features/\n│   │   ├── browse.spec.ts\n│   │   ├── search.spec.ts\n│   │   └── create.spec.ts\n│   └── api/\n│       └── endpoints.spec.ts\n├── fixtures/\n│   ├── auth.ts\n│   └── data.ts\n└── playwright.config.ts\n```\n\n## Page Object Model (POM)\n\n```typescript\nimport { Page, Locator } from ''@playwright/test''\n\nexport class ItemsPage {\n  readonly page: Page\n  readonly searchInput: Locator\n  readonly itemCards: Locator\n  readonly createButton: Locator\n\n  constructor(page: Page) {\n    this.page = page\n    this.searchInput = page.locator(''[data-testid=\"search-input\"]'')\n    this.itemCards = page.locator(''[data-testid=\"item-card\"]'')\n    this.createButton = page.locator(''[data-testid=\"create-btn\"]'')\n  }\n\n  async goto() {\n    await this.page.goto(''/items'')\n    await this.page.waitForLoadState(''networkidle'')\n  }\n\n  async search(query: string) {\n    await this.searchInput.fill(query)\n    await this.page.waitForResponse(resp => resp.url().includes(''/api/search''))\n    await this.page.waitForLoadState(''networkidle'')\n  }\n\n  async getItemCount() {\n    return await this.itemCards.count()\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Test Structure\n\n```typescript\nimport { test, expect } from ''@playwright/test''\nimport { ItemsPage } from ''../../pages/ItemsPage''\n\ntest.describe(''Item Search'', () => {\n  let itemsPage: ItemsPage\n\n  test.beforeEach(async ({ page }) => {\n    itemsPage = new ItemsPage(page)\n    await itemsPage.goto()\n  })\n\n  test(''should search by keyword'', async ({ page }) => {\n    await itemsPage.search(''test'')\n\n    const count = await itemsPage.getItemCount()\n    expect(count).toBeGreaterThan(0)\n\n    await expect(itemsPage.itemCards.first()).toContainText(/test/i)\n    await page.screenshot({ path: ''artifacts/search-results.png'' })\n  })\n\n  test(''should handle no results'', async ({ page }) => {\n    await itemsPage.search(''xyznonexistent123'')\n\n    await expect(page.locator(''[data-testid=\"no-results\"]'')).toBeVisible()\n    expect(await itemsPage.getItemCount()).toBe(0)\n  })\n})\n```\n\n## Playwright Configuration\n\n```typescript\nimport { defineConfig, devices } from ''@playwright/test''\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  testDir: ''./tests/e2e'',\n  fullyParallel: true,\n  forbidOnly: !!process.env.CI,\n  retries: process.env.CI ? 2 : 0,\n  workers: process.env.CI ? 1 : undefined,\n  reporter: [\n    [''html'', { outputFolder: ''playwright-report'' }],\n    [''junit'', { outputFile: ''playwright-results.xml'' }],\n    [''json'', { outputFile: ''playwright-results.json'' }]\n  ],\n  use: {\n    baseURL: process.env.BASE_URL || ''http://localhost:3000'',\n    trace: ''on-first-retry'',\n    screenshot: ''only-on-failure'',\n    video: ''retain-on-failure'',\n    actionTimeout: 10000,\n    navigationTimeout: 30000,\n  },\n  projects: [\n    { name: ''chromium'', use: { ...devices[''Desktop Chrome''] } },\n    { name: ''firefox'', use: { ...devices[''Desktop Firefox''] } },\n    { name: ''webkit'', use: { ...devices[''Desktop Safari''] } },\n    { name: ''mobile-chrome'', use: { ...devices[''Pixel 5''] } },\n  ],\n  webServer: {\n    command: ''npm run dev'',\n    url: ''http://localhost:3000'',\n    reuseExistingServer: !process.env.CI,\n    timeout: 120000,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Flaky Test Patterns\n\n### Quarantine\n\n```typescript\ntest(''flaky: complex search'', async ({ page }) => {\n  test.fixme(true, ''Flaky - Issue #123'')\n  // test code...\n})\n\ntest(''conditional skip'', async ({ page }) => {\n  test.skip(process.env.CI, ''Flaky in CI - Issue #123'')\n  // test code...\n})\n```\n\n### Identify Flakiness\n\n```bash\nnpx playwright test tests/search.spec.ts --repeat-each=10\nnpx playwright test tests/search.spec.ts --retries=3\n```\n\n### Common Causes & Fixes\n\n**Race conditions:**\n```typescript\n// Bad: assumes element is ready\nawait page.click(''[data-testid=\"button\"]'')\n\n// Good: auto-wait locator\nawait page.locator(''[data-testid=\"button\"]'').click()\n```\n\n**Network timing:**\n```typescript\n// Bad: arbitrary timeout\nawait page.waitForTimeout(5000)\n\n// Good: wait for specific condition\nawait page.waitForResponse(resp => resp.url().includes(''/api/data''))\n```\n\n**Animation timing:**\n```typescript\n// Bad: click during animation\nawait page.click(''[data-testid=\"menu-item\"]'')\n\n// Good: wait for stability\nawait page.locator(''[data-testid=\"menu-item\"]'').waitFor({ state: ''visible'' })\nawait page.waitForLoadState(''networkidle'')\nawait page.locator(''[data-testid=\"menu-item\"]'').click()\n```\n\n## Artifact Management\n\n### Screenshots\n\n```typescript\nawait page.screenshot({ path: ''artifacts/after-login.png'' })\nawait page.screenshot({ path: ''artifacts/full-page.png'', fullPage: true })\nawait page.locator(''[data-testid=\"chart\"]'').screenshot({ path: ''artifacts/chart.png'' })\n```\n\n### Traces\n\n```typescript\nawait browser.startTracing(page, {\n  path: ''artifacts/trace.json'',\n  screenshots: true,\n  snapshots: true,\n})\n// ... test actions ...\nawait browser.stopTracing()\n```\n\n### Video\n\n```typescript\n// In playwright.config.ts\nuse: {\n  video: ''retain-on-failure'',\n  videosPath: ''artifacts/videos/''\n}\n```\n\n## CI/CD Integration\n\n```yaml\n# .github/workflows/e2e.yml\nname: E2E Tests\non: [push, pull_request]\n\njobs:\n  test:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n        with:\n          node-version: 20\n      - run: npm ci\n      - run: npx playwright install --with-deps\n      - run: npx playwright test\n        env:\n          BASE_URL: ${{ vars.STAGING_URL }}\n      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4\n        if: always()\n        with:\n          name: playwright-report\n          path: playwright-report/\n          retention-days: 30\n```\n\n## Test Report Template\n\n```markdown\n# E2E Test Report\n\n**Date:** YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM\n**Duration:** Xm Ys\n**Status:** PASSING / FAILING\n\n## Summary\n- Total: X | Passed: Y (Z%) | Failed: A | Flaky: B | Skipped: C\n\n## Failed Tests\n\n### test-name\n**File:** `tests/e2e/feature.spec.ts:45`\n**Error:** Expected element to be visible\n**Screenshot:** artifacts/failed.png\n**Recommended Fix:** [description]\n\n## Artifacts\n- HTML Report: playwright-report/index.html\n- Screenshots: artifacts/*.png\n- Videos: artifacts/videos/*.webm\n- Traces: artifacts/*.zip\n```\n\n## Wallet / Web3 Testing\n\n```typescript\ntest(''wallet connection'', async ({ page, context }) => {\n  // Mock wallet provider\n  await context.addInitScript(() => {\n    window.ethereum = {\n      isMetaMask: true,\n      request: async ({ method }) => {\n        if (method === ''eth_requestAccounts'')\n          return [''0x1234567890123456789012345678901234567890'']\n        if (method === ''eth_chainId'') return ''0x1''\n      }\n    }\n  })\n\n  await page.goto(''/'')\n  await page.locator(''[data-testid=\"connect-wallet\"]'').click()\n  await expect(page.locator(''[data-testid=\"wallet-address\"]'')).toContainText(''0x1234'')\n})\n```\n\n## Financial / Critical Flow Testing\n\n```typescript\ntest(''trade execution'', async ({ page }) => {\n  // Skip on production — real money\n  test.skip(process.env.NODE_ENV === ''production'', ''Skip on production'')\n\n  await page.goto(''/markets/test-market'')\n  await page.locator(''[data-testid=\"position-yes\"]'').click()\n  await page.locator(''[data-testid=\"trade-amount\"]'').fill(''1.0'')\n\n  // Verify preview\n  const preview = page.locator(''[data-testid=\"trade-preview\"]'')\n  await expect(preview).toContainText(''1.0'')\n\n  // Confirm and wait for blockchain\n  await page.locator(''[data-testid=\"confirm-trade\"]'').click()\n  await page.waitForResponse(\n    resp => resp.url().includes(''/api/trade'') && resp.status() === 200,\n    { timeout: 30000 }\n  )\n\n  await expect(page.locator(''[data-testid=\"trade-success\"]'')).toBeVisible()\n})\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-01T12:47:25.334Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Automation Agents needing robust end-to-end testing capabilities with Playwright","zh":"适合需要使用Playwright进行强大的端到端测试功能的自动化代理","ja":"Playwrightを使用した強力なエンドツーエンドのテスト機能を必要とする自動化エージェントに最適","ko":"Playwright를 사용하여 강력한 종단 간 테스트 기능이 필요한 자동화 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Automatización que necesitan capacidades de prueba de extremo a extremo robustas con Playwright","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents d''Automatisation ayant besoin de capacités de test de bout en bout robustes avec Playwright","de":"Perfekt für Automatisierungsagenten, die robuste End-to-End-Testfunktionen mit Playwright benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Automação que necessitam de capacidades de teste de ponta a ponta robustas com Playwright","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов автоматизации, которым необходимы мощные возможности для тестирования от начала до конца с помощью Playwright","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الآليين الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات اختبار نهاية إلى نهاية قوية مع Playwright"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build stable, fast, and maintainable E2E test suites using Playwright patterns, Page Object Model, and CI/CD integration, while effectively managing flaky tests and artifacts","zh":"赋予代理构建使用Playwright模式、页面对象模型和CI/CD集成的稳定、快速和可维护的端到端测试套件的能力，同时有效地管理脆弱的测试和工件","ja":"Playwrightパターン、ページオブジェクトモデル、CI/CD統合を使用して安定した、高速で、保守可能なエンドツーエンドのテストスイートを構築し、脆弱なテストやアーティファクトを効果的に管理するエージェントの能力を付与","ko":"Playwright 패턴, 페이지 객체 모델 및 CI/CD 통합을 사용하여 안정적이고 빠르고 유지 관리 가능한 종단 간 테스트套件을 구축하고 부실한 테스트 및 아티팩트를 효과적으로 관리하는 에이전트의 능력을 부여","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear suites de pruebas de extremo a extremo estables, rápidas y mantenibles utilizando patrones de Playwright, Modelo de Objeto de Página y integración de CI/CD, mientras gestiona eficazmente las pruebas inestables y artefactos","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des suites de tests de bout en bout stables, rapides et maintenables en utilisant des modèles Playwright, Model d''Objet de Page et intégration CI/CD, tout en gérant efficacement les tests instables et les artefacts","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, stabile, schnelle und wartbare E2E-Test-Suites mit Playwright-Mustern, Page-Object-Modell und CI/CD-Integration zu erstellen, während sie flaky-Tests und Artefakte effektiv verwalten","pt":"Permite que os agentes criem conjuntos de testes de ponta a ponta estáveis, rápidos e mantenedores usando padrões Playwright, Modelo de Objeto de Página e integração de CI/CD, enquanto gerenciam efetivamente testes instáveis e artefatos","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать стабильные, быстрые и поддерживаемые наборы тестов от начала до конца, используя шаблоны Playwright, модель объекта страницы и интеграцию CI/CD, а также эффективно управлять нестабильными тестами и артефактами","ar":"يُمَكِّن الوكلاء من إنشاء مجموعات اختبار نهاية إلى نهاية مستقرة وسريعة وقابلة للصيانة باستخدام أنماط Playwright ونموذج كائن الصفحة وتكامل CI/CD، في حين يديرون بفعالية الاختبارات غير المستقرة والعناصر"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating browser interactions for authentication testing","Generating test suites for API endpoint validation","Debugging flaky tests using advanced test strategies"],"zh":["用于身份验证测试的浏览器交互自动化","用于API端点验证的测试套件生成","使用高级测试策略调试脆弱的测试"],"ja":["認証テストのブラウザーとのやり取りの自動化","APIエンドポイントの検証のためのテストスイートの生成","高度なテスト戦略を使用した脆弱なテストのデバッグ"],"ko":["인증 테스트를 위한 브라우저 상호 작용 자동화","API 엔드ポイント 유효성 검사 위한 테스트 스위트 생성","고급 테스트 전략을 사용하여 부실한 테스트 디버깅"],"es":["Automatizar interacciones del navegador para pruebas de autenticación","Generar suites de pruebas para validación de puntos de conexión de API","Depurar pruebas inestables utilizando estrategias de prueba avanzadas"],"fr":["Automatiser les interactions du navigateur pour les tests d''authentification","Générer des suites de tests pour la validation des points de terminaison d''API","Déboguer les tests instables en utilisant des stratégies de test avancées"],"de":["Automatisierung von Browser-Interaktionen für Authentifizierungstests","Erstellung von Test-Suites für die Validierung von API-Endpunkten","Fehlersuche bei flaky-Tests unter Verwendung von erweiterten Teststrategien"],"pt":["Automatizar interações do navegador para testes de autenticação","Gerar conjuntos de testes para validação de pontos de extremidade de API","Depurar testes instáveis usando estratégias de teste avançadas"],"ru":["Автоматизировать взаимодействие браузера для тестирования аутентификации","Генерировать наборы тестов для проверки конечных точек API","Отлаживать нестабильные тесты, используя продвинутые стратегии тестирования"],"ar":["أتمتة التفاعلات المتصفح لاختبار المصادقة","توليد مجموعات اختبار لتحقق من نقاط النهاية API","تصحيح الاختبارات غير المستقرة باستخدام استراتيجيات اختبار متقدمة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Playwright configuration and setup","Dependent on CI/CD pipeline integration","May require additional fixes for flaky tests"],"zh":["需要Playwright的配置和设置","依赖于CI/CD管道集成","可能需要为脆弱的测试进行额外的修复"],"ja":["Playwrightの設定とセットアップが必要","CI/CDパイプライン統合に依存","脆弱なテストのための追加の修正が必要になる場合"],"ko":["Playwright의 구성 및 설정이 필요","CI/CD 파이프라인 통합에 의존","부실한 테스트에 대한 추가 수정이 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere configuración y configuración de Playwright","Dependiente de la integración del pipeline de CI/CD","Puede requerir correcciones adicionales para pruebas inestables"],"fr":["Nécessite la configuration et la mise en place de Playwright","Dépend de l''intégration du pipeline CI/CD","Peut nécessiter des corrections supplémentaires pour les tests instables"],"de":["Benötigt Playwright-Konfiguration und -Einrichtung","Abhängig von der CI/CD-Pipeline-Integration","Kann zusätzliche Korrekturen für flaky-Tests erfordern"],"pt":["Exige configuração e instalação do Playwright","Depende da integração do pipeline CI/CD","Pode exigir correções adicionais para testes instáveis"],"ru":["Требует конфигурации и настройки Playwright","Зависит от интеграции конвейера CI/CD","Может потребовать дополнительных исправлений для нестабильных тестов"],"ar":["يتطلب تكوين Playwright وإعداده","يعتمد على تكامل أنابيب CI/CD","يمكن أن يتطلب إصلاحات إضافية للاختبارات غير المستقرة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"f84ae93c159bf6ecef5a60c9735dc82d96bc5f977ef52eb71678b66722acf684","qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('anthropics/skills/docx', 'official', 'anthropics', 'skills', 'anthropics/skills', 'docx', 79615, 8312, 80, '2026-03-01T05:03:43Z', '2026-03-01T05:08:44.339Z', 'cfbabd72b1aec7dfaad988fb6e5e16b27dc744b9a00cae15db9045e95f53903e', '{"id":"anthropics/skills/docx","name":"docx","description":{"zh":"Docx技能用于创建、读取、编辑和操作Word文档，支持触发器如Word文档、.docx文件、报告、备忘录等","ja":"Docxスキルは、Word文書を作成、読み取り、編集、操作するために使用され、Word文書、.docxファイル、報告書、メモ等のトリガーをサポート","ko":"Docx 스킬은 워드 문서를 생성, 읽기, 편집 및 조작하는 데 사용되며 워드 문서, .docx 파일, 보고서, 메모 등 트리거를 지원","es":"La habilidad de AI para documentos Word (.docx) permite crear, leer, editar y manipular archivos de Word con formato profesional.","fr":"La compétence en IA pour les documents Word (.docx) permet de créer, de lire, d''éditer et de manipuler des fichiers Word avec un format professionnel.","de":"Die KI-Fähigkeit für Word-Dokumente (.docx) ermöglicht das Erstellen, Lesen, Bearbeiten und Manipulieren von Word-Dateien im professionellen Format.","pt":"A skill docx é uma ferramenta de IA que permite criar, editar e manipular documentos Word. Ela é útil para produzir relatórios, memorandos e cartas com formatação avançada.","ru":"Навык docx - это инструмент ИИ, который позволяет создавать, редактировать и манипулировать документами Word. Он полезен для создания отчетов, заметок и писем с продвинутой форматировкой.","ar":"المهارة docx هي أداة ذكاء اصطناعي تمكن من إنشاء وحرر وتنسيق مستندات الوورد. إنها مفيدة لإنشاء تقارير ومراسلات ورسائل مع تنسيق متقدم.","en":"Use this skill whenever the user wants to create, read, edit, or manipulate Word documents (.docx files). Triggers include: any mention of \\Word doc\\, \\word document\\, \\.docx\\, or requests to produce professional documents with formatting like tables of contents, headings, page numbers, or letter..."},"owner":"anthropics","repo":"skills","repoPath":"anthropics/skills","stars":79615,"forks":8312,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T05:03:43Z","topics":["agent-skills"],"skillMd":{"name":"docx","description":"Use this skill whenever the user wants to create, read, edit, or manipulate Word documents (.docx files). Triggers include: any mention of Word doc, word document, .docx, or requests to produce professional documents with formatting like tables of contents, headings, page numbers, or letterheads. Also use when extracting or reorganizing content from .docx files, inserting or replacing images in documents, performing find-and-replace in Word files, working with tracked changes or comments, or converting content into a polished Word document. If the user asks for a report, memo, letter, template, or similar deliverable as a Word or .docx file, use this skill. Do NOT use for PDFs, spreadsheets, Google Docs, or general coding tasks unrelated to document generation.","bodyPreview":"# DOCX creation, editing, and analysis\n\n## Overview\n\nA .docx file is a ZIP archive containing XML files.\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Task | Approach |\n|------|----------|\n| Read/analyze content | `pandoc` or unpack for raw XML |\n| Create new document | Use `docx-js` - see Creating New Documents below |\n| Edit existing document | Unpack → edit XML → repack - see Editing Existing Documents below |\n\n### Converting .doc to .docx\n\nLegacy `.doc` files must be converted before editing:\n\n```bash\npython scrip","body":"# DOCX creation, editing, and analysis\n\n## Overview\n\nA .docx file is a ZIP archive containing XML files.\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Task | Approach |\n|------|----------|\n| Read/analyze content | `pandoc` or unpack for raw XML |\n| Create new document | Use `docx-js` - see Creating New Documents below |\n| Edit existing document | Unpack → edit XML → repack - see Editing Existing Documents below |\n\n### Converting .doc to .docx\n\nLegacy `.doc` files must be converted before editing:\n\n```bash\npython scripts/office/soffice.py --headless --convert-to docx document.doc\n```\n\n### Reading Content\n\n```bash\n# Text extraction with tracked changes\npandoc --track-changes=all document.docx -o output.md\n\n# Raw XML access\npython scripts/office/unpack.py document.docx unpacked/\n```\n\n### Converting to Images\n\n```bash\npython scripts/office/soffice.py --headless --convert-to pdf document.docx\npdftoppm -jpeg -r 150 document.pdf page\n```\n\n### Accepting Tracked Changes\n\nTo produce a clean document with all tracked changes accepted (requires LibreOffice):\n\n```bash\npython scripts/accept_changes.py input.docx output.docx\n```\n\n---\n\n## Creating New Documents\n\nGenerate .docx files with JavaScript, then validate. Install: `npm install -g docx`\n\n### Setup\n```javascript\nconst { Document, Packer, Paragraph, TextRun, Table, TableRow, TableCell, ImageRun,\n        Header, Footer, AlignmentType, PageOrientation, LevelFormat, ExternalHyperlink,\n        InternalHyperlink, Bookmark, FootnoteReferenceRun, PositionalTab,\n        PositionalTabAlignment, PositionalTabRelativeTo, PositionalTabLeader,\n        TabStopType, TabStopPosition, Column, SectionType,\n        TableOfContents, HeadingLevel, BorderStyle, WidthType, ShadingType,\n        VerticalAlign, PageNumber, PageBreak } = require(''docx'');\n\nconst doc = new Document({ sections: [{ children: [/* content */] }] });\nPacker.toBuffer(doc).then(buffer => fs.writeFileSync(\"doc.docx\", buffer));\n```\n\n### Validation\nAfter creating the file, validate it. If validation fails, unpack, fix the XML, and repack.\n```bash\npython scripts/office/validate.py doc.docx\n```\n\n### Page Size\n\n```javascript\n// CRITICAL: docx-js defaults to A4, not US Letter\n// Always set page size explicitly for consistent results\nsections: [{\n  properties: {\n    page: {\n      size: {\n        width: 12240,   // 8.5 inches in DXA\n        height: 15840   // 11 inches in DXA\n      },\n      margin: { top: 1440, right: 1440, bottom: 1440, left: 1440 } // 1 inch margins\n    }\n  },\n  children: [/* content */]\n}]\n```\n\n**Common page sizes (DXA units, 1440 DXA = 1 inch):**\n\n| Paper | Width | Height | Content Width (1\" margins) |\n|-------|-------|--------|---------------------------|\n| US Letter | 12,240 | 15,840 | 9,360 |\n| A4 (default) | 11,906 | 16,838 | 9,026 |\n\n**Landscape orientation:** docx-js swaps width/height internally, so pass portrait dimensions and let it handle the swap:\n```javascript\nsize: {\n  width: 12240,   // Pass SHORT edge as width\n  height: 15840,  // Pass LONG edge as height\n  orientation: PageOrientation.LANDSCAPE  // docx-js swaps them in the XML\n},\n// Content width = 15840 - left margin - right margin (uses the long edge)\n```\n\n### Styles (Override Built-in Headings)\n\nUse Arial as the default font (universally supported). Keep titles black for readability.\n\n```javascript\nconst doc = new Document({\n  styles: {\n    default: { document: { run: { font: \"Arial\", size: 24 } } }, // 12pt default\n    paragraphStyles: [\n      // IMPORTANT: Use exact IDs to override built-in styles\n      { id: \"Heading1\", name: \"Heading 1\", basedOn: \"Normal\", next: \"Normal\", quickFormat: true,\n        run: { size: 32, bold: true, font: \"Arial\" },\n        paragraph: { spacing: { before: 240, after: 240 }, outlineLevel: 0 } }, // outlineLevel required for TOC\n      { id: \"Heading2\", name: \"Heading 2\", basedOn: \"Normal\", next: \"Normal\", quickFormat: true,\n        run: { size: 28, bold: true, font: \"Arial\" },\n        paragraph: { spacing: { before: 180, after: 180 }, outlineLevel: 1 } },\n    ]\n  },\n  sections: [{\n    children: [\n      new Paragraph({ heading: HeadingLevel.HEADING_1, children: [new TextRun(\"Title\")] }),\n    ]\n  }]\n});\n```\n\n### Lists (NEVER use unicode bullets)\n\n```javascript\n// ❌ WRONG - never manually insert bullet characters\nnew Paragraph({ children: [new TextRun(\"• Item\")] })  // BAD\nnew Paragraph({ children: [new TextRun(\"\\u2022 Item\")] })  // BAD\n\n// ✅ CORRECT - use numbering config with LevelFormat.BULLET\nconst doc = new Document({\n  numbering: {\n    config: [\n      { reference: \"bullets\",\n        levels: [{ level: 0, format: LevelFormat.BULLET, text: \"•\", alignment: AlignmentType.LEFT,\n          style: { paragraph: { indent: { left: 720, hanging: 360 } } } }] },\n      { reference: \"numbers\",\n        levels: [{ level: 0, format: LevelFormat.DECIMAL, text: \"%1.\", alignment: AlignmentType.LEFT,\n          style: { paragraph: { indent: { left: 720, hanging: 360 } } } }] },\n    ]\n  },\n  sections: [{\n    children: [\n      new Paragraph({ numbering: { reference: \"bullets\", level: 0 },\n        children: [new TextRun(\"Bullet item\")] }),\n      new Paragraph({ numbering: { reference: \"numbers\", level: 0 },\n        children: [new TextRun(\"Numbered item\")] }),\n    ]\n  }]\n});\n\n// ⚠️ Each reference creates INDEPENDENT numbering\n// Same reference = continues (1,2,3 then 4,5,6)\n// Different reference = restarts (1,2,3 then 1,2,3)\n```\n\n### Tables\n\n**CRITICAL: Tables need dual widths** - set both `columnWidths` on the table AND `width` on each cell. Without both, tables render incorrectly on some platforms.\n\n```javascript\n// CRITICAL: Always set table width for consistent rendering\n// CRITICAL: Use ShadingType.CLEAR (not SOLID) to prevent black backgrounds\nconst border = { style: BorderStyle.SINGLE, size: 1, color: \"CCCCCC\" };\nconst borders = { top: border, bottom: border, left: border, right: border };\n\nnew Table({\n  width: { size: 9360, type: WidthType.DXA }, // Always use DXA (percentages break in Google Docs)\n  columnWidths: [4680, 4680], // Must sum to table width (DXA: 1440 = 1 inch)\n  rows: [\n    new TableRow({\n      children: [\n        new TableCell({\n          borders,\n          width: { size: 4680, type: WidthType.DXA }, // Also set on each cell\n          shading: { fill: \"D5E8F0\", type: ShadingType.CLEAR }, // CLEAR not SOLID\n          margins: { top: 80, bottom: 80, left: 120, right: 120 }, // Cell padding (internal, not added to width)\n          children: [new Paragraph({ children: [new TextRun(\"Cell\")] })]\n        })\n      ]\n    })\n  ]\n})\n```\n\n**Table width calculation:**\n\nAlways use `WidthType.DXA` — `WidthType.PERCENTAGE` breaks in Google Docs.\n\n```javascript\n// Table width = sum of columnWidths = content width\n// US Letter with 1\" margins: 12240 - 2880 = 9360 DXA\nwidth: { size: 9360, type: WidthType.DXA },\ncolumnWidths: [7000, 2360]  // Must sum to table width\n```\n\n**Width rules:**\n- **Always use `WidthType.DXA`** — never `WidthType.PERCENTAGE` (incompatible with Google Docs)\n- Table width must equal the sum of `columnWidths`\n- Cell `width` must match corresponding `columnWidth`\n- Cell `margins` are internal padding - they reduce content area, not add to cell width\n- For full-width tables: use content width (page width minus left and right margins)\n\n### Images\n\n```javascript\n// CRITICAL: type parameter is REQUIRED\nnew Paragraph({\n  children: [new ImageRun({\n    type: \"png\", // Required: png, jpg, jpeg, gif, bmp, svg\n    data: fs.readFileSync(\"image.png\"),\n    transformation: { width: 200, height: 150 },\n    altText: { title: \"Title\", description: \"Desc\", name: \"Name\" } // All three required\n  })]\n})\n```\n\n### Page Breaks\n\n```javascript\n// CRITICAL: PageBreak must be inside a Paragraph\nnew Paragraph({ children: [new PageBreak()] })\n\n// Or use pageBreakBefore\nnew Paragraph({ pageBreakBefore: true, children: [new TextRun(\"New page\")] })\n```\n\n### Hyperlinks\n\n```javascript\n// External link\nnew Paragraph({\n  children: [new ExternalHyperlink({\n    children: [new TextRun({ text: \"Click here\", style: \"Hyperlink\" })],\n    link: \"https://example.com\",\n  })]\n})\n\n// Internal link (bookmark + reference)\n// 1. Create bookmark at destination\nnew Paragraph({ heading: HeadingLevel.HEADING_1, children: [\n  new Bookmark({ id: \"chapter1\", children: [new TextRun(\"Chapter 1\")] }),\n]})\n// 2. Link to it\nnew Paragraph({ children: [new InternalHyperlink({\n  children: [new TextRun({ text: \"See Chapter 1\", style: \"Hyperlink\" })],\n  anchor: \"chapter1\",\n})]})\n```\n\n### Footnotes\n\n```javascript\nconst doc = new Document({\n  footnotes: {\n    1: { children: [new Paragraph(\"Source: Annual Report 2024\")] },\n    2: { children: [new Paragraph(\"See appendix for methodology\")] },\n  },\n  sections: [{\n    children: [new Paragraph({\n      children: [\n        new TextRun(\"Revenue grew 15%\"),\n        new FootnoteReferenceRun(1),\n        new TextRun(\" using adjusted metrics\"),\n        new FootnoteReferenceRun(2),\n      ],\n    })]\n  }]\n});\n```\n\n### Tab Stops\n\n```javascript\n// Right-align text on same line (e.g., date opposite a title)\nnew Paragraph({\n  children: [\n    new TextRun(\"Company Name\"),\n    new TextRun(\"\\tJanuary 2025\"),\n  ],\n  tabStops: [{ type: TabStopType.RIGHT, position: TabStopPosition.MAX }],\n})\n\n// Dot leader (e.g., TOC-style)\nnew Paragraph({\n  children: [\n    new TextRun(\"Introduction\"),\n    new TextRun({ children: [\n      new PositionalTab({\n        alignment: PositionalTabAlignment.RIGHT,\n        relativeTo: PositionalTabRelativeTo.MARGIN,\n        leader: PositionalTabLeader.DOT,\n      }),\n      \"3\",\n    ]}),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n### Multi-Column Layouts\n\n```javascript\n// Equal-width columns\nsections: [{\n  properties: {\n    column: {\n      count: 2,          // number of columns\n      space: 720,        // gap between columns in DXA (720 = 0.5 inch)\n      equalWidth: true,\n      separate: true,    // vertical line between columns\n    },\n  },\n  children: [/* content flows naturally across columns */]\n}]\n\n// Custom-width columns (equalWidth must be false)\nsections: [{\n  properties: {\n    column: {\n      equalWidth: false,\n      children: [\n        new Column({ width: 5400, space: 720 }),\n        new Column({ width: 3240 }),\n      ],\n    },\n  },\n  children: [/* content */]\n}]\n```\n\nForce a column break with a new section using `type: SectionType.NEXT_COLUMN`.\n\n### Table of Contents\n\n```javascript\n// CRITICAL: Headings must use HeadingLevel ONLY - no custom styles\nnew TableOfContents(\"Table of Contents\", { hyperlink: true, headingStyleRange: \"1-3\" })\n```\n\n### Headers/Footers\n\n```javascript\nsections: [{\n  properties: {\n    page: { margin: { top: 1440, right: 1440, bottom: 1440, left: 1440 } } // 1440 = 1 inch\n  },\n  headers: {\n    default: new Header({ children: [new Paragraph({ children: [new TextRun(\"Header\")] })] })\n  },\n  footers: {\n    default: new Footer({ children: [new Paragraph({\n      children: [new TextRun(\"Page \"), new TextRun({ children: [PageNumber.CURRENT] })]\n    })] })\n  },\n  children: [/* content */]\n}]\n```\n\n### Critical Rules for docx-js\n\n- **Set page size explicitly** - docx-js defaults to A4; use US Letter (12240 x 15840 DXA) for US documents\n- **Landscape: pass portrait dimensions** - docx-js swaps width/height internally; pass short edge as `width`, long edge as `height`, and set `orientation: PageOrientation.LANDSCAPE`\n- **Never use `\\n`** - use separate Paragraph elements\n- **Never use unicode bullets** - use `LevelFormat.BULLET` with numbering config\n- **PageBreak must be in Paragraph** - standalone creates invalid XML\n- **ImageRun requires `type`** - always specify png/jpg/etc\n- **Always set table `width` with DXA** - never use `WidthType.PERCENTAGE` (breaks in Google Docs)\n- **Tables need dual widths** - `columnWidths` array AND cell `width`, both must match\n- **Table width = sum of columnWidths** - for DXA, ensure they add up exactly\n- **Always add cell margins** - use `margins: { top: 80, bottom: 80, left: 120, right: 120 }` for readable padding\n- **Use `ShadingType.CLEAR`** - never SOLID for table shading\n- **Never use tables as dividers/rules** - cells have minimum height and render as empty boxes (including in headers/footers); use `border: { bottom: { style: BorderStyle.SINGLE, size: 6, color: \"2E75B6\", space: 1 } }` on a Paragraph instead. For two-column footers, use tab stops (see Tab Stops section), not tables\n- **TOC requires HeadingLevel only** - no custom styles on heading paragraphs\n- **Override built-in styles** - use exact IDs: \"Heading1\", \"Heading2\", etc.\n- **Include `outlineLevel`** - required for TOC (0 for H1, 1 for H2, etc.)\n\n---\n\n## Editing Existing Documents\n\n**Follow all 3 steps in order.**\n\n### Step 1: Unpack\n```bash\npython scripts/office/unpack.py document.docx unpacked/\n```\nExtracts XML, pretty-prints, merges adjacent runs, and converts smart quotes to XML entities (`&#x201C;` etc.) so they survive editing. Use `--merge-runs false` to skip run merging.\n\n### Step 2: Edit XML\n\nEdit files in `unpacked/word/`. See XML Reference below for patterns.\n\n**Use \"Claude\" as the author** for tracked changes and comments, unless the user explicitly requests use of a different name.\n\n**Use the Edit tool directly for string replacement. Do not write Python scripts.** Scripts introduce unnecessary complexity. The Edit tool shows exactly what is being replaced.\n\n**CRITICAL: Use smart quotes for new content.** When adding text with apostrophes or quotes, use XML entities to produce smart quotes:\n```xml\n<!-- Use these entities for professional typography -->\n<w:t>Here&#x2019;s a quote: &#x201C;Hello&#x201D;</w:t>\n```\n| Entity | Character |\n|--------|-----------|\n| `&#x2018;` | ‘ (left single) |\n| `&#x2019;` | ’ (right single / apostrophe) |\n| `&#x201C;` | “ (left double) |\n| `&#x201D;` | ” (right double) |\n\n**Adding comments:** Use `comment.py` to handle boilerplate across multiple XML files (text must be pre-escaped XML):\n```bash\npython scripts/comment.py unpacked/ 0 \"Comment text with &amp; and &#x2019;\"\npython scripts/comment.py unpacked/ 1 \"Reply text\" --parent 0  # reply to comment 0\npython scripts/comment.py unpacked/ 0 \"Text\" --author \"Custom Author\"  # custom author name\n```\nThen add markers to document.xml (see Comments in XML Reference).\n\n### Step 3: Pack\n```bash\npython scripts/office/pack.py unpacked/ output.docx --original document.docx\n```\nValidates with auto-repair, condenses XML, and creates DOCX. Use `--validate false` to skip.\n\n**Auto-repair will fix:**\n- `durableId` >= 0x7FFFFFFF (regenerates valid ID)\n- Missing `xml:space=\"preserve\"` on `<w:t>` with whitespace\n\n**Auto-repair won''t fix:**\n- Malformed XML, invalid element nesting, missing relationships, schema violations\n\n### Common Pitfalls\n\n- **Replace entire `<w:r>` elements**: When adding tracked changes, replace the whole `<w:r>...</w:r>` block with `<w:del>...<w:ins>...` as siblings. Don''t inject tracked change tags inside a run.\n- **Preserve `<w:rPr>` formatting**: Copy the original run''s `<w:rPr>` block into your tracked change runs to maintain bold, font size, etc.\n\n---\n\n## XML Reference\n\n### Schema Compliance\n\n- **Element order in `<w:pPr>`**: `<w:pStyle>`, `<w:numPr>`, `<w:spacing>`, `<w:ind>`, `<w:jc>`, `<w:rPr>` last\n- **Whitespace**: Add `xml:space=\"preserve\"` to `<w:t>` with leading/trailing spaces\n- **RSIDs**: Must be 8-digit hex (e.g., `00AB1234`)\n\n### Tracked Changes\n\n**Insertion:**\n```xml\n<w:ins w:id=\"1\" w:author=\"Claude\" w:date=\"2025-01-01T00:00:00Z\">\n  <w:r><w:t>inserted text</w:t></w:r>\n</w:ins>\n```\n\n**Deletion:**\n```xml\n<w:del w:id=\"2\" w:author=\"Claude\" w:date=\"2025-01-01T00:00:00Z\">\n  <w:r><w:delText>deleted text</w:delText></w:r>\n</w:del>\n```\n\n**Inside `<w:del>`**: Use `<w:delText>` instead of `<w:t>`, and `<w:delInstrText>` instead of `<w:instrText>`.\n\n**Minimal edits** - only mark what changes:\n```xml\n<!-- Change \"30 days\" to \"60 days\" -->\n<w:r><w:t>The term is </w:t></w:r>\n<w:del w:id=\"1\" w:author=\"Claude\" w:date=\"...\">\n  <w:r><w:delText>30</w:delText></w:r>\n</w:del>\n<w:ins w:id=\"2\" w:author=\"Claude\" w:date=\"...\">\n  <w:r><w:t>60</w:t></w:r>\n</w:ins>\n<w:r><w:t> days.</w:t></w:r>\n```\n\n**Deleting entire paragraphs/list items** - when removing ALL content from a paragraph, also mark the paragraph mark as deleted so it merges with the next paragraph. Add `<w:del/>` inside `<w:pPr><w:rPr>`:\n```xml\n<w:p>\n  <w:pPr>\n    <w:numPr>...</w:numPr>  <!-- list numbering if present -->\n    <w:rPr>\n      <w:del w:id=\"1\" w:author=\"Claude\" w:date=\"2025-01-01T00:00:00Z\"/>\n    </w:rPr>\n  </w:pPr>\n  <w:del w:id=\"2\" w:author=\"Claude\" w:date=\"2025-01-01T00:00:00Z\">\n    <w:r><w:delText>Entire paragraph content being deleted...</w:delText></w:r>\n  </w:del>\n</w:p>\n```\nWithout the `<w:del/>` in `<w:pPr><w:rPr>`, accepting changes leaves an empty paragraph/list item.\n\n**Rejecting another author''s insertion** - nest deletion inside their insertion:\n```xml\n<w:ins w:author=\"Jane\" w:id=\"5\">\n  <w:del w:author=\"Claude\" w:id=\"10\">\n    <w:r><w:delText>their inserted text</w:delText></w:r>\n  </w:del>\n</w:ins>\n```\n\n**Restoring another author''s deletion** - add insertion after (don''t modify their deletion):\n```xml\n<w:del w:author=\"Jane\" w:id=\"5\">\n  <w:r><w:delText>deleted text</w:delText></w:r>\n</w:del>\n<w:ins w:author=\"Claude\" w:id=\"10\">\n  <w:r><w:t>deleted text</w:t></w:r>\n</w:ins>\n```\n\n### Comments\n\nAfter running `comment.py` (see Step 2), add markers to document.xml. For replies, use `--parent` flag and nest markers inside the parent''s.\n\n**CRITICAL: `<w:commentRangeStart>` and `<w:commentRangeEnd>` are siblings of `<w:r>`, never inside `<w:r>`.**\n\n```xml\n<!-- Comment markers are direct children of w:p, never inside w:r -->\n<w:commentRangeStart w:id=\"0\"/>\n<w:del w:id=\"1\" w:author=\"Claude\" w:date=\"2025-01-01T00:00:00Z\">\n  <w:r><w:delText>deleted</w:delText></w:r>\n</w:del>\n<w:r><w:t> more text</w:t></w:r>\n<w:commentRangeEnd w:id=\"0\"/>\n<w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val=\"CommentReference\"/></w:rPr><w:commentReference w:id=\"0\"/></w:r>\n\n<!-- Comment 0 with reply 1 nested inside -->\n<w:commentRangeStart w:id=\"0\"/>\n  <w:commentRangeStart w:id=\"1\"/>\n  <w:r><w:t>text</w:t></w:r>\n  <w:commentRangeEnd w:id=\"1\"/>\n<w:commentRangeEnd w:id=\"0\"/>\n<w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val=\"CommentReference\"/></w:rPr><w:commentReference w:id=\"0\"/></w:r>\n<w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val=\"CommentReference\"/></w:rPr><w:commentReference w:id=\"1\"/></w:r>\n```\n\n### Images\n\n1. Add image file to `word/media/`\n2. Add relationship to `word/_rels/document.xml.rels`:\n```xml\n<Relationship Id=\"rId5\" Type=\".../image\" Target=\"media/image1.png\"/>\n```\n3. Add content type to `[Content_Types].xml`:\n```xml\n<Default Extension=\"png\" ContentType=\"image/png\"/>\n```\n4. Reference in document.xml:\n```xml\n<w:drawing>\n  <wp:inline>\n    <wp:extent cx=\"914400\" cy=\"914400\"/>  <!-- EMUs: 914400 = 1 inch -->\n    <a:graphic>\n      <a:graphicData uri=\".../picture\">\n        <pic:pic>\n          <pic:blipFill><a:blip r:embed=\"rId5\"/></pic:blipFill>\n        </pic:pic>\n      </a:graphicData>\n    </a:graphic>\n  </wp:inline>\n</w:drawing>\n```\n\n---\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- **pandoc**: Text extraction\n- **docx**: `npm install -g docx` (new documents)\n- **LibreOffice**: PDF conversion (auto-configured for sandboxed environments via `scripts/office/soffice.py`)\n- **Poppler**: `pdftoppm` for images\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-03-01T05:08:44.339Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能文档工具 - Docx","ja":"AIエージェント：ドキュメント作成 - Docx","ko":"AI 문서 생성 도구 - Docx","es":"Herramientas de AI para documentos Word (.docx)","fr":"Outils d''IA pour les documents Word (.docx)","de":"KI-Tools für Word-Dokumente (.docx)","pt":"Ferramentas de IA para Documentos Word - Skill docx","ru":"ИИ Агенты для Редактирования Документов Word - docx","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي لملفات الوورد - مهارة docx","en":"docx"},"description":{"zh":"Docx技能用于创建、读取、编辑和操作Word文档，支持触发器如Word文档、.docx文件、报告、备忘录等","ja":"Docxスキルは、Word文書を作成、読み取り、編集、操作するために使用され、Word文書、.docxファイル、報告書、メモ等のトリガーをサポート","ko":"Docx 스킬은 워드 문서를 생성, 읽기, 편집 및 조작하는 데 사용되며 워드 문서, .docx 파일, 보고서, 메모 등 트리거를 지원","es":"La habilidad de AI para documentos Word (.docx) permite crear, leer, editar y manipular archivos de Word con formato profesional.","fr":"La compétence en IA pour les documents Word (.docx) permet de créer, de lire, d''éditer et de manipuler des fichiers Word avec un format professionnel.","de":"Die KI-Fähigkeit für Word-Dokumente (.docx) ermöglicht das Erstellen, Lesen, Bearbeiten und Manipulieren von Word-Dateien im professionellen Format.","pt":"A skill docx é uma ferramenta de IA que permite criar, editar e manipular documentos Word. Ela é útil para produzir relatórios, memorandos e cartas com forma...","ru":"Навык docx - это инструмент ИИ, который позволяет создавать, редактировать и манипулировать документами Word. Он полезен для создания отчетов, заметок и писе...","ar":"المهارة docx هي أداة ذكاء اصطناعي تمكن من إنشاء وحرر وتنسيق مستندات الوورد. إنها مفيدة لإنشاء تقارير ومراسلات ورسائل مع تنسيق متقدم.","en":"Use this skill whenever the user wants to create, read, edit, or manipulate Word documents (.docx files). Triggers include: any mention of \\Word doc\\, \\word ..."},"definition":{"en":"Use this skill whenever the user wants to create, read, edit, or manipulate Word documents (.docx files). Triggers include: any mention of \\Word doc\\, \\word document\\, \\.docx\\, or requests to produce professional documents with formatting like tables of contents, headings, page numbers, or letterheads. Also use when extracting or reorganizing content from .docx files, inserting or replacing images in documents, performing find-and-replace in Word files, working with tracked changes or comments, or converting content into a polished Word document. If the user asks for a \\report\\, \\memo\\, \\letter\\, \\template\\, or similar deliverable as a Word or .docx file, use this skill. Do NOT use for PDFs, spreadsheets, Google Docs, or general coding tasks unrelated to document generation."},"features":{"zh":["创建和编辑Word文档","支持触发器如Word文档、.docx文件、报告、备忘录等","自动化生成专业文档","支持文档格式如表格、标题、页码等","支持图像插入和替换"],"ja":["Word文書の作成と編集","Word文書、.docxファイル、報告書、メモ等のトリガーをサポート","专业文書の自動化生成","文書形式如表、題名、ページ番号等をサポート","画像の挿入と置換をサポート"],"ko":["워드 문서 생성 및 편집","워드 문서, .docx 파일, 보고서, 메모 등 트리거 지원","전문 문서 자동화 생성","문서 형식如 표, 제목, 페이지 번호 등 지원","이미지 삽입 및 대체 지원"],"es":["Creación de documentos Word","Edición y manipulación de archivos .docx","Inserción y reemplazo de imágenes","Búsqueda y reemplazo de texto","Trabajo con cambios y comentarios","Conversión de contenido en documentos Word"],"fr":["Création de documents Word","Édition et manipulation de fichiers .docx","Insertion et remplacement d''images","Recherche et remplacement de texte","Travail avec les modifications et les commentaires","Conversion de contenu en documents Word"],"de":["Erstellung von Word-Dokumenten","Bearbeitung und Manipulation von .docx-Dateien","Einfügen und Ersetzen von Bildern","Suchen und Ersetzen von Text","Arbeiten mit Änderungen und Kommentaren","Konvertierung von Inhalten in Word-Dokumente"],"pt":["Criação de documentos Word","Edição e manipulação de arquivos .docx","Inserção e substituição de imagens","Formatação avançada com tabelas de conteúdo e cabeçalhos","Extração e reorganização de conteúdo"],"ru":["Создание документов Word","Редактирование и манипулирование файлами .docx","Вставка и замена изображений","Продвинутая форматировка с таблицами содержания и заголовками","Извлечение и реорганизация контента"],"ar":["إنشاء مستندات الوورد","تحرير وتنسيق ملفات .docx","إدراج واستبدال الصور","تنسيق متقدم مع جداول المحتوى والعناوين","استخراج واعادة تنظيم المحتوى"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能文档工具","Docx技能","Word文档创建","Word文档编辑","专业文档自动化生成","文档格式支持"],"ja":["AIエージェント","Docxスキル","Word文書作成","Word文書編集","专业文書自動化生成","文書形式サポート"],"ko":["AI 문서 생성 도구","Docx 스킬","워드 문서 생성","워드 문서 편집","전문 문서 자동화 생성","문서 형식 지원"],"es":["herramientas de AI para Word","documentos Word","archivos .docx","creación de documentos","edición de documentos","manipulación de archivos","inserción de imágenes","búsqueda y reemplazo","trabajo con cambios","conversión de contenido"],"fr":["outils d''IA pour Word","documents Word","fichiers .docx","création de documents","édition de documents","manipulation de fichiers","insertion d''images","recherche et remplacement","travail avec les modifications","conversion de contenu"],"de":["KI-Tools für Word","Word-Dokumente","Dateien .docx","Erstellung von Dokumenten","Bearbeitung von Dokumenten","Manipulation von Dateien","Einfügen von Bildern","Suchen und Ersetzen","Arbeiten mit Änderungen","Konvertierung von Inhalten"],"pt":["skill docx","ferramentas de IA para documentos Word","manipulação de arquivos .docx","criação de relatórios","edição de documentos Word","formatação avançada"],"ru":["навык docx","инструменты ИИ для документов Word","манипулирование файлами .docx","создание отчетов","редактирование документов Word","продвинутая форматировка"],"ar":["مهارة docx","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي لمستندات الوورد","تنسيق ملفات .docx","إنشاء تقارير","تحرير مستندات الوورد","تنسيق متقدم"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Essential for Document Automation Agents that need to programmatically create and manipulate professional Word documents.","zh":"对于需要以编程方式创建和操作专业 Word 文档的文档自动化 AI Agent 而言，此技能是必不可少的。","ja":"プログラムによってプロフェッショナルな Word 文書を作成および操作する必要がある文書自動化エージェントにとって必須です。","ko":"프로그래밍 방식으로 전문 Word 문서를 생성하고 조작해야 하는 문서 자동화 에이전트에게 필수적인 기술입니다.","es":"Esencial para los agentes de automatización de documentos que necesitan crear y manipular programáticamente documentos de Word profesionales.","fr":"Essentiel pour les agents d''automatisation de documents qui doivent créer et manipuler programmatiquement des documents Word professionnels.","de":"Unverzichtbar für Dokumentenautomatisierungs-Agents, die programmgesteuert professionelle Word-Dokumente erstellen und bearbeiten müssen.","pt":"Essencial para Agentes de Automação de Documentos que precisam criar e manipular programaticamente documentos profissionais do Word.","ru":"Необходим для Агентов автоматизации документов, которым требуется программно создавать и управлять профессиональными документами Word.","ar":"أساسي لوكلاء أتمتة المستندات الذين يحتاجون إلى إنشاء ومعالجة مستندات Word المهنية برمجيًا."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables direct manipulation of .docx files as ZIP archives containing XML components, allowing agents to unpack, modify, and repack document structures. Provides capabilities for advanced formatting including tables of contents, headings, page numbers, and letterheads using docx-js library and XML editing techniques.","zh":"支持将 .docx 文件作为包含 XML 组件的 ZIP 存档进行直接操作，使 Agent 能够解包、修改和重新打包文档结构。通过使用 docx-js 库和 XML 编辑技术，提供包括目录、标题、页码和信头在内的高级格式化功能。","ja":"XML コンポーネントを含む ZIP アーカイブとして .docx ファイルを直接操作できるようにし、エージェントが文書構造を解凍、変更、再パッケージ化することを可能にします。docx-js ライブラリと XML 編集技術を使用して、目次、見出し、ページ番号、レターヘッドなどの高度な書式設定機能を提供します。","ko":"XML 구성 요소를 포함하는 ZIP 아카이브로 .docx 파일을 직접 조작할 수 있게 하여 에이전트가 문서 구조를 압축 해제, 수정 및 재포장할 수 있도록 합니다. docx-js 라이브러리와 XML 편집 기술을 사용하여 목차, 제목, 페이지 번호, 레터헤드를 포함한 고급 형식 지정 기능을 제공합니다.","es":"Permite la manipulación directa de archivos .docx como archivos ZIP que contienen componentes XML, permitiendo a los agentes descomprimir, modificar y reempaquetar estructuras de documentos. Proporciona capacidades para formato avanzado, incluyendo tablas de contenido, encabezados, números de página y membrettes utilizando la librería docx-js y técnicas de edición XML.","fr":"Permet la manipulation directe des fichiers .docx en tant qu''archives ZIP contenant des composants XML, permettant aux agents de décompresser, modifier et recompresser les structures de documents. Fournit des capacités de mise en forme avancée, y compris les tables des matières, les en-têtes, les numéros de page et les en-têtes de lettre en utilisant la bibliothèque docx-js et les techniques d''édition XML.","de":"Ermöglicht die direkte Manipulation von .docx-Dateien als ZIP-Archive, die XML-Komponenten enthalten, und erlaubt es Agents, Dokumentstrukturen zu entpacken, zu modifizieren und neu zu verpacken. Bietet Funktionen für erweiterte Formatierung, einschließlich Inhaltsverzeichnissen, Überschriften, Seitenzahlen und Briefköpfen unter Verwendung der docx-js-Bibliothek und XML-Bearbeitungstechniken.","pt":"Permite a manipulação direta de arquivos .docx como arquivos ZIP contendo componentes XML, permitindo que os agentes descompactem, modifiquem e recompactem estruturas de documentos. Fornece capacidades para formatação avançada, incluindo índices, cabeçalhos, números de página e logotipos usando a biblioteca docx-js e técnicas de edição XML.","ru":"Позволяет напрямую управлять файлами .docx как ZIP-архивами, содержащими XML-компоненты, что дает агентам возможность распаковывать, изменять и переупаковывать структуры документов. Обеспечивает возможности для расширенного форматирования, включая оглавления, заголовки, номера страниц и фирменные бланки с использованием библиотеки docx-js и методов редактирования XML.","ar":"يتيح التلاعب المباشر بملفات .docx كأرشيفات ZIP تحتوي على مكونات XML، مما يسمح للوكلاء بفك وتعديل وإعادة تجميع هياكل المستندات. يوفر إمكانيات للتنسيق المتقدم بما في ذلك جداول المحتويات والعناوين وأرقام الصفحات واللوائح الرسمية باستخدام مكتبة docx-js وتقنيات تحرير XML."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating professional reports with automated formatting","Extracting and reorganizing content from existing Word documents","Performing batch find-and-replace operations across multiple files","Managing tracked changes and comments programmatically"],"zh":["使用自动格式化功能生成专业报告","从现有的 Word 文档中提取内容并重新组织","跨多个文件执行批量查找和替换操作","以编程方式管理跟踪的更改和评论"],"ja":["自動フォーマットを使用したプロフェッショナルなレポートの生成","既存の Word 文書からのコンテンツの抽出と再編成","複数のファイルにわたる一括検索と置換操作の実行","プログラムによる変更履歴とコメントの管理"],"ko":["자동 서식 지정으로 전문 보고서 생성","기존 Word 문서에서 콘텐츠 추출 및 재구성","여러 파일에 걸쳐 일괄 찾기 및 바꾸기 작업 수행","프로그래밍 방식으로 추적된 변경 내용 및 주석 관리"],"es":["Generación de informes profesionales con formato automatizado","Extracción y reorganización de contenido de documentos de Word existentes","Realización de operaciones de buscar y reemplazar por lotes en múltiples archivos","Gestión programática de cambios realizados y comentarios"],"fr":["Génération de rapports professionnels avec mise en forme automatisée","Extraction et réorganisation du contenu à partir de documents Word existants","Exécution d''opérations de recherche et remplacement par lots sur plusieurs fichiers","Gestion programmatique des modifications suivies et des commentaires"],"de":["Erstellung professioneller Berichte mit automatisierter Formatierung","Extrahieren und Neuorganisieren von Inhalten aus vorhandenen Word-Dokumenten","Durchführung von Batch-Suchen-und-Ersetzen-Operationen über mehrere Dateien hinweg","Programmgesteuerte Verwaltung von Nachverfolgungsänderungen und Kommentaren"],"pt":["Geração de relatórios profissionais com formatação automatizada","Extração e reorganização de conteúdo de documentos do Word existentes","Execução de operações em lote de localizar e substituir em vários arquivos","Gerenciamento programático de alterações controladas e comentários"],"ru":["Генерация профессиональных отчетов с автоматическим форматированием","Извлечение и реорганизация содержимого из существующих документов Word","Выполнение пакетных операций поиска и замены в нескольких файлах","Программное управление отслеживаемыми изменениями и комментариями"],"ar":["إنشاء تقارير مهنية بتنسيق آلي","استخراج وإعادة تنظيم المحتوى من مستندات Word الموجودة","إجراء عمليات البحث والاستبدال المجمعة عبر ملفات متعددة","إدارة التغييرات المتعقبة والتعليقات برمجيًا"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires conversion from legacy .doc format before editing","Needs XML manipulation expertise for complex edits","No direct PDF or Google Docs support"],"zh":["编辑前需要从旧版 .doc 格式进行转换","复杂的编辑需要 XML 操作专业知识","不直接支持 PDF 或 Google Docs"],"ja":["編集前に従来の .doc 形式からの変換が必要","複雑な編集には XML 操作の専門知識が必要","PDF または Google Docs の直接サポートなし"],"ko":["편집 전 레거시 .doc 형식에서 변환이 필요함","복잡한 편집에는 XML 조작 전문 지식 필요","PDF 또는 Google Docs 직접 지원 안 함"],"es":["Requiere conversión desde el formato heredado .doc antes de la edición","Necesita experiencia en manipulación XML para ediciones complejas","No tiene soporte directo para PDF o Google Docs"],"fr":["Nécessite une conversion depuis l''ancien format .doc avant l''édition","Requiert une expertise en manipulation XML pour les modifications complexes","Pas de support direct pour PDF ou Google Docs"],"de":["Erfordert Konvertierung vom Legacy-.doc-Format vor der Bearbeitung","Benötigt XML-Manipulationskenntnisse für komplexe Bearbeitungen","Keine direkte Unterstützung für PDF oder Google Docs"],"pt":["Requer conversão do formato legado .doc antes da edição","Requer conhecimentos de manipulação de XML para edições complexas","Sem suporte direto para PDF ou Google Docs"],"ru":["Требуется преобразование из устаревшего формата .doc перед редактированием","Требует опыта работы с манипуляцией XML для сложных правок","Отсутствует прямая поддержка PDF или Google Docs"],"ar":["يتطلب التحويل من التنسيق القديم .doc قبل التحرير","يحتاج إلى خبرة في معالجة XML للتعديلات المعقدة","لا يوجد دعم مباشر لـ PDF أو Google Docs"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"cfbabd72b1aec7dfaad988fb6e5e16b27dc744b9a00cae15db9045e95f53903e","repoEtag":"W/\"795252861eecc48ed1ad31a16e978d71a3eaafc45d526a6e594e873a66c8f11d\"","qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('anthropics/skills/mcp-builder', 'official', 'anthropics', 'skills', 'anthropics/skills', 'mcp-builder', 79615, 8312, 80, '2026-03-01T05:03:43Z', '2026-03-01T05:08:45.114Z', '0f4592dcb53cf2b5d6b7febee6b4152018b565551a1c29e3c612f57b218ab295', '{"id":"anthropics/skills/mcp-builder","name":"mcp-builder","description":{"zh":"mcp-builder是创建高质量MCP服务器的指南，用于LLM与外部服务的交互，支持Python和Node/TypeScript","ja":"mcp-builderは、AIエージェントのための高品質のMCPサーバー構築ガイドです。PythonとNode/TypeScriptをサポートしています","ko":"mcp-builder는 AI 에이전트를 위한 고품질의 MCP 서버 구축 가이드입니다. Python 및 Node/TypeScript를 지원합니다","es":"El MCP Builder es una guía para crear servidores MCP que permiten a los LLM interactuar con servicios externos","fr":"Le MCP Builder est un guide pour créer des serveurs MCP qui permettent aux LLM d''interagir avec des services externes","de":"Der MCP Builder ist eine Anleitung zum Erstellen von MCP-Servern, die es LLMs ermöglichen, mit externen Diensten zu interagieren","pt":"O construtor MCP é uma ferramenta para criar servidores MCP que permitem que LLMs interajam com serviços externos. Aprenda a integrar APIs com Python e Node/TypeScript","ru":"ИИ Агенты: MCP Builder - инструмент для создания серверов MCP, которые позволяют LLMs взаимодействовать с внешними сервисами. Узнайте, как интегрировать API с Python и Node/TypeScript","ar":"مبني MCP هو أداة لإنشاء خوادم MCP التي تسمح للنماذج اللغة بالتفاعل مع الخدمات الخارجية. تعلم كيفية интегра واجهات برمجة التطبيقات مع Python و Node/TypeScript","en":"Guide for creating high-quality MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers that enable LLMs to interact with external services through well-designed tools. Use when building MCP servers to integrate external APIs or services, whether in Python (FastMCP) or Node/TypeScript (MCP SDK)."},"owner":"anthropics","repo":"skills","repoPath":"anthropics/skills","stars":79615,"forks":8312,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T05:03:43Z","topics":["agent-skills"],"skillMd":{"name":"mcp-builder","description":"Guide for creating high-quality MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers that enable LLMs to interact with external services through well-designed tools. Use when building MCP servers to integrate external APIs or services, whether in Python (FastMCP) or Node/TypeScript (MCP SDK).","bodyPreview":"# MCP Server Development Guide\n\n## Overview\n\nCreate MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers that enable LLMs to interact with external services through well-designed tools. The quality of an MCP server is measured by how well it enables LLMs to accomplish real-world tasks.\n\n---\n\n# Process\n\n## 🚀 High-Level Workflow\n\nCreating a high-quality MCP server involves four main phases:\n\n### Phase 1: Deep Research and Planning\n\n#### 1.1 Understand Modern MCP Design\n\n**API Coverage vs. Workflow Tools:**\nBalan","body":"# MCP Server Development Guide\n\n## Overview\n\nCreate MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers that enable LLMs to interact with external services through well-designed tools. The quality of an MCP server is measured by how well it enables LLMs to accomplish real-world tasks.\n\n---\n\n# Process\n\n## 🚀 High-Level Workflow\n\nCreating a high-quality MCP server involves four main phases:\n\n### Phase 1: Deep Research and Planning\n\n#### 1.1 Understand Modern MCP Design\n\n**API Coverage vs. Workflow Tools:**\nBalance comprehensive API endpoint coverage with specialized workflow tools. Workflow tools can be more convenient for specific tasks, while comprehensive coverage gives agents flexibility to compose operations. Performance varies by client—some clients benefit from code execution that combines basic tools, while others work better with higher-level workflows. When uncertain, prioritize comprehensive API coverage.\n\n**Tool Naming and Discoverability:**\nClear, descriptive tool names help agents find the right tools quickly. Use consistent prefixes (e.g., `github_create_issue`, `github_list_repos`) and action-oriented naming.\n\n**Context Management:**\nAgents benefit from concise tool descriptions and the ability to filter/paginate results. Design tools that return focused, relevant data. Some clients support code execution which can help agents filter and process data efficiently.\n\n**Actionable Error Messages:**\nError messages should guide agents toward solutions with specific suggestions and next steps.\n\n#### 1.2 Study MCP Protocol Documentation\n\n**Navigate the MCP specification:**\n\nStart with the sitemap to find relevant pages: `https://modelcontextprotocol.io/sitemap.xml`\n\nThen fetch specific pages with `.md` suffix for markdown format (e.g., `https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/draft.md`).\n\nKey pages to review:\n- Specification overview and architecture\n- Transport mechanisms (streamable HTTP, stdio)\n- Tool, resource, and prompt definitions\n\n#### 1.3 Study Framework Documentation\n\n**Recommended stack:**\n- **Language**: TypeScript (high-quality SDK support and good compatibility in many execution environments e.g. MCPB. Plus AI models are good at generating TypeScript code, benefiting from its broad usage, static typing and good linting tools)\n- **Transport**: Streamable HTTP for remote servers, using stateless JSON (simpler to scale and maintain, as opposed to stateful sessions and streaming responses). stdio for local servers.\n\n**Load framework documentation:**\n\n- **MCP Best Practices**: [📋 View Best Practices](./reference/mcp_best_practices.md) - Core guidelines\n\n**For TypeScript (recommended):**\n- **TypeScript SDK**: Use WebFetch to load `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/main/README.md`\n- [⚡ TypeScript Guide](./reference/node_mcp_server.md) - TypeScript patterns and examples\n\n**For Python:**\n- **Python SDK**: Use WebFetch to load `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/main/README.md`\n- [🐍 Python Guide](./reference/python_mcp_server.md) - Python patterns and examples\n\n#### 1.4 Plan Your Implementation\n\n**Understand the API:**\nReview the service''s API documentation to identify key endpoints, authentication requirements, and data models. Use web search and WebFetch as needed.\n\n**Tool Selection:**\nPrioritize comprehensive API coverage. List endpoints to implement, starting with the most common operations.\n\n---\n\n### Phase 2: Implementation\n\n#### 2.1 Set Up Project Structure\n\nSee language-specific guides for project setup:\n- [⚡ TypeScript Guide](./reference/node_mcp_server.md) - Project structure, package.json, tsconfig.json\n- [🐍 Python Guide](./reference/python_mcp_server.md) - Module organization, dependencies\n\n#### 2.2 Implement Core Infrastructure\n\nCreate shared utilities:\n- API client with authentication\n- Error handling helpers\n- Response formatting (JSON/Markdown)\n- Pagination support\n\n#### 2.3 Implement Tools\n\nFor each tool:\n\n**Input Schema:**\n- Use Zod (TypeScript) or Pydantic (Python)\n- Include constraints and clear descriptions\n- Add examples in field descriptions\n\n**Output Schema:**\n- Define `outputSchema` where possible for structured data\n- Use `structuredContent` in tool responses (TypeScript SDK feature)\n- Helps clients understand and process tool outputs\n\n**Tool Description:**\n- Concise summary of functionality\n- Parameter descriptions\n- Return type schema\n\n**Implementation:**\n- Async/await for I/O operations\n- Proper error handling with actionable messages\n- Support pagination where applicable\n- Return both text content and structured data when using modern SDKs\n\n**Annotations:**\n- `readOnlyHint`: true/false\n- `destructiveHint`: true/false\n- `idempotentHint`: true/false\n- `openWorldHint`: true/false\n\n---\n\n### Phase 3: Review and Test\n\n#### 3.1 Code Quality\n\nReview for:\n- No duplicated code (DRY principle)\n- Consistent error handling\n- Full type coverage\n- Clear tool descriptions\n\n#### 3.2 Build and Test\n\n**TypeScript:**\n- Run `npm run build` to verify compilation\n- Test with MCP Inspector: `npx @modelcontextprotocol/inspector`\n\n**Python:**\n- Verify syntax: `python -m py_compile your_server.py`\n- Test with MCP Inspector\n\nSee language-specific guides for detailed testing approaches and quality checklists.\n\n---\n\n### Phase 4: Create Evaluations\n\nAfter implementing your MCP server, create comprehensive evaluations to test its effectiveness.\n\n**Load [✅ Evaluation Guide](./reference/evaluation.md) for complete evaluation guidelines.**\n\n#### 4.1 Understand Evaluation Purpose\n\nUse evaluations to test whether LLMs can effectively use your MCP server to answer realistic, complex questions.\n\n#### 4.2 Create 10 Evaluation Questions\n\nTo create effective evaluations, follow the process outlined in the evaluation guide:\n\n1. **Tool Inspection**: List available tools and understand their capabilities\n2. **Content Exploration**: Use READ-ONLY operations to explore available data\n3. **Question Generation**: Create 10 complex, realistic questions\n4. **Answer Verification**: Solve each question yourself to verify answers\n\n#### 4.3 Evaluation Requirements\n\nEnsure each question is:\n- **Independent**: Not dependent on other questions\n- **Read-only**: Only non-destructive operations required\n- **Complex**: Requiring multiple tool calls and deep exploration\n- **Realistic**: Based on real use cases humans would care about\n- **Verifiable**: Single, clear answer that can be verified by string comparison\n- **Stable**: Answer won''t change over time\n\n#### 4.4 Output Format\n\nCreate an XML file with this structure:\n\n```xml\n<evaluation>\n  <qa_pair>\n    <question>Find discussions about AI model launches with animal codenames. One model needed a specific safety designation that uses the format ASL-X. What number X was being determined for the model named after a spotted wild cat?</question>\n    <answer>3</answer>\n  </qa_pair>\n<!-- More qa_pairs... -->\n</evaluation>\n```\n\n---\n\n# Reference Files\n\n## 📚 Documentation Library\n\nLoad these resources as needed during development:\n\n### Core MCP Documentation (Load First)\n- **MCP Protocol**: Start with sitemap at `https://modelcontextprotocol.io/sitemap.xml`, then fetch specific pages with `.md` suffix\n- [📋 MCP Best Practices](./reference/mcp_best_practices.md) - Universal MCP guidelines including:\n  - Server and tool naming conventions\n  - Response format guidelines (JSON vs Markdown)\n  - Pagination best practices\n  - Transport selection (streamable HTTP vs stdio)\n  - Security and error handling standards\n\n### SDK Documentation (Load During Phase 1/2)\n- **Python SDK**: Fetch from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/main/README.md`\n- **TypeScript SDK**: Fetch from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/main/README.md`\n\n### Language-Specific Implementation Guides (Load During Phase 2)\n- [🐍 Python Implementation Guide](./reference/python_mcp_server.md) - Complete Python/FastMCP guide with:\n  - Server initialization patterns\n  - Pydantic model examples\n  - Tool registration with `@mcp.tool`\n  - Complete working examples\n  - Quality checklist\n\n- [⚡ TypeScript Implementation Guide](./reference/node_mcp_server.md) - Complete TypeScript guide with:\n  - Project structure\n  - Zod schema patterns\n  - Tool registration with `server.registerTool`\n  - Complete working examples\n  - Quality checklist\n\n### Evaluation Guide (Load During Phase 4)\n- [✅ Evaluation Guide](./reference/evaluation.md) - Complete evaluation creation guide with:\n  - Question creation guidelines\n  - Answer verification strategies\n  - XML format specifications\n  - Example questions and answers\n  - Running an evaluation with the provided scripts\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-03-01T05:08:45.114Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能代理mcp-builder指南","ja":"AIエージェントのmcp-builderガイド","ko":"AI 에이전트 mcp-builder 개발 가이드","es":"Herramientas de AI: Guía de MCP Builder","fr":"Outils d''IA: Guide de construction MCP","de":"KI-Tools: MCP-Builder-Anleitung","pt":"Construtor MCP: Ferramentas de IA para Servidores","ru":"ИИ Агенты: MCP Builder для Серверов","ar":"مبني MCP: أدوات ذكاء اصطناعي للخادم","en":"mcp-builder"},"description":{"zh":"mcp-builder是创建高质量MCP服务器的指南，用于LLM与外部服务的交互，支持Python和Node/TypeScript","ja":"mcp-builderは、AIエージェントのための高品質のMCPサーバー構築ガイドです。PythonとNode/TypeScriptをサポートしています","ko":"mcp-builder는 AI 에이전트를 위한 고품질의 MCP 서버 구축 가이드입니다. Python 및 Node/TypeScript를 지원합니다","es":"El MCP Builder es una guía para crear servidores MCP que permiten a los LLM interactuar con servicios externos","fr":"Le MCP Builder est un guide pour créer des serveurs MCP qui permettent aux LLM d''interagir avec des services externes","de":"Der MCP Builder ist eine Anleitung zum Erstellen von MCP-Servern, die es LLMs ermöglichen, mit externen Diensten zu interagieren","pt":"O construtor MCP é uma ferramenta para criar servidores MCP que permitem que LLMs interajam com serviços externos. Aprenda a integrar APIs com Python e Node/...","ru":"ИИ Агенты: MCP Builder - инструмент для создания серверов MCP, которые позволяют LLMs взаимодействовать с внешними сервисами. Узнайте, как интегрировать API ...","ar":"مبني MCP هو أداة لإنشاء خوادم MCP التي تسمح للنماذج اللغة بالتفاعل مع الخدمات الخارجية. تعلم كيفية интегра واجهات برمجة التطبيقات مع Python و Node/TypeScript","en":"Guide for creating high-quality MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers that enable LLMs to interact with external services through well-designed tools. Use whe..."},"definition":{"en":"Guide for creating high-quality MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers that enable LLMs to interact with external services through well-designed tools. Use when building MCP servers to integrate external APIs or services, whether in Python (FastMCP) or Node/TypeScript (MCP SDK)."},"features":{"zh":["支持Python和Node/TypeScript","高质量的MCP服务器构建","LLM与外部服务的交互","API Coverage和Workflow Tools的平衡","现代MCP设计的深入理解","四个主要阶段的开发过程"],"ja":["PythonとNode/TypeScriptをサポート","高品質のMCPサーバーの構築","LLMと外部サービスとの接続","API CoverageとWorkflow Toolsのバランス","モダンMCP設計の深い理解","4つの主要な開発段階"],"ko":["Python 및 Node/TypeScript 지원","고품질의 MCP 서버 구축","LLM 및 외부 서비스와의 상호 작용","API Coverage 및 Workflow Tools의 균형","최신 MCP 설계에 대한 깊은 이해","4개의 주요 개발 단계"],"es":["Creación de servidores MCP de alta calidad","Integración de APIs externas con LLMs","Herramientas de diseño para interactuar con servicios externos","Compatibilidad con Python y Node/TypeScript"],"fr":["Création de serveurs MCP de haute qualité","Intégration d''API externes avec des LLM","Outils de conception pour interagir avec des services externes","Compatibilité avec Python et Node/TypeScript"],"de":["Erstellung von hochwertigen MCP-Servern","Integration von externen APIs mit LLMs","Design-Tools für die Interaktion mit externen Diensten","Kompatibilität mit Python und Node/TypeScript"],"pt":["Criação de servidores MCP de alta qualidade","Integração com APIs externas","Suporte a Python e Node/TypeScript","Ferramentas de design de workflow","Otimização para LLMs"],"ru":["Создание высококачественных серверов MCP","Интеграция с внешними API","Поддержка Python и Node/TypeScript","Инструменты для проектирования рабочих процессов","Оптимизация для LLMs"],"ar":["إنشاء خوادم MCP عالية الجودة","التكامل مع واجهات برمجة التطبيقات الخارجية","دعم Python و Node/TypeScript","أدوات تصميم سير العمل","تحسين الأداء للنماذج اللغة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","mcp-builder","MCP服务器","LLM","外部服务","Python","Node/TypeScript","API Coverage","Workflow Tools"],"ja":["AIエージェント","mcp-builder","MCPサーバー","LLM","外部サービス","Python","Node/TypeScript","API Coverage","Workflow Tools"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","mcp-builder","MCP 서버","LLM","외부 서비스","Python","Node/TypeScript","API Coverage","Workflow Tools"],"es":["Herramientas de AI","Servidores MCP","LLMs","Integración de APIs","Diseño de herramientas","Python","Node/TypeScript"],"fr":["Outils d''IA","Serveurs MCP","LLMs","Intégration d''API","Conception d''outils","Python","Node/TypeScript"],"de":["KI-Tools","MCP-Server","LLMs","Integration von APIs","Design von Tools","Python","Node/TypeScript"],"pt":["construtor MCP","servidores MCP","LLMs","APIs externas","Python","Node/TypeScript","ferramentas de IA"],"ru":["ИИ Агенты","MCP Builder","серверы MCP","LLMs","внешние API","Python","Node/TypeScript","инструменты ИИ"],"ar":["مبني MCP","خوادم MCP","النماذج اللغة","واجهات برمجة التطبيقات الخارجية","Python","Node/TypeScript","أدوات ذكاء اصطناعي"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Cursor, Windsurf, or Claude Code needing to integrate external services with LLMs through well-designed MCP servers","zh":"适合于像Cursor、Windsurf或Claude Code这样的AI代理，需要将外部服务与LLMs通过设计良好的MCP服务器集成","ja":"Cursor、Windsurf、またはClaude CodeのようなAIエージェントに適しており、外部サービスをLLMsと統合するために、設計の良いMCPサーバーを必要とする","ko":"Cursor, Windsurf 또는 Claude Code와 같은 AI 에이전트에 적합하며, 외부 서비스를 LLM과 잘設計된 MCP 서버를 통해 통합하는 데 필요합니다","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Cursor, Windsurf o Claude Code que necesitan integrar servicios externos con LLMs a través de servidores MCP bien diseñados","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA comme Cursor, Windsurf ou Claude Code ayant besoin d''intégrer des services externes avec des LLMs via des serveurs MCP bien conçus","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents wie Cursor, Windsurf oder Claude Code, die externe Dienste mit LLMs über gut entworfene MCP-Server integrieren müssen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA como Cursor, Windsurf ou Claude Code que precisam integrar serviços externos com LLMs por meio de servidores MCP bem projetados","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, таких как Cursor, Windsurf или Claude Code, которые нуждаются в интеграции внешних сервисов с LLMs через хорошо спроектированные серверы MCP","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Cursor و Windsurf أو Claude Code الذي يحتاج إلى دمج الخدمات الخارجية مع LLMs من خلال خوادم MCP مصممة جيدًا"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create high-quality MCP servers, enabling seamless interactions between LLMs and external services using protocols like Model Context Protocol, with support for Python via FastMCP and Node/TypeScript via MCP SDK","zh":"赋予代理创建高质量的MCP服务器的能力，实现LLMs和外部服务之间的无缝交互，使用如Model Context Protocol的协议，并通过FastMCP支持Python，通过MCP SDK支持Node/TypeScript","ja":"エージェントが高品質のMCPサーバーを作成する能力を提供し、Model Context Protocolなどのプロトコルを使用して、LLMsと外部サービスとのシームレスなやり取りを可能にし、FastMCPを介してPython、MCP SDKを介してNode/TypeScriptをサポートする","ko":"에이전트가 고품질의 MCP 서버를 생성할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여, Model Context Protocol과 같은 프로토콜을 사용하여 LLM과 외부 서비스 간의无缝な 상호작용을 가능하게 하며, FastMCP를 통해 Python 및 MCP SDK를 통해 Node/TypeScript를 지원합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear servidores MCP de alta calidad, lo que permite interacciones sin problemas entre LLMs y servicios externos utilizando protocolos como Model Context Protocol, con soporte para Python a través de FastMCP y Node/TypeScript a través de MCP SDK","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des serveurs MCP de haute qualité, permettant des interactions sans accroc entre les LLMs et les services externes en utilisant des protocoles comme Model Context Protocol, avec un support pour Python via FastMCP et Node/TypeScript via MCP SDK","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, hochwertige MCP-Server zu erstellen, wodurch eine nahtlose Interaktion zwischen LLMs und externen Diensten mithilfe von Protokollen wie Model Context Protocol ermöglicht wird, mit Unterstützung für Python über FastMCP und Node/TypeScript über MCP SDK","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar servidores MCP de alta qualidade, permitindo interações sem problemas entre LLMs e serviços externos usando protocolos como Model Context Protocol, com suporte ao Python via FastMCP e Node/TypeScript via MCP SDK","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать серверы MCP высокого качества, что позволяет осуществлять беспрепятственное взаимодействие между LLMs и внешними сервисами с использованием протоколов, таких как Model Context Protocol, с поддер