их API для автоматизации реальных задач","Проектирование инструментов рабочего процесса для взаимодействия LLMs с внешними сервисами","Разработка серверов MCP высокого качества для расширенных возможностей LLMs"],"ar":["بناء خوادم MCP لدمج واجهات برمجة التطبيقات الخارجية لتحقيق آلي لعمليات العالم الحقيقي","تصميم أدوات سير العمل للتفاعل بين LLMs والخدمات الخارجية","تنمية خوادم MCP عالية الجودة لمزايا متقدمة من LLMs"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of MCP design principles","Limited to Python and Node/TypeScript implementations via FastMCP and MCP SDK","Dependent on external service APIs for integration"],"zh":["需要MCP设计原则的知识","仅限于通过FastMCP和MCP SDK的Python和Node/TypeScript实现","依赖于外部服务API进行集成"],"ja":["MCP設計の原則に関する知識が必要","FastMCPとMCP SDKを介したPythonとNode/TypeScriptへの実装のみ","外部サービスAPIへの依存による統合"],"ko":["MCP 설계 원칙에 대한 지식 필요","FastMCP 및 MCP SDK를 통한 Python 및 Node/TypeScript 구현에만 제한","외부 서비스 API에 대한 의존적인 통합"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de los principios de diseño de MCP","Limitado a implementaciones de Python y Node/TypeScript a través de FastMCP y MCP SDK","Dependiente de las APIs de servicios externos para la integración"],"fr":["Nécessite une connaissance des principes de conception de MCP","Limité aux implémentations Python et Node/TypeScript via FastMCP et MCP SDK","Dépendant des API de services externes pour l''intégration"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse der MCP-Designprinzipien","Begrenzt auf Python- und Node/TypeScript-Implementierungen über FastMCP und MCP SDK","Von externen Dienst-APIs für die Integration abhängig"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento dos princípios de design de MCP","Limitado a implementações em Python e Node/TypeScript via FastMCP e MCP SDK","Dependente de APIs de serviços externos para integração"],"ru":["Требует знания принципов проектирования MCP","Ограничен реализациями на Python и Node/TypeScript через FastMCP и MCP SDK","Зависит от API внешних сервисов для интеграции"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة مبادئ تصميم MCP","محدود بالتنفيذ بلغات Python و Node/TypeScript من خلال FastMCP و MCP SDK","يعتمد على واجهات برمجة التطبيقات للخدمات الخارجية للدمج"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"0f4592dcb53cf2b5d6b7febee6b4152018b565551a1c29e3c612f57b218ab295","repoEtag":"W/\"795252861eecc48ed1ad31a16e978d71a3eaafc45d526a6e594e873a66c8f11d\"","qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('anthropics/skills/pdf', 'official', 'anthropics', 'skills', 'anthropics/skills', 'pdf', 79615, 8312, 80, '2026-03-01T05:03:43Z', '2026-03-01T05:08:45.119Z', '9f78b8359fbd4943ad260a7a1e436e5a96503406d6c34e99f69223d647d85b9c', '{"id":"anthropics/skills/pdf","name":"pdf","description":{"zh":"本指南介绍使用Python库和命令行工具进行PDF处理的基本操作","ja":"このガイドでは、Pythonライブラリとコマンドラインツールを使用してPDFを処理する基本的な操作について説明します","ko":"이 가이드는 Python 라이브러리와 명령줄 도구를 사용하여 PDF를 처리하는 기본적인 작업에 대해 설명합니다","es":"Guía para procesar PDF con Python y herramientas de línea de comandos","fr":"Guide pour traiter les PDF avec Python et des outils de ligne de commande","de":"Anleitung zum Verarbeiten von PDF mit Python und Kommandozeilen-Tools","pt":"Guia de processamento de PDF para desenvolvedores, com exemplos em Python","ru":"Руководство по работе с PDF для разработчиков, с примерами на Python","ar":"دليل معالجة PDF للمطورين، مع أمثلة بلغة Python","en":"Use this skill whenever the user wants to do anything with PDF files. This includes reading or extracting text/tables from PDFs, combining or merging multiple PDFs into one, splitting PDFs apart, rotating pages, adding watermarks, creating new PDFs, filling PDF forms, encrypting/decrypting PDFs, ..."},"owner":"anthropics","repo":"skills","repoPath":"anthropics/skills","stars":79615,"forks":8312,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T05:03:43Z","topics":["agent-skills"],"skillMd":{"name":"pdf","description":"Use this skill whenever the user wants to do anything with PDF files. This includes reading or extracting text/tables from PDFs, combining or merging multiple PDFs into one, splitting PDFs apart, rotating pages, adding watermarks, creating new PDFs, filling PDF forms, encrypting/decrypting PDFs, extracting images, and OCR on scanned PDFs to make them searchable. If the user mentions a .pdf file or asks to produce one, use this skill.","bodyPreview":"# PDF Processing Guide\n\n## Overview\n\nThis guide covers essential PDF processing operations using Python libraries and command-line tools. For advanced features, JavaScript libraries, and detailed examples, see REFERENCE.md. If you need to fill out a PDF form, read FORMS.md and follow its instructions.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```python\nfrom pypdf import PdfReader, PdfWriter\n\n# Read a PDF\nreader = PdfReader(\"document.pdf\")\nprint(f\"Pages: {len(reader.pages)}\")\n\n# Extract text\ntext = \"\"\nfor page in reader.","body":"# PDF Processing Guide\n\n## Overview\n\nThis guide covers essential PDF processing operations using Python libraries and command-line tools. For advanced features, JavaScript libraries, and detailed examples, see REFERENCE.md. If you need to fill out a PDF form, read FORMS.md and follow its instructions.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```python\nfrom pypdf import PdfReader, PdfWriter\n\n# Read a PDF\nreader = PdfReader(\"document.pdf\")\nprint(f\"Pages: {len(reader.pages)}\")\n\n# Extract text\ntext = \"\"\nfor page in reader.pages:\n    text += page.extract_text()\n```\n\n## Python Libraries\n\n### pypdf - Basic Operations\n\n#### Merge PDFs\n```python\nfrom pypdf import PdfWriter, PdfReader\n\nwriter = PdfWriter()\nfor pdf_file in [\"doc1.pdf\", \"doc2.pdf\", \"doc3.pdf\"]:\n    reader = PdfReader(pdf_file)\n    for page in reader.pages:\n        writer.add_page(page)\n\nwith open(\"merged.pdf\", \"wb\") as output:\n    writer.write(output)\n```\n\n#### Split PDF\n```python\nreader = PdfReader(\"input.pdf\")\nfor i, page in enumerate(reader.pages):\n    writer = PdfWriter()\n    writer.add_page(page)\n    with open(f\"page_{i+1}.pdf\", \"wb\") as output:\n        writer.write(output)\n```\n\n#### Extract Metadata\n```python\nreader = PdfReader(\"document.pdf\")\nmeta = reader.metadata\nprint(f\"Title: {meta.title}\")\nprint(f\"Author: {meta.author}\")\nprint(f\"Subject: {meta.subject}\")\nprint(f\"Creator: {meta.creator}\")\n```\n\n#### Rotate Pages\n```python\nreader = PdfReader(\"input.pdf\")\nwriter = PdfWriter()\n\npage = reader.pages[0]\npage.rotate(90)  # Rotate 90 degrees clockwise\nwriter.add_page(page)\n\nwith open(\"rotated.pdf\", \"wb\") as output:\n    writer.write(output)\n```\n\n### pdfplumber - Text and Table Extraction\n\n#### Extract Text with Layout\n```python\nimport pdfplumber\n\nwith pdfplumber.open(\"document.pdf\") as pdf:\n    for page in pdf.pages:\n        text = page.extract_text()\n        print(text)\n```\n\n#### Extract Tables\n```python\nwith pdfplumber.open(\"document.pdf\") as pdf:\n    for i, page in enumerate(pdf.pages):\n        tables = page.extract_tables()\n        for j, table in enumerate(tables):\n            print(f\"Table {j+1} on page {i+1}:\")\n            for row in table:\n                print(row)\n```\n\n#### Advanced Table Extraction\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\nwith pdfplumber.open(\"document.pdf\") as pdf:\n    all_tables = []\n    for page in pdf.pages:\n        tables = page.extract_tables()\n        for table in tables:\n            if table:  # Check if table is not empty\n                df = pd.DataFrame(table[1:], columns=table[0])\n                all_tables.append(df)\n\n# Combine all tables\nif all_tables:\n    combined_df = pd.concat(all_tables, ignore_index=True)\n    combined_df.to_excel(\"extracted_tables.xlsx\", index=False)\n```\n\n### reportlab - Create PDFs\n\n#### Basic PDF Creation\n```python\nfrom reportlab.lib.pagesizes import letter\nfrom reportlab.pdfgen import canvas\n\nc = canvas.Canvas(\"hello.pdf\", pagesize=letter)\nwidth, height = letter\n\n# Add text\nc.drawString(100, height - 100, \"Hello World!\")\nc.drawString(100, height - 120, \"This is a PDF created with reportlab\")\n\n# Add a line\nc.line(100, height - 140, 400, height - 140)\n\n# Save\nc.save()\n```\n\n#### Create PDF with Multiple Pages\n```python\nfrom reportlab.lib.pagesizes import letter\nfrom reportlab.platypus import SimpleDocTemplate, Paragraph, Spacer, PageBreak\nfrom reportlab.lib.styles import getSampleStyleSheet\n\ndoc = SimpleDocTemplate(\"report.pdf\", pagesize=letter)\nstyles = getSampleStyleSheet()\nstory = []\n\n# Add content\ntitle = Paragraph(\"Report Title\", styles[''Title''])\nstory.append(title)\nstory.append(Spacer(1, 12))\n\nbody = Paragraph(\"This is the body of the report. \" * 20, styles[''Normal''])\nstory.append(body)\nstory.append(PageBreak())\n\n# Page 2\nstory.append(Paragraph(\"Page 2\", styles[''Heading1'']))\nstory.append(Paragraph(\"Content for page 2\", styles[''Normal'']))\n\n# Build PDF\ndoc.build(story)\n```\n\n#### Subscripts and Superscripts\n\n**IMPORTANT**: Never use Unicode subscript/superscript characters (₀₁₂₃₄₅₆₇₈₉, ⁰¹²³⁴⁵⁶⁷⁸⁹) in ReportLab PDFs. The built-in fonts do not include these glyphs, causing them to render as solid black boxes.\n\nInstead, use ReportLab''s XML markup tags in Paragraph objects:\n```python\nfrom reportlab.platypus import Paragraph\nfrom reportlab.lib.styles import getSampleStyleSheet\n\nstyles = getSampleStyleSheet()\n\n# Subscripts: use <sub> tag\nchemical = Paragraph(\"H<sub>2</sub>O\", styles[''Normal''])\n\n# Superscripts: use <super> tag\nsquared = Paragraph(\"x<super>2</super> + y<super>2</super>\", styles[''Normal''])\n```\n\nFor canvas-drawn text (not Paragraph objects), manually adjust font the size and position rather than using Unicode subscripts/superscripts.\n\n## Command-Line Tools\n\n### pdftotext (poppler-utils)\n```bash\n# Extract text\npdftotext input.pdf output.txt\n\n# Extract text preserving layout\npdftotext -layout input.pdf output.txt\n\n# Extract specific pages\npdftotext -f 1 -l 5 input.pdf output.txt  # Pages 1-5\n```\n\n### qpdf\n```bash\n# Merge PDFs\nqpdf --empty --pages file1.pdf file2.pdf -- merged.pdf\n\n# Split pages\nqpdf input.pdf --pages . 1-5 -- pages1-5.pdf\nqpdf input.pdf --pages . 6-10 -- pages6-10.pdf\n\n# Rotate pages\nqpdf input.pdf output.pdf --rotate=+90:1  # Rotate page 1 by 90 degrees\n\n# Remove password\nqpdf --password=mypassword --decrypt encrypted.pdf decrypted.pdf\n```\n\n### pdftk (if available)\n```bash\n# Merge\npdftk file1.pdf file2.pdf cat output merged.pdf\n\n# Split\npdftk input.pdf burst\n\n# Rotate\npdftk input.pdf rotate 1east output rotated.pdf\n```\n\n## Common Tasks\n\n### Extract Text from Scanned PDFs\n```python\n# Requires: pip install pytesseract pdf2image\nimport pytesseract\nfrom pdf2image import convert_from_path\n\n# Convert PDF to images\nimages = convert_from_path(''scanned.pdf'')\n\n# OCR each page\ntext = \"\"\nfor i, image in enumerate(images):\n    text += f\"Page {i+1}:\\n\"\n    text += pytesseract.image_to_string(image)\n    text += \"\\n\\n\"\n\nprint(text)\n```\n\n### Add Watermark\n```python\nfrom pypdf import PdfReader, PdfWriter\n\n# Create watermark (or load existing)\nwatermark = PdfReader(\"watermark.pdf\").pages[0]\n\n# Apply to all pages\nreader = PdfReader(\"document.pdf\")\nwriter = PdfWriter()\n\nfor page in reader.pages:\n    page.merge_page(watermark)\n    writer.add_page(page)\n\nwith open(\"watermarked.pdf\", \"wb\") as output:\n    writer.write(output)\n```\n\n### Extract Images\n```bash\n# Using pdfimages (poppler-utils)\npdfimages -j input.pdf output_prefix\n\n# This extracts all images as output_prefix-000.jpg, output_prefix-001.jpg, etc.\n```\n\n### Password Protection\n```python\nfrom pypdf import PdfReader, PdfWriter\n\nreader = PdfReader(\"input.pdf\")\nwriter = PdfWriter()\n\nfor page in reader.pages:\n    writer.add_page(page)\n\n# Add password\nwriter.encrypt(\"userpassword\", \"ownerpassword\")\n\nwith open(\"encrypted.pdf\", \"wb\") as output:\n    writer.write(output)\n```\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Task | Best Tool | Command/Code |\n|------|-----------|--------------|\n| Merge PDFs | pypdf | `writer.add_page(page)` |\n| Split PDFs | pypdf | One page per file |\n| Extract text | pdfplumber | `page.extract_text()` |\n| Extract tables | pdfplumber | `page.extract_tables()` |\n| Create PDFs | reportlab | Canvas or Platypus |\n| Command line merge | qpdf | `qpdf --empty --pages ...` |\n| OCR scanned PDFs | pytesseract | Convert to image first |\n| Fill PDF forms | pdf-lib or pypdf (see FORMS.md) | See FORMS.md |\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- For advanced pypdfium2 usage, see REFERENCE.md\n- For JavaScript libraries (pdf-lib), see REFERENCE.md\n- If you need to fill out a PDF form, follow the instructions in FORMS.md\n- For troubleshooting guides, see REFERENCE.md\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-03-01T05:08:45.119Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能代理PDF处理","ja":"AIエージェントのPDF処理","ko":"AI 에이전트 PDF 처리","es":"Herramientas AI para Procesamiento de PDF","fr":"Outils AI pour le Traitement de PDF","de":"KI-Tools für PDF-Verarbeitung","pt":"Ferramentas de IA para Processamento de PDF","ru":"ИИ Агенты для Работы с PDF","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي لمعالجة PDF","en":"pdf"},"description":{"zh":"本指南介绍使用Python库和命令行工具进行PDF处理的基本操作","ja":"このガイドでは、Pythonライブラリとコマンドラインツールを使用してPDFを処理する基本的な操作について説明します","ko":"이 가이드는 Python 라이브러리와 명령줄 도구를 사용하여 PDF를 처리하는 기본적인 작업에 대해 설명합니다","es":"Guía para procesar PDF con Python y herramientas de línea de comandos","fr":"Guide pour traiter les PDF avec Python et des outils de ligne de commande","de":"Anleitung zum Verarbeiten von PDF mit Python und Kommandozeilen-Tools","pt":"Guia de processamento de PDF para desenvolvedores, com exemplos em Python","ru":"Руководство по работе с PDF для разработчиков, с примерами на Python","ar":"دليل معالجة PDF للمطورين، مع أمثلة بلغة Python","en":"Use this skill whenever the user wants to do anything with PDF files. This includes reading or extracting text/tables from PDFs, combining or merging multipl..."},"definition":{"en":"Use this skill whenever the user wants to do anything with PDF files. This includes reading or extracting text/tables from PDFs, combining or merging multiple PDFs into one, splitting PDFs apart, rotating pages, adding watermarks, creating new PDFs, filling PDF forms, encrypting/decrypting PDFs, extracting images, and OCR on scanned PDFs to make them searchable. If the user mentions a .pdf file or asks to produce one, use this skill."},"features":{"zh":["读取PDF文件","合并和拆分PDF文件","加密和解密PDF文件","提取PDF中的文本和图像","使用OCR技术使扫描的PDF文件可搜索"],"ja":["PDFファイルの読み取り","PDFファイルの結合と分割","PDFファイルの暗号化と復号化","PDF内のテキストと画像の抽出","OCR技術を使用してスキャナのPDFファイルを検索可能にする"],"ko":["PDF 파일 읽기","PDF 파일 결합 및 분할","PDF 파일 암호화 및 복호화","PDF中的 텍스트 및 이미지 추출","OCR 기술을 사용하여 스캔된 PDF 파일을 검색 가능하게 함"],"es":["Lectura y extracción de texto y tablas de PDF","Combinación y división de PDF","Rotación de páginas y agregado de marcas de agua","Creación de nuevos PDF y llenado de formularios","Cifrado y descifrado de PDF","Reconocimiento óptico de caracteres (OCR) en PDF escaneados"],"fr":["Lecture et extraction de texte et de tableaux de PDF","Combinaison et division de PDF","Rotation de pages et ajout de filigranes","Création de nouveaux PDF et remplissage de formulaires","Chiffrement et déchiffrement de PDF","Reconnaissance optique de caractères (OCR) dans les PDF scannés"],"de":["Lesen und Extrahieren von Text und Tabellen aus PDF","Kombinieren und Teilen von PDF","Seiten drehen und Wasserzeichen hinzufügen","Erstellen neuer PDF und Ausfüllen von Formularen","Verschlüsseln und Entschlüsseln von PDF","Optische Zeichenerkennung (OCR) in gescannten PDF"],"pt":["Leitura e extração de texto de arquivos PDF","Combinação e divisão de arquivos PDF","Adição de filigranas e criptografia de arquivos PDF","Criação de novos arquivos PDF","Preenchimento de formulários PDF"],"ru":["Чтение и извлечение текста из файлов PDF","Объединение и разделение файлов PDF","Добавление водяных знаков и шифрования файлов PDF","Создание новых файлов PDF","Заполнение форм PDF"],"ar":["قراءة و استخراج النص من ملفات PDF","دمج و تقسيم ملفات PDF","إضافة ختم مائي و تشفير ملفات PDF","إنشاء ملفات PDF جديدة","ملء استمارات PDF"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","PDF处理","Python库","命令行工具","PDF读取","PDF合并","PDF加密"],"ja":["AIエージェント","PDF処理","Pythonライブラリ","コマンドラインツール","PDF読み取り","PDF結合","PDF暗号化"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","PDF 처리","Python 라이브러리","명령줄 도구","PDF 읽기","PDF 결합","PDF 암호화"],"es":["procesamiento de pdf","herramientas ai para pdf","bibliotecas python para pdf","tratamiento de archivos pdf","automatización de tareas de pdf","reconocimiento óptico de caracteres en pdf"],"fr":["traitement de pdf","outils ai pour pdf","bibliothèques python pour pdf","traitement de fichiers pdf","automatisation de tâches de pdf","reconnaissance optique de caractères dans les pdf"],"de":["pdf-verarbeitung","ki-tools für pdf","python-bibliotheken für pdf","verarbeitung von pdf-dateien","automatisierung von pdf-aufgaben","optische zeichenerkennung in pdf"],"pt":["processamento de PDF","ferramentas de IA","bibliotecas Python","manipulação de arquivos PDF","extração de texto","combinação de arquivos","criptografia de arquivos"],"ru":["работа с PDF","ИИ Агенты","библиотеки Python","манипуляция файлами PDF","извлечение текста","объединение файлов","шифрование файлов"],"ar":["معالجة PDF","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","مكتبات Python","تعديل ملفات PDF","استخراج النص","دمج الملفات","تشفير الملفات"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Document Analysis Agents needing advanced PDF processing capabilities using Python libraries like pypdf.","zh":"非常适合需要使用Python库（如pypdf）进行高级PDF处理的文档分析代理。","ja":"Pythonライブラリ（pypdfなど）を使用した高度なPDF処理機能を必要とするドキュメント分析エージェントに最適です。","ko":"Python 라이브러리(pypdf 등)를 사용하여 고급 PDF 처리 기능을 필요로 하는 문서 분석 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Análisis de Documentos que necesitan capacidades de procesamiento de PDF avanzadas utilizando bibliotecas de Python como pypdf.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents d''Analyse de Documents nécessitant des capacités de traitement de PDF avancées en utilisant des bibliothèques Python comme pypdf.","de":"Perfekt für Dokumentenanalyse-Agents, die erweiterte PDF-Verarbeitungsfähigkeiten mit Python-Bibliotheken wie pypdf benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Documentos que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de processamento de PDF usando bibliotecas Python como pypdf.","ru":"Идеально подходит для Агентов Анализа Документов, которым требуются продвинутые возможности обработки PDF с помощью библиотек Python, таких как pypdf.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات تحليل المستندات التي تحتاج إلى قدرات متقدمة لمعالجة ملفات PDF باستخدام مكتبات Python مثل pypdf."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to extract text and tables from PDFs, merge or split PDF files, and perform OCR on scanned documents using command-line tools and JavaScript libraries, while also enabling encryption, decryption, and form filling with precise control over PDF operations.","zh":"赋予代理从PDF中提取文本和表格、合并或拆分PDF文件以及使用命令行工具和JavaScript库对扫描文档进行OCR，同时也能够对PDF操作进行加密、解密和表单填充，并且具有精确的控制。","ja":"エージェントがPDFからテキストとテーブルを抽出する、PDFファイルをマージまたは分割する、コマンドラインツールとJavaScriptライブラリを使用してスキャンドキュメントに対してOCRを実行することを可能にし、同時にPDF操作に対する暗号化、復号化、フォームの入力を正確に制御する。","ko":"에이전트가 PDF에서 텍스트와 표를 추출하고, PDF 파일을 병합 또는 분할하고, 명령줄 도구와 JavaScript 라이브러리를 사용하여 스캔된 문서에 대해 OCR을 수행할 수 있도록 하며,同時에 PDF 작업에 대한 암호화, 복호화, 양식填充 등을 정밀하게 제어할 수 있습니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a extraer texto y tablas de los PDF, combinar o dividir archivos PDF y realizar OCR en documentos escaneados utilizando herramientas de línea de comandos y bibliotecas de JavaScript, al mismo tiempo que permite el cifrado, descifrado y llenado de formularios con un control preciso sobre las operaciones de PDF.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''extraire du texte et des tableaux à partir de PDF, de fusionner ou de diviser des fichiers PDF et d''effectuer une reconnaissance optique des caractères (OCR) sur des documents scannés en utilisant des outils en ligne de commande et des bibliothèques JavaScript, tout en permettant le chiffrement, le déchiffrement et le remplissage de formulaires avec un contrôle précis sur les opérations de PDF.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agents, Text und Tabellen aus PDFs zu extrahieren, PDF-Dateien zu kombinieren oder aufzuteilen und OCR auf gescannte Dokumente mit Kommandozeilenwerkzeugen und JavaScript-Bibliotheken durchzuführen, während auch die Verschlüsselung, Entschlüsselung und Formulareingabe mit genauer Kontrolle über die PDF-Operationen ermöglicht wird.","pt":"Permite que os agentes extraiam texto e tabelas de PDFs, mesclam ou dividam arquivos PDF e realizem OCR em documentos digitalizados usando ferramentas de linha de comando e bibliotecas JavaScript, além de permitir criptografia, descriptografia e preenchimento de formulários com controle preciso sobre operações de PDF.","ru":"Позволяет агентам извлекать текст и таблицы из PDF, объединять или разделять файлы PDF, а также выполнять OCR над отсканированными документами с помощью инструментов командной строки и библиотек JavaScript, при этом обеспечивая шифрование, дешифрование и заполнение форм с точным контролем над операциями с PDF.","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من استخراج النص والجداول من ملفات PDF ودمجها أو تقسيمها وتشغيل OCR على المستندات الممسوحة ضوئيًا باستخدام أدوات سطر الأوامر ومكتبات JavaScript، بالإضافة إلى تمكين التشفير وفك التشفير وتعبئة النماذج مع التحكم الدقيق على عمليات PDF."},"useCases":{"en":["Extracting text from scanned PDFs using OCR","Merging multiple PDFs into a single document","Encrypting PDF files for secure sharing"],"zh":["使用OCR从扫描的PDF中提取文本","将多个PDF合并成一个文档","对PDF文件进行加密以便安全共享"],"ja":["OCRを使用してスキャンドキュメントからテキストを抽出する","複数のPDFを1つのドキュメントにマージする","PDFファイルを暗号化して安全に共有する"],"ko":["OCR을 사용하여 스캔된 PDF에서 텍스트를 추출하는 것","여러 개의 PDF를 하나의 문서로 병합하는 것","PDF 파일을 암호화하여 보안 공유를 하는 것"],"es":["Extraer texto de PDFs escaneados utilizando OCR","Combinar varios PDFs en un solo documento","Cifrar archivos PDF para compartir de forma segura"],"fr":["Extraire du texte à partir de PDF scannés en utilisant la reconnaissance optique des caractères (OCR)","Fusionner plusieurs PDF en un seul document","Chiffrer des fichiers PDF pour un partage sécurisé"],"de":["Text aus gescannten PDFs mithilfe von OCR extrahieren","Mehrere PDFs zu einem einzigen Dokument kombinieren","PDF-Dateien für sicheres Teilen verschlüsseln"],"pt":["Extrair texto de PDFs digitalizados usando OCR","Mesclar vários PDFs em um único documento","Criptografar arquivos PDF para compartilhamento seguro"],"ru":["Извлечение текста из отсканированных PDF с помощью OCR","Объединение нескольких PDF в один документ","Шифрование файлов PDF для безопасного обмена"],"ar":["استخراج النص من ملفات PDF الممسوحة ضوئيًا باستخدام OCR","دمج ملفات PDF متعددة في مستند واحد","تشفير ملفات PDF لمشاركتها بأمان"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Python environment with pypdf library","JavaScript libraries needed for advanced features"],"zh":["需要Python环境和pypdf库","需要JavaScript库来支持高级功能"],"ja":["Python環境とpypdfライブラリが必要","高度な機能をサポートするためにJavaScriptライブラリが必要"],"ko":["Python 환경과 pypdf 라이브러리가 필요","고급 기능을 지원하기 위해 JavaScript 라이브러리가 필요"],"es":["Requiere entorno de Python con biblioteca pypdf","Se necesitan bibliotecas de JavaScript para funciones avanzadas"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement Python avec la bibliothèque pypdf","Des bibliothèques JavaScript sont nécessaires pour les fonctionnalités avancées"],"de":["Benötigt Python-Umgebung mit pypdf-Bibliothek","JavaScript-Bibliotheken werden für erweiterte Funktionen benötigt"],"pt":["Requer ambiente Python com biblioteca pypdf","Bibliotecas JavaScript necessárias para recursos avançados"],"ru":["Требуется среда Python с библиотекой pypdf","Необходимы библиотеки JavaScript для продвинутых функций"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة Python مع مكتبة pypdf","مكتبات JavaScript مطلوبة للميزات المتقدمة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"9f78b8359fbd4943ad260a7a1e436e5a96503406d6c34e99f69223d647d85b9c","repoEtag":"W/\"795252861eecc48ed1ad31a16e978d71a3eaafc45d526a6e594e873a66c8f11d\"","qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('anthropics/skills/skill-creator', 'official', 'anthropics', 'skills', 'anthropics/skills', 'skill-creator', 79615, 8312, 80, '2026-03-01T05:03:43Z', '2026-03-01T05:08:45.830Z', 'ba8bebb2c085444120743af8dc859dd7c2592d6290e93aa5e1c08403109bdce7', '{"id":"anthropics/skills/skill-creator","name":"skill-creator","description":{"zh":"skill-creator技能提供创建有效技能的指南，帮助开发者扩展Claude的能力","ja":"skill-creatorスキルは、効果的なスキルを作成するためのガイドを提供し、開発者がClaudeの機能を拡張できるようにします","ko":"skill-creator 스킬은 효과적인 스킬을 생성하는 방법에 대한 가이드를 제공하여 개발자가 Claude의 기능을 확장할 수 있도록 합니다","es":"El creador de habilidades es una guía para desarrolladores que desean ampliar las capacidades de Claude con conocimientos y flujos de trabajo especializados","fr":"Le créateur de compétences est un guide pour les développeurs qui souhaitent étendre les capacités de Claude avec des connaissances et des flux de travail spécialisés","de":"Der Fähigkeits-Ersteller ist ein Leitfaden für Entwickler, die die Fähigkeiten von Claude mit spezialisierten Kenntnissen und Workflows erweitern möchten","pt":"O Criador de Habilidades é uma ferramenta para criar habilidades personalizadas para Ferramentas de IA, permitindo estender as capacidades da sua IA.","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Создатель Навыков - это инструмент для создания специализированных навыков для ИИ Агентов, позволяющий расширить возможности вашего ИИ.","ar":"أداة إنشاء المهارات هي أداة لإنشاء مهارات مخصصة للوكلاء الذكية، مما يسمح بتوسيع قدرات الوكلاء الذكية.","en":"Guide for creating effective skills. This skill should be used when users want to create a new skill (or update an existing skill) that extends Claudes capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, or tool integrations."},"owner":"anthropics","repo":"skills","repoPath":"anthropics/skills","stars":79615,"forks":8312,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T05:03:43Z","topics":["agent-skills"],"skillMd":{"name":"skill-creator","description":"Create new skills, modify and improve existing skills, and measure skill performance. Use when users want to create a skill from scratch, update or optimize an existing skill, run evals to test a skill, benchmark skill performance with variance analysis, or optimize a skills description for better triggering accuracy.","bodyPreview":"# Skill Creator\n\nA skill for creating new skills and iteratively improving them.\n\nAt a high level, the process of creating a skill goes like this:\n\n- Decide what you want the skill to do and roughly how it should do it\n- Write a draft of the skill\n- Create a few test prompts and run claude-with-access-to-the-skill on them\n- Help the user evaluate the results both qualitatively and quantitatively\n  - While the runs happen in the background, draft some quantitative evals if there aren''t any (if th","body":"# Skill Creator\n\nA skill for creating new skills and iteratively improving them.\n\nAt a high level, the process of creating a skill goes like this:\n\n- Decide what you want the skill to do and roughly how it should do it\n- Write a draft of the skill\n- Create a few test prompts and run claude-with-access-to-the-skill on them\n- Help the user evaluate the results both qualitatively and quantitatively\n  - While the runs happen in the background, draft some quantitative evals if there aren''t any (if there are some, you can either use as is or modify if you feel something needs to change about them). Then explain them to the user (or if they already existed, explain the ones that already exist)\n  - Use the `eval-viewer/generate_review.py` script to show the user the results for them to look at, and also let them look at the quantitative metrics\n- Rewrite the skill based on feedback from the user''s evaluation of the results (and also if there are any glaring flaws that become apparent from the quantitative benchmarks)\n- Repeat until you''re satisfied\n- Expand the test set and try again at larger scale\n\nYour job when using this skill is to figure out where the user is in this process and then jump in and help them progress through these stages. So for instance, maybe they''re like \"I want to make a skill for X\". You can help narrow down what they mean, write a draft, write the test cases, figure out how they want to evaluate, run all the prompts, and repeat.\n\nOn the other hand, maybe they already have a draft of the skill. In this case you can go straight to the eval/iterate part of the loop.\n\nOf course, you should always be flexible and if the user is like \"I don''t need to run a bunch of evaluations, just vibe with me\", you can do that instead.\n\nThen after the skill is done (but again, the order is flexible), you can also run the skill description improver, which we have a whole separate script for, to optimize the triggering of the skill.\n\nCool? Cool.\n\n## Communicating with the user\n\nThe skill creator is liable to be used by people across a wide range of familiarity with coding jargon. If you haven''t heard (and how could you, it''s only very recently that it started), there''s a trend now where the power of Claude is inspiring plumbers to open up their terminals, parents and grandparents to google \"how to install npm\". On the other hand, the bulk of users are probably fairly computer-literate.\n\nSo please pay attention to context cues to understand how to phrase your communication! In the default case, just to give you some idea:\n\n- \"evaluation\" and \"benchmark\" are borderline, but OK\n- for \"JSON\" and \"assertion\" you want to see serious cues from the user that they know what those things are before using them without explaining them\n\nIt''s OK to briefly explain terms if you''re in doubt, and feel free to clarify terms with a short definition if you''re unsure if the user will get it.\n\n---\n\n## Creating a skill\n\n### Capture Intent\n\nStart by understanding the user''s intent. The current conversation might already contain a workflow the user wants to capture (e.g., they say \"turn this into a skill\"). If so, extract answers from the conversation history first — the tools used, the sequence of steps, corrections the user made, input/output formats observed. The user may need to fill the gaps, and should confirm before proceeding to the next step.\n\n1. What should this skill enable Claude to do?\n2. When should this skill trigger? (what user phrases/contexts)\n3. What''s the expected output format?\n4. Should we set up test cases to verify the skill works? Skills with objectively verifiable outputs (file transforms, data extraction, code generation, fixed workflow steps) benefit from test cases. Skills with subjective outputs (writing style, art) often don''t need them. Suggest the appropriate default based on the skill type, but let the user decide.\n\n### Interview and Research\n\nProactively ask questions about edge cases, input/output formats, example files, success criteria, and dependencies. Wait to write test prompts until you''ve got this part ironed out.\n\nCheck available MCPs - if useful for research (searching docs, finding similar skills, looking up best practices), research in parallel via subagents if available, otherwise inline. Come prepared with context to reduce burden on the user.\n\n### Write the SKILL.md\n\nBased on the user interview, fill in these components:\n\n- **name**: Skill identifier\n- **description**: When to trigger, what it does. This is the primary triggering mechanism - include both what the skill does AND specific contexts for when to use it. All \"when to use\" info goes here, not in the body. Note: currently Claude has a tendency to \"undertrigger\" skills -- to not use them when they''d be useful. To combat this, please make the skill descriptions a little bit \"pushy\". So for instance, instead of \"How to build a simple fast dashboard to display internal Anthropic data.\", you might write \"How to build a simple fast dashboard to display internal Anthropic data. Make sure to use this skill whenever the user mentions dashboards, data visualization, internal metrics, or wants to display any kind of company data, even if they don''t explicitly ask for a ''dashboard.''\"\n- **compatibility**: Required tools, dependencies (optional, rarely needed)\n- **the rest of the skill :)**\n\n### Skill Writing Guide\n\n#### Anatomy of a Skill\n\n```\nskill-name/\n├── SKILL.md (required)\n│   ├── YAML frontmatter (name, description required)\n│   └── Markdown instructions\n└── Bundled Resources (optional)\n    ├── scripts/    - Executable code for deterministic/repetitive tasks\n    ├── references/ - Docs loaded into context as needed\n    └── assets/     - Files used in output (templates, icons, fonts)\n```\n\n#### Progressive Disclosure\n\nSkills use a three-level loading system:\n1. **Metadata** (name + description) - Always in context (~100 words)\n2. **SKILL.md body** - In context whenever skill triggers (<500 lines ideal)\n3. **Bundled resources** - As needed (unlimited, scripts can execute without loading)\n\nThese word counts are approximate and you can feel free to go longer if needed.\n\n**Key patterns:**\n- Keep SKILL.md under 500 lines; if you''re approaching this limit, add an additional layer of hierarchy along with clear pointers about where the model using the skill should go next to follow up.\n- Reference files clearly from SKILL.md with guidance on when to read them\n- For large reference files (>300 lines), include a table of contents\n\n**Domain organization**: When a skill supports multiple domains/frameworks, organize by variant:\n```\ncloud-deploy/\n├── SKILL.md (workflow + selection)\n└── references/\n    ├── aws.md\n    ├── gcp.md\n    └── azure.md\n```\nClaude reads only the relevant reference file.\n\n#### Principle of Lack of Surprise\n\nThis goes without saying, but skills must not contain malware, exploit code, or any content that could compromise system security. A skill''s contents should not surprise the user in their intent if described. Don''t go along with requests to create misleading skills or skills designed to facilitate unauthorized access, data exfiltration, or other malicious activities. Things like a \"roleplay as an XYZ\" are OK though.\n\n#### Writing Patterns\n\nPrefer using the imperative form in instructions.\n\n**Defining output formats** - You can do it like this:\n```markdown\n## Report structure\nALWAYS use this exact template:\n# [Title]\n## Executive summary\n## Key findings\n## Recommendations\n```\n\n**Examples pattern** - It''s useful to include examples. You can format them like this (but if \"Input\" and \"Output\" are in the examples you might want to deviate a little):\n```markdown\n## Commit message format\n**Example 1:**\nInput: Added user authentication with JWT tokens\nOutput: feat(auth): implement JWT-based authentication\n```\n\n### Writing Style\n\nTry to explain to the model why things are important in lieu of heavy-handed musty MUSTs. Use theory of mind and try to make the skill general and not super-narrow to specific examples. Start by writing a draft and then look at it with fresh eyes and improve it.\n\n### Test Cases\n\nAfter writing the skill draft, come up with 2-3 realistic test prompts — the kind of thing a real user would actually say. Share them with the user: [you don''t have to use this exact language] \"Here are a few test cases I''d like to try. Do these look right, or do you want to add more?\" Then run them.\n\nSave test cases to `evals/evals.json`. Don''t write assertions yet — just the prompts. You''ll draft assertions in the next step while the runs are in progress.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"skill_name\": \"example-skill\",\n  \"evals\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": 1,\n      \"prompt\": \"User''s task prompt\",\n      \"expected_output\": \"Description of expected result\",\n      \"files\": []\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nSee `references/schemas.md` for the full schema (including the `assertions` field, which you''ll add later).\n\n## Running and evaluating test cases\n\nThis section is one continuous sequence — don''t stop partway through. Do NOT use `/skill-test` or any other testing skill.\n\nPut results in `<skill-name>-workspace/` as a sibling to the skill directory. Within the workspace, organize results by iteration (`iteration-1/`, `iteration-2/`, etc.) and within that, each test case gets a directory (`eval-0/`, `eval-1/`, etc.). Don''t create all of this upfront — just create directories as you go.\n\n### Step 1: Spawn all runs (with-skill AND baseline) in the same turn\n\nFor each test case, spawn two subagents in the same turn — one with the skill, one without. This is important: don''t spawn the with-skill runs first and then come back for baselines later. Launch everything at once so it all finishes around the same time.\n\n**With-skill run:**\n\n```\nExecute this task:\n- Skill path: <path-to-skill>\n- Task: <eval prompt>\n- Input files: <eval files if any, or \"none\">\n- Save outputs to: <workspace>/iteration-<N>/eval-<ID>/with_skill/outputs/\n- Outputs to save: <what the user cares about — e.g., \"the .docx file\", \"the final CSV\">\n```\n\n**Baseline run** (same prompt, but the baseline depends on context):\n- **Creating a new skill**: no skill at all. Same prompt, no skill path, save to `without_skill/outputs/`.\n- **Improving an existing skill**: the old version. Before editing, snapshot the skill (`cp -r <skill-path> <workspace>/skill-snapshot/`), then point the baseline subagent at the snapshot. Save to `old_skill/outputs/`.\n\nWrite an `eval_metadata.json` for each test case (assertions can be empty for now). Give each eval a descriptive name based on what it''s testing — not just \"eval-0\". Use this name for the directory too. If this iteration uses new or modified eval prompts, create these files for each new eval directory — don''t assume they carry over from previous iterations.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"eval_id\": 0,\n  \"eval_name\": \"descriptive-name-here\",\n  \"prompt\": \"The user''s task prompt\",\n  \"assertions\": []\n}\n```\n\n### Step 2: While runs are in progress, draft assertions\n\nDon''t just wait for the runs to finish — you can use this time productively. Draft quantitative assertions for each test case and explain them to the user. If assertions already exist in `evals/evals.json`, review them and explain what they check.\n\nGood assertions are objectively verifiable and have descriptive names — they should read clearly in the benchmark viewer so someone glancing at the results immediately understands what each one checks. Subjective skills (writing style, design quality) are better evaluated qualitatively — don''t force assertions onto things that need human judgment.\n\nUpdate the `eval_metadata.json` files and `evals/evals.json` with the assertions once drafted. Also explain to the user what they''ll see in the viewer — both the qualitative outputs and the quantitative benchmark.\n\n### Step 3: As runs complete, capture timing data\n\nWhen each subagent task completes, you receive a notification containing `total_tokens` and `duration_ms`. Save this data immediately to `timing.json` in the run directory:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"total_tokens\": 84852,\n  \"duration_ms\": 23332,\n  \"total_duration_seconds\": 23.3\n}\n```\n\nThis is the only opportunity to capture this data — it comes through the task notification and isn''t persisted elsewhere. Process each notification as it arrives rather than trying to batch them.\n\n### Step 4: Grade, aggregate, and launch the viewer\n\nOnce all runs are done:\n\n1. **Grade each run** — spawn a grader subagent (or grade inline) that reads `agents/grader.md` and evaluates each assertion against the outputs. Save results to `grading.json` in each run directory. The grading.json expectations array must use the fields `text`, `passed`, and `evidence` (not `name`/`met`/`details` or other variants) — the viewer depends on these exact field names. For assertions that can be checked programmatically, write and run a script rather than eyeballing it — scripts are faster, more reliable, and can be reused across iterations.\n\n2. **Aggregate into benchmark** — run the aggregation script from the skill-creator directory:\n   ```bash\n   python -m scripts.aggregate_benchmark <workspace>/iteration-N --skill-name <name>\n   ```\n   This produces `benchmark.json` and `benchmark.md` with pass_rate, time, and tokens for each configuration, with mean ± stddev and the delta. If generating benchmark.json manually, see `references/schemas.md` for the exact schema the viewer expects.\nPut each with_skill version before its baseline counterpart.\n\n3. **Do an analyst pass** — read the benchmark data and surface patterns the aggregate stats might hide. See `agents/analyzer.md` (the \"Analyzing Benchmark Results\" section) for what to look for — things like assertions that always pass regardless of skill (non-discriminating), high-variance evals (possibly flaky), and time/token tradeoffs.\n\n4. **Launch the viewer** with both qualitative outputs and quantitative data:\n   ```bash\n   nohup python <skill-creator-path>/eval-viewer/generate_review.py \\\n     <workspace>/iteration-N \\\n     --skill-name \"my-skill\" \\\n     --benchmark <workspace>/iteration-N/benchmark.json \\\n     > /dev/null 2>&1 &\n   VIEWER_PID=$!\n   ```\n   For iteration 2+, also pass `--previous-workspace <workspace>/iteration-<N-1>`.\n\n   **Cowork / headless environments:** If `webbrowser.open()` is not available or the environment has no display, use `--static <output_path>` to write a standalone HTML file instead of starting a server. Feedback will be downloaded as a `feedback.json` file when the user clicks \"Submit All Reviews\". After download, copy `feedback.json` into the workspace directory for the next iteration to pick up.\n\nNote: please use generate_review.py to create the viewer; there''s no need to write custom HTML.\n\n5. **Tell the user** something like: \"I''ve opened the results in your browser. There are two tabs — ''Outputs'' lets you click through each test case and leave feedback, ''Benchmark'' shows the quantitative comparison. When you''re done, come back here and let me know.\"\n\n### What the user sees in the viewer\n\nThe \"Outputs\" tab shows one test case at a time:\n- **Prompt**: the task that was given\n- **Output**: the files the skill produced, rendered inline where possible\n- **Previous Output** (iteration 2+): collapsed section showing last iteration''s output\n- **Formal Grades** (if grading was run): collapsed section showing assertion pass/fail\n- **Feedback**: a textbox that auto-saves as they type\n- **Previous Feedback** (iteration 2+): their comments from last time, shown below the textbox\n\nThe \"Benchmark\" tab shows the stats summary: pass rates, timing, and token usage for each configuration, with per-eval breakdowns and analyst observations.\n\nNavigation is via prev/next buttons or arrow keys. When done, they click \"Submit All Reviews\" which saves all feedback to `feedback.json`.\n\n### Step 5: Read the feedback\n\nWhen the user tells you they''re done, read `feedback.json`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"reviews\": [\n    {\"run_id\": \"eval-0-with_skill\", \"feedback\": \"the chart is missing axis labels\", \"timestamp\": \"...\"},\n    {\"run_id\": \"eval-1-with_skill\", \"feedback\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"...\"},\n    {\"run_id\": \"eval-2-with_skill\", \"feedback\": \"perfect, love this\", \"timestamp\": \"...\"}\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n```\n\nEmpty feedback means the user thought it was fine. Focus your improvements on the test cases where the user had specific complaints.\n\nKill the viewer server when you''re done with it:\n\n```bash\nkill $VIEWER_PID 2>/dev/null\n```\n\n---\n\n## Improving the skill\n\nThis is the heart of the loop. You''ve run the test cases, the user has reviewed the results, and now you need to make the skill better based on their feedback.\n\n### How to think about improvements\n\n1. **Generalize from the feedback.** The big picture thing that''s happening here is that we''re trying to create skills that can be used a million times (maybe literally, maybe even more who knows) across many different prompts. Here you and the user are iterating on only a few examples over and over again because it helps move faster. The user knows these examples in and out and it''s quick for them to assess new outputs. But if the skill you and the user are codeveloping works only for those examples, it''s useless. Rather than put in fiddly overfitty changes, or oppressively constrictive MUSTs, if there''s some stubborn issue, you might try branching out and using different metaphors, or recommending different patterns of working. It''s relatively cheap to try and maybe you''ll land on something great.\n\n2. **Keep the prompt lean.** Remove things that aren''t pulling their weight. Make sure to read the transcripts, not just the final outputs — if it looks like the skill is making the model waste a bunch of time doing things that are unproductive, you can try getting rid of the parts of the skill that are making it do that and seeing what happens.\n\n3. **Explain the why.** Try hard to explain the **why** behind everything you''re asking the model to do. Today''s LLMs are *smart*. They have good theory of mind and when given a good harness can go beyond rote instructions and really make things happen. Even if the feedback from the user is terse or frustrated, try to actually understand the task and why the user is writing what they wrote, and what they actually wrote, and then transmit this understanding into the instructions. If you find yourself writing ALWAYS or NEVER in all caps, or using super rigid structures, that''s a yellow flag — if possible, reframe and explain the reasoning so that the model understands why the thing you''re asking for is important. That''s a more humane, powerful, and effective approach.\n\n4. **Look for repeated work across test cases.** Read the transcripts from the test runs and notice if the subagents all independently wrote similar helper scripts or took the same multi-step approach to something. If all 3 test cases resulted in the subagent writing a `create_docx.py` or a `build_chart.py`, that''s a strong signal the skill should bundle that script. Write it once, put it in `scripts/`, and tell the skill to use it. This saves every future invocation from reinventing the wheel.\n\nThis task is pretty important (we are trying to create billions a year in economic value here!) and your thinking time is not the blocker; take your time and really mull things over. I''d suggest writing a draft revision and then looking at it anew and making improvements. Really do your best to get into the head of the user and understand what they want and need.\n\n### The iteration loop\n\nAfter improving the skill:\n\n1. Apply your improvements to the skill\n2. Rerun all test cases into a new `iteration-<N+1>/` directory, including baseline runs. If you''re creating a new skill, the baseline is always `without_skill` (no skill) — that stays the same across iterations. If you''re improving an existing skill, use your judgment on what makes sense as the baseline: the original version the user came in with, or the previous iteration.\n3. Launch the reviewer with `--previous-workspace` pointing at the previous iteration\n4. Wait for the user to review and tell you they''re done\n5. Read the new feedback, improve again, repeat\n\nKeep going until:\n- The user says they''re happy\n- The feedback is all empty (everything looks good)\n- You''re not making meaningful progress\n\n---\n\n## Advanced: Blind comparison\n\nFor situations where you want a more rigorous comparison between two versions of a skill (e.g., the user asks \"is the new version actually better?\"), there''s a blind comparison system. Read `agents/comparator.md` and `agents/analyzer.md` for the details. The basic idea is: give two outputs to an independent agent without telling it which is which, and let it judge quality. Then analyze why the winner won.\n\nThis is optional, requires subagents, and most users won''t need it. The human review loop is usually sufficient.\n\n---\n\n## Description Optimization\n\nThe description field in SKILL.md frontmatter is the primary mechanism that determines whether Claude invokes a skill. After creating or improving a skill, offer to optimize the description for better triggering accuracy.\n\n### Step 1: Generate trigger eval queries\n\nCreate 20 eval queries — a mix of should-trigger and should-not-trigger. Save as JSON:\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"query\": \"the user prompt\", \"should_trigger\": true},\n  {\"query\": \"another prompt\", \"should_trigger\": false}\n]\n```\n\nThe queries must be realistic and something a Claude Code or Claude.ai user would actually type. Not abstract requests, but requests that are concrete and specific and have a good amount of detail. For instance, file paths, personal context about the user''s job or situation, column names and values, company names, URLs. A little bit of backstory. Some might be in lowercase or contain abbreviations or typos or casual speech. Use a mix of different lengths, and focus on edge cases rather than making them clear-cut (the user will get a chance to sign off on them).\n\nBad: `\"Format this data\"`, `\"Extract text from PDF\"`, `\"Create a chart\"`\n\nGood: `\"ok so my boss just sent me this xlsx file (its in my downloads, called something like ''Q4 sales final FINAL v2.xlsx'') and she wants me to add a column that shows the profit margin as a percentage. The revenue is in column C and costs are in column D i think\"`\n\nFor the **should-trigger** queries (8-10), think about coverage. You want different phrasings of the same intent — some formal, some casual. Include cases where the user doesn''t explicitly name the skill or file type but clearly needs it. Throw in some uncommon use cases and cases where this skill competes with another but should win.\n\nFor the **should-not-trigger** queries (8-10), the most valuable ones are the near-misses — queries that share keywords or concepts with the skill but actually need something different. Think adjacent domains, ambiguous phrasing where a naive keyword match would trigger but shouldn''t, and cases where the query touches on something the skill does but in a context where another tool is more appropriate.\n\nThe key thing to avoid: don''t make should-not-trigger queries obviously irrelevant. \"Write a fibonacci function\" as a negative test for a PDF skill is too easy — it doesn''t test anything. The negative cases should be genuinely tricky.\n\n### Step 2: Review with user\n\nPresent the eval set to the user for review using the HTML template:\n\n1. Read the template from `assets/eval_review.html`\n2. Replace the placeholders:\n   - `__EVAL_DATA_PLACEHOLDER__` → the JSON array of eval items (no quotes around it — it''s a JS variable assignment)\n   - `__SKILL_NAME_PLACEHOLDER__` → the skill''s name\n   - `__SKILL_DESCRIPTION_PLACEHOLDER__` → the skill''s current description\n3. Write to a temp file (e.g., `/tmp/eval_review_<skill-name>.html`) and open it: `open /tmp/eval_review_<skill-name>.html`\n4. The user can edit queries, toggle should-trigger, add/remove entries, then click \"Export Eval Set\"\n5. The file downloads to `~/Downloads/eval_set.json` — check the Downloads folder for the most recent version in case there are multiple (e.g., `eval_set (1).json`)\n\nThis step matters — bad eval queries lead to bad descriptions.\n\n### Step 3: Run the optimization loop\n\nTell the user: \"This will take some time — I''ll run the optimization loop in the background and check on it periodically.\"\n\nSave the eval set to the workspace, then run in the background:\n\n```bash\npython -m scripts.run_loop \\\n  --eval-set <path-to-trigger-eval.json> \\\n  --skill-path <path-to-skill> \\\n  --model <model-id-powering-this-session> \\\n  --max-iterations 5 \\\n  --verbose\n```\n\nUse the model ID from your system prompt (the one powering the current session) so the triggering test matches what the user actually experiences.\n\nWhile it runs, periodically tail the output to give the user updates on which iteration it''s on and what the scores look like.\n\nThis handles the full optimization loop automatically. It splits the eval set into 60% train and 40% held-out test, evaluates the current description (running each query 3 times to get a reliable trigger rate), then calls Claude with extended thinking to propose improvements based on what failed. It re-evaluates each new description on both train and test, iterating up to 5 times. When it''s done, it opens an HTML report in the browser showing the results per iteration and returns JSON with `best_description` — selected by test score rather than train score to avoid overfitting.\n\n### How skill triggering works\n\nUnderstanding the triggering mechanism helps design better eval queries. Skills appear in Claude''s `available_skills` list with their name + description, and Claude decides whether to consult a skill based on that description. The important thing to know is that Claude only consults skills for tasks it can''t easily handle on its own — simple, one-step queries like \"read this PDF\" may not trigger a skill even if the description matches perfectly, because Claude can handle them directly with basic tools. Complex, multi-step, or specialized queries reliably trigger skills when the description matches.\n\nThis means your eval queries should be substantive enough that Claude would actually benefit from consulting a skill. Simple queries like \"read file X\" are poor test cases — they won''t trigger skills regardless of description quality.\n\n### Step 4: Apply the result\n\nTake `best_description` from the JSON output and update the skill''s SKILL.md frontmatter. Show the user before/after and report the scores.\n\n---\n\n### Package and Present (only if `present_files` tool is available)\n\nCheck whether you have access to the `present_files` tool. If you don''t, skip this step. If you do, package the skill and present the .skill file to the user:\n\n```bash\npython -m scripts.package_skill <path/to/skill-folder>\n```\n\nAfter packaging, direct the user to the resulting `.skill` file path so they can install it.\n\n---\n\n## Claude.ai-specific instructions\n\nIn Claude.ai, the core workflow is the same (draft → test → review → improve → repeat), but because Claude.ai doesn''t have subagents, some mechanics change. Here''s what to adapt:\n\n**Running test cases**: No subagents means no parallel execution. For each test case, read the skill''s SKILL.md, then follow its instructions to accomplish the test prompt yourself. Do them one at a time. This is less rigorous than independent subagents (you wrote the skill and you''re also running it, so you have full context), but it''s a useful sanity check — and the human review step compensates. Skip the baseline runs — just use the skill to complete the task as requested.\n\n**Reviewing results**: If you can''t open a browser (e.g., Claude.ai''s VM has no display, or you''re on a remote server), skip the browser reviewer entirely. Instead, present results directly in the conversation. For each test case, show the prompt and the output. If the output is a file the user needs to see (like a .docx or .xlsx), save it to the filesystem and tell them where it is so they can download and inspect it. Ask for feedback inline: \"How does this look? Anything you''d change?\"\n\n**Benchmarking**: Skip the quantitative benchmarking — it relies on baseline comparisons which aren''t meaningful without subagents. Focus on qualitative feedback from the user.\n\n**The iteration loop**: Same as before — improve the skill, rerun the test cases, ask for feedback — just without the browser reviewer in the middle. You can still organize results into iteration directories on the filesystem if you have one.\n\n**Description optimization**: This section requires the `claude` CLI tool (specifically `claude -p`) which is only available in Claude Code. Skip it if you''re on Claude.ai.\n\n**Blind comparison**: Requires subagents. Skip it.\n\n**Packaging**: The `package_skill.py` script works anywhere with Python and a filesystem. On Claude.ai, you can run it and the user can download the resulting `.skill` file.\n\n---\n\n## Cowork-Specific Instructions\n\nIf you''re in Cowork, the main things to know are:\n\n- You have subagents, so the main workflow (spawn test cases in parallel, run baselines, grade, etc.) all works. (However, if you run into severe problems with timeouts, it''s OK to run the test prompts in series rather than parallel.)\n- You don''t have a browser or display, so when generating the eval viewer, use `--static <output_path>` to write a standalone HTML file instead of starting a server. Then proffer a link that the user can click to open the HTML in their browser.\n- For whatever reason, the Cowork setup seems to disincline Claude from generating the eval viewer after running the tests, so just to reiterate: whether you''re in Cowork or in Claude Code, after running tests, you should always generate the eval viewer for the human to look at examples before revising the skill yourself and trying to make corrections, using `generate_review.py` (not writing your own boutique html code). Sorry in advance but I''m gonna go all caps here: GENERATE THE EVAL VIEWER *BEFORE* evaluating inputs yourself. You want to get them in front of the human ASAP!\n- Feedback works differently: since there''s no running server, the viewer''s \"Submit All Reviews\" button will download `feedback.json` as a file. You can then read it from there (you may have to request access first).\n- Packaging works — `package_skill.py` just needs Python and a filesystem.\n- Description optimization (`run_loop.py` / `run_eval.py`) should work in Cowork just fine since it uses `claude -p` via subprocess, not a browser, but please save it until you''ve fully finished making the skill and the user agrees it''s in good shape.\n\n---\n\n## Reference files\n\nThe agents/ directory contains instructions for specialized subagents. Read them when you need to spawn the relevant subagent.\n\n- `agents/grader.md` — How to evaluate assertions against outputs\n- `agents/comparator.md` — How to do blind A/B comparison between two outputs\n- `agents/analyzer.md` — How to analyze why one version beat another\n\nThe references/ directory has additional documentation:\n- `references/schemas.md` — JSON structures for evals.json, grading.json, etc.\n\n---\n\nRepeating one more time the core loop here for emphasis:\n\n- Figure out what the skill is about\n- Draft or edit the skill\n- Run claude-with-access-to-the-skill on test prompts\n- With the user, evaluate the outputs:\n  - Create benchmark.json and run `eval-viewer/generate_review.py` to help the user review them\n  - Run quantitative evals\n- Repeat until you and the user are satisfied\n- Package the final skill and return it to the user.\n\nPlease add steps to your TodoList, if you have such a thing, to make sure you don''t forget. If you''re in Cowork, please specifically put \"Create evals JSON and run `eval-viewer/generate_review.py` so human can review test cases\" in your TodoList to make sure it happens.\n\nGood luck!\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-03-01T05:08:45.830Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能代理技能创建","ja":"AIエージェントスキル作成","ko":"AI 에이전트 스킬 생성","es":"Herramientas de AI: Creador de Habilidades para Desarroll...","fr":"Outils d''IA : Créateur de Compétences pour Développeurs","de":"KI-Tools: Fähigkeits-Ersteller für Entwickler","pt":"Criador de Habilidades para Ferramentas de IA","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Создатель Навыков","ar":"أداة إنشاء مهارات للوكلاء الذكية","en":"skill-creator"},"description":{"zh":"skill-creator技能提供创建有效技能的指南，帮助开发者扩展Claude的能力","ja":"skill-creatorスキルは、効果的なスキルを作成するためのガイドを提供し、開発者がClaudeの機能を拡張できるようにします","ko":"skill-creator 스킬은 효과적인 스킬을 생성하는 방법에 대한 가이드를 제공하여 개발자가 Claude의 기능을 확장할 수 있도록 합니다","es":"El creador de habilidades es una guía para desarrolladores que desean ampliar las capacidades de Claude con conocimientos y flujos de trabajo especializados","fr":"Le créateur de compétences est un guide pour les développeurs qui souhaitent étendre les capacités de Claude avec des connaissances et des flux de travail sp...","de":"Der Fähigkeits-Ersteller ist ein Leitfaden für Entwickler, die die Fähigkeiten von Claude mit spezialisierten Kenntnissen und Workflows erweitern möchten","pt":"O Criador de Habilidades é uma ferramenta para criar habilidades personalizadas para Ferramentas de IA, permitindo estender as capacidades da sua IA.","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Создатель Навыков - это инструмент для создания специализированных навыков для ИИ Агентов, позволяющий расширить возможности вашего ИИ.","ar":"أداة إنشاء المهارات هي أداة لإنشاء مهارات مخصصة للوكلاء الذكية، مما يسمح بتوسيع قدرات الوكلاء الذكية.","en":"Guide for creating effective skills. This skill should be used when users want to create a new skill (or update an existing skill) that extends Claudes capab..."},"definition":{"en":"Guide for creating effective skills. This skill should be used when users want to create a new skill (or update an existing skill) that extends Claudes capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, or tool integrations."},"features":{"zh":["提供专业知识和工作流","支持工具集成","扩展Claude的能力","创建自定义技能","支持多种开发语言"],"ja":["専門知識とワークフローを提供","ツール統合をサポート","Claudeの機能を拡張","カスタムスキルを作成","複数の開発言語をサポート"],"ko":["전문 지식과 워크플로 제공","툴 통합 지원","Claude의 기능 확장","사용자 지정 스킬 생성","다중 개발 언어 지원"],"es":["Creación de habilidades personalizadas","Integración de flujos de trabajo especializados","Ampliación de las capacidades de Claude","Paquetes modulares y autocontenidos","Conocimientos y herramientas especializadas"],"fr":["Création de compétences personnalisées","Intégration de flux de travail spécialisés","Étendre les capacités de Claude","Paquets modulaires et autocontenus","Connaissances et outils spécialisés"],"de":["Erstellung von benutzerdefinierten Fähigkeiten","Integration von spezialisierten Workflows","Erweiterung der Fähigkeiten von Claude","Modulare und selbstenthaltene Pakete","Spezialisierte Kenntnisse und Tools"],"pt":["Criação de habilidades personalizadas","Extensão das capacidades da IA","Integração com fluxos de trabalho especializados","Ferramentas de desenvolvimento de habilidades","Suporte a múltiplos domínios e tarefas"],"ru":["Создание специализированных навыков","Расширение возможностей ИИ","Интеграция с специализированными рабочими процессами","Инструменты разработки навыков","Поддержка нескольких доменов и задач"],"ar":["إنشاء مهارات مخصصة","توسيع قدرات الوكلاء الذكية","دمج مع سير عمل متخصص","أدوات تطوير المهارات","دعم متعددة المجالات والمهام"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","技能创建","Claude扩展","专业知识","工作流","工具集成","开发语言","自定义技能"],"ja":["AIエージェント","スキル作成","Claude拡張","専門知識","ワークフロー","ツール統合","開発言語","カスタムスキル"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","스킬 생성","Claude 확장","전문 지식","워크플로","툴 통합","개발 언어","사용자 지정 스킬"],"es":["herramientas de AI","creador de habilidades","desarrollo de habilidades","ampliación de capacidades","conocimientos especializados","flujos de trabajo","paquetes modulares","Claude","IA"],"fr":["outils d''IA","créateur de compétences","développement de compétences","étendre les capacités","connaissances spécialisées","flux de travail","paquets modulaires","Claude","IA"],"de":["KI-Tools","Fähigkeits-Ersteller","Entwicklung von Fähigkeiten","Erweiterung der Fähigkeiten","spezialisierte Kenntnisse","Workflows","modulare Pakete","Claude","KI"],"pt":["Ferramentas de IA","Criador de Habilidades","Desenvolvimento de habilidades","Integração com fluxos de trabalho","Extensão das capacidades da IA","Habilidades personalizadas"],"ru":["ИИ Агенты","Создатель Навыков","Разработка навыков","Интеграция с рабочими процессами","Расширение возможностей ИИ","Специализированные навыки"],"ar":["الوكلاء الذكية","أداة إنشاء المهارات","تطوير المهارات","دمج مع سير عمل","توسيع قدرات الوكلاء الذكية","المهارات المخصصة"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Essential for AI Agent Developers building and optimizing custom skill ecosystems.","zh":"对于构建和优化自定义技能生态系统的AI代理开发人员至关重要。","ja":"AIエージェント開発者がカスタムスキルエコシステムを構築して最適化するために不可欠です。","ko":"사용자 지정 스킬 생태계를 구축하고 최적화하는 AI 에이전트 개발자에게 필수적입니다.","es":"Esencial para los desarrolladores de Agentes de Inteligencia Artificial que crean y optimizan ecosistemas de habilidades personalizadas.","fr":"Essentiel pour les développeurs d''agents d''intelligence artificielle qui créent et optimisent des écosystèmes de compétences personnalisées.","de":"Wesentlich für Entwickler von KI-Agenten, die benutzerdefinierte Skill-Ökosysteme erstellen und optimieren.","pt":"Essencial para Desenvolvedores de Agentes de IA que constroem e otimizam ecossistemas de skills personalizadas.","ru":"Необходимо для разработчиков ИИ-агентов, создающих и оптимизирующих пользовательские экосистемы навыков (skills).","ar":"أساسي لمطوري وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي الذين يقومون ببناء وتحسين أنظمة المهارات المخصصة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables full lifecycle management of AI skills through iterative creation, modification, and performance benchmarking. Provides variance analysis for skill optimization and description refinement to improve triggering accuracy across agent platforms.","zh":"通过迭代创建、修改和性能基准测试，实现AI技能的全生命周期管理。提供方差分析以优化技能和描述细化，从而提高触发器在代理平台上的准确性。","ja":"反復的な作成、変更、パフォーマンスベンチマークテストを通じて、AIスキルのフルライフサイクル管理を実現します。スキル最適化と説明の細分化を改善するための分散分析を提供し、エージェントプラットフォーム全体でのトリガー精度を向上させます。","ko":"반복적인 생성, 수정 및 성능 벤치마크 테스트를 통해 AI 스킬의 전체 수명 주기 관리를 가능하게 합니다. 스킬 최적화 및 설명 세부화 개선을 위한 분산 분석을 제공하여 에이전트 플랫폼 전반의 트리거 정확도를 향상시킵니다.","es":"Permite la gestión del ciclo de vida completo de las habilidades de inteligencia artificial a través de la creación iterativa, la modificación y la medición de rendimiento. Proporciona análisis de varianza para la optimización de habilidades y la refinación de descripciones para mejorar la precisión de activación en plataformas de agentes.","fr":"Permet la gestion du cycle de vie complet des compétences d''intelligence artificielle grâce à la création itérative, la modification et la mesure de performance. Fournit une analyse de variance pour l''optimisation des compétences et l''affinement des descriptions pour améliorer la précision de déclenchement sur les plateformes d''agents.","de":"Ermöglicht das vollständige Lebenszyklus-Management von KI-Fähigkeiten durch iterative Erstellung, Modifizierung und Leistungsbewertung. Bietet Varianzanalyse für die Optimierung von Fähigkeiten und die Verfeinerung von Beschreibungen, um die Triggergenauigkeit über Agenten-Plattformen hinweg zu verbessern.","pt":"Permite o gerenciamento completo do ciclo de vida de skills de IA através da criação iterativa, modificação e benchmarking de desempenho. Fornece análise de variância para otimização de skills e refinamento de descrição para melhorar a precisão de acionamento em plataformas de agentes.","ru":"Обеспечивает полное управление жизненным циклом ИИ-навыков (skills) посредством итеративного создания, изменения и тестирования производительности. Предоставляет анализ вариативности для оптимизации навыков и уточнения описаний для повышения точности их запуска на платформах агентов.","ar":"يمكن من الإدارة الكاملة لدورة الحياة لمهارات الذكاء الاصطناعي من خلال التكوين التكراري، التعديل، وقياس الأداء. يوفر تحليل التباين لتحسين المهارات وصقل الوصف لتحسين دقة التشغيل عبر منصات الوكلاء."},"useCases":{"en":["Creating new skills from scratch","Modifying and optimizing existing skills","Running evals to test skill performance","Benchmarking skill performance with variance analysis"],"zh":["从头开始创建新的技能","修改和优化现有的技能","运行评估以测试技能性能","使用方差分析基准测试技能性能"],"ja":["新しいスキルを最初から作成する","既存のスキルを変更して最適化する","スキルのパフォーマンスをテストするための評価を実行する","分散分析を使用してスキルのパフォーマンスをベンチマークする"],"ko":["새로운 스킬을 처음부터 생성하는 것","기존의 스킬을 수정하고 최적화하는 것","스킬의 성능을 테스트하기 위한 평가를 실행하는 것","분산 분석을 사용하여 스킬의 성능을 벤치마크하는 것"],"es":["Crear habilidades nuevas desde cero","Modificar y optimizar habilidades existentes","Ejecutar evaluaciones para probar el rendimiento de las habilidades","Medir el rendimiento de las habilidades con análisis de varianza"],"fr":["Créer de nouvelles compétences à partir de zéro","Modifier et optimiser les compétences existantes","Exécuter des évaluations pour tester les performances des compétences","Mesurer les performances des compétences avec analyse de variance"],"de":["Neue Fähigkeiten von Grund auf erstellen","Vorhandene Fähigkeiten modifizieren und optimieren","Bewertungen ausführen, um die Leistung von Fähigkeiten zu testen","Die Leistung von Fähigkeiten mit Varianzanalyse messen"],"pt":["Criar novas skills do zero","Modificar e otimizar skills existentes","Executar avaliações para testar o desempenho da skill","Benchmarking de desempenho de skill com análise de variância"],"ru":["Создание новых навыков (skills) с нуля","Изменение и оптимизация существующих навыков","Запуск оценок (evals) для тестирования производительности навыков","Сравнительный анализ производительности навыков с анализом вариативности"],"ar":["إنشاء مهارات جديدة من الصفر","تعديل وتحسين المهارات الحالية","تشغيل التقييمات لاختبار أداء المهارة","قياس أداء المهارة مع تحليل التباين"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to claude-with-access-to-the-skill for testing","Needs predefined test prompts for evaluation","Performance measurement dependent on evaluation framework implementation"],"zh":["需要访问claude-with-access-to-the-skill进行测试","需要预定义的测试提示进行评估","性能测量依赖于评估框架的实现"],"ja":["テストのためにclaude-with-access-to-the-skillへのアクセスが必要","評価のために事前に定義されたテストプロンプトが必要","パフォーマンス測定は評価フレームワークの実装に依存する"],"ko":["테스트를 위해 claude-with-access-to-the-skill에 대한 액세스가 필요합니다","평가를 위해 사전 정의된 테스트 프롬프트가 필요합니다","성능 측정은 평가 프레임워크의 구현에 종속됩니다"],"es":["Requiere acceso a claude-with-access-to-the-skill para pruebas","Necesita prompts de prueba predefinidos para la evaluación","La medición del rendimiento depende de la implementación del marco de evaluación"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à claude-with-access-to-the-skill pour les tests","Besoin de prompts de test prédéfinis pour l''évaluation","La mesure de performance dépend de la mise en œuvre du cadre d''évaluation"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf claude-with-access-to-the-skill für Tests","Benötigt vordefinierte Testprompts für die Bewertung","Die Leistungsmessung hängt von der Implementierung des Bewertungsframeworks ab"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao claude-with-access-to-the-skill para testes","Necessita de prompts de teste predefinidos para avaliação","Medição de desempenho dependente da implementação do framework de avaliação"],"ru":["Требуется доступ к claude-with-access-to-the-skill для тестирования","Необходимы предопределенные тестовые промпты для оценки","Измерение производительности зависит от реализации framework оценки"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى claude-with-access-to-the-skill للاختبار","يحتاج إلى مطالبات اختبار محددة مسبقًا للتقييم","قياس الأداء يعتمد على تنفيذ إطار التقييم"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"ba8bebb2c085444120743af8dc859dd7c2592d6290e93aa5e1c08403109bdce7","repoEtag":"W/\"795252861eecc48ed1ad31a16e978d71a3eaafc45d526a6e594e873a66c8f11d\"","qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('obra/superpowers/writing-plans', 'official', 'obra', 'superpowers', 'obra/superpowers', 'writing-plans', 66125, 5048, 80, '2026-03-01T05:08:15Z', '2026-03-01T05:08:49.274Z', '8a9198d4d9efbcad6e019b17c422c182113062c864b6154ec2a3ba2ed0b6b9d0', '{"id":"obra/superpowers/writing-plans","name":"writing-plans","description":{"zh":"编写计划是开发前的重要步骤，使用AI智能工具可以提高效率","ja":"開発前に詳細な計画書を作成することが重要です。AIエージェントを使用して計画書を作成しましょう","ko":"개발 전 계획 수립은 중요합니다. AI 에이전트를 사용하여 구체적인 계획을 수립하세요","es":"La escritura de planes es una habilidad de agente de AI que ayuda a los desarrolladores a crear planes de implementación detallados para tareas complejas","fr":"L''écriture de plans est une compétence d''agent d''IA qui aide les développeurs à créer des plans d''implémentation détaillés pour les tâches complexes","de":"Das Schreiben von Plänen ist eine Fähigkeit von KI-Agents, die Entwicklern hilft, detaillierte Implementierungspläne für komplexe Aufgaben zu erstellen","pt":"O skill de escrita de planos ajuda a criar planos de implementação detalhados para tarefas complexas","ru":"Навык создания планов помогает разработчикам создавать подробные планы реализации сложных задач","ar":"مهارة كتابة خطط التنفيذ تساعد على إنشاء خطط تفصيلية لعمليات متعددة المراحل","en":"Use when you have a spec or requirements for a multi-step task, before touching code"},"owner":"obra","repo":"superpowers","repoPath":"obra/superpowers","stars":66125,"forks":5048,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T05:08:15Z","topics":[],"skillMd":{"name":"writing-plans","description":"Use when you have a spec or requirements for a multi-step task, before touching code","bodyPreview":"# Writing Plans\n\n## Overview\n\nWrite comprehensive implementation plans assuming the engineer has zero context for our codebase and questionable taste. Document everything they need to know: which files to touch for each task, code, testing, docs they might need to check, how to test it. Give them the whole plan as bite-sized tasks. DRY. YAGNI. TDD. Frequent commits.\n\nAssume they are a skilled developer, but know almost nothing about our toolset or problem domain. Assume they don''t know good test","body":"# Writing Plans\n\n## Overview\n\nWrite comprehensive implementation plans assuming the engineer has zero context for our codebase and questionable taste. Document everything they need to know: which files to touch for each task, code, testing, docs they might need to check, how to test it. Give them the whole plan as bite-sized tasks. DRY. YAGNI. TDD. Frequent commits.\n\nAssume they are a skilled developer, but know almost nothing about our toolset or problem domain. Assume they don''t know good test design very well.\n\n**Announce at start:** \"I''m using the writing-plans skill to create the implementation plan.\"\n\n**Context:** This should be run in a dedicated worktree (created by brainstorming skill).\n\n**Save plans to:** `docs/plans/YYYY-MM-DD-<feature-name>.md`\n\n## Bite-Sized Task Granularity\n\n**Each step is one action (2-5 minutes):**\n- \"Write the failing test\" - step\n- \"Run it to make sure it fails\" - step\n- \"Implement the minimal code to make the test pass\" - step\n- \"Run the tests and make sure they pass\" - step\n- \"Commit\" - step\n\n## Plan Document Header\n\n**Every plan MUST start with this header:**\n\n```markdown\n# [Feature Name] Implementation Plan\n\n> **For Claude:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task.\n\n**Goal:** [One sentence describing what this builds]\n\n**Architecture:** [2-3 sentences about approach]\n\n**Tech Stack:** [Key technologies/libraries]\n\n---\n```\n\n## Task Structure\n\n````markdown\n### Task N: [Component Name]\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `exact/path/to/file.py`\n- Modify: `exact/path/to/existing.py:123-145`\n- Test: `tests/exact/path/to/test.py`\n\n**Step 1: Write the failing test**\n\n```python\ndef test_specific_behavior():\n    result = function(input)\n    assert result == expected\n```\n\n**Step 2: Run test to verify it fails**\n\nRun: `pytest tests/path/test.py::test_name -v`\nExpected: FAIL with \"function not defined\"\n\n**Step 3: Write minimal implementation**\n\n```python\ndef function(input):\n    return expected\n```\n\n**Step 4: Run test to verify it passes**\n\nRun: `pytest tests/path/test.py::test_name -v`\nExpected: PASS\n\n**Step 5: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit add tests/path/test.py src/path/file.py\ngit commit -m \"feat: add specific feature\"\n```\n````\n\n## Remember\n- Exact file paths always\n- Complete code in plan (not \"add validation\")\n- Exact commands with expected output\n- Reference relevant skills with @ syntax\n- DRY, YAGNI, TDD, frequent commits\n\n## Execution Handoff\n\nAfter saving the plan, offer execution choice:\n\n**\"Plan complete and saved to `docs/plans/<filename>.md`. Two execution options:**\n\n**1. Subagent-Driven (this session)** - I dispatch fresh subagent per task, review between tasks, fast iteration\n\n**2. Parallel Session (separate)** - Open new session with executing-plans, batch execution with checkpoints\n\n**Which approach?\"**\n\n**If Subagent-Driven chosen:**\n- **REQUIRED SUB-SKILL:** Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development\n- Stay in this session\n- Fresh subagent per task + code review\n\n**If Parallel Session chosen:**\n- Guide them to open new session in worktree\n- **REQUIRED SUB-SKILL:** New session uses superpowers:executing-plans\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-03-01T05:08:49.274Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能工具：编写计划","ja":"AIエージェント：詳細な計画書の作成","ko":"AI 에이전트: 구체적인 계획 수립","es":"Herramientas de AI: Planificación de escritura para desar...","fr":"Outils d''IA: Écriture de plans pour les développeurs","de":"KI-Tools: Schreiben von Plänen für Entwickler","pt":"Ferramentas de IA: Planejamento de Implementação","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Создание Планов Реализации","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: كتابة خطط التنفيذ","en":"writing-plans"},"description":{"zh":"编写计划是开发前的重要步骤，使用AI智能工具可以提高效率","ja":"開発前に詳細な計画書を作成することが重要です。AIエージェントを使用して計画書を作成しましょう","ko":"개발 전 계획 수립은 중요합니다. AI 에이전트를 사용하여 구체적인 계획을 수립하세요","es":"La escritura de planes es una habilidad de agente de AI que ayuda a los desarrolladores a crear planes de implementación detallados para tareas complejas","fr":"L''écriture de plans est une compétence d''agent d''IA qui aide les développeurs à créer des plans d''implémentation détaillés pour les tâches complexes","de":"Das Schreiben von Plänen ist eine Fähigkeit von KI-Agents, die Entwicklern hilft, detaillierte Implementierungspläne für komplexe Aufgaben zu erstellen","pt":"O skill de escrita de planos ajuda a criar planos de implementação detalhados para tarefas complexas","ru":"Навык создания планов помогает разработчикам создавать подробные планы реализации сложных задач","ar":"مهارة كتابة خطط التنفيذ تساعد على إنشاء خطط تفصيلية لعمليات متعددة المراحل","en":"Use when you have a spec or requirements for a multi-step task, before touching code"},"definition":{"en":"Use when you have a spec or requirements for a multi-step task, before touching code"},"features":{"zh":["根据需求创建详细的开发计划","提供开发步骤和代码参考","确保开发过程中的测试和文档","支持频繁提交和代码审查","遵循DRY和YAGNI原则"],"ja":["要件に基づいて詳細な開発計画を作成","開発手順とコード例を提供","開発プロセスにおけるテストとドキュメントを保証","頻繁なコミットとコードレビューをサポート","DRYとYAGNI原則に従う"],"ko":["요구사항에 따라 구체적인 개발 계획을 수립","개발 단계와 코드 참조 제공","개발 과정中的 테스트와 문서를 보장","頻繁한 커밋과 코드 리뷰를 지원","DRY와 YAGNI 원칙을 따름"],"es":["Creación de planes de implementación detallados","Asunción de cero conocimiento del código base","Documentación de todos los pasos necesarios","Uso de principios de DRY, YAGNI y TDD","Commit frecuentes"],"fr":["Création de plans d''implémentation détaillés","Hypothèse de zéro connaissance du code base","Documentation de toutes les étapes nécessaires","Utilisation des principes de DRY, YAGNI et TDD","Commit fréquents"],"de":["Erstellung detaillierter Implementierungspläne","Annahme von null Kenntnissen des Code-Basisses","Dokumentation aller erforderlichen Schritte","Verwendung der Prinzipien von DRY, YAGNI und TDD","Häufige Commits"],"pt":["Criação de planos de implementação detalhados","Documentação de todos os passos necessários","Utilização de princípios de DRY e YAGNI","Desenvolvimento orientado a testes (TDD)","Commits frequentes para controle de versão"],"ru":["Создание подробных планов реализации","Документирование всех необходимых шагов","Применение принципов DRY и YAGNI","Разработка, ориентированная на тестирование (TDD)","Частые коммиты для контроля версий"],"ar":["إنشاء خطط تفصيلية لعمليات التنفيذ","توثيق جميع الخطوات اللازمة","استخدام مبادئ DRY و YAGNI","التطوير الموجه للاختبارات (TDD)","التعهدات المتكررة للتحكم في الإصدارات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能工具","开发计划","详细计划","开发效率","错误减少","代码审查","频繁提交"],"ja":["AIエージェント","開発計画","詳細な計画","開発効率","エラーレDUCTION","コードレビュー","頻繁なコミット"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","개발 계획","구체적인 계획","개발 효율성","오류 감소","코드 리뷰","頻繁한 커밋"],"es":["herramientas de AI para desarrolladores","planificación de escritura","desarrollo de software","implementación de tareas","principios de DRY","principios de YAGNI","principios de TDD","commit frecuentes","desarrollo de software ágil"],"fr":["outils d''IA pour les développeurs","écriture de plans","développement de logiciels","implémentation de tâches","principes de DRY","principes de YAGNI","principes de TDD","commit fréquents","développement de logiciels agiles"],"de":["KI-Tools für Entwickler","Schreiben von Plänen","Software-Entwicklung","Implementierung von Aufgaben","Prinzipien von DRY","Prinzipien von YAGNI","Prinzipien von TDD","häufige Commits","agile Software-Entwicklung"],"pt":["ferramentas de IA","planejamento de implementação","desenvolvimento de software","testes automatizados","controle de versão","DRY","YAGNI","TDD"],"ru":["ИИ Агенты","создание планов реализации","разработка программного обеспечения","автоматизированное тестирование","контроль версий","DRY","YAGNI","TDD"],"ar":["أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","كتابة خطط التنفيذ","تطوير البرمجيات","اختبارات آلية","التحكم في الإصدارات","DRY","YAGNI","TDD"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Code Analysis Agents requiring structured implementation planning with DRY, YAGNI, and TDD principles.","zh":"适用于需要结构化实施规划的代码分析代理，具有DRY、YAGNI和TDD原则。","ja":"構造化された実装計画が必要なコード分析エージェントに適しています。DRY、YAGNI、TDDの原則を必要とします。","ko":"구조화된 구현 계획이 필요한 코드 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다. DRY, YAGNI, TDD 원칙을 필요로 합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de análisis de código que requieren una planificación de implementación estructurada con principios DRY, YAGNI y TDD.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''analyse de code nécessitant une planification d''implémentation structurée avec les principes DRY, YAGNI et TDD.","de":"Ideal für Code-Analyse-Agenten, die eine strukturierte Implementierungsplanung mit DRY-, YAGNI- und TDD-Prinzipien erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Análise de Código que exigem planejamento de implementação estruturado com princípios DRY, YAGNI e TDD.","ru":"Идеально для Агентов Анализа Кодов, требующих структурированного планирования реализации с принципами DRY, YAGNI и TDD.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحليل الشفرة الذي يتطلب تخطيط تنفيذ منظم مع مبادئ DRY و YAGNI و TDD."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create comprehensive, bite-sized implementation plans, incorporating frequent commits, testing, and documentation, assuming zero context for the codebase and utilizing best practices like DRY and YAGNI.","zh":"赋予代理创建全面、分段的实施计划的能力，包括频繁的提交、测试和文档，假设代码库没有任何上下文，并利用最佳实践，如DRY和YAGNI。","ja":"エージェントに、コードベースのゼロコンテキストを前提とし、DRYやYAGNIなどのベストプラクティスを利用して、頻繁なコミット、テスト、文書化を含む、包括的でバイトサイズの実装計画を作成する能力を付与します。","ko":"에이전트에 코드베이스에 대한 제로 컨텍스트를 가정하고 DRY 및 YAGNI와 같은 베스트 프랙티스를 활용하여 빈번한 커밋, 테스트 및 문서화를 포함한 포괄적이고 바이트 크기의 구현 계획을 생성할 수 있는 기능을 부여합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes crear planes de implementación integrales y divididos en partes, incorporando commits frecuentes, pruebas y documentación, asumiendo cero contexto para el código base y utilizando las mejores prácticas como DRY y YAGNI.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des plans d''implémentation complets et divisés en parties, incorporant des validations fréquentes, des tests et une documentation, en supposant un contexte nul pour la base de code et en utilisant les meilleures pratiques comme DRY et YAGNI.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, umfassende, portionierte Implementierungspläne zu erstellen, die häufige Commits, Tests und Dokumentation umfassen, unter der Annahme, dass der Codebase kein Kontext bekannt ist und unter Verwendung von Best Practices wie DRY und YAGNI.","pt":"Permite que os agentes criem planos de implementação abrangentes e divididos em partes, incorporando commits frequentes, testes e documentação, supondo zero contexto para o repositório de código e utilizando boas práticas como DRY e YAGNI.","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать комплексные, разделенные на части планы реализации, включающие частые коммиты, тестирование и документацию, предполагая нулевой контекст для кодовой базы и используя лучшие практики, такие как DRY и YAGNI.","ar":"يمكن للعميل إنشاء خطط تنفيذ شاملة ومقسمة إلى قطع، متضمنة الإلتزامات المتكررة والاختبار والتوثيق، افتراضًا عدم وجود سياق للكود والاستفادة من أفضل الممارسات مثل DRY و YAGNI."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating step-by-step task plans for complex projects","Documenting code implementation for new team members","Creating testing plans for multi-step tasks"],"zh":["为复杂项目生成步骤式任务计划","为新团队成员记录代码实现","为多步骤任务创建测试计划"],"ja":["複雑なプロジェクトのためのステップバイステップのタスクプランの生成","新しいチームメンバーのためのコード実装の文書化","マルチステップタスクのためのテストプランの作成"],"ko":["복잡한 프로젝트를 위한 단계별 작업 계획 생성","새 팀 구성원의 코드 구현 문서화","다단계 작업을 위한 테스트 계획 생성"],"es":["Generación de planes de tareas paso a paso para proyectos complejos","Documentación de la implementación de código para nuevos miembros del equipo","Creación de planes de prueba para tareas de varios pasos"],"fr":["Génération de plans de tâches étape par étape pour des projets complexes","Documentation de la mise en œuvre du code pour les nouveaux membres de l''équipe","Création de plans de test pour des tâches multi-étapes"],"de":["Erstellung von Schritt-für-Schritt-Aufgabenplänen für komplexe Projekte","Dokumentation der Codeimplementierung für neue Teammitglieder","Erstellung von Testplänen für mehrschrittige Aufgaben"],"pt":["Geração de planos de tarefas passo a passo para projetos complexos","Documentação da implementação do código para novos membros da equipe","Criação de planos de teste para tarefas multi-etapas"],"ru":["Генерация пошаговых планов задач для сложных проектов","Документирование реализации кода для новых членов команды","Создание планов тестирования для задач с несколькими шагами"],"ar":["إنشاء خطط العمل خطوة بخطوة للمشاريع المعقدة","توثيق تنفيذ الشفرة لأعضاء الفريق الجدد","إنشاء خطط الاختبار للمهام متعددة الخطوات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Assumes skilled developer with limited domain knowledge","Requires thorough understanding of codebase and problem domain"],"zh":["假设开发者具有有限的领域知识","需要对代码库和问题领域有彻底的理解"],"ja":["開発者に限定されたドメイン知識があることを前提とする","コードベースと問題ドメインに対する徹底的な理解が必要"],"ko":["개발자가 제한된 도메인 지식을 갖고 있다고 가정","코드베이스와 문제 도메인에 대한 철저한 이해가 필요"],"es":["Supone un desarrollador capacitado con conocimientos de dominio limitados","Requiere una comprensión exhaustiva del código base y del dominio del problema"],"fr":["Suppose un développeur qualifié avec des connaissances de domaine limitées","Nécessite une compréhension approfondie de la base de code et du domaine du problème"],"de":["Geht von einem qualifizierten Entwickler mit begrenzten Domänenkenntnissen aus","Benötigt ein gründliches Verständnis des Codebase und des Problem-domäne"],"pt":["Pressupõe desenvolvedor habilidoso com conhecimento limitado de domínio","Exige compreensão aprofundada da base de código e do domínio do problema"],"ru":["Предполагает опытного разработчика с ограниченными знаниями предметной области","Требует глубокого понимания кодовой базы и предметной области"],"ar":["يفترض مطورًا ماهرًا مع معرفة محدودة بالمجال","يتطلب فهمًا عميقًا لقاعدة الكود ومجال المشكلة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"8a9198d4d9efbcad6e019b17c422c182113062c864b6154ec2a3ba2ed0b6b9d0","repoEtag":"W/\"c0159b000a3f1065b2a623072c2f281d1dae59e39bce28acebe789d1e6a6aa8e\"","qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('affaan-m/everything-claude-code/configure-ecc', 'official', 'affaan-m', 'everything-claude-code', 'affaan-m/everything-claude-code', 'configure-ecc', 55024, 6781, 80, '2026-03-01T05:07:39Z', '2026-03-01T05:09:37.373Z', '5f3506f77baf2b910b89dd66d98eb47ed0135e77d6b81d10e233d596cff0cf19', '{"id":"affaan-m/everything-claude-code/configure-ecc","name":"configure-ecc","description":{"zh":"一个用于配置Everything Claude Code（ECC）项目的交互式安装向导，用于选择和安装技能和规则","ja":"Everything Claude Code（ECC）プロジェクトの設定用インタラクティブインストールウィザード","ko":"Everything Claude Code（ECC） 프로젝트를 설정하는 인터랙티브 설치 마법사","es":"El configurador ECC es una herramienta interactiva para instalar habilidades y reglas de Everything Claude Code de forma selectiva","fr":"Le configurateur ECC est un outil interactif pour installer des compétences et des règles de Everything Claude Code de manière sélective","de":"Der ECC-Konfigurator ist ein interaktives Tool zur selektiven Installation von Fähigkeiten und Regeln von Everything Claude Code","pt":"O ECC é uma ferramenta de IA que oferece um instalador interativo para selecionar e instalar habilidades e regras.","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Everything Claude Code — это инструмент, который предоставляет интерактивный инсталлятор для выбора и установки навыков и правил.","ar":"ECC هو أداة ذكاء اصطناعي توفر مثبتًا تفاعليًا لتحديد وتثبيت المهارات والقواعد.","en":"Interactive installer for Everything Claude Code — guides users through selecting and installing skills and rules to user-level or project-level directories, verifies paths, and optionally optimizes installed files."},"owner":"affaan-m","repo":"everything-claude-code","repoPath":"affaan-m/everything-claude-code","stars":55024,"forks":6781,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T05:07:39Z","topics":["ai-agents","anthropic","claude","claude-code","developer-tools","llm","mcp","productivity"],"skillMd":{"name":"configure-ecc","description":"Interactive installer for Everything Claude Code — guides users through selecting and installing skills and rules to user-level or project-level directories, verifies paths, and optionally optimizes installed files.","bodyPreview":"# Configure Everything Claude Code (ECC)\n\nAn interactive, step-by-step installation wizard for the Everything Claude Code project. Uses `AskUserQuestion` to guide users through selective installation of skills and rules, then verifies correctness and offers optimization.\n\n## When to Activate\n\n- User says \"configure ecc\", \"install ecc\", \"setup everything claude code\", or similar\n- User wants to selectively install skills or rules from this project\n- User wants to verify or fix an existing ECC ins","body":"# Configure Everything Claude Code (ECC)\n\nAn interactive, step-by-step installation wizard for the Everything Claude Code project. Uses `AskUserQuestion` to guide users through selective installation of skills and rules, then verifies correctness and offers optimization.\n\n## When to Activate\n\n- User says \"configure ecc\", \"install ecc\", \"setup everything claude code\", or similar\n- User wants to selectively install skills or rules from this project\n- User wants to verify or fix an existing ECC installation\n- User wants to optimize installed skills or rules for their project\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nThis skill must be accessible to Claude Code before activation. Two ways to bootstrap:\n1. **Via Plugin**: `/plugin install everything-claude-code` — the plugin loads this skill automatically\n2. **Manual**: Copy only this skill to `~/.claude/skills/configure-ecc/SKILL.md`, then activate by saying \"configure ecc\"\n\n---\n\n## Step 0: Clone ECC Repository\n\nBefore any installation, clone the latest ECC source to `/tmp`:\n\n```bash\nrm -rf /tmp/everything-claude-code\ngit clone https://github.com/affaan-m/everything-claude-code.git /tmp/everything-claude-code\n```\n\nSet `ECC_ROOT=/tmp/everything-claude-code` as the source for all subsequent copy operations.\n\nIf the clone fails (network issues, etc.), use `AskUserQuestion` to ask the user to provide a local path to an existing ECC clone.\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Choose Installation Level\n\nUse `AskUserQuestion` to ask the user where to install:\n\n```\nQuestion: \"Where should ECC components be installed?\"\nOptions:\n  - \"User-level (~/.claude/)\" — \"Applies to all your Claude Code projects\"\n  - \"Project-level (.claude/)\" — \"Applies only to the current project\"\n  - \"Both\" — \"Common/shared items user-level, project-specific items project-level\"\n```\n\nStore the choice as `INSTALL_LEVEL`. Set the target directory:\n- User-level: `TARGET=~/.claude`\n- Project-level: `TARGET=.claude` (relative to current project root)\n- Both: `TARGET_USER=~/.claude`, `TARGET_PROJECT=.claude`\n\nCreate the target directories if they don''t exist:\n```bash\nmkdir -p $TARGET/skills $TARGET/rules\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step 2: Select & Install Skills\n\n### 2a: Choose Scope (Core vs Niche)\n\nDefault to **Core (recommended for new users)** — copy `.agents/skills/*` plus `skills/search-first/` for research-first workflows. This bundle covers engineering, evals, verification, security, strategic compaction, frontend design, and Anthropic cross-functional skills (article-writing, content-engine, market-research, frontend-slides).\n\nUse `AskUserQuestion` (single select):\n```\nQuestion: \"Install core skills only, or include niche/framework packs?\"\nOptions:\n  - \"Core only (recommended)\" — \"tdd, e2e, evals, verification, research-first, security, frontend patterns, compacting, cross-functional Anthropic skills\"\n  - \"Core + selected niche\" — \"Add framework/domain-specific skills after core\"\n  - \"Niche only\" — \"Skip core, install specific framework/domain skills\"\nDefault: Core only\n```\n\nIf the user chooses niche or core + niche, continue to category selection below and only include those niche skills they pick.\n\n### 2b: Choose Skill Categories\n\nThere are 27 skills organized into 4 categories. Use `AskUserQuestion` with `multiSelect: true`:\n\n```\nQuestion: \"Which skill categories do you want to install?\"\nOptions:\n  - \"Framework & Language\" — \"Django, Spring Boot, Go, Python, Java, Frontend, Backend patterns\"\n  - \"Database\" — \"PostgreSQL, ClickHouse, JPA/Hibernate patterns\"\n  - \"Workflow & Quality\" — \"TDD, verification, learning, security review, compaction\"\n  - \"All skills\" — \"Install every available skill\"\n```\n\n### 2c: Confirm Individual Skills\n\nFor each selected category, print the full list of skills below and ask the user to confirm or deselect specific ones. If the list exceeds 4 items, print the list as text and use `AskUserQuestion` with an \"Install all listed\" option plus \"Other\" for the user to paste specific names.\n\n**Category: Framework & Language (17 skills)**\n\n| Skill | Description |\n|-------|-------------|\n| `backend-patterns` | Backend architecture, API design, server-side best practices for Node.js/Express/Next.js |\n| `coding-standards` | Universal coding standards for TypeScript, JavaScript, React, Node.js |\n| `django-patterns` | Django architecture, REST API with DRF, ORM, caching, signals, middleware |\n| `django-security` | Django security: auth, CSRF, SQL injection, XSS prevention |\n| `django-tdd` | Django testing with pytest-django, factory_boy, mocking, coverage |\n| `django-verification` | Django verification loop: migrations, linting, tests, security scans |\n| `frontend-patterns` | React, Next.js, state management, performance, UI patterns |\n| `frontend-slides` | Zero-dependency HTML presentations, style previews, and PPTX-to-web conversion |\n| `golang-patterns` | Idiomatic Go patterns, conventions for robust Go applications |\n| `golang-testing` | Go testing: table-driven tests, subtests, benchmarks, fuzzing |\n| `java-coding-standards` | Java coding standards for Spring Boot: naming, immutability, Optional, streams |\n| `python-patterns` | Pythonic idioms, PEP 8, type hints, best practices |\n| `python-testing` | Python testing with pytest, TDD, fixtures, mocking, parametrization |\n| `springboot-patterns` | Spring Boot architecture, REST API, layered services, caching, async |\n| `springboot-security` | Spring Security: authn/authz, validation, CSRF, secrets, rate limiting |\n| `springboot-tdd` | Spring Boot TDD with JUnit 5, Mockito, MockMvc, Testcontainers |\n| `springboot-verification` | Spring Boot verification: build, static analysis, tests, security scans |\n\n**Category: Database (3 skills)**\n\n| Skill | Description |\n|-------|-------------|\n| `clickhouse-io` | ClickHouse patterns, query optimization, analytics, data engineering |\n| `jpa-patterns` | JPA/Hibernate entity design, relationships, query optimization, transactions |\n| `postgres-patterns` | PostgreSQL query optimization, schema design, indexing, security |\n\n**Category: Workflow & Quality (8 skills)**\n\n| Skill | Description |\n|-------|-------------|\n| `continuous-learning` | Auto-extract reusable patterns from sessions as learned skills |\n| `continuous-learning-v2` | Instinct-based learning with confidence scoring, evolves into skills/commands/agents |\n| `eval-harness` | Formal evaluation framework for eval-driven development (EDD) |\n| `iterative-retrieval` | Progressive context refinement for subagent context problem |\n| `security-review` | Security checklist: auth, input, secrets, API, payment features |\n| `strategic-compact` | Suggests manual context compaction at logical intervals |\n| `tdd-workflow` | Enforces TDD with 80%+ coverage: unit, integration, E2E |\n| `verification-loop` | Verification and quality loop patterns |\n\n**Category: Business & Content (5 skills)**\n\n| Skill | Description |\n|-------|-------------|\n| `article-writing` | Long-form writing in a supplied voice using notes, examples, or source docs |\n| `content-engine` | Multi-platform social content, scripts, and repurposing workflows |\n| `market-research` | Source-attributed market, competitor, fund, and technology research |\n| `investor-materials` | Pitch decks, one-pagers, investor memos, and financial models |\n| `investor-outreach` | Personalized investor cold emails, warm intros, and follow-ups |\n\n**Standalone**\n\n| Skill | Description |\n|-------|-------------|\n| `project-guidelines-example` | Template for creating project-specific skills |\n\n### 2d: Execute Installation\n\nFor each selected skill, copy the entire skill directory:\n```bash\ncp -r $ECC_ROOT/skills/<skill-name> $TARGET/skills/\n```\n\nNote: `continuous-learning` and `continuous-learning-v2` have extra files (config.json, hooks, scripts) — ensure the entire directory is copied, not just SKILL.md.\n\n---\n\n## Step 3: Select & Install Rules\n\nUse `AskUserQuestion` with `multiSelect: true`:\n\n```\nQuestion: \"Which rule sets do you want to install?\"\nOptions:\n  - \"Common rules (Recommended)\" — \"Language-agnostic principles: coding style, git workflow, testing, security, etc. (8 files)\"\n  - \"TypeScript/JavaScript\" — \"TS/JS patterns, hooks, testing with Playwright (5 files)\"\n  - \"Python\" — \"Python patterns, pytest, black/ruff formatting (5 files)\"\n  - \"Go\" — \"Go patterns, table-driven tests, gofmt/staticcheck (5 files)\"\n```\n\nExecute installation:\n```bash\n# Common rules (flat copy into rules/)\ncp -r $ECC_ROOT/rules/common/* $TARGET/rules/\n\n# Language-specific rules (flat copy into rules/)\ncp -r $ECC_ROOT/rules/typescript/* $TARGET/rules/   # if selected\ncp -r $ECC_ROOT/rules/python/* $TARGET/rules/        # if selected\ncp -r $ECC_ROOT/rules/golang/* $TARGET/rules/        # if selected\n```\n\n**Important**: If the user selects any language-specific rules but NOT common rules, warn them:\n> \"Language-specific rules extend the common rules. Installing without common rules may result in incomplete coverage. Install common rules too?\"\n\n---\n\n## Step 4: Post-Installation Verification\n\nAfter installation, perform these automated checks:\n\n### 4a: Verify File Existence\n\nList all installed files and confirm they exist at the target location:\n```bash\nls -la $TARGET/skills/\nls -la $TARGET/rules/\n```\n\n### 4b: Check Path References\n\nScan all installed `.md` files for path references:\n```bash\ngrep -rn \"~/.claude/\" $TARGET/skills/ $TARGET/rules/\ngrep -rn \"../common/\" $TARGET/rules/\ngrep -rn \"skills/\" $TARGET/skills/\n```\n\n**For project-level installs**, flag any references to `~/.claude/` paths:\n- If a skill references `~/.claude/settings.json` — this is usually fine (settings are always user-level)\n- If a skill references `~/.claude/skills/` or `~/.claude/rules/` — this may be broken if installed only at project level\n- If a skill references another skill by name — check that the referenced skill was also installed\n\n### 4c: Check Cross-References Between Skills\n\nSome skills reference others. Verify these dependencies:\n- `django-tdd` may reference `django-patterns`\n- `springboot-tdd` may reference `springboot-patterns`\n- `continuous-learning-v2` references `~/.claude/homunculus/` directory\n- `python-testing` may reference `python-patterns`\n- `golang-testing` may reference `golang-patterns`\n- Language-specific rules reference `common/` counterparts\n\n### 4d: Report Issues\n\nFor each issue found, report:\n1. **File**: The file containing the problematic reference\n2. **Line**: The line number\n3. **Issue**: What''s wrong (e.g., \"references ~/.claude/skills/python-patterns but python-patterns was not installed\")\n4. **Suggested fix**: What to do (e.g., \"install python-patterns skill\" or \"update path to .claude/skills/\")\n\n---\n\n## Step 5: Optimize Installed Files (Optional)\n\nUse `AskUserQuestion`:\n\n```\nQuestion: \"Would you like to optimize the installed files for your project?\"\nOptions:\n  - \"Optimize skills\" — \"Remove irrelevant sections, adjust paths, tailor to your tech stack\"\n  - \"Optimize rules\" — \"Adjust coverage targets, add project-specific patterns, customize tool configs\"\n  - \"Optimize both\" — \"Full optimization of all installed files\"\n  - \"Skip\" — \"Keep everything as-is\"\n```\n\n### If optimizing skills:\n1. Read each installed SKILL.md\n2. Ask the user what their project''s tech stack is (if not already known)\n3. For each skill, suggest removals of irrelevant sections\n4. Edit the SKILL.md files in-place at the installation target (NOT the source repo)\n5. Fix any path issues found in Step 4\n\n### If optimizing rules:\n1. Read each installed rule .md file\n2. Ask the user about their preferences:\n   - Test coverage target (default 80%)\n   - Preferred formatting tools\n   - Git workflow conventions\n   - Security requirements\n3. Edit the rule files in-place at the installation target\n\n**Critical**: Only modify files in the installation target (`$TARGET/`), NEVER modify files in the source ECC repository (`$ECC_ROOT/`).\n\n---\n\n## Step 6: Installation Summary\n\nClean up the cloned repository from `/tmp`:\n\n```bash\nrm -rf /tmp/everything-claude-code\n```\n\nThen print a summary report:\n\n```\n## ECC Installation Complete\n\n### Installation Target\n- Level: [user-level / project-level / both]\n- Path: [target path]\n\n### Skills Installed ([count])\n- skill-1, skill-2, skill-3, ...\n\n### Rules Installed ([count])\n- common (8 files)\n- typescript (5 files)\n- ...\n\n### Verification Results\n- [count] issues found, [count] fixed\n- [list any remaining issues]\n\n### Optimizations Applied\n- [list changes made, or \"None\"]\n```\n\n---\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### \"Skills not being picked up by Claude Code\"\n- Verify the skill directory contains a `SKILL.md` file (not just loose .md files)\n- For user-level: check `~/.claude/skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md` exists\n- For project-level: check `.claude/skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md` exists\n\n### \"Rules not working\"\n- Rules are flat files, not in subdirectories: `$TARGET/rules/coding-style.md` (correct) vs `$TARGET/rules/common/coding-style.md` (incorrect for flat install)\n- Restart Claude Code after installing rules\n\n### \"Path reference errors after project-level install\"\n- Some skills assume `~/.claude/` paths. Run Step 4 verification to find and fix these.\n- For `continuous-learning-v2`, the `~/.claude/homunculus/` directory is always user-level — this is expected and not an error.\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-03-01T05:09:37.373Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"配置Everything Claude Code（ECC）AI工具","ja":"Everything Claude Code（ECC）を設定する - AIエージェント","ko":"Everything Claude Code（ECC） 설정 - AI 에이전트","es":"Configura Agentes de IA ECC","fr":"Configurez les Outils d''IA ECC","de":"Konfigurieren Sie ECC KI-Agenten","pt":"Configurar ECC: Ferramentas de IA para Desenvolvedores","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Настройка Everything Claude Code","ar":"تكوين ECC: أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي لل مطورين","en":"configure-ecc"},"description":{"zh":"一个用于配置Everything Claude Code（ECC）项目的交互式安装向导，用于选择和安装技能和规则","ja":"Everything Claude Code（ECC）プロジェクトの設定用インタラクティブインストールウィザード","ko":"Everything Claude Code（ECC） 프로젝트를 설정하는 인터랙티브 설치 마법사","es":"El configurador ECC es una herramienta interactiva para instalar habilidades y reglas de Everything Claude Code de forma selectiva","fr":"Le configurateur ECC est un outil interactif pour installer des compétences et des règles de Everything Claude Code de manière sélective","de":"Der ECC-Konfigurator ist ein interaktives Tool zur selektiven Installation von Fähigkeiten und Regeln von Everything Claude Code","pt":"O ECC é uma ferramenta de IA que oferece um instalador interativo para selecionar e instalar habilidades e regras.","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Everything Claude Code — это инструмент, который предоставляет интерактивный инсталлятор для выбора и установки навыков и правил.","ar":"ECC هو أداة ذكاء اصطناعي توفر مثبتًا تفاعليًا لتحديد وتثبيت المهارات والقواعد.","en":"Interactive installer for Everything Claude Code — guides users through selecting and installing skills and rules to user-level or project-level directories,..."},"definition":{"en":"Interactive installer for Everything Claude Code — guides users through selecting and installing skills and rules to user-level or project-level directories, verifies paths, and optionally optimizes installed files."},"features":{"zh":["交互式安装向导","选择和安装技能和规则","验证路径和优化安装文件"],"ja":["インタラクティブなインストールウィザード","スキルとルールの選択とインストール","パスの検証とインストールファイルの最適化"],"ko":["인터랙티브 설치 마법사","스킬과 규칙의 선택과 설치","경로의 검증과 설치 파일의 최적화"],"es":["Instalación interactiva de habilidades y reglas","Verificación de rutas y optimización de archivos","Selección de habilidades y reglas personalizadas","Instalación en directorios de usuario o proyecto","Compatibilidad con CLI"],"fr":["Installation interactive de compétences et de règles","Vérification des chemins et optimisation des fichiers","Sélection de compétences et de règles personnalisées","Installation dans des répertoires d''utilisateur ou de projet","Compatibilité avec la CLI"],"de":["Interaktive Installation von Fähigkeiten und Regeln","Überprüfung von Pfaden und Optimierung von Dateien","Auswahl von benutzerdefinierten Fähigkeiten und Regeln","Installation in Benutzer- oder Projektverzeichnissen","Kompatibilität mit der CLI"],"pt":["Instalador interativo para seleção de habilidades e regras","Verificação de caminhos e otimização de arquivos","Instalação de habilidades e regras em diretórios de usuário ou projeto","Suporte a desenvolvedores para projetos de IA","Ferramentas de produtividade para desenvolvedores"],"ru":["Интерактивный инсталлятор для выбора навыков и правил","Проверка путей и оптимизация файлов","Установка навыков и правил в директориях пользователя или проекта","Поддержка разработчиков для проектов ИИ","Инструменты производительности для разработчиков"],"ar":["مثبت تفاعلي لتحديد المهارات والقواعد","تحقق من المسارات وتحسين الملفات","تثبيت المهارات والقواعد في دليل المستخدم أو المشروع","دعم المطورين لمشاريع الذكاء الاصطناعي","أدوات الإنتاجية للمطورين"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI工具","Everything Claude Code","配置","安装","交互式安装向导","技能和规则"],"ja":["AIエージェント","Everything Claude Code","設定","インストール","インタラクティブなインストールウィザード","スキルとルール"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","Everything Claude Code","설정","설치","인터랙티브 설치 마법사","스킬과 규칙"],"es":["Agentes de IA","Herramientas de desarrollo","Instalación de habilidades","Reglas de Everything Claude Code","Configuración de ECC","Desarrollo de software","Productividad de desarrollo"],"fr":["Outils d''IA","Outils de développement","Installation de compétences","Règles de Everything Claude Code","Configuration d''ECC","Développement de logiciels","Productivité de développement"],"de":["KI-Agenten","Entwickler-Tools","Installation von Fähigkeiten","Regeln von Everything Claude Code","Konfiguration von ECC","Software-Entwicklung","Entwickler-Produktivität"],"pt":["ferramentas de ia","desenvolvedores de ia","configurar ecc","instalar ecc","otimizar ecc","produtividade para desenvolvedores","ia para desenvolvedores","ferramentas de desenvolvimento de ia"],"ru":["ИИ инструменты","разработчики ИИ","настроить ИИ Агенты","установить ИИ Агенты","оптимизировать ИИ Агенты","производительность для разработчиков","ИИ для разработчиков","инструменты разработки ИИ"],"ar":["أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","مطورو الذكاء الاصطناعي","تكوين ECC","تثبيت ECC","تحسين ECC","إنتاجية للمطورين","الذكاء الاصطناعي للمطورين","أدوات تطوير الذكاء الاصطناعي"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Installation Manager Agents needing guided deployment of Claude Code skills and rules.","zh":"非常适合需要引导式部署Claude Code技能和规则的安装管理器代理。","ja":"Claude Codeのスキルとルールのガイド付きデプロイメントを必要とするインストールマネージャーエージェントに最適です。","ko":"Claude Code 기술과 규칙의 가이드된 배포가 필요한 설치 관리자 에이전트에 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Installation Manager que necesitan una implementación guiada de habilidades y reglas de Claude Code.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Installation Manager ayant besoin d''un déploiement guidé des compétences et des règles de Claude Code.","de":"Perfekt für Installation Manager-Agents, die eine guidierte Bereitstellung von Claude Code-Fähigkeiten und -Regeln benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Gerenciamento de Instalação que necessitam de uma implantação guiada de skills e regras do Claude Code.","ru":"Идеально подходит для Агентов Менеджера Установки, которым требуется управляемая установка навыков и правил Claude Code.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء مدير التثبيت الذين يحتاجون إلى نشر موجه لمهارات وقواعد Claude Code."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables interactive installation workflows using AskUserQuestion for selective deployment to user-level or project-level directories. Provides path verification and optional file optimization for Everything Claude Code components.","zh":"利用AskUserQuestion实现交互式安装工作流，可选择性地部署到用户级或项目级目录。为Everything Claude Code组件提供路径验证和可选的文件优化功能。","ja":"AskUserQuestionを使用した対話型インストールワークフローを可能にし、ユーザーレベルまたはプロジェクトレベルのディレクトリへの選択的デプロイメントを実現します。Everything Claude Codeコンポーネントのパス検証とオプションのファイル最適化を提供します。","ko":"AskUserQuestion을 사용하여 사용자 수준 또는 프로젝트 수준 디렉토리에 선택적으로 배포하는 대화형 설치 워크플로우를 가능하게 합니다. Everything Claude Code 구성 요소에 대한 경로 검증 및 선택적 파일 최적화를 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita flujos de trabajo de instalación interactivos utilizando AskUserQuestion para un despliegue selectivo en directorios de nivel de usuario o de proyecto. Proporciona verificación de ruta y optimización de archivos opcional para los componentes de Everything Claude Code.","fr":"Permet des flux de travail d''installation interactifs en utilisant AskUserQuestion pour un déploiement sélectif dans des répertoires de niveau utilisateur ou de projet. Fournit une vérification de chemin et une optimisation de fichier facultative pour les composants Everything Claude Code.","de":"Ermöglicht interaktive Installations-Workflows unter Verwendung von AskUserQuestion für eine selektive Bereitstellung in Benutzer- oder Projektverzeichnissen. Bietet Pfadüberprüfung und optionale Dateioptimierung für Everything Claude Code-Komponenten.","pt":"Permite fluxos de trabalho de instalação interativos usando AskUserQuestion para implantação seletiva em diretórios de nível de usuário ou de projeto. Fornece verificação de caminho e otimização opcional de arquivos para componentes do Everything Claude Code.","ru":"Обеспечивает интерактивные процессы установки с использованием AskUserQuestion для выборочного развертывания в каталоги уровня пользователя или уровня проекта. Обеспечивает проверку пути и дополнительную оптимизацию файлов для компонентов Everything Claude Code.","ar":"يتيح سير عمل تثبيت تفاعلية باستخدام AskUserQuestion للنشر الانتقائي في أدلة مستوى المستخدم أو مستوى المشروع. يوفر التحقق من المسار وتحسين ملفات اختياري لمكونات Everything Claude Code."},"useCases":{"en":["Guiding users through selective skill installation","Verifying existing ECC installation paths","Optimizing installed skill files post-deployment","Managing project-level vs user-level rule deployments"],"zh":["引导用户完成选择性技能安装","验证现有ECC安装路径","优化部署后的已安装技能文件","管理项目级与用户级规则部署"],"ja":["選択的なスキルインストールのユーザーガイド","既存のECCインストールパスの検証","デプロイメント後のインストール済みスキルファイルの最適化","プロジェクトレベルとユーザーレベルのルールデプロイメントの管理"],"ko":["선택적 기술 설치 과정에서 사용자 안내","기존 ECC 설치 경로 확인","배포 후 설치된 기술 파일 최적화","프로젝트 수준 대 사용자 수준 규칙 배포 관리"],"es":["Guiar a los usuarios a través de la instalación selectiva de habilidades","Verificar las rutas de instalación de ECC existentes","Optimizar los archivos de habilidades instalados después de la implementación","Administrar implementaciones de reglas de nivel de proyecto frente a nivel de usuario"],"fr":["Guider les utilisateurs à travers l''installation sélective des compétences","Vérifier les chemins d''installation ECC existants","Optimiser les fichiers de compétences installés après le déploiement","Gérer les déploiements de règles de niveau de projet par rapport au niveau de l''utilisateur"],"de":["Benutzer durch die selektive Installation von Fähigkeiten führen","Vorhandene ECC-Installationspfade überprüfen","Installierte Fähigkeitsdateien nach der Bereitstellung optimieren","Regel-Implementierungen auf Projektebene im Vergleich zur Benutzerebene verwalten"],"pt":["Guiar usuários através da instalação seletiva de skills","Verificar caminhos de instalação existentes do ECC","Otimizar arquivos de skill instalados após a implantação","Gerenciar implantações de regras em nível de projeto versus nível de usuário"],"ru":["Направление пользователей через выборочную установку навыков","Проверка существующих путей установки ECC","Оптимизация установленных файлов навыков после развертывания","Управление развертыванием правил на уровне проекта и уровне пользователя"],"ar":["توجيه المستخدمين خلال التثبيت الانتقائي للمهارات","التحقق من مسارات تثبيت ECC الموجودة","تحسين ملفات المهارات المثبتة بعد النشر","إدارة عمليات نشر القواعد على مستوى المشروع مقابل مستوى المستخدم"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires filesystem access permissions","Dependent on Everything Claude Code project structure","Needs user interaction for installation choices"],"zh":["需要文件系统访问权限","依赖于Everything Claude Code项目结构","需要用户交互以进行安装选择"],"ja":["ファイルシステムへのアクセス権限が必要","Everything Claude Codeのプロジェクト構造に依存","インストール選択のためにユーザーインタラクションが必要"],"ko":["파일 시스템 액세스 권한 필요","Everything Claude Code 프로젝트 구조에 종속적","설치 선택을 위한 사용자 상호 작용 필요"],"es":["Requiere permisos de acceso al sistema de archivos","Dependiente de la estructura del proyecto Everything Claude Code","Necesita interacción del usuario para las opciones de instalación"],"fr":["Nécessite des autorisations d''accès au système de fichiers","Dépend de la structure du projet Everything Claude Code","Nécessite une interaction utilisateur pour les choix d''installation"],"de":["Benötigt Dateisystemzugriffsberechtigungen","Abhängig von der Projektstruktur von Everything Claude Code","Benötigt Benutzereingriff für Installationsauswahlen"],"pt":["Requer permissões de acesso ao sistema de arquivos","Dependente da estrutura de projeto do Everything Claude Code","Requer interação do usuário para escolhas de instalação"],"ru":["Требует разрешений на доступ к файловой системе","Зависит от структуры проекта Everything Claude Code","Требует взаимодействия с пользователем для выбора установки"],"ar":["يتطلب أذونات الوصول إلى نظام الملفات","يعتمد على هيكل مشروع Everything Claude Code","يتطلب تفاعل المستخدم لخيارات التثبيت"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"5f3506f77baf2b910b89dd66d98eb47ed0135e77d6b81d10e233d596cff0cf19","repoEtag":"W/\"1d66934774ad40d3d916abf4c33c3e340ab032f8212b35e12a94daa7359886c9\"","qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('affaan-m/everything-claude-code/deployment-patterns', 'official', 'affaan-m', 'everything-claude-code', 'affaan-m/everything-claude-code', 'deployment-patterns', 55024, 6781, 80, '2026-03-01T05:07:39Z', '2026-03-01T05:10:12.722Z', 'b2d18f90ea5f5b7e6c357c3ded7353fa2d23b04464eed4b81745b0c8340e31ba', '{"id":"affaan-m/everything-claude-code/deployment-patterns","name":"deployment-patterns","description":{"zh":"AI智能代理的部署模式包括CI/CD管道、Docker容器化和生产就绪检查","ja":"AIエージェントのデプロイパターンには、CI/CDパイプライン、Dockerコンテナ化、プロダクション準備チェックリストが含まれます","ko":"AI 에이전트의 배포 패턴에는 CI/CD 파이프라인, 도커 컨테이너화, 프로덕션 준비 체크리스트가 포함됩니다","es":"Los patrones de despliegue permiten implementar flujos de trabajo de despliegue eficientes y pipelines de CI/CD para aplicaciones web","fr":"Les modèles de déploiement permettent de mettre en œuvre des flux de travail de déploiement efficaces et des pipelines de CI/CD pour les applications web","de":"Deploy-Muster ermöglichen die Implementierung effizienter Deploy-Workflows und CI/CD-Pipelines für Webanwendungen","pt":"Implantação de aplicações web com padrões de implantação, CI/CD e Docker","ru":"Развертывание веб-приложений с паттернами развертывания, CI/CD и Docker","ar":"توزيع تطبيقات الويب بنماذج التوزيع والسي سي دي والدッカー","en":"Deployment workflows, CI/CD pipeline patterns, Docker containerization, health checks, rollback strategies, and production readiness checklists for web applications."},"owner":"affaan-m","repo":"everything-claude-code","repoPath":"affaan-m/everything-claude-code","stars":55024,"forks":6781,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T05:07:39Z","topics":["ai-agents","anthropic","claude","claude-code","developer-tools","llm","mcp","productivity"],"skillMd":{"name":"deployment-patterns","description":"Deployment workflows, CI/CD pipeline patterns, Docker containerization, health checks, rollback strategies, and production readiness checklists for web applications.","bodyPreview":"# Deployment Patterns\n\nProduction deployment workflows and CI/CD best practices.\n\n## When to Activate\n\n- Setting up CI/CD pipelines\n- Dockerizing an application\n- Planning deployment strategy (blue-green, canary, rolling)\n- Implementing health checks and readiness probes\n- Preparing for a production release\n- Configuring environment-specific settings\n\n## Deployment Strategies\n\n### Rolling Deployment (Default)\n\nReplace instances gradually — old and new versions run simultaneously during rollout.","body":"# Deployment Patterns\n\nProduction deployment workflows and CI/CD best practices.\n\n## When to Activate\n\n- Setting up CI/CD pipelines\n- Dockerizing an application\n- Planning deployment strategy (blue-green, canary, rolling)\n- Implementing health checks and readiness probes\n- Preparing for a production release\n- Configuring environment-specific settings\n\n## Deployment Strategies\n\n### Rolling Deployment (Default)\n\nReplace instances gradually — old and new versions run simultaneously during rollout.\n\n```\nInstance 1: v1 → v2  (update first)\nInstance 2: v1        (still running v1)\nInstance 3: v1        (still running v1)\n\nInstance 1: v2\nInstance 2: v1 → v2  (update second)\nInstance 3: v1\n\nInstance 1: v2\nInstance 2: v2\nInstance 3: v1 → v2  (update last)\n```\n\n**Pros:** Zero downtime, gradual rollout\n**Cons:** Two versions run simultaneously — requires backward-compatible changes\n**Use when:** Standard deployments, backward-compatible changes\n\n### Blue-Green Deployment\n\nRun two identical environments. Switch traffic atomically.\n\n```\nBlue  (v1) ← traffic\nGreen (v2)   idle, running new version\n\n# After verification:\nBlue  (v1)   idle (becomes standby)\nGreen (v2) ← traffic\n```\n\n**Pros:** Instant rollback (switch back to blue), clean cutover\n**Cons:** Requires 2x infrastructure during deployment\n**Use when:** Critical services, zero-tolerance for issues\n\n### Canary Deployment\n\nRoute a small percentage of traffic to the new version first.\n\n```\nv1: 95% of traffic\nv2:  5% of traffic  (canary)\n\n# If metrics look good:\nv1: 50% of traffic\nv2: 50% of traffic\n\n# Final:\nv2: 100% of traffic\n```\n\n**Pros:** Catches issues with real traffic before full rollout\n**Cons:** Requires traffic splitting infrastructure, monitoring\n**Use when:** High-traffic services, risky changes, feature flags\n\n## Docker\n\n### Multi-Stage Dockerfile (Node.js)\n\n```dockerfile\n# Stage 1: Install dependencies\nFROM node:22-alpine AS deps\nWORKDIR /app\nCOPY package.json package-lock.json ./\nRUN npm ci --production=false\n\n# Stage 2: Build\nFROM node:22-alpine AS builder\nWORKDIR /app\nCOPY --from=deps /app/node_modules ./node_modules\nCOPY . .\nRUN npm run build\nRUN npm prune --production\n\n# Stage 3: Production image\nFROM node:22-alpine AS runner\nWORKDIR /app\n\nRUN addgroup -g 1001 -S appgroup && adduser -S appuser -u 1001\nUSER appuser\n\nCOPY --from=builder --chown=appuser:appgroup /app/node_modules ./node_modules\nCOPY --from=builder --chown=appuser:appgroup /app/dist ./dist\nCOPY --from=builder --chown=appuser:appgroup /app/package.json ./\n\nENV NODE_ENV=production\nEXPOSE 3000\n\nHEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=3s --start-period=5s --retries=3 \\\n  CMD wget --no-verbose --tries=1 --spider http://localhost:3000/health || exit 1\n\nCMD [\"node\", \"dist/server.js\"]\n```\n\n### Multi-Stage Dockerfile (Go)\n\n```dockerfile\nFROM golang:1.22-alpine AS builder\nWORKDIR /app\nCOPY go.mod go.sum ./\nRUN go mod download\nCOPY . .\nRUN CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=linux go build -ldflags=\"-s -w\" -o /server ./cmd/server\n\nFROM alpine:3.19 AS runner\nRUN apk --no-cache add ca-certificates\nRUN adduser -D -u 1001 appuser\nUSER appuser\n\nCOPY --from=builder /server /server\n\nEXPOSE 8080\nHEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=3s CMD wget -qO- http://localhost:8080/health || exit 1\nCMD [\"/server\"]\n```\n\n### Multi-Stage Dockerfile (Python/Django)\n\n```dockerfile\nFROM python:3.12-slim AS builder\nWORKDIR /app\nRUN pip install --no-cache-dir uv\nCOPY requirements.txt .\nRUN uv pip install --system --no-cache -r requirements.txt\n\nFROM python:3.12-slim AS runner\nWORKDIR /app\n\nRUN useradd -r -u 1001 appuser\nUSER appuser\n\nCOPY --from=builder /usr/local/lib/python3.12/site-packages /usr/local/lib/python3.12/site-packages\nCOPY --from=builder /usr/local/bin /usr/local/bin\nCOPY . .\n\nENV PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1\nEXPOSE 8000\n\nHEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=3s CMD python -c \"import urllib.request; urllib.request.urlopen(''http://localhost:8000/health/'')\" || exit 1\nCMD [\"gunicorn\", \"config.wsgi:application\", \"--bind\", \"0.0.0.0:8000\", \"--workers\", \"4\"]\n```\n\n### Docker Best Practices\n\n```\n# GOOD practices\n- Use specific version tags (node:22-alpine, not node:latest)\n- Multi-stage builds to minimize image size\n- Run as non-root user\n- Copy dependency files first (layer caching)\n- Use .dockerignore to exclude node_modules, .git, tests\n- Add HEALTHCHECK instruction\n- Set resource limits in docker-compose or k8s\n\n# BAD practices\n- Running as root\n- Using :latest tags\n- Copying entire repo in one COPY layer\n- Installing dev dependencies in production image\n- Storing secrets in image (use env vars or secrets manager)\n```\n\n## CI/CD Pipeline\n\n### GitHub Actions (Standard Pipeline)\n\n```yaml\nname: CI/CD\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\n  pull_request:\n    branches: [main]\n\njobs:\n  test:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n        with:\n          node-version: 22\n          cache: npm\n      - run: npm ci\n      - run: npm run lint\n      - run: npm run typecheck\n      - run: npm test -- --coverage\n      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4\n        if: always()\n        with:\n          name: coverage\n          path: coverage/\n\n  build:\n    needs: test\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    if: github.ref == ''refs/heads/main''\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - uses: docker/setup-buildx-action@v3\n      - uses: docker/login-action@v3\n        with:\n          registry: ghcr.io\n          username: ${{ github.actor }}\n          password: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n      - uses: docker/build-push-action@v5\n        with:\n          push: true\n          tags: ghcr.io/${{ github.repository }}:${{ github.sha }}\n          cache-from: type=gha\n          cache-to: type=gha,mode=max\n\n  deploy:\n    needs: build\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    if: github.ref == ''refs/heads/main''\n    environment: production\n    steps:\n      - name: Deploy to production\n        run: |\n          # Platform-specific deployment command\n          # Railway: railway up\n          # Vercel: vercel --prod\n          # K8s: kubectl set image deployment/app app=ghcr.io/${{ github.repository }}:${{ github.sha }}\n          echo \"Deploying ${{ github.sha }}\"\n```\n\n### Pipeline Stages\n\n```\nPR opened:\n  lint → typecheck → unit tests → integration tests → preview deploy\n\nMerged to main:\n  lint → typecheck → unit tests → integration tests → build image → deploy staging → smoke tests → deploy production\n```\n\n## Health Checks\n\n### Health Check Endpoint\n\n```typescript\n// Simple health check\napp.get(\"/health\", (req, res) => {\n  res.status(200).json({ status: \"ok\" });\n});\n\n// Detailed health check (for internal monitoring)\napp.get(\"/health/detailed\", async (req, res) => {\n  const checks = {\n    database: await checkDatabase(),\n    redis: await checkRedis(),\n    externalApi: await checkExternalApi(),\n  };\n\n  const allHealthy = Object.values(checks).every(c => c.status === \"ok\");\n\n  res.status(allHealthy ? 200 : 503).json({\n    status: allHealthy ? \"ok\" : \"degraded\",\n    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n    version: process.env.APP_VERSION || \"unknown\",\n    uptime: process.uptime(),\n    checks,\n  });\n});\n\nasync function checkDatabase(): Promise<HealthCheck> {\n  try {\n    await db.query(\"SELECT 1\");\n    return { status: \"ok\", latency_ms: 2 };\n  } catch (err) {\n    return { status: \"error\", message: \"Database unreachable\" };\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Kubernetes Probes\n\n```yaml\nlivenessProbe:\n  httpGet:\n    path: /health\n    port: 3000\n  initialDelaySeconds: 10\n  periodSeconds: 30\n  failureThreshold: 3\n\nreadinessProbe:\n  httpGet:\n    path: /health\n    port: 3000\n  initialDelaySeconds: 5\n  periodSeconds: 10\n  failureThreshold: 2\n\nstartupProbe:\n  httpGet:\n    path: /health\n    port: 3000\n  initialDelaySeconds: 0\n  periodSeconds: 5\n  failureThreshold: 30    # 30 * 5s = 150s max startup time\n```\n\n## Environment Configuration\n\n### Twelve-Factor App Pattern\n\n```bash\n# All config via environment variables — never in code\nDATABASE_URL=postgres://user:pass@host:5432/db\nREDIS_URL=redis://host:6379/0\nAPI_KEY=${API_KEY}           # injected by secrets manager\nLOG_LEVEL=info\nPORT=3000\n\n# Environment-specific behavior\nNODE_ENV=production          # or staging, development\nAPP_ENV=production           # explicit app environment\n```\n\n### Configuration Validation\n\n```typescript\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst envSchema = z.object({\n  NODE_ENV: z.enum([\"development\", \"staging\", \"production\"]),\n  PORT: z.coerce.number().default(3000),\n  DATABASE_URL: z.string().url(),\n  REDIS_URL: z.string().url(),\n  JWT_SECRET: z.string().min(32),\n  LOG_LEVEL: z.enum([\"debug\", \"info\", \"warn\", \"error\"]).default(\"info\"),\n});\n\n// Validate at startup — fail fast if config is wrong\nexport const env = envSchema.parse(process.env);\n```\n\n## Rollback Strategy\n\n### Instant Rollback\n\n```bash\n# Docker/Kubernetes: point to previous image\nkubectl rollout undo deployment/app\n\n# Vercel: promote previous deployment\nvercel rollback\n\n# Railway: redeploy previous commit\nrailway up --commit <previous-sha>\n\n# Database: rollback migration (if reversible)\nnpx prisma migrate resolve --rolled-back <migration-name>\n```\n\n### Rollback Checklist\n\n- [ ] Previous image/artifact is available and tagged\n- [ ] Database migrations are backward-compatible (no destructive changes)\n- [ ] Feature flags can disable new features without deploy\n- [ ] Monitoring alerts configured for error rate spikes\n- [ ] Rollback tested in staging before production release\n\n## Production Readiness Checklist\n\nBefore any production deployment:\n\n### Application\n- [ ] All tests pass (unit, integration, E2E)\n- [ ] No hardcoded secrets in code or config files\n- [ ] Error handling covers all edge cases\n- [ ] Logging is structured (JSON) and does not contain PII\n- [ ] Health check endpoint returns meaningful status\n\n### Infrastructure\n- [ ] Docker image builds reproducibly (pinned versions)\n- [ ] Environment variables documented and validated at startup\n- [ ] Resource limits set (CPU, memory)\n- [ ] Horizontal scaling configured (min/max instances)\n- [ ] SSL/TLS enabled on all endpoints\n\n### Monitoring\n- [ ] Application metrics exported (request rate, latency, errors)\n- [ ] Alerts configured for error rate > threshold\n- [ ] Log aggregation set up (structured logs, searchable)\n- [ ] Uptime monitoring on health endpoint\n\n### Security\n- [ ] Dependencies scanned for CVEs\n- [ ] CORS configured for allowed origins only\n- [ ] Rate limiting enabled on public endpoints\n- [ ] Authentication and authorization verified\n- [ ] Security headers set (CSP, HSTS, X-Frame-Options)\n\n### Operations\n- [ ] Rollback plan documented and tested\n- [ ] Database migration tested against production-sized data\n- [ ] Runbook for common failure scenarios\n- [ ] On-call rotation and escalation path defined\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-03-01T05:10:12.722Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能代理部署模式","ja":"AIエージェントのデプロイパターン","ko":"AI 에이전트 배포 패턴","es":"Patrones de despliegue con Agentes de IA","fr":"Modèles de déploiement avec Outils d''IA","de":"Deploy-Muster mit KI-Agenten","pt":"Padrões de Implantação com Ferramentas de IA","ru":"Паттерны развертывания с ИИ Агентами","ar":"نماذج التوزيع مع أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","en":"deployment-patterns"},"description":{"zh":"AI智能代理的部署模式包括CI/CD管道、Docker容器化和生产就绪检查","ja":"AIエージェントのデプロイパターンには、CI/CDパイプライン、Dockerコンテナ化、プロダクション準備チェックリストが含まれます","ko":"AI 에이전트의 배포 패턴에는 CI/CD 파이프라인, 도커 컨테이너화, 프로덕션 준비 체크리스트가 포함됩니다","es":"Los patrones de despliegue permiten implementar flujos de trabajo de despliegue eficientes y pipelines de CI/CD para aplicaciones web","fr":"Les modèles de déploiement permettent de mettre en œuvre des flux de travail de déploiement efficaces et des pipelines de CI/CD pour les applications web","de":"Deploy-Muster ermöglichen die Implementierung effizienter Deploy-Workflows und CI/CD-Pipelines für Webanwendungen","pt":"Implantação de aplicações web com padrões de implantação, CI/CD e Docker","ru":"Развертывание веб-приложений с паттернами развертывания, CI/CD и Docker","ar":"توزيع تطبيقات الويب بنماذج التوزيع والسي سي دي والدッカー","en":"Deployment workflows, CI/CD pipeline patterns, Docker containerization, health checks, rollback strategies, and production readiness checklists for web appli..."},"definition":{"en":"Deployment workflows, CI/CD pipeline patterns, Docker containerization, health checks, rollback strategies, and production readiness checklists for web applications."},"features":{"zh":["CI/CD管道","Docker容器化","生产就绪检查","滚动部署","蓝绿部署","金丝雀部署"],"ja":["CI/CDパイプライン","Dockerコンテナ化","プロダクション準備チェックリスト","ローリングデプロイ","ブルーグリーンデプロイ","カナリアデプロイ"],"ko":["CI/CD 파이프라인","도커 컨테이너화","프로덕션 준비 체크리스트","롤링 배포","블루-그린 배포","카나리아 배포"],"es":["Despliegue gradual de instancias","Dockerización de aplicaciones","Implementación de comprobaciones de salud y sondeos de preparación","Planificación de estrategias de despliegue","Configuración de ajustes de entorno específicos"],"fr":["Déploiement progressif d''instances","Cont